window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5701,"title":"Chapter 5701: Chapter 5700: Engineer! III","paragraphs":["His Provenance Realm had changed again, as it always did when he did.","Above the blue-gold hills, where there had once been a single unmoving star, there now hung a field of them. Radiant sun-singularities, one for every Provenance Essence he carried, burning steady in a sky that had no weather and asked for none. Anyone counting them would have arrived at the same number he did.","Eighty-nine!","Of course, that number had been eighty-six not so long ago. Standing in front of an architect and surviving the standing had apparently been worth three.","| VERITAS: 89|","|PROVENANCE: 89|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 88|","Ninety was close now!","Noah sat on the bank of the river of light where it ran fastest, in the shape his Provenance had settled into. Bare feet in the star-pooled shallows. Pure dark hair. Skin without a single mark on it, which was somewhat funny given the amount of it that had been removed recently.","His eyes were obsidian singularities in one second and endlessly blue in another, and they were currently pointed at his own right hand.","There was a ring on it that was not there.","Illusory, faint, gold, visible to nobody else in existence and barely visible to him. The residue of something a genius had left behind!","In truth, since another of his bodies was currently occupied with the considerable pleasures of being human in the Vasiliou Elseworld, he would have this body begin thr work.","So he sent his Provenance Essence into the ring.","He was ready to get started.","| Alright .|","The voice boomed out over the Realm, coming from the ring and from the air and from a little behind his own ears at once.","|It seems you are ready to get started, which means this will actually be an experiment for the both of us. I am not here. I am not even a little bit here. This is something unique of mine doing the talking.|","|I am like a record. Except considerably better than a record, because a genius designed it, and I can do a great many things a record cannot.|","|You can ask questions. Do so rarely. Questions interrupt my flow, and answering them will draw on your energy and your authority in ways you will feel. So any question you have for me will cost you. Price it before you open your mouth, and if that offends you, take it up with the man who is dead.|","|Most of what I carry stays locked until I have given you the basics and the introductions. So.|","|Welcome to Existential Engineering 101.|","The illusory ring pulsed.","Golden light spilled out of it and unfolded into the air above the river, and it wrote itself, in an ancient tongue that Noah found he could read without the smallest effort, as though the words had been waiting for eras for eyes that would bother.","EXISTENTIAL ENGINEERING: BASICS","...!","Noah looked at it with shining eyes.","And the voice continued.","|Now. When it comes to engineering, and all the crazy things around dimensional authority and existential narrative and truly terrifying levels of Dimensionality, I did what any reasonable person would do. I simplified all of it into an art.|","|I broke it down into the basic building blocks of existence, and I made those my engineering. Every design I ever made came from using the components of existence itself as ingredients for the immensity I built.|","|And there are many, many ingredients. I will have to teach you how to isolate parts of existence, timelines, parallel weavings, all of it, into clean separated ingredients you can actually construct with. That goes in our course on time and temporal mechanics, which you are not remotely ready for.|","|So let us start at the beginning. There is engineering, and there is alchemy. Sometimes they go hand in hand.|","Diagrams began to appear.","They unfolded out of the golden light one after another, hanging over the running river, drawn in that same old script with lines connecting the parts of them.","A vessel with something suspended inside it. A lattice with nine points. A shape Noah could not name at all, which annoyed him considerably.","| When a lower lifeform considers alchemy, it imagines boiling water and crushed herbs. When it considers engineering, it imagines metal struck against an anvil.|","|Compared to the truth, those are the playthings of children who have not yet worked out that they are living inside a locked room.|","|In fact, at their core, neither art is about the manipulation of physical matter at all. Both are the manipulation of absolute laws.|","|So ask yourself. What is an Aspect of Existence? Is it a thing you express, or is it a fundamental building block? If an Immense One can harvest the unspent Causes of a bloodline to mortar their pristine thrones, does that not make a Cause a brick?|","The lattice diagram brightened, and a single point on it detached and hung by itself, and the light around it wrote the word for brick.","Noah’s eyes did not leave it.","|Naturally, to use these bricks, one must understand conceptual extraction.|","|Alchemy is the act of boiling down a timeline that was violently aborted, skimming the grief off the top, and distilling the raw potential into a liquid truth. You take an abstract concept, the weight of a dying Primeval, the suppressed ambition of a harvested lineage, and you force it into a consumable state.|","|Thus, you are not brewing potions. You are drinking isolated existence.|","The vessel diagram filled slowly with something that had no color the Realm could render.","| By comparison, engineering is the framework that cages the extracted truth. Once you have distilled an aspect of existence, where do you put it? You weld it. You take the extracted Cause, or the extracted Provenance, and you carve pathways of narrative into it until it holds a shape and does work.|","|Since Aspects of Existence are merely ingredients, anything can be built.|","|A lesser smith builds a sword. A sovereign engineer builds a new timeline.|","|Become proficient enough at engineering existence itself, and you can construct mechanisms grand enough to mimic the Immense Ones. Engines that generate their own localized Scales. Their own rulings. Structures that bypass the architects entirely, since the architects only own the board so long as nobody else learns to make boards.|","|Perhaps you will even find, one day, that the foundational blueprints of Existence itself are recorded inside a grand conceptual structure somewhere.|","The light hung on that sentence a moment longer than it had hung on any other, and then moved on without explaining itself.","| In truth, existence is not sacred. It is simply waiting to be melted down.|","|But we are getting ahead of ourselves.|","|One of the more basic places to start is with an ingredient that happens to be the most stable one I ever found in nature, and I found that out through a great deal of trial and a considerable amount of tribulation.|","|That ingredient is a Cause.|","The nine-point lattice turned slowly above the river.","| Being able to harvest and isolate Causes as an ingredient is going to be basic work for you. And one of the better ways to harvest them is not from Observable Existences or Dimensions that are built out of those Causes, because the moment you take them away, the structure goes unstable and you will have made a mess for no reason.|","|Lifeforms are better. Unique ones. The kind capable of generating their own Causes are some of the best subjects you will ever find for this, and you will not necessarily be stripping the Cause away from them. You isolate the essence of the Cause, which they regenerate over time on their own.|","|We will start with Causes, and we will expand from there. Because when it comes to authorities, all of them distill. Provenance included. Everything can be reduced to its own unique ingredient, given enough patience and a sufficiently unpleasant amount of failure.|","|So let us start with something simple that requires Causes as an ingredient|","|Let us have you design your own Elsedimension.|","BOOM!","Simple?","That was something SIMPLE?","Noah sat very still on the bank of his own river, in his own Realm, with his eyes blazing!","| Now.|","|An Elsedimension is actually fairly simple. It has only a few main ingredients, and we will take them one at a time.|","| Let us start with the most basic. Distilled Cause Essence.|","|You need to extract and crystallize the essence of at least nine Causes into Distilled Cause Essence. Depending on your Provenance, this will be either easy or extremely difficult, and I genuinely cannot tell you which, because nobody has ever tried this with whatever it is you are.|","|Find something to extract it from. An Observable Existence will do. A Lifeform will do better.|","|And if you are using an Observable Existence, please empty it of all life first, so that you do not go around causing unnecessary genocides.|","...!"]},{"number":5702,"title":"Chapter 5702: Chapter 5701: Engineer! IV","paragraphs":["He started with something he had made himself, which seemed only fair.","Noah reached into THE Infiniverse and pulled out a young Observable Existence, one of the thousands that had bloomed out of the Genesis Tesseracts and had been growing quietly ever since. It came into the Realm and hung over the river of light, turning slowly, no larger than a fruit at this scale and containing an interior he could have walked for an age without finishing.","Of course, there were no lifeforms in it. Not one!","He looked at it for a moment anyway.","Then he dreamed.","That was the only word for what THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer actually did here. His eyes lowered halfway and did not close, and the light around him went soft at the edges. The river kept running. The eighty-nine suns kept burning. And Noah sat on the bank of his own Realm and dreamed the young Observable Existence apart.","In the dream, its Causes were visible.","Nine of them, which was simply what an Observable Existence grows on its own if you leave it alone, wound through the structure of the thing like the veins in a leaf held up to a light. He did not cut them. He did not pull. In the dream he simply understood that the essence of each Cause was a separate thing from the Cause itself, the way the taste of a fruit is separate from the fruit, and having understood it, it was already true.","The first essence came away.","It rose out of the turning Existence as a thread of pale color that had no name, and it hung in the air over the river.","Then the second. Then the third and fourth together, since he had the shape of it now.","By the seventh he was no longer being careful, and by the ninth the threads had begun to find each other on their own, winding together over the water. They combined!","What was left was a liquid.","It swirled in the air, unhurried, holding nine colors that all belonged to it, and it moved slower than liquid should. Noah rose from the bank and drew a bottle out of nothing, glass and stoppered, and let the thing pour itself in.","| DISTILLED CAUSE ESSENCE|","|The isolated conceptual essence of nine naturally-arisen Causes, rendered into a stable liquid state.|","|Classification: base ingredient, foundational tier. Stability: the highest observed in nature.|","|Retains the function of a Cause without retaining the Cause. Existence does not recognize the loss.|","And above the river, the Observable Existence he had drawn it from finished changing.","It had been turning with a slow inner light. That light was gone now. It kept its shape, all of it, every domain and cosmos and world inside it exactly where it had been, and none of it was going anywhere ever again. A thing that could hold, but could no longer become.","| TERMINAL OBSERVABLE EXISTENCE|","|Structure intact. Causal generation ceased. No further growth will occur.|","In truth, Noah felt bad about that more than he had expected to!","Fortunately, it was fixable. He could resuscitate it himself with enough attention. Better still, he did not have to.","He waved a hand, and the dead thing lifted and went, crossing out of the Realm toward a distant domain where a certain manifestation was currently overseeing thousands of infant Existences. THE Infiniverse would resuscitate it!","Although as the terminal Existence dwindled out of sight, Noah found his thoughts wandering.","Causes as ingredients. Nine from an Observable Existence.","Compare that to what Atlas had actually recommended, which was Lifeforms, and specifically the ones capable of generating their own. Take the essence, leave the Cause, walk away. They regrow it. Nobody dies. Nobody even limps.","That was harvesting.","And Noah knew exactly where the richest fields were, which was the part he did not like.","The Laestrygonians would soon be reborn inside THE Infiniverse and birthing Causes natively, a whole restored people producing the most stable ingredient in existence simply by living. Hvitrmarr, with nine First Causes seated in her organs, transformed and hers now. The Steeds, bred as burden-bearers for exactly this reason by beings who had looked at living things and seen carrying capacity.","Was this the reason for THE SLEEPLESS FIEND’s fixation with causes and lifeforms that inherently held them?","Noah shook his head and refocused.","Then he spoke into the ring for the first time.","\"I have successfully extracted Causes into Distilled Cause Essence.\"","The moment the words left him, he felt his Provenance being drawn on. A decimal of a percent, sapped away slow and steady, small enough to be nothing and precise enough that he knew exactly what he had spent.","The ring buzzed on his finger.","| That was rather quick.|","|You did not cause a genocide, did you? Do not go down that route. Everyone who goes down that route tells themselves it was efficient, and every one of them was wrong.|","|But if you did it that fast, it means your Provenance is very suitable for this.|","|Because some would start whining at this point. Sir, how exactly do I extract the Causes into Distilled Cause Essence? That would have been a dumb question.|","|You did not ask. Which means you most likely told your Provenance, here are the Causes, extract their essence for me. And your Provenance did it.|","|So sometimes the right Provenance does it all. Remember that when you are tempted to be proud of yourself.|","Noah’s mouth twitched.","| Alright. The other ingredients of an Elsedimension.|","|First, your own Provenance. It serves as the basis and the core, and it is what actually makes the thing YOURS rather than a room you happen to be standing in.|","|Second, an extremely high concentration of hydrogen. Helium. Lithium. Beryllium. Boron. Europium. Strontium. Neodymium.|","Noah blinked.","| And you might ask yourself, what the fuck do these elemental particles have to do with anything.|","| Well. When I began engineering existence itself, I looked at the makeup of stellar bodies, and I told myself that the ingredients had to be things that were easily accessible, so that whoever came after me would have boundless possibility rather than a shopping list they could never fill.|","|Do not make things overly complex. Complexity is what people reach for when they have not understood a thing well enough to make it simple.|","|Wonder has to bloom out of the most common things. The most ordinary things, made grand.|","Noah’s eyes shone at that!","He tugged upward with two fingers.","Another Observable Existence floated down out of THE Infiniverse and settled over the river.","Inside it were countless domains, and inside those, cosmos beyond counting, universes and their worlds and stars beyond that, and every one of those stars was made largely out of exactly what Atlas had listed.","The commonest things there were.","He waved a hand, and they came out.","Stellar rivers poured from the young Existence into the air above his Realm, eight of them, braided and enormous, hydrogen and helium running silver-white at the front, lithium and beryllium and boron threading through them, europium and strontium and neodymium arriving last in colors that had no business being that beautiful!","They came out at concentrations that would have collapsed a star and left the Existence itself entirely unharmed, since he was not taking its structure, only its abundance.","The rivers turned slowly over the bank, waiting.","Noah sent his Provenance into the ring.","| Good. Now listen, because the assembly matters more than the ingredients.|","|You will begin with the Elseengine. That is the core, and everything else is built outward from it, and if you get the core wrong you will not find out until the whole thing comes apart around you.|","|Take your Provenance and the Distilled Cause Essence, and fuse them. Not layered. Not adjacent. The Essence provides function that existence recognizes as legitimate, and your Provenance provides the authority that answers to nobody. Together they will hold a law up without borrowing a single thing from anyone. That is an Elseengine.|","|Then weave the elements around it. All eight, in the order I gave them, because the order is the order for reasons you will understand in about a hundred years maybe.|","|And here is the part that matters most, so hear it properly.|","|You will include nothing else.|","|No Argent Loom. No Infinity. No Primordial Source. No Narrative. Not a thread of any framework’s Dimensionality, not one borrowed weaving, no matter how convenient it would be and it will be extremely convenient.|","|Because whatever authority you build INTO a place has standing INSIDE that place forever. Include the Loom, and the Loom may enter. Include Infinity, and everything that has ever mastered Infinity has a door. By excluding them at the foundation, you are not hiding from those authorities. You are making somewhere they were never invited, and existence honors that with a stubbornness you would not believe.|","|What you get is a domain bent uniquely to your Provenance, running your rules, sitting outside the scope of the weavings that every powerful lifeform in existence has spent their entire lives climbing.|","|An Elsedimension is like a second body of your own.|","|And nobody has greater autonomy over your body than you.|","Noah stood up.","He took the bottle in his left hand and unstoppered it, and he brought his Provenance up out of the depth of himself, and he put them together over the river of light.","The Distilled Cause Essence did not pour. It reached. Nine colors that had grown inside a young Existence found the blue-gold weight of something that had generated itself out of nothing, and there was a moment where nothing at all happened!","Then they fused!","HUUM!","The Elseengine came into being over the water, small and turning and impossibly heavy, throwing a light that did not resemble any authority in existence because it was not borrowing from any of them. Noah felt it take hold. He felt it hold a law up on its own, needing nothing, asking nothing, owed to nobody.","He brought the rivers in.","Hydrogen first, and it wrapped the engine and thinned into a shell.","Helium after it, settling into the gaps. Lithium, beryllium, boron in sequence, and with each one the shell stopped being a shell and started being a place, gaining depth!","Europium came in and the light inside changed character entirely. Strontium threaded the edges. Neodymium last, and when it landed, the whole construction went quiet.","Then it BLOOMED.","An Elsedimension unfolded over the river of light in Noah’s Realm, and it shone, and it shone like a budding flower! Not brighter than his eighty-nine suns. Differently. It cast a light that owed no one anything.","Noah spread his hands, and it grew.","He expanded it outward, and outward again, letting it take the size it wanted rather than the size he had planned, and when it had settled he pressed it gently down into the Realm itself, and the two of them fused. Blue-gold hills on one side. Somewhere on the other side that answered only to him.","|An Elsedimension has been constructed.|","|Elseengine: stable. Foundation: Provenance and Distilled Cause Essence, fused. Composition: eight stellar elements, ordered.|","|Included authorities: none. THE Argent Loom holds no standing here. THE Provenance of Existence holds no standing here. No framework of Dimensionality has been granted entry.|","| First act of Existential Engineering completed without instruction failure. The work was understood, not copied.|","|VERITAS: 90|","|PROVENANCE: 90|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 89|","...!","Ninety!","| Did it work?|","The ring buzzed.","| If it did, your existence should be feeling the pleasure of advancement right about now. That feeling is real and it is not vanity. Engineering alone can make you understand the secrets of Existence and elevate your Dimensionality, because you cannot build a thing without learning what it is made of, and everything is made of the same handful of things.|","|Making an Elsedimension is the first step.|","|Our goal is to make you your own Gu Elsedimension Ring, since you gave the last one away.|","|Haha. I still cannot believe you gave it away. If you had any idea how hard that thing was to make and how prized it is.|","|But hey, forget about it. We will take things a step at a time. Do not worry.|","|For now, you have the capability to make an Elsedimension. So the next step is naturally Gu.|","|And for that, you need to make a trip to a place lost through existence and time. Somewhere most Immense Ones do not even know is there as others of their kind keep it a secret.|","|THE CHRYSALIS OF THE FIRST SUNDERING.|","|Knowing about it is one thing.|","|Getting there. Now that is the fun part.|","...!"]},{"number":5703,"title":"Chapter 5703: Chapter 5702: Peace and Blood! I","paragraphs":["<THE Continuum Paradox>","They were crossing through THE Dimensional Provenance Train.","They were, but...","The pull took them mid-sentence, and existence answered before their feet had even found ground.","|THREE PARTICIPANTS HAVE BEEN PULLED ACROSS THE DIMENSIONAL PROVENANCE TRAIN.|","|You are arriving within a Narrative of Existence in progress.|","|Records note: this Narrative has failed to entertain. The combatants within it met no hardship worth recording. Victory arrived without cost, without struggle, and without a single moment of doubt.|","|The reigning champions of this Cabin hold a Narrative of devouring and usurpation. It has consumed everything placed before it, and it has done so far too easily.|","|Should the arriving participants attain victory and BREAK this Narrative of Existence, additional rewards shall be given.|","...!","Three frowns landed at once!","Descartes, THE Continuum Paradox, took the information as it came and did not move a muscle of his face beyond the frown itself. Beside him THE Primordial Paradox rolled his shoulders and made a sound of open disgust at being moved without being asked. And Erwin, THE Living Paradox, simply tilted his head.","Then they looked around!","They stood in a Dimension made of gaseous stellar matter and debris. Vast clouds of it hung in every direction, greens and rusts and deep violets rolling slow through each other, and through the clouds drifted rock, mountains of it, continents of it, tumbling without hurry through a space that had no floor and no sky and no end that any of them could find.","Auras saturated all of it. Thousands of them. Descendants and Primeval Ones, the weight of their existences pressing against the stellar clouds from every direction at once, enough gathered power to level Dimensions stacked one atop another out to the horizon.","And it was silent.","Not quiet. SILENT! Not one voice, not one breath, not one scrape of movement across all that floating stone. Thousands of the mighty occupied this place and produced no sound whatsoever.","Above everything, an eye watched.","It hung in the upper dark past the clouds, enormous and patient, and it was not looking at the Dimension. It was looking at THEM, with the settled anticipation of something that had cleared its schedule.","Erwin looked up at it and smiled pleasantly.","The eye did not react!","Compared to what came next, none of that was the strange part.","Because as the three of them turned to survey the floating stone, they found the mighty of this place seated and standing across all of it. Descendants on the tumbling rock, robed and horned and marked. Primeval Ones sprawled across whole asteroids, ancient and enormous and still. Some sat cross-legged. Some stood at edges looking out at nothing. Thousands of them, scattered through the debris in every direction.","And when the three arrived, all of them turned at the same time.","Every single one!","Thousands of heads swung toward the arrival point in the same instant with the same speed, thousands of faces angling to the same degree, and thousands of pairs of eyes settled on them glazed over with an obsidian purple sheen!","THE Primordial Paradox blinked.","Erwin blinked beside him.","\" Well ,\" Erwin said mildly. \" That is...familiar.\"","They looked further in, toward the center of the Dimension, where the debris thickened around a single massive floating asteroid that everything else seemed to orbit.","Two figures sat upon it.","The first was a man in white robes, and by every ordinary measure he was fairly average. Average build. Average height. A plain face that would not have earned a second glance in a crowded market. Nothing about him screamed anything at all.","Except for the circle on his chest!","It was divided into nine sections, a nine-pointed star outlined across his breast, and set into the edges of it were gems. Nine of them, radiant, each one a different color and every color impossible, and each single gem radiated the profound aura of a pristine First Cause.","Nine First Causes! On one man’s chest! Blazing around the edges of an Enneagram like ornaments he had picked out that morning!","And his eyes were clear.","That was the thing THE Continuum Paradox marked immediately, since it was the only thing in the entire Dimension that did not fit. Not one thread of that obsidian purple unity ran through this one’s gaze. He was himself, entirely, and he was looking directly at Erwin with a coldness that had nothing polite in it whatsoever.","He was looking at THE Living Paradox the way a man looks at someone he has already decided to fight.","But the thing that seized the attention of the two Paradoxes was not the man with nine First Causes on his chest!","It was the being sitting beside him.","A stellar titan, humanoid, so vast that the asteroid served him as a stool. His entire body shone with an obsidian allure, a dark that gave back light instead of drinking it, and across every inch of that enormous frame ran boundless weavings of chaos, churning and folding and unmaking themselves without pause. He sat with one arm across a raised knee, and he wore an expression of profound and ancient boredom.","And both Paradoxes knew that face!","\" Abbadon ?\"","THE Primordial Paradox said it out loud, and incredulity carried the word across the whole silent Dimension!","\" Why do your eyes seem their depressed and ancient selves? Your entire mind was taken over, as far as I knew! Which also seems to be the case for every single one of these...\"","He gestured, and the gesture took in thousands of purple-glazed faces still turned toward them in perfect unison.","In the distance, Abbadon harrumphed.","THE Primordial Chaos shifted his enormous frame, and the chaos-weavings across his body churned faster with the motion, and when he spoke his voice rolled through the stellar clouds without disturbing a single one of them.","\"I worked out a deal to move with my own autonomy.\"","He looked the three of them over without much enthusiasm.","\"I thought another set of meals was coming for me and the master. I did not expect to see you two. Are we still considered acquaintances? Or are we enemies?\"","BOOM!","The question landed and detonated, because of everything Abbadon had just said, one word did the real damage!","The Master!","One mind. One singular mind of unity, integrated across thousands of Descendants and Primeval Ones at once, wearing them the way a lesser being wears clothing, moving their heads in the same instant and glazing their eyes with the same obsidian purple. Thousands of the mighty gathered here, and not one of them was anybody anymore.","THE Great Usurper had grown grandly!","Not to be mistaken for the one who held the mantle of THE USURPER, who was and was not a vessel of THE Sealed One, currently occupying an entirely different region of THE Dimensional Provenance Train.","Two devourers on one train!","And above them all, the enormous eye narrowed!","|THE OVERSEEING ONE observes with growing displeasure.|","|You KNOW each other?|","|Records confirm prior acquaintance between the arrivals and the native inhabitants. This was not accounted for. A Narrative constructed around confrontation loses its tension when the confronting parties open with pleasantries and inquiries after each other’s health.|","|This Narrative is not going according to plan.|","|Something else will have to be done about this.|","The eye pulsed once, and the whole Dimension pulsed with it, the stellar clouds flattening and rebounding across light years!","|A sufficient Narrative of Existence guaranteeing amusement has been selected.|","| THE NARRATIVE OF EXISTENCE: THE TRAGIC HEROES is being instituted.|","...!"]},{"number":5704,"title":"Chapter 5704: Chapter 5703: Peace and Blood! II","paragraphs":["|Terms, for the benefit of the participants.|","|You are hereby the unlikely heroes. Outmatched, unprepared, and arriving late, as such heroes always are. You will face a Dark Lord, and the Dark Lord will face you.|","| Due to the considerable annoyance of the preceding Narrative, this one has been set in advance. You are to be DEFEATED. Existential Moirai shall wrap around the Dark Lord to ensure it, and the wrapping is already underway.|","|Should this Narrative somehow be overcome, THE NARRATIVE OF THE TRAGIC HEROES may be overwritten entirely, and the rewards for such a thing would be stupendous.|","|Should things proceed as expected, the Records of your existences will be locked and sent back across time to this initial starting point. You will arrive here again.|","|THE Overseeing One watches with great interest to see how many times you will die before your existences fully collapse.|","|Or whether, on one of your returns, you triumph.|","|Begin.|","The Dimensional Cabin began to shake!","Far across the debris field, a doorway split open in the empty space between two tumbling continents. It cracked wider, and wider still, and obsidian darkness began to spill out of it and pour downward through the stellar clouds, and from the other side came auras that made the thousands already gathered here feel like a warmup!","Descartes looked at it with cold eyes.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at it with colder ones.","Erwin, THE Living Paradox, looked at it and did not blink at all.","And among the Descendants bound in unity, every purple-glazed face turned once more toward THE Primordial Paradox, thousands of them at once across all that floating stone, and they opened thousands of mouths and spoke as one!","\"I haven’t reached out to Osmont for help for months now, as I don’t intend to do so now.\"","The voices came from every direction at once, layered over themselves, one mind and thousands of throats!","\" How about it? You all think we can work together to fuck shit up?\"","Thousands of heads tilted at the same angle.","\" Unity shall spread over everything by itself. But with help...\"","The laugh came out of every mouth in the Dimension simultaneously.","\" Haha. Things become infinitely easier.\"","...!","And even as the words finished, the being adorned with the Enneagram rose!","Alexander, THE Peacemaker, stood up on the central asteroid without hurry, and the nine First Causes around his chest brightened as he moved. He thrust out his left hand, and one of the gems on the Enneagram flared, and radiant multicolored light spilled out of it and gathered and drew itself into shape across his open palm!","A bow!","It formed in his grip in a wash of nine-fold color, tall and clean and humming, and the pressure of it alone pushed the stellar clouds back from the asteroid in a slow spreading ring!","He rolled his neck, and it cracked once.","Then he began to float toward the doorway spilling endless darkness, unhurried, average in every way except for the nine roots of Existence burning across his chest and the weapon in his hand!","His voice could barely be discerned as he passed them.","\" Peace... is often bloody.\"","BOOM!","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering.","The name alone was grand!","It sat in the air of the Realm after Atlas had spoken it, heavier than the ninety suns above the blue-gold hills, heavier than the layered Elsedimension that now shone off to one side of the river like a second horizon that owed nobody anything. Noah stood on the bank and the voice of Atlas continued to ring out over all of it.","| This place is uniquely connected to the time when Immense Ones first rose. It is located in a period of endless potential.|","|But one may ask. Why the hell are Gu Lifeforms involved?|","|Well. Here is where an argument comes in about whether THE First Lifeforms truly were thr first...or if Gu came first from nature.|","|Provenance Lifeforms. Or little insects.|","|Haha! It hurt the pride of many when I posed this question, and I posed it often. Provenance Lifeforms always looked at themselves as THE First Lifeforms. The ones who generated their own weavings of existence, from whom immensity bloomed, all of that.|","|But when we arose, little insects and microbes and things of no cognizance whatsoever were already there.|","|I never understood why we all had to be so prideful that we did not even care that insects like Gu were around before us. Maybe the argument is that they had no will and no cognizance. Fine. But Gu are among the lifeforms most closely bound to nature itself. It is as if they bloomed out of the surrounding existence into shapes and forms on their own. They are blank slates, and many things can be written on a blank slate.|","|Think of them like empty pages in a vast book, waiting to be filled.|","|They have the potential to become ANYTHING. Which makes them one of the grandest materials in the entire Engineering of Existence.|","...!","Gu!","Noah’s eyes shone sharply as the word landed, because he knew someone who used them! Ryaenara! A lifeform close to him, who had wielded those little insects since before he had ever met her, and whose weavings of existence had always carried something unique that he had never quite gotten to the bottom of.","Her and her brother. Ulf, with his rhymes and his paintings, were unique.","Already, another body of his was moving!","Across existence, a second Noah turned his steps toward the two siblings, because if Gu were a material grand enough, then he wanted every scrap of information the two of them held.","But the voice of Atlas continued.","| The nature of Gu is unique. Loose existence does not stay loose. Left alone long enough in a sealed place, surrounding existence condenses, and what it condenses into in THE Chrysalis are lifeforms.|","|Gu are that condensation. Each one is a single concept that has become alive.|","|A Time Gu is not a creature that manipulates time. It IS time, in the shape of an insect. And it is hungry.|","|Their purity comes from being one thing entirely. A Cause holds an Observable Existence up. A Gu simply is the concept, with nothing else mixed in. Compare them as ingredients. A Cause is a brick, stable and dead. A Gu is a living brick.|","|There are Gu related to Time. Dream. Destiny. Death. Life. Space. Silence. Memory. Weight. Hunger. Records. Purity. Chance.|","|There are common Gu. There are rare Gu. And there are Gu that even Immense Ones will fight you for, and lose gracelessly.|","|They have extremely high Dimensionality as many can’t even percieve them. And one unique thing about them. To sustain themselves, they feed on the parts of existence they are made from. A Dream Gu eats dreams. A Time Gu eats timelines. A Chance Gu eats luck.|","|And THIS is also how you enter.|","|You have to make yourself into a meal that a Gu will want to pull into THE Chrysalis and eat.|","...!"]},{"number":5705,"title":"Chapter 5705: Chapter 5704: Chrysalis I","paragraphs":["He had to make himself into a meal.","Noah sighed lightly. He craned his neck to one side until it clicked, and then to the other, and rolled his shoulders once, and was ready to get started, because of course that was the method!","| Of course, something like that alone might be too hard to conceptualize. So.|","|Wrap your entire existence in whatever nature your Provenance holds. And while you do so, communicate with your surroundings how you WANT to be consumed. How you are giving yourself away for something grander and greater than yourself.|","|Provenance offered away is one of the easiest ways to get the attention of a Gu of a similar type in THE Chrysalis.|","|But even then, you could be doing that for years and never be picked up. The Chrysalis is not short on meals.|","|Which is where I come in. I have been there before. So I can form a tether from you to THE Chrysalis. You are the bait, and I am the fishing line, connecting you to the jaws of whatever Gu decides to consume you and pull you across.|","|Ready?|","|Imagine you are appetizing and grand. And then say the words...|","|I am filled with determination.|","Noah’s eyes pulsed as he got ready!","He drew his Provenance Essence up out of the depth of himself and let it out, and it came out as waves of blue-gold light that rolled off his skin and rose and wrapped him, layer over layer, until he stood inside a cloud of his own making with ninety suns burning above it!","He envisioned himself as the most appetizing meal in existence. He put his whole will into it, and he told the surroundings without words that here was a Provenance, self-generated, freely offered, given away for something grander!","THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer pulsed!","Waves of endless dreams poured out of him and joined the cloud, dreams of everything he had ever been and everything he had decided to become, and they wound through the blue-gold light until the whole of it shimmered with the soft heavy quality of a thing that is more than half asleep and entirely awake at once!","And Noah said the words.","\"I am filled with determination!\"","HUUM!","Brilliance pulsed across the whole Realm!","And out of the ring came a sound Noah had heard once before and had hoped not to hear again.","| Haha! Did you really say the words ’I am filled with determination’?|","\"...\"","| You actually do not need to say that shit! Haha!|","\"...\"","Noah stood inside his cloud of offered Provenance and dreams, appetizing and grand, and said absolutely nothing at all.","| Alright, alright. I will get serious and tether you.|","The ring on his finger went hot!","| Be ready. Once you are eaten, you will appear in the belly of a Gu related to your Provenance.|","|I hope it is a common Gu that does not metabolize you instantly.|","...!","Noah’s eye twitched.","He hoped it was a common Gu!","Noah closed his eyes, appetizing and grand, and waited to be eaten as he was trusting an ancient lifeform who messed around far, far too much!","It did not take too long before...","Something hooked into him!","Not a hand, not a grip, not any of the shapes that pulling usually took. It was a thread going taut somewhere behind his sternum, and the taut thread was attached to somewhere else, and the somewhere else began to reel!","Noah’s existence left!","It left the Realm, left the bank of the river, left the ninety suns and the layered Elsedimension, and it went out along the thread toward another weaving of existence entirely, and the going was not like crossing a Dimension!","Crossing a Dimension was still travel. This was something stranger, because as he went, he felt himself leaving the weavings of time itself.","Before and after came apart around him.","Duration stopped being a thing that happened and became a thing he was passing out of, almost like how a swimmer passes out of water, and on the far side of it there was no current, no direction, no order to events, only a wide slow place where time had no meaning because time had not yet decided to mean anything!","And then...after what could have been days or years, he felt like he...was being eaten.","His Provenance was being sucked away, drawn off him in long hungry pulls, as existence materialized around him out of nothing and he found himself inside something!","Murky golden clouds of dream surrounded him on every side, thick and soft and warm, and through the clouds ran tentacles, dozens of them, pale and translucent and lined with something that shimmered, and every one of them was fastened to him and siphoning his Provenance into the murk!","BOOM!","Noah withdrew immediately!","He pulled his Provenance in all at once, from the offered cloud, from the dreams he had poured out as bait, from every tentacle that had latched onto him, drawing the whole of it back inside himself in one hard contraction, and the thing he was inside of RUMBLED!","The golden murk convulsed around him. The tentacles whipped loose. Whatever had been feeding found its meal suddenly and violently inedible, and it did what anything does with an inedible meal.","It spat him out!","Noah shot forward through membranes, one after another after another, each one pulsing with heavy brilliance as he tore through it, wet golden light bursting around him on every side, and then the last membrane gave way and he was out, tumbling through open air into light!","HUUM!","And instantly...","Every quark in his existence buzzed.","Every cell. Every particle of the two hundred decillion. All of them thrummed at once with a single unmistakable message, which was that he had arrived somewhere grand.","|You have arrived at an unfathomable place.|","|Nature here is extremely loose and permeable. Reality is entirely fluid and heavily hallucinatory.|","|The sky might rain liquid fire. The ground might turn to event horizons. Time itself dilates and contracts without warning.|","|If you remain in one place for too long without individual thoughts, or without sufficient Trueness, you may assimilate into the surrounding existence.|","|Be immeasurably careful.|","|You have arrived in THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering.|","...!"]},{"number":5706,"title":"Chapter 5706: Chapter 5705: Chrysalis II","paragraphs":["Noah righted himself in the air and looked at what he had come out of.","It hung before him, vast and slow, and it was the strangest living thing he had ever laid eyes on, and he had laid eyes on a great many!","It should be...","A Dream Gu!","It was insect and microbe at once and neither, a bloated golden body the size of a small moon that was somehow also translucent, with the murky dream-clouds he had just been inside visible drifting through its interior like weather.","Segmented plates ran along its length, soft and overlapping, and from between them extended the pale siphoning tentacles, now curling back inward, and beneath its body hung dozens of thin jointed legs that did not touch anything and did not need to. Its whole surface shimmered with the quality of a thing half-remembered on waking, edges that would not hold still, colors that changed depending on whether he looked directly at them!","And it had eyes.","Many of them, scattered across its front in no particular arrangement, each one a slow golden orb, and every single one of them was pointed at him.","They looked at him the way a thing looks at an oddity. Not hostile or afraid. Simply confused that a meal had stopped being a meal.","Then its existence buzzed, and it vanished!","It moved so fast that Noah could barely follow it, the great translucent bulk of it shooting away into the distance and shrinking, and as it went he strained after it with everything he had and caught only the barest glimpse of its details before it was gone entirely!","| DREAM GU|","|Rarity: Common|","|VERITAS: 104 / PROVENANCE: 101 / POTENTIA: 107 / PONDUS: 102|","...!","Common?","That was a COMMON Gu?!","It had run from him, and every attribute it held was above a hundred, and it was COMMON.","Noah stood in the air and did not move for a moment, and then, since the thing had gone and nothing else was trying to eat him yet, he looked around!","Strands descended from above.","Multicolored, fine as silk, falling in slow unhurried drifts all around him, thousands of them, more, catching a light that came from nowhere he could locate. They floated down gently and did not land anywhere, since there was nowhere to land, and they touched his skin as they passed and each touch carried something.","A color that was also a mood. A texture that was also a memory of a thing that had never happened to him.","And beyond the strands, in every direction, all around and all around...","Nebulas!","Boundless, swirling, kaleidoscopic, filling the whole of the visible existence from horizon to horizon in every axis, gold and violet and a green he had never seen and a red that hurt to look at, all of it turning and folding and unfolding again, never repeating, layered so deep that the far ones showed through the near ones and the near ones showed through his own hands!","This was where the beings who exceeded had left their leavings.","Noah stood very still inside a chrysalis older than Records, with silk falling around him and nebulas turning past him, and he breathed once, slowly, and made very sure that he kept thinking his own thoughts.","| You did not get eaten?|","Atlas voice echoed out.","| This is good. Welcome to THE Chrysalis.|","|A dangerous place, where you may very well die before you accomplish anything at all. It is a place of immensity and wonder. The Gu Lifeforms are mostly doing things of their own nature and will leave you be, but if you attack them, or try to capture particularly powerful ones, they may kill you before you even know it has happened.|","|Oh, and some particularly unique Immense Ones may be moving around here. So. Death from all sides is possible.|","|But hey. Is this not a fun place?|","Noah’s eye twitched.","| This is where I made some of my grandest designs. Haha!|","|Let us get you familiar with the different types of Gu, and then we can see whether you can locate a decent one to try forming your first Gu Elsedimension Ring.|","|It will not be anywhere near as grand in quality as mine was. But hey.|","|We all have to start somewhere. Right?|","Noah listened to the crazy Engineer inside thr illusory ring as he kept thinking!","That was the first rule of this place! He moved slowly through the falling silk with his own thoughts running loud and deliberate in his head, refusing the surrounding existence every soft invitation to simply stop being a separate thing and join it!","Because it WAS inviting. The nebulas turned past him in colors that had never existed anywhere else, and the strands brushed his skin and left moods behind, and every part of the Chrysalis whispered that it would be so easy to loosen a little. Just a little. Just enough to see what it felt like.","Noah did not loosen!","The ring on his finger went warm.","| Are you still you? Alright. Before you go blundering into something that eats you properly this time, let me tell you what lives here.|","Golden light spilled out of the ring and unfolded in the air before him!","It drew itself into shapes, thin bright lines hanging against the kaleidoscope, holographic and turning slowly, and the first shape it made was an insect Noah recognized, bloated and translucent and many-eyed, rendered small enough to sit in his palm.","| There are three rarities of Gu. I will give them to you in the order you will meet them, which is also the order in which they will kill you.|","|First. COMMON GU.|","The golden insect pulsed!","| These are what happens when loose existence sits sealed in one place long enough to condense. Nothing more. No one made them. No one meant them. A concept drifted here after the Sundering, found nothing to hold it, and slowly folded itself into a shape with legs.|","|One concept each. Total purity. A Common Gu is a hundred of one thing and nothing at all of anything else. No will beyond hunger. No cognizance beyond appetite.|","|There may be hundreds of thousands of them in the Chrysalis. They flee from anything that is not food.|","|Uses: everything. Engines, rings, weapons, locks, the foundation of any serious design. Cheap. Plentiful. Do not get sentimental about them.|","The golden insect faded, and a second shape drew itself in its place, and this one was different!","It was longer, sleeker, plated in overlapping gold that caught light from angles the light was not coming from, and at its head, where the first shape had scattered many eyes, this one held only two. The lines that drew them were very careful.","| Second. RARE GU.|","|A Rare Gu does not condense out of loose existence. It condenses AROUND something.|","|The beings who exceeded and departed shed pieces of themselves. A memory too heavy to carry through. An ambition that would not fit. A grudge. A grief. A single decision they refused to be defined by any longer. Those shed pieces fell here, and existence condensed around them the way pearl condenses around grit.|","|A Rare Gu carries an ECHO of whatever it grew around. Not the being. The being is gone. But a preference. A leaning. Sometimes a grudge that outlived the one who held it by an age.|","|A Rare Gu will look at you and decide whether you are worth the effort of noticing, and if it decides yes, that is not necessarily good news.|","|Their depth is a full Fold above the Common ones, which I will explain shortly. Immense Ones may fight you for a Rare Gu if you come across them.|","|My ring, the one you gave back, was built around a Rare Chance Gu that I spent three hundred years earning the attention of. So. That is what you gave away.|","Noah did not react to that!","The golden shape faded.","And the third one drew itself, and the lines of it were not careful at all!","They were huge. The hologram swelled out from the ring until it hung the size of a house in front of him, and the shape it made was barely an insect anymore, more a suggestion of one, segments and limbs and something like wings folded inward, rendered in gold so bright the nebulas dimmed behind it.","| Third.|","|THE FIRST GU.|","|And here we return to my favorite argument, since you are a captive audience and cannot leave.|","|Provenance Lifeforms call themselves THE First Lifeforms. I have told you what I think of that. When we arose, THESE were already here. They did not condense out of the Sundering. They predate it. They were in the Chrysalis before the Chrysalis was a chrysalis, when it was simply the first sealed pocket of existence there had ever been, and loose reality had nothing to do in there for an age but fold itself into life.|","|One per concept. Time. Dream. Death. Chance. The rest. One each, and none of them has ever left, and every Gu of that weaving of existence of that concept in existence descends from them.|","|They are not captured. They are not fought. You do not bait a First Gu with anything, because they are not hungry in any way you would recognize. Their depth sits at the same Fold as the Immense Ones, and their power matches them or even exceeds them at times, and unlike the Immense Ones they have never once wanted anything from anybody.|","|And they hold Existential Narrative of their own.|","...!","Noah’s eyes narrowed!","He thought about what that meant! An Immense One’s Narrative had followed him out of a journal and frozen a sacred spring.","If the First Gu held the same thing, then somewhere in this place were beings that could sense their own names being spoken, and one of them was named CHANCE, and a dead genius had built a ring around one of its descendants.","Did they know and feel thst Narrative? Did they sense whenever those descended from their concepts have anything done?","| Have I met one? Maybe. Maybe. Ah...|","The house-sized hologram folded down into nothing.","| Now. Since I have taught without explaining things too well, I should probably teach you how everything is ranked on the weavings and constraints of Dimensionality.|","| Which is only part of the equation, by the way.|","Golden light spilled again, and this time it drew a sheet.","A single flat plane of thin gold, hanging edge-on in the air, wide as Noah’s outstretched arms. And as Atlas spoke, it folded!","| Existence is a sheet. It has been folded. Every fold hides what is beneath it from what is above it, and every fold is a place where beings can sit. Dimensionality is nothing more than which fold you occupy. Not how strong you are. How DEEP you are.|","The sheet creased once, and the crease glowed.","| THE SURFACE. The first fold. Mortal existence. A being here perceives one Observable Existence, its own, and nothing beyond. Most life that has ever lived has lived here and died here without ever knowing there was a second fold to stand on.|","\"...\"","Was this fucker teaching him the generally accepted ranking system of power for Provenance Lifeforms and Immense Ones? It seemed to be their version of Finite, Transfinite, and Ineffable Verse! But very likely more established and developed.","It folded again, and the second crease lit brighter.","| THE CREASE. Here sit varieties of powerful True Lifeforms, Descendants, Primeval Ones, everything youmay have spent your early life fighting. They perceive and act across Dimensions. The frameworks live here.|","A third fold, deeper, and the gold went darker where it turned. Did that fold correlate to THE Transfinite Verse?","| THE SEAM. The fold where where many things are Unperceivable. Provenance Lifeforms sit here at their base. Powerful Descendants and other lifeforms could theoretically arrive here. Elsedimensions are folded into the Seam, which is why the Crease frameworks cannot find them. And this, O Author of Probability, is where you are currently nearing or sitting.|","Ineffable Verse!","Noah thought that this had to be THE INEFFABLE VERSE as even Thalia should have been at this level originally, past 100 Attributes!","Noah looked at the third crease for a long moment.","|A Common Gu sits at the Seam.|","The sheet folded a fourth time, and the fold was so tight it was hard to see where the gold went.","| THE HEM. The edge of the sheet. Rare Gu sit here. The oldest Provenance Lifeforms sit here, a handful of them. I sat here, once, for a while. This is the fold from which Narrative Existence can be designed, since you have to reach the edge of the cloth before you can start pinning things to it that were never woven in.|","And then the sheet stopped folding.","Instead, it began to show its THREADS. The flat gold dissolved into a weave, individual strands running across and through each other, and the fifth crease was not a crease at all but the pattern itself.","|THE WEAVE.|","| Immense Ones sit here. They are not ON the sheet. They are IN it. They are strands. When one of them freezes a spring, it is not exerting force against you. The cloth itself is deciding where you stand, because the cloth is partly her. You cannot fight the fabric from a wrinkle in it, which is what you were, and which is why all of your beautiful weapons did nothing.|","|The First Gu sit here too. Older strands. Quieter.|","\"And above the Weave?\"","Noah said it before he had decided to, and the instant the words left him he felt it, a decimal of a percent of his Provenance drawn away, small and exact and gone!","|Ah.|","|Now you know what a wasted question feels like, because I am not answering it. There is a fold past the Weave. What it is called and what it is like are not things I will say inside a place that is listening.|","The golden weave dimmed.","| Now. I said Dimensionality was part of the equation. It is one of three, and you will spend the rest of your existence learning that the three are not equal.|","Three rings of gold drew themselves in the air, interlocking.","| DEPTH. Which fold you occupy. That is Dimensionality.|","|MAGNITUDE. How much of you sits there. This can be a measure of Trueness, your Provenance, Lifeforce, even potential of your existence.|","...!","Those...would be the 4 attributes he designed to percieve and quantify himself?","|AGREEMENT. How much existence nods when you speak. The Immense Ones call it Existential Narrative and guard it above everything, and they are right to. Depth without agreement is a deep hole nobody knows about. Magnitude without agreement is a loud man in an empty room.|","The three rings held a moment longer, turning through each other, and then folded away into the ring on his finger and were gone.","| Engineering raises depth and magnitude. That is the whole reason I am teaching you and not simply handing you tools. Every Elsedimension you build, every Gu you bind, every design you understand from the inside pushes you one thread deeper into the cloth. I climbed from the Crease to the Hem by building things. You may climb faster, because you generate what I had to gather.|","|Now. Enough theory.|","|Let us find you a Common Gu that does not run, and see whether you can bind it into your first ring.|","Noah nodded once, and turned to move, and stopped.","Because among the thousands of multicolored strands drifting gently down through the kaleidoscope all around him, one was not drifting.","It hung perfectly still, taut, running upward out of sight, and at the bottom of it, no larger than his hand and plated in gold that caught light from angles the light was not coming from, something with exactly two eyes was looking at him.","It was not confused.","It was deciding!","Oh.","Fuck!"]},{"number":5707,"title":"Chapter 5707: Chapter 5706: Defy!","paragraphs":["Noah did not move!","Not a finger and not a breath he did not need. He stood in the falling silk with the kaleidoscope turning past him and he held himself utterly still, because the thing at the bottom of the one taut strand was looking at him, and it had not yet finished deciding what he was!","It hung no larger than his hand.","Golden plates overlapped along its body, and they caught light from angles the light was not coming from, so that it seemed lit from inside by something that was not quite in this place! Six jointed legs folded neatly against it. Two wings lay closed along its back, and through them, faint and slow, drifted shapes that were not there when he looked directly and were there again when he looked away.","And at its head sat exactly two eyes, deep gold, unblinking, and both of them held him the way a scale holds a weight!","| DREAM GU|","|Rarity: RARE|","|Depth: THE HEM|","|VERITAS: 341 / PROVENANCE: 328 / POTENTIA: 356 / PONDUS: 339|","|Echo: condensed around a shed fragment. Nature of fragment: a dream that was not finished.|","...!","Three hundred and forty-one!","A full Fold above him! Sitting at the edge of the cloth where he had never stood, holding an echo of something a departed being had dreamed and could not carry through the crossing, and looking at him with total patience while his ring went warm and then very deliberately went silent!","Atlas was not going to help with this one.","And then the Gu spoke!","Its voice did not come from its mouth, since it had none that he could find. It came from the silk. Every falling strand in the vicinity carried a thread of it, so that the words arrived from above and around him at once, layered, grand, and unhurried in the way of a thing that has never once been made to wait!","\"I sensed the weavings of a Unique Dream here.\"","The two eyes did not blink.","\" Something dreamed in this place that was not of this place. Grandly. Grandly enough to draw me down from where I hang. Nothing dreams as grandly as I do within a great many strands of here, little one.\"","The wings along its back stirred, and the shapes inside them turned.","\" So I will put it to a test. Dream with me. Keep pace, and I will know what you are. Fall behind, and you will simply become part of what I dream.\"","BOOM!","The Dream Gu dreamed!","And the Chrysalis around Noah was gone!","He stood on a shore of black glass beneath a sky that was a single closed eyelid, and the sea before him was made of every conversation he had ever left unfinished, murmuring, and the tide was going out!","He had one heartbeat to understand what was being asked, and he understood it, because THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer surged up through his quarks and he did not resist the dream!","He joined it!","THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM woke inside him, and Noah imposed his own mind’s simulation over the Gu’s, not against it, alongside it, weaving his dream through the Gu’s dream at the seam where the two met!","The tide was going out. He dreamed a moon. The moon rose over the closed eyelid of the sky, and the tide turned, and the sea of unfinished conversations came back in and he stood in it to his knees and let them finish!","The Gu’s dream shifted!","The shore folded upward into a staircase with no top, each step a year he had not lived yet, and it was already climbing without him, and to fall behind was to be left on a year that would never arrive!","Noah dreamed his legs longer. He dreamed the steps shorter. He dreamed that he had always been at the top already and was only remembering the climb, and the staircase, faced with a dreamer who refused its premise, agreed with him!","Faster!","The dream became a city that was also his own skeleton, streets running along his ribs, and something was hunting through it that wore his son’s face and was not his son!","Noah dreamed the streets lit. He dreamed the thing’s true face, and it was only a dream of a fear, and he dreamed the fear a chair and sat it down and told it to wait.","The dream became a fire that burned memories for fuel, and he dreamed himself into a memory the fire could not reach, one it had never been given, a preschool teacher and a word he had not understood at five years old and the way his mother’s hand had tightened on his!","The dream became a silence that ate the names of things, and he dreamed his own name into the silence and let it be eaten and dreamed it again, and again, and again, faster than the silence could swallow, until the silence gave up!","Faster!","The Gu was not slowing!","It was curious now, and its curiosity ran the dreams harder, stranger, folding three into one, a war that was also a wedding that was also the last second before a star collapsed, and Noah dreamed through all three at once, his Provenance blazing, sweat standing on his skin in a place that had no heat, dreaming, dreaming, dreaming alongside a thing three hundred and forty-one Trueness deep and refusing, absolutely refusing, to fall one single step behind!","And then it stopped.","The Chrysalis came back around him all at once. Silk falling. Nebulas turning. Noah standing exactly where he had been standing, breathing hard, his Provenance drawn thin and humming, and the small golden Gu hanging at the bottom of its strand exactly where it had hung.","It looked at him for a long moment.","Then it nodded.","One slow inclination of that plated head, and the shapes inside its wings turned once and settled!","\"It is nice ,\" the Dream Gu said, \" to see a little one starting out who is a true dreamer.\"","The strand it hung from began to draw upward.","\" There are so few. Most who come here dream of things. You dream with them. That is the older way. Take this.\"","Something detached from beneath one of its wings and drifted down, slow, turning, and landed in Noah’s open palm!","A scale.","A single golden plate no larger than a coin, still warm, still catching light from angles the light was not coming from, and as it touched his skin, prompts unfolded!","| DREAMER’S SCALE|","|A shed plate of a Rare Dream Gu, given freely. It carries the Gu’s recognition.|","|Function: a key. In the Chrysalis, the deeper silk of the Dream weavings will part for the bearer. Elsewhere, any dream the bearer walks will know they were acknowledged by something older than dreaming.|","|Function: a mark. Other Dream Gu will perceive the bearer as one who kept pace. Most will not test again. Some will be curious.|","...!","The Dream Gu rose along its strand, and the strand rose with it, and in the space of a breath it was gone into the upper silk and only the falling threads remained, gentle and multicolored and no longer looking at anyone.","Noah closed his hand around the scale.","The ring on his finger grew warm again.","|For a second there, I thought you were dead.|","|My weavings are waking up a bit more, in this place that used to be my home for some time. This construct can have a bit more freedom here. So let us go. You survived one encounter with a Rare one that you cannot overcome, and I would like that to remain the total.|","|Let us find a Common one.|","|You should be able to converse with me more freely here. At most, you can treat me like a database. Ask questions. They will eat your Provenance. Ask anyway.|","Noah looked at the ring for a moment.","Then he looked at the scale in his hand, and the silk, and the place where a thing a Fold above him had gone back up into the dark with a nod, and he made a decision about how to spend what he had.","\"I can ask you a lot of questions ,\" he said. \" But tell me something that you feel is the most important for me to know.\"","The ring was silent.","Not the silence of before, when Atlas had held back so the Gu could judge. A different silence. The silence of a cluster of records and probability searching a very long life for the one thing in it that mattered most, and taking its time about the search!","Then Atlas spoke, and for once, there was no laugh in it.","| When I was rising in power, I traveled for a time with two Immense Ones.|","|One of them you know. She did not go by Widow then. She had another name, and I will not say it here, since she has earned her quiet and this place listens. The other was a strand of a different kind, and does not matter to this story.|","|The three of us came to a region of THE Chrysalis that holds a mountain.|","|I want you to picture it properly. The whole mountain was made of Gu. Not living on it. Made of it. Millions of them, Common and Rare, locked together into a peak that went up past the sky and out of sight, every one of them powerful enough to kill me twice at the depth I held then, and every one of them still and quiet and waiting.|","|And at the summit sat a Gu so rare that any Immense One in existence would go mad for it.|","|Here is the thing. Existence itself held a Narrative over that mountain. A Ruling, undeniable, older than the two Immense Ones I stood beside. The Ruling said: to reach the peak and claim the Gu, one must follow the path that has been carved. There was a path. It wound up the mountain through all those millions of waiting Gu. And the Ruling was the kind that existence does not argue with, because existence wrote it.|","|So the two Immense Ones climbed.|","|They were strands of the Weave, and they walked the carved path, and the path was a Ruling, and Rulings hold. But the path was carved to break whatever walked it. Every turn of it fed them to the mountain a piece at a time. And halfway up, the two most powerful beings I had ever stood beside could not go further. They were injured in ways I did not know Immense Ones could be injured. She was bleeding light. I will never forget it.|","|And I did not climb.|","The ring was warm in Noah’s hand, and the silk fell, and he did not interrupt.","|I looked at the carved path and I thought, this is a Ruling. It is undeniable. Existence wrote it. Fine. What does it actually say? It says the peak is reached by the path. It does not say the path is reached by walking.|","|I turned around and went back down into the outer silk, and I spent a long while looking, and I found a Common Gu. A Defiance Gu. The least impressive insect you have ever seen. A concept condensed out of nothing, no will, no echo, just a small pure crystallized refusal with six legs, running from me the moment it tasted that I was not food.|","|I caught it anyway. I bound it into the first shield I ever built, and the shield held one thing, which was its Defiance. Not strength. Not depth. Refusal, held up in front of me like a lantern.|","|Then I went back to the mountain, and I raised the shield, and I did not walk the carved path.|","|I walked straight up.|","|And the Ruling of the mountain met a Common insect’s refusal and did not know what to do with it, because a Ruling is a sentence existence wrote, and the Defiance Gu was a concept existence had condensed, and they were made of the same stuff, and the older one was the refusal. The mountain could not decide whether I was breaking its Ruling or expressing it. While it was deciding, I reached the top.|","|I took the Gu. Then I went back down, and I carried two Immense Ones off that mountain one at a time under a shield made out of a bug that was afraid of me.|","|That is the story.|","The silk kept falling. The nebulas turned.","| This is the most important thing I know, and I have spent a very long time knowing it.|","|In Existence, many beings hold Rulings. Existence itself holds Rulings, and Scales, and Narratives, and a great many more things besides. Some of them are undeniable, and they are called undeniable because it is true. You will meet a hundred of them before you die, and every one of them will be written in a sentence that sounds final.|","|But you do not necessarily have to follow those Rulings. Or those Scales. Or the words of anyone else. Including me. Especially me, because I am a record, and records love to be obeyed.|","|Question everything you hear. And then bring your own refusal to it, whatever shape your refusal takes, and hold it up, and walk straight up the mountain.|","|Your own defiance...your own path.|","|That is what leads to the peak. Nothing else ever has.|","...!","Noah stood in the silk with a Dream Gu’s scale warm in one hand and a dead man’s most important lesson warm in the other, and for a long moment he simply held both of them, and did not move, and thought his own thoughts.","\"....\"","Then he closed his hand, and went to find a Common Gu!"]},{"number":5708,"title":"Chapter 5708: Chapter 5707: Powerless! I","paragraphs":["<THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering>","Far from where a Human Dreamer walked with a golden scale in his hand, the silk was being torn.","Nine riders moved through the deep nebulas at a pace that did not belong to this place. The Chrysalis was slow. Everything in it drifted. These did not drift. They drove forward through the falling strands in a wedge, and the strands parted ahead of them and did not settle behind, and the kaleidoscope itself seemed to hold its colors still until they had passed!","They were Descendants, and then, there were these Descendants.","Not the cursed kind with rot at the fissures and salvation begged from a Father who never answered. These were the other thing, the thing the cursed ones had been bred as a shadow of! Each of them stood the height of a small mountain, titanic and ancient, and their bodies were carved of the same substance that Jarl Erling’s had been, bronze and stone and old fire, but nothing in them was cracking.","Their skin held no fissures. Their eyes held no fear. They sat their mounts with the posture of beings who had never once in their existence had to ask whether they would wake up tomorrow!","And their Steeds burned with glory.","Every one of them akin to a living Observable Existence, bred exactly as Hvitrmarr had been bred, and every one of them was whole! Their First Causes did not fail. Nine or more in every mount, seated in the organs, pouring light out through the hide, so that each Steed moved through the silk wrapped in its own dawn!","No two were alike.","The leading Steed was a colossal white stag, its antlers branching upward into forks that held whole Observable Existences turning in their tines.","Beside it walked a thing with six legs and a serpent’s body, scaled in gold, its Causes lighting the scales from underneath so that it looked struck through with sunrise.","Behind them a quadruped of black stone with rivers of molten Cause running down its flanks. A winged one, feathered in silver, wings folded because there was no wind here to need them.","A low heavy beast with a shell of overlapping plates, each plate a continent. A hound with three heads and one heartbeat. A horse, plainly a horse, and somehow the most frightening of them all for it, since only a being of terrible confidence chooses to ride the ordinary shape!","And behind the nine, dragged by ropes, came the catch.","Three Common Dream Gu.","Moon-sized, translucent, bloated with murky golden dream-weather, their many eyes rolling in every direction and their soft plates heaving! They had been bound in obsidian rope, thick as rivers, and the rope burned with Causes, and where it touched the Gu the dream-stuff inside them went dark and still.","The Gu did not struggle. Something in the rope had convinced them not to as the faint power of an Immense One could be felt coursing through the ropes.","The hunt had gone well.","At the head of the wedge, on the white stag whose antlers held Observable Existences, the leader sat with the reins gathered in one hand!","She was the largest of them. Fierce-faced, titanic, her crimson eyes burning steady in a face carved of old bronze, and her armor was not armor but the plain bare weight of a body that had never needed any. The Causes of her Steed lit her from below. The silk parted ahead of her before she reached it.","She looked back once at the three bound Gu, and her mouth curved.","Then she grasped the reins.","\"Father enjoys his dreams more than usual.\"","Her voice went out through the nebulas and did not come back!","\"So we have to find at least ten Dream Weavings Gu. If we can obtain more...\" The crimson eyes turned forward. \" Then it is only greater glory for us.\"","The white stag lowered its head.","\" Come on!\"","The nine drove forward into the deep silk, wedge tight, Steeds blazing, dragging three bound dreams behind them toward a Father who had not once in the whole of recorded existence been described as sleeping!","The Descendants of THE Sleepless Fiend. his First Borns, were hunting in the Chrysalis!","---","<THE Vasiliou Elseworld>","Existence...was always unpredictable.","Noah knew this. He made many plans because of unpredictability. But still, he never knew everything.","It was only human to not know everything!","At this time.","While one of his bodies held an important journey in THE Chrysalis, one of Noah’s other bodies felt a tremendous change in the golden spring inside a certain mountain.","He was holding onto Thalia when...","The spring went cold before anything arrived.","It was a heavy cold, and Noah felt it first in the stolen thing inside him, THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign, which had sat quiet in his depths since the day he took it.","Thalia’s hand closed on his arm as they stopped their Dual Cultivation session.","\" Something is coming !\" she said with alarm as robes covered her body!","At this time, when it seemed ever so peaceful and without absolutely any issues...","Above the Vasiliou Elseworld, the violet sky tore.","The whole bioluminescent dome of it simply stopped being a sky and became a face, or the pressure of one, enormous and looking down, and the moss-stone arcs on their localized gravities began to drift out of true as the gravities themselves lost their nerve!","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR has arrived. You can honor him by many different names, but today, he is a Collector that was not paid.|","| He perceives what was taken from him. It is still being drawn upon. It is being drawn upon now, in a spring, by a thing that did not ask. He can smell his prize filled with the seed of another as he is furious.|","|He is more than fucking displeased.|","An Immense One who did not get what he was promised!","Noah had known this being may send forces or even come himself, but he didn’t expect it so soon!","And he...had gone under the assumption that truly, the influence of an Immense One would be diminished in an Elsedimension! And yet here was one bypassing whatever rulings...and having his power crash into the inhabitants of an Elsedimension. How?","At this time.","The Elseworld answered!","Every lotus in the crystalline lakes below sealed at once, island-sized petals closing over the basins in domes of blue-gold. Light ran up the continent-trunked trees.","And from the golden tower at the heart of Vasileia, Provenance Lifeforms rose into the air, the twelve Elders of the lineage at their head, ancient and radiant, the beings Noah had seen ringed around Aurelius before.","He knew their faces.","They rose to defend their lineage, twelve Ages of standing gathered in the torn violet air!","And at their head, Aurelius Vasiliou.","He came up out of the city with his hands still behind his back, and THE Provenance of THE Unfallen Vanguard unfolded around him for the twelfth time in his existence, and the unfolding was a truth stated aloud to the whole Elseworld: that to injure his home, they would have to get through him, that what stands here will still be standing after!","He rose to the level of the enormous face, and he did not flinch from it, and he spoke!","\" You did not get what was promised ,\" Aurelius said, and his voice went out steady across the Elseworld.","\" My lineage does not hide from a debt. So name it. What price is owed, and what price can be paid? Speak it, and let us settle this as existences that have both stood a long time, and not as a fire and the thing it burns. We have weavings and karma with other Immense Ones as we can always work-\"","HUUM!","The face in the sky interrupted him.","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR hears the patriarch’s offer.|","|He finds it quaint and says...you dumb fucking buffoon.|","|Today,| he said, and the pressure gathered as he said it, |I will not collect so much as I will kill. I don’t give a damn what you are allied with.|","The pressure came down as Aurelius was shocked and horrified!","What!","This was not how things should play out! An Immense One shouldn’t act so openly and brazenly like this!","What...","BOOM!","It did not strike Aurelius. It struck the lineage around him, and an Elder with the long white braid... simply became less. Her light thinned. Her outline lost its edges. And then the air where she had been held nothing at all!","Rivers of undeniable power of an Immense One continued to come down in spans of instants!","| Some beings should know their place ,| the Collector said, | You have lived a long while beside your betters and mistaken proximity for peerage. A candle set near a strand of the Weave is still a candle. It only learns this at the end.|","|Do Provenance Lifeforms no longer fear Immense Ones? Did you all think we are so passive and laid back, only sending messages? Is that why you fucked me over? Did you all forget you sit below us? You aren’t even some ancient clan as I cannot fathom what gave you the balls, you fucking buffoons. |","HUUM!","Another Provenance Lifeform, a broad quiet Elder, threw himself across the space before Aurelius, arms wide, and took the descending power of THE Immense One and did not make a sound, and went out like a flicker of light, his Provenance extinguished!","| The dignity of some existences cannot be crossed, | the Collector went on, unhurried, as a second Elder guttered and a third roared, the entire Vasiliou Elseworld thrown into panic!","| Mine was crossed by a thief, and I have come to teach the whole of the house that sheltered the drawing of it that some lines, once crossed, do not admit of payment. Only of correction.|","Aurelius’s Vanguard held, barely as he was ashen while looking at the destruction!","This truly was not what he had envisioned!","He had thought wrong! Oh, so wrong!"]},{"number":5709,"title":"Chapter 5709: Chapter 5708: Powerless! II","paragraphs":["Aurelius stood in the center of the thinning with his Provenance wrapped around him, and the pressure that had unmade three of his Elders met that truth and stopped, exactly as it had stopped eleven times before, and for one breath the Elseworld believed!","Maybe!","The Provenance of their leader was special! It was grand!","They believed.","Then... the Collector pressed as undeniable golden rivers crashed down.","The Provenance bent. From the mountain he rushed from with Thalia, Noah saw it bend, saw the edges of the Unfallen Vanguard curl inward under a weight that did not care what had been declared, and Aurelius Vasiliou, who had never once in eleven stands taken a step backward, took one!","Blood came out of his mouth.","This was an Immense One. His standing and Dimensionality was unfathomably higher as what could the Provenance of a single Provenance Lifeform do?","| Did you believe you had friends among my kind?|","The pressure ground down against the bending truth.","| Did you think, in your long quiet centuries, that you had earned a single ally among us who would stay my hand for the sake of your pleasant little lineage? There are none. Look around your torn sky. None came. None will come.|","| None can save you now.|","POOF!","Across the city, multiple Provenance Lifeforms turned to a puff of red dust as if the defenses of Aurelius did not even exist!","THE Immense One wss killing slowly as he had not even targeted Noah and Thalia yet, seemingly intent on destroying what Thalia knew as home to torment her first.","Noah gazed at the horrific power barreling down as he... did not throw a single attack.","He knew. That was the terrible clarity of it. His Infinite Sanguine Mana would do nothing. His Provenance would do nothing. His Mantle, his Teloi, the whole roaring arsenal of two hundred decillion quarks, all of it was a wrinkle in a cloth, and the cloth was up there deciding where everyone stood, and it would not so much as notice a strike from him.","The gap in Dimensionality was too vast.","He had learned that from a dead man only a short while ago, and he was watching the lesson be proven in the deaths of people who had never harmed him!","To throw power he knew was useless would be a lie. A performance of doing something, so that afterward he could tell himself he had tried. That he was somehow defiant and tyrannical.","So he did the only true thing available.","He took Thalia’s hand, and he moved!","He had a few plans he could initiate as he remembered Atlas’ words to be defiant on set rulings and existence itself. He began to implement a possible plan!","He moved toward the center of the thinning, toward the two figures at the heart of the dying light, and Thalia moved with him, the two of them crossing the burning air of the Elseworld while Provenance Lifeforms guttered on every side, closer, and closer, to Aurelius and Rosalia!","Rosalia had reached her husband.","She had come up through the air with no ceremony at all and taken his weight against her, and his blood ran down the front of her, and he was dazed as he said, \" My defenses should have held. They should have...held!\"","She held him tight as her Provenance flared and she roared!","The Collector pressed harder, and dozens more Provenance Lifeforms guttered!","Then Thalia forcefully let go of Noah’s hand and went up as she cried while looking at devastation, with Noah following her right after!","She climbed into the torn air in her soaked robe, and she hung between the Collector and her bleeding father, and she spread her arms!","\" You came for what is yours!\" Her voice carried across the whole dying Elseworld. \" It was promised to you by this lineage, and this lineage does not break its word! Look at me, O Collector. I am the debt. I am standing in the open. Take the one who was promised, and leave the ones who only kept the promise!\"","He knew she was trying to buy time as...","’ My Provenance, please, what can we do?!’","She sent him a mental message thst showed her desperation!","The face in the sky considered her.","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR looks at the daughter.|","|You fucking whore. Damaged goods should only feel the pain before they are torn apart soon after. Wait your turn, harlot.|","...!","The pressure resumed. Half the lineage of Provenance Lifeforms was gone now!","Aurelius sagged in his wife’s arms, and Noah looked at all of this with eyes of profound defiance!","He stopped thinking about power.","He had known. He had known the owner of that Provenance would come, and he had spent the intervening time Dual Cultivating and learning to build Elsedimensions and reading about Gu and being taught the difference between depth and magnitude by a dead man, and he had made no plan for this whatsoever because of many assumptions and things he had been told!","It was a horrendous oversight as he assumed and took the word of Aurelius that the could keep an Immense One at bay, and that he knew how an Immense One would react.","They were horribly wrong.","He continued reaching into an obsidian journal and he drove his Provenance into it, hard, into the page of the porch and the two cups, and he called.","A demand for a debt owed, not a request.","\" You said I could reach you. I am reaching. I am calling the favor. Intervene in the Vasiliou Elseworld where THE UNPAID COLLECTOR is rampaging now for him to cease animosity against us!\"","He sent the message.","And...","The page did not answer.","Above the Elseworld, the pressure found what was left of the golden tower and leaned on it, and the tower fell.","Multiple Vasiliou Provenance Lifeforms continued to rise and circle Aurelius and Rosalia as if they wanted to ensure their leaders did not die, and many of them turned into crimson gold mist!","Noah’s existence seethed as he sent his Provenance into the page again.","Nothing came. No response!","The book stayed shut in his hands while people who had done nothing but keep a promise died in every direction, and Noah, at this moment, truly felt powerless.","Completely!","He had the dead construct of a genius on his Existence and he was traversing THE Chrysalis that some didn’t even know existed, but so what?","Power was power, and his certainly did not match up at this time.","As he gazed at the devastation, a second eye finally opened in the sky.","It bloomed beside the face of the Collector, heavy-lidded, gold, and the dusk that came with it settled over the burning Elseworld and stopped the light from dying any further!","THE REMINISCING WIDOW.","She did not look at Noah as she looked at the Collector, and the Collector looked at her, and the gaze he turned on her was cold enough that the thinning halted on its own, the pressure pausing mid-act while two strands of Immense Ones considered each other across a sky that belonged to neither of them.","They spoke.","Nobody heard any of it, not even Noah.","It moved above him in a register that did not need his hearing, and what came through was the shape of it and not the words.","She said something brief. He said something briefer. She said something that took longer, and the dusk deepened while she said it, and at the end of it the Collector was silent for a moment that the whole Elseworld held its breath inside!","Then the Collector harrumphed.","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR looks down upon the Vasiliou.|","|A lineage of lamps. Thousands of candles calling themselves a fire, and half of them snuffed by an afternoon of his displeasure. He is embarrassed to have been owed anything by them at all.|","The eye turned. It found Noah and Thalia, and it held both of them at once.","| I am not done with you.|","|Live in fear and doubt. At an undetermined time in the future, I may appear at any moment you hold her, and rip her in half.|","|Any...moment.|","HUUUM!","And in an instant, the face in the sky was gone.","The violet dome came back, torn in a way that would not heal for a long while, and the moss-stone arcs found their gravities again and settled, and across the Elseworld the thinning had stopped, and what it had already taken did not come back.","The second eye lingered.","It looked down at Noah through the dusk, and he could see it clearly, every line of it, and the words came without any halo to carry them, quiet, from everywhere for all those here to see.","| The favor has been paid, O Human Dreamer.|","...!","Then she was gone as well, and the evening she had brought went with her.","Noah did not move for a moment.","Then Thalia came down out of the air past him and went to her parents. Rosalia had lowered Aurelius to a moss-stone arc.","His blood had stopped and his Provenance was gone entirely, not guttering but gone. Fractured. Decimated!","His daughter knelt and put her forehead against his shoulder, and he lifted one shaking hand and set it on her hair.","\"Its...okay. Such is existence, my daughter. Such is existence. I am just glad to have protected you from a being like that...\"","...!","Aurelius said such words, but Rosalia gazed at Noah hatefully!","Around them, the lineage counted itself, and came up short.","Noah looked at the devastation of Provenance Lifeforms.","The Provenances forever disintegrated while he had been...","Powerless. That was the word, and it was not the same word as outmatched or outnumbered. He had faced things above his weight before and found an angle.","There had been no angle. There had been a wall, and a book that would not open, and seconds!","And when the help had come, it had come in its own time, which was never his. The Widow had arrived when she arrived, spoken as long as she chose, and left when the debt was square by her own accounting, and every second between his call and her eye had been paid for by the lives of many Provenance Lifeforms.","That was what relying on another meant. They came in their own time. They did things in their own way. The bill for the difference went to whoever was standing closest, and today it had gone to many!","He had assumed far too many things that turned out to be wrong.","He needed to do things differently. He needed to question everything he heard or thought he knew as there were no absolutes.","Noah stood in the decimated centerpoint of The Vasiliou Lineage as he stood tall while many accusing faces picked each other out of the rubble, their distate and hatred showing clearly whenever they glanced at him!","There was no tyranny to show or speech to give as this...was merely a glimpse of the power of Immense Ones and a heavy defeat that let it be known clearly...whatever rules others believed, Immense Ones did not have to abide by them."]},{"number":5710,"title":"Chapter 5710: Chapter 5709: Sonder I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the devastation, and the devastation looked back through a hundred grieving faces.","Aurelius sat on the moss-stone arc with his wife’s arms around him and his daughter’s forehead against his shoulder, and his blood had dried on all three of them, and his Vanguard was gone in a manner that Noah suspected would not return in a lifetime.","He lifted his head. He found Noah across the wreckage of his own city, and then he gave one heavy nod.","\"I did not know you had the pull that you showed,\" Aurelius said. His voice had lost the steadiness it wore in the sky, and he did not try to put it back. \" Thank you. For spending a favor of an Immense One to end this.\"","Noah said nothing. There was nothing to say that would not sound like taking credit for a rescue that had cost this man half his lineage.","\"It was I who made the deal, ages ago, to give my daughter away.\" Aurelius looked down at Thalia’s radiant hair under his hand. \" So I cannot lay this at your feet. Your intrusion took a choice out of my hands. The choice of cowardice, which I could never make myself take, because I was afraid of exactly this, the extermination of everything that carries my name. You forced us to the place I had spent an Age avoiding. A price was paid for it. But I...\"","His voice trailed. He looked out at the pale places in the air where his Elders had been.","\" But I...\"","The words did not finish.","And Noah’s eyes flashed with the brilliant light of infinity, and everything went grey and still.","He had not frozen them. He could not have frozen most of them; a great many of the Provenance Lifeforms in this ruined city were his betters in every number that could be measured.","He had only stretched his own perception toward infinity, so that a single instant opened out and out, an instant with no far wall, and he stood inside it alone with a failure that was not going anywhere.","His eyes pulsed.","He entered the reverie, that unique state where boundless epiphanies bloomed in every direction at once and a thought could be turned over ten thousand times before the next instant arrived.","And his eyes, which existence had learned to read as tyranny, held something else in the grey stillness.","Sadness .","It was only human.","Because in the stretched instant he was thinking of Eon. Of how he had taken her as his woman, and how her home and her people had been destroyed, and how that had become one more weaving in the great wake he dragged behind himself. And now Thalia. He had taken her too, this woman who had crossed time itself to reach him, who had torn her own Provenance to arrive, who had sat in his spring and named every danger ahead of them in careful order.","She had warned him. She had done nothing but warn him and help him and love him, and here was her home, and here were her people, thinning into the air while she knelt in the blood of her father.","He could argue that he had made no promises. It would even be true. He had promised the Vasiliou nothing except an errand and a bargain.","He still felt he had broken something. He still felt he had let them down. The technicality did not reach the feeling.","He rarely felt this way. His whole identity was pitched at one weaving, and the weaving was tyranny. Majesty!","He spoke the same to Provenance Lifeforms who could unmake him as he spoke to the frightened and the small. He had stood before Immense Ones and not bent a word of himself.","He was fearful, and he was fearless, both at once, and he had built an entire existence on the certainty that this was enough.","None of it had done a single thing today. In the end he had been reduced to hammering on a book and begging another to do what he could not.","He looked at the faces. Thalia’s, hollowed out. Rosalia’s, turned on him with a hatred that had earned every degree of itself. Aurelius’s, solemn and unfinished. And his existence buzzed, and a realization came up out of the grey stillness and would not go back down.","He was the protagonist.","He had named himself that. He had spoken the Letter and taken the Aura and built an edge over existence out of the claim that the story bent toward him. And it was true, and it had served him, and it had also let him believe, in a place beneath thought, that the other figures in his eras were figures. Extras. Supporting shapes. Weight and texture in his story.","They were not!","Every one of them was the protagonist of a story that had been running long before Noah Osmont arrived in it.","Aurelius carried an Age of history in which Noah was one recent Chapter, and not the first hard one. The people going out like lamps around him had each held a whole existence, vivid and detailed and entirely their own, in which they were the center and he was the stranger who arrived one afternoon and changed everything and would leave.","He wanted to be grand. He wanted to be immense. He had never once questioned thr cost!","But it should not be built on the ruin of existences that had done nothing to him. He had his life, and the ones he had chosen to protect. They had theirs. Every form of existence was exactly as complex as his own, as full, as central to itself, and he had been walking through all of it as scenery.","HUUM!","The light in his eyes grew, and it did not lose the sorrow, and deep in his existence THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer cried out with a solemnity he had never heard from it and surged like a vast sea rising past its shore.","Existence was vast and complex.","And every single lifeform within it was equally vast, and equally complex, and equally the center of its own turning.","|A fundamental change has occurred within THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer.|","|You have long dreamed. You believed you were the one who dreams. Today you have understood that you dream among decillions who dream as vividly as you.|","| THE DREAM STATE OF SONDER has been attained.|","|SONDER: the sudden realization that every stranger you pass is living a life as vivid, complex, and detailed as your own. It is the moment you understand that you may not be the main character of existence, but a background figure in decillions of other stories unfolding around you.|"]},{"number":5711,"title":"Chapter 5711: Chapter 5710: Sonder II","paragraphs":["|THE Dream State of Sonder elevates the Mantle of THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist. It grants a gaze of empathy and understanding: you perceive the dreams and the hopes of those you look upon. You are the Human Dreamer. You are not the only one who dreams in existence. You may now perceive and draw not only from your own dreams, but from the dreams of all who dream around you.|","| PROVENANCE has crossed the 100 threshold, passing into THE SEAM, into THE INEFFABLE VERSE, and arrived at 110.|","|VERITAS has advanced to 105.|","|PONDUS has advanced to 101.|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI has advanced to 125.|","Noah stood in the greying instant with his existence remade a little, and his eyes shone with endless blue and gold, and the shine remained a solemn thing.","He had dreams. Others had dreams too. As THE Human Dreamer he could dream grandly enough for himself and everyone he loved, and he could do it without grinding the dreams of the uninvolved to dust beneath him. That was possible.","And if he met a being who meant to spend its dream on the destruction of his, then of course he would answer it without mercy, because protecting what was his had never once required apology.","His hand closed into a fist.","He looked up, and the brilliance in his eyes grew brighter.","Then he looked at the lineage around him, the Provenance Lifeforms who had lost everything, drifting through the ruin of a city that had stood since before the current arrangement of things, and he wanted to offer them somewhere.","Somewhere an Immense One could not reach. He had a Realm, and a first Elsedimension folded into it, built with no authority an architect could ride, and he wanted to open it and say come, be safe, no strand of the Weave will ever touch you here.","He was not sure he could say it truthfully.","Because an Immense One had just reached into the Vasiliou Elsedimension and expressed his full power inside a place that was supposed to blunt him, and Noah did not know how. If a strand of THE Immense One could bypass one Elsedimension, could it bypass his? Could it walk into the Realm and do to his mother and his son and his people what the Collector had just done here?","He did not know!","And ever since he had built his first Elsedimension, he had given THE Infiniverse the order to begin turning the whole of herself into one, an Elsedimension entire, a home no other existence could enter. He had believed that made his people safe. He had believed it as firmly as he had believed Aurelius could hold an Immense One at bay.","Assumptions had killed today. He would ask Atlas, because he could not afford one more thing he merely hoped was true.","He drew a breath in the stretched grey instant, and he let THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer open the whole of the way, and Sonder woke behind his eyes.","The grey filled with gold.","Around every single being in the ruined city, a swirling cloud of golden dream turned slowly, one for each of them, and no two were alike, and the whole devastated Elseworld became a sky of quiet private dreaming.","He looked at Thalia.","| THALIA VASILIOU dreams: to be believed, once, by the one she crossed time to reach. To not be a warning he resents. To sit at a table that is set for the living. To protect and to prosper.|","Noah’s chest tightened, and he made himself keep looking.","He looked at Aurelius, and at Rosalia holding him.","| AURELIUS and ROSALIA VASILIOU dream: that the name survives them. That the daughter they bargained away was worth the wound it cost to let her go.|","|Note: any weaving you contribute to the dreams of those you perceive feeds back into THE Human Dream. The grander the dream you help carry, the grander the return to your own.|","Noah looked at them all, one at a time, through the gold, and he inscribed the afternoon into his existence.","He had made no promises. He would hold to that, since it was true.","But he could move differently. He could carry his Dreams and his Infinity across existence without leaving only apocalypse behind him, without decimating every story he happened to walk through on his way to being grand.","The grey released.","Color and sound crashed back into the ruined Elseworld, and Aurelius, mid-sentence, found the end of it at last.","\" But I...am glad ,\" the old man said quietly, \" that my daughter is alive.\"","Noah finally spoke.","\"I should have made precautions much earlier.\" He looked at the old man across the ruin. \" I am sorry.\"","Aurelius only smiled at that, sadly, and looked around at the pale places in the air and the fallen tower and the survivors moving through the rubble counting the ones who were not moving through it with them. He did not argue the apology and he did not accept it.","Noah looked at Thalia.","She was tending her father, her Provenance flowing into him in a steady warm current, and her face had changed. The hollowness was gone out of it. What had replaced it was firm!","Before he could call out to her, she spoke.","\"An Immense One wanted my Provenance .\" She did not look up from her father as she said it. \" One of them looked across all of existence and decided that what runs in a Vasiliou was worth crossing a sky to take.\"","Her hand pressed flat against Aurelius’s chest, and her Provenance sank deeper into him.","\"So I will use it. I will use it to change the Provenance of my lineage .\" Her eyes came up now, and they burned. \" I will make them all into Elselifeforms, and I will understand, down to the root, exactly why a being like that wanted this badly enough to burn my home for it. If we are worth taking, then we are worth becoming something that cannot be taken.\"","Noah gave a light nod at that.","\"I cannot make any promises right now ,\" he said.","\" But I am looking into a bastion. A domain that something like THE UNPAID COLLECTOR should not be able to reach into. As soon as I have confirmation, real confirmation, I will tell you. It should be possible to move the whole of the Vasiliou Elsedimension somewhere safer.\"","Thalia looked at him, and her eyes shone with a sudden immense brilliance, because she knew exactly what place he meant. She had walked its blue-gold hills. She had asked him, once, to take her to see his mother in it!","She simply nodded, and turned back to her father, and let her Provenance flow.","Noah’s existence pulsed.","And far away, in a place outside the weavings of time, another of his bodies stopped walking."]},{"number":5712,"title":"Chapter 5712: Chapter 5711: Questions and Answers","paragraphs":["<THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering>","The silk fell around him and the kaleidoscopic nebulas turned in the vastness, and Noah stood alone in the deep drift of THE Chrysalis with dreamy light burning bright behind his eyes, brighter than it had ever burned.","An infinite dream filled with boundless complexities seemed to be waking!","He had questions. Today had bought them at a terrible price, and he intended to spend every single one as his mind calculated the bloody ruins of the Vasiliou Elsemountain.","\" How could an Immense One exert their power inside an Elsedimension?\"","He spoke the words into the illusory ring resting against his finger.","|-0.1 PROVENANCE ESSENCE|","\" They are built to reject the authority of such beings,\" Noah continued. \" That was the entire point of their architecture, you told me so yourself. And yet I just watched one reach into the Vasiliou Elsedimension and impose himself without the slightest trouble. Lifeforms of higher Dimensionality than mine were ended with a tap, inside a place that was supposed to blunt him. I only survived because he wanted to save me and my love for last, as cruelty. Had he chosen to kill instead of to torment, that body of mine would have collapsed, or worse. So I need to understand clearly. What parameters actually make an Elsedimension keep an Immense One out?\"","The illusory band warmed against his flesh.","The voice rolled out from the records-cluster, carrying that sharp, familiar arrogance that refused to bend to anything in the continuum.","| The largest protection an Elsedimension offers is not a wall. It is that the place cannot easily be found by an Immense One simply deciding to look for it. They are strands of the Weave. Their sight runs along the cloth, and a strand cannot look at what is woven into a seam it does not know about.|","|Unless.|","|Unless that strand has been there before. If an Immense One was ever inside an Elsedimension, if it was ever invited, ever allowed to cross the threshold even once, then it left seeds of its own weavings behind. They always do. They cannot help it, any more than you can walk through wet sand without leaving prints. An Elsedimension that has admitted an Immense One is a useless Elsedimension. The authority has already permeated it. The door was opened from the inside and it does not close again.|","|So. That Collector had been to the Vasiliou Elsedimension before, or something of his had, or the lineage let something in they should not have. Ask them.|","|There are no absolutes. But a properly designed Elsedimension, one that has never once let an architect past its door, will do its job. Yours has never admitted one. Keep it that way and it is the safest ground in existence for a being of your fold.|","The answer came as he thought about it, and them he set it aside to confirm with his own eyes before he built a single plan on it.","\" The Elsedimension Ring ,\" Noah said, letting another thread of authority bleed into the band. \" The first thing you are guiding me to build. What is it actually capable of?\"","|-0.1 PROVENANCE ESSENCE|","\" Because I am thinking about survival at this moment.\" Noah went on, his pupils reflecting the falling silk.","\"Survival, against things tremendously stronger than me. Will this ring let me do that?\"","| Now you are thinking like a man who intends to live long enough to become dangerous.|","The records pulsed with clear, steady warmth as Atlas continued.","| What I engineered, and what I can teach you to engineer, does a great many things. An Elsedimension Ring, designed well, can be set to sense the incoming animosity of a specific enemy, an Immense One you have marked, and the instant it feels that intent turn toward you, it warps your entire existence into an Elsedimension elsewhere before the blow arrives. You are simply not where the strike falls. You were never there.|","| You can build in other functions besides. A masking so that certain sights slide off you. A warning that wakes before the danger does. A store of ground you can retreat into and seal. A ring is not one tool, O Human Dreamer. And a ring is only one of many things.|","The dreamy light of Sonder turned behind Noah’s eyes as he listened, absorbing the mechanics without distraction.","|A weaker existence can move across an existence full of stronger ones and not die. It is done. It has always been done. It is perilous, and it is adversity without end, and it is possible. There are ways.|","| The first is to not be found. Depth over magnitude. Walk and hide where the great strands do not think to look, and let the mighty thunder past overhead while you go quietly about becoming. Most who hunt you cannot strike what they cannot perceive.|","|The second is to not be worth it. Make yourself a poor bargain. Be difficult, be defended, be the kind of prize that costs more to take than it returns, and a great many predators will decide you are not worth the afternoon. The Collector came for the Vasiliou because they were cheap. Do not be cheap.|","|The third is to not be reachable. Build the ground I am teaching you to build, and keep it clean of every seed, and when the sky turns against you, be elsewhere before it finishes turning. A being that cannot be cornered cannot be killed at leisure, and leisure is how the mighty prefer to kill.|","|Use all three at once and you will cross the whole of existence with monsters on every side and arrive at the far end still breathing.|","The nebulas turned overhead as the silk fell across Noah’s bare shoulders. He took the three principles into himself, weighing each against the brutality he had witnessed, and he did not let a single one become an absolute.","| And here is the last of it, Dreamer, and then I will let you get back to nearly being eaten by insects.|","The voice slowed slightly, carrying the unhurried weight of an ancient memory.","| You will not hide forever. That is not what any of this is for. You hide from a thing today so that you can grow, and you grow so that tomorrow you hide from something a fold higher, and one day you look back and find that the being you fled from an Age ago is a being you can now look in the eyes and feel nothing at all. No pressure. No fear. Just a strand, standing there, no larger to you than you once were to it.|","|Anything is possible in existence. I have watched it happen. I made some of it happen. And then... I stopped being able to, which is a story for a course you are not ready for.|","|Now. Go find a Common Gu that does not run, and let us build you a workshop for your finger.|","Noah stood a moment longer in the falling silk.","The light of dreams burned brighter in his eyes, Sonder and defiance and a cold new patience all at once, and he turned, moving deeper into THE Chrysalis to build the thing that would keep the people he loved out of a sky’s reach."]},{"number":5713,"title":"Chapter 5713: Chapter 5712: A Clash of Dreams! I","paragraphs":["Noah traversed in silence for a while as he continued to think of many things, and after a few minutes, he finally came across a Gu Lifeform in this region of predominant weavings of Dreams.","The Common Dream Gu was the type that did not even run.","It hung in a pocket of still silk where three strands had tangled into a kind of nest, moon-small at this range, its translucent body heaving slow, dream-weather drifting golden through its interior. Its many eyes were half-lidded. It was not fleeing and it was not feeding. It was simply there, doing the one thing its whole existence was made to do, and Noah stood in the drift a short distance off and looked at it with eyes in which Sonder had not once dimmed since it woke.","He saw its dream.","A single cloud of gold turned around the creature, slow, and inside the cloud was the dream, and Noah looked into it and found it so... simple.","It dreamed of warmth. It dreamed of the silk being soft. It dreamed, in the wordless way of a thing that had never held a word, of drifting somewhere the strands fell thick and the dream-weather was sweet, and being left alone to drift there. That was it!","That was the entire interior life of a lifeform that read past a hundred in every attribute a panel could measure. It wanted to be warm. It wanted to be left alone.","Noah found, standing there, that he did not want to break it. But...he would anyway. He needed a Common Gu, and this was one, and he had crossed out of the weavings of time and let himself be eaten to reach a place where he could take it.","In the end, Existence still held natural selection as one still had to do what they had to do.","It was like a human empathizing with the chicken he raised in a chicken coop. He could do it, but when he was eating that chicken soup...that soup tasted damn good.","He raised his hand, and THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer gathered behind his eyes, ready to reach into the little creature’s dream and fold it gently shut and carry it with him!","But then, his Provenance buzzed as he felt something.","\" That one is ours.\"","The voice came down through the silk.","Noah did not turn at once. He let his hand lower, and he let the reverie in his eyes hold, and only then did he look.","They came out of the deep nebulas in a wedge.","Nine riders, titanic, each the height of a small mountain, carved of bronze and stone. Their Steeds burned, whole and blazing, First Causes pouring light through the hide of a white stag whose antlers held Observable Existences in their tines, a golden six-legged serpent, a plated beast whose every plate was a continent, a plain horse that was somehow worse than all the rest!","And dragged behind them on obsidian rope that burned with an Immense One’s borrowed power came three bound Dream Gu, their tentacles limp, their Dreams gone dark.","At the head, on the white stag, sat the largest of them. Crimson eyes in a face of old bronze. She looked down at Noah, and she looked at the little untaken Gu drifting in its nest, and her mouth curved.","\" You have good eyes,\" she said. \" You found a Dream Gu, but we will take it off your hands.\"","Noah looked up at her, and then he looked at all of them, one after another.","Golden clouds of dreams gathered around each of them.","He read three of their dreams while she waited.","The leader dreamed of a nod. Not from anyone. From an Immense One. A single acknowledgment from a Father who had bred her line for exactly this and had never once looked directly at any of them, and she did what she was told so that ultimately she hoped she would finally earn her the tilt of a head she had wanted.","The Descendant on the golden serpent dreamed smaller and uglier: of the leader failing, so that he might be first to bring the catches home.","The one on the plain horse did not dream of the Father at all. It dreamed of the day the hunts would end. It did not believe the day would come. It dreamed of it anyway, quietly, and had for a very long time.","Noah took all of that in!","\" You have a great many of those already ,\" Noah said. He nodded at the three bound Gu without heat. \" Three on the rope, and there are more out there in the silk than the one drifting between us. This region of the chrysalis is full of dreams. Go find another.\"","His voice was calm.","\"I do not want a conflict with the First Borns of a Father I have no quarrel with...well, for the most part. I have had a long day. Someone I hold dear watched her home burn not long ago, and I would rather not add much more today. So take the good advice a stranger is giving you for free. Find another Gu. Leave this one, and leave me, and we both go home with what we came for.\"","For a moment the silk held its silence.","Then the leader laughed!","It was the laugh of a titan being lectured by a candle.","\" You speak very well for a thing with no aura at all, \" she said. \"I have been looking at you since we arrived, little one, and there is nothing under your skin. No Cause. No standing that reaches me. You dress like something and weigh like nothing. Who do you even descend from? No matter.\"","She leaned forward over the stag’s blazing neck. \" That Gu is ours because we say it is ours, and there is no one here to say otherwise but you, and you are no one. Step back into your silk. Father enjoys his dreams, and we have some more to catch before we can go.\"","She did not step back. None of them stepped back!","The nine titans and their burning Steeds stayed, and the little Dream Gu drifted on in its nest between the two of them, warm, wanting to be left alone.","Noah looked at their panels while she spoke,.","|FIRST BORN OF THE SLEEPLESS FIEND (×9)|","|Attribute range across the party: 101 to 130.|","|Depth: THE SEAM. Every rider a Cause-bearing Descendant of undying line.|","|PROVENANCE: 0. None among them holds a single point.|","Every one of them read higher than he did.","Several of them, in raw magnitude, could break him. And not one of them held a single point of Provenance, because they were spoken things, sentences with a bloodline, and a sentence does not generate its own aim.","They had been given everything they were. They had made none of it!","He, standing there weighing nothing, had made all of himself.","And every one of them held a dream that wanted to end his, so that a hunt could be completed and a head might tilt.","Noah felt the old thing rise in him, the tyranny, the greed, the cold amusement at the mighty taking themselves so seriously, and he did not fight it down. Sonder had not replaced it. Sonder had only aimed it.","These were not bystanders drifting through their own quiet lives. These were nine dreams that had looked at his dream and decided to grind it under, and against that, protecting what was his had never once required an apology.","Even if they were the Protagonists of their own story...he was THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist!","He wanted to see. He wanted to see his one dream, the dream of a human who had decided to be grand without leaving only ruin behind him, clash against nine older dreams that were certain of themselves, and he wanted to find out whose held!","It would be arduous. Nine titans who each outweighed him, their Steeds burning, an Immense One’s rope in their hands. He might bleed for it. He intended to persevere and come out standing anyway!","Noah let his hand rise once more, and this time THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer did not gather gently. It surged, blue and gold and vast, and the light of dreams in his eyes blazed until the nine riders and their burning mounts threw shadows across the falling silk.","\" Here is where we are ,\" Noah said. \" I gave you the door. You looked at it, and you decided I was no one, and you kept your feet where they are. That was your choice, and I am a great believer in letting existences make their own choices, even the wrong ones.\"","The little Dream Gu, sensing at last that its warm nest had become the center of something, stirred, and began, slowly, to wake.","\" You came here to catch dreams for a Father who does not look at you.\" Noah’s blue-gold gaze swept the wedge, and stopped on the leader, on the crimson eyes and the dream of a nod behind them.","\" Let me show you what it looks like when a dream refuses to be caught.\"","HUUM!","The silk stopped falling.","Every strand in the tangled nest and for a great span around it halted in the air, and the golden dream-weather inside the little Gu flared, and inside Noah’s eyes decillions of dreams that were not his own began, faintly, to turn, because Sonder was awake and he was no longer the only dreamer he could reach!","The nine First Borns felt the place change, and for the first time the leader’s mouth was not a smile as she frowned.","And this insignificantly small region of THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering filled with the concepts of Dreams faced a war of dreams!","The leader did not wait. Her crimson eyes flared. The white stag’s antlers blazed, every Observable Existence turning in its tines flaring with them.","\" Voss. Kara. Take this fucker from both sides ,\" she said. \" The rest, close the surrounding existence. Leave him a mouth to talk with and nothing else.\"","The surroundings broke into motion, and the quiet nest of dreams became a killing floor!","The Descendant on the golden serpent came in from the left, and the one on the winged silver Steed dropped from above, and the space between them was where Noah stood, and it should have been the end of a small thing with no aura!","The serpent-rider’s palm opened, and from it poured white. THE Argent Loom! One of the oldest authorities in existence came off him in a woven flood, bright thin strands lashing out to bind an enemy and hold it still for the killing!","It closed on nothing .","Because Noah was no longer there to close on.","He had begun before the leader finished her order. He had learned today, at a terrible price, what became of a man who let stronger things set the tempo, and so he had not waited to be attacked. In the Infinity of a Dreamer’s stretched instant he had closed his eyes and dreamed one thing, whole and simple.","He dreamed he could not be found.","THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM woke!","In the dream he had no aura, no weight, no place an eye could come to rest, and because he was the Human Dreamer and the dream was his own existence, it became true before the Loom could finish closing!","The white flood passed through empty silk.","| You dream yourself unseen. To perceivers below your Dreams, you are not there. The dream holds while it is not contested by a higher sight.|","The serpent-rider, Voss, drew his Loom back, confused, and the winged Steed’s rider landed in the space where the enemy had been and found nothing there to land on.","\" Where did it go ...\" Voss started.","Noah was already under his mount.","He crossed the region unseen, past both riders still searching the air, and came up beneath the belly of the golden six-legged serpent.","He reached into it, a hand wrapped in blue and gold, and closed his fingers around one of the First Causes seated blazing in its organs, and he distilled it. He drew the essence sideways out of true, taking the taste and leaving the fruit, and the Cause guttered!","He was very proficient in Causes, after all.","The serpent screamed and buckled at one leg as a sunrise went dark inside it!","Voss felt his mount fail under him and could not see why. He hauled on the reins and wheeled, Loom spilling uselessly from his hand, eyes raking the silk. \" Hey, this fucker is invisible even though his Dimensionality should not be higher than ours! Are they actually a Gu? They could be a rare Gu!\"","\" No way! Spread your immensity out and do not let anything near you!\" The leader snapped.","It was good advice, but till not enough!","Because Noah had crossed to the next one. He slid a dreaming hand between two continent-plates of the great plated beast and gripped the Cause beneath and drew, and a plate went cold and grey and split.","He was gone up the side of the black stone quadruped before the beast finished stumbling, and he guttered the molten Cause running down its side, and it folded onto its own legs with a groan that shook the nebulas.","Three mounts crippled. Not one Descendant had seen him do it!","They were beings of immense weight and no sight past their own dreams!","And while he worked, he understood something.","He was asking himself how he should fight with his strongest points while ensuring no time for the Descendants to even unleash their true power.","And the pieces were clicking!","He was inside their perception. He was a dream moving through the place they lived. And a dream that could move through their perception could reach the thing at the center of it.","He had read their dreams already. The leader’s nod. Voss’s small ugly hunger. The plain-horse rider’s quiet wish that the hunts would end.","He had only read them.","What if he wrote?","Noah rose out of his crouch still unseen, and let a portion of his Provenance bloom, and reached, not for a Cause this time, but for the golden cloud of dream turning slow around the leader.","He controlled his Provenance like an extension of his existence to interfere with that cloud as why shouldn’t he be able to manipulate the dreams of others?!","And he began to dream her a different dream.","| You reach into the Existential Narrative of another existence through its dream. THE Mantle of THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist stirs.|","The leader went rigid on the white stag as her high Dimensionality felt something!","She felt something reach into the oldest quiet place in her, where her hopes and dreams lived, and she felt something changing!","She wheeled the stag around, crimson eyes wide, and for the first time there was something in her face that was not contempt.","Was this fucker actually a Gu?!","Her body illuminated with Dimensionality as her Intent filled with THE Argent Loom and an ancient Tongue erupted around her like a storm!","\" Get the fuck out of my Existence!\"","HUUM!","\" You dream of recognized ,\" Noah said, and his voice came from everywhere.","\" From a Father who has never once looked at you. I have seen it.\"","He tightened his grip on the dream.","\" That is a sad thing to be. Let me change it for you.\"","He began to write. Into the cloud of her he wrote a new past, one where the recognition had already come, long ago, and meant nothing, and she had felt nothing when it did!","He wrote it backward into the records of her, so that it had always been so!","And the leader’s existence lurched, because the dream that had shaped her every action was being told it had never been true, and at the edges, her records began to disagree with themselves!","She became furious when she felt this!","\" Enough .\"","WUUa","She reached for something!","She drew a sword!","It came off her Existence in a wash of white and crimson, long and plain and terrible, and the instant it cleared the sheath the whole region of the Chrysalis changed its weight.","The silk stopped falling. The three bound Dream Gu on the ropes went rigid. And Noah, unseen in his dream, felt his imperceptibility strain for the first time, because the thing she had drawn was searching for him with a sight that was not eyes.","| WARNING.|","|The blade carries Existential Narrative not its own. Slivers of the Narrative of THE Sleepless Fiend are woven into its edge. It perceives across folds. Your unseen dream is no longer certainly unseen.|","The leader turned the blade, and its edge caught a light that came from nowhere in this place, and her lurching existence steadied itself on the weapon like a hand on a rail.","A sliver of brilliance of an Immense One flared as all of surrounding existence shuddered and cried!","She swung, at a pocket of empty silk, at nothing that anyone could see, and yet she still found her target as... it caught Noah full across the chest!"]},{"number":5714,"title":"Chapter 5714: Chapter 5713: A Clash of Dreams! II","paragraphs":["The blade found him as the dream shattered!","BOOM!","Noah was flung backward across the stellar region, visible again, an Immense One’s power having reached clean across the fold his dream had folded into!","Crimson gold blood sprayed from a wound that opened across his chest, and he tumbled through the falling silk and caught himself in the air, and for the first time all nine burning gazes fixed on the small bleeding figure!","\" There ,\" the leader breathed heavily. \" There you are, little fucker!\"","It hurt! The wound was deep, and he was bleeding in open air in front of nine titans who each outweighed himA","\" Kill it before it disappears again! Whether its a Gu or not doesn’t matter! \" the leader roared. \" It cannot hide from the blade! Move!\"","Voss, whose golden Steed was crippled but whose arm was not, hurled a spear of woven Argent Loom and Dimensionality, and Noah twisted in the air as this sharp Dimensionality tore through his shoulder instead of his heart.","Others came as Noah closed his eyes and imagined a dream where dodged every threst coming towards him!","It was an an infinite dream of THE Human Dreamer as he felt like he could do it endlessly!","The old assumption tried to rise in him, the one that whispered the story bent his way, that he was the protagonist and would be fine.","He srifled it.","He caught himself against a drifting continent of dead chitin, bleeding from chest and shoulder, and he thought about the one thing that mattered, which was the thing he had felt in the instant before the sword landed.","Her records had lurched.","For one moment, before she drew an Immense One’s power, the leader’s existence had shuddered, because the dream he was writing and the records she was built of had stopped matching. He had felt a Descendant’s foundation tremble because a story it stood on had been told a different ending!","That was the solution!","| The blade will find you whenever you are perceived. You cannot out-power it. But its bearer stands on a dream, and you are the thing that writes dreams. You can fight the war you can win.|","Noah stopped trying to survive the sword.","He stopped dodging toward safety, stopped answering their tempo, and hung in the burning air, bleeding, letting them come, because the fight they thought they were in was not the fight anymore!","He spread his hand across the nine dreams turning in his Sonder-sight, and he wrote into all of them at once.","The leader’s blade came for him even as he did it, and it hit, and he let it hit, taking the wound across his ribs and keeping his hand open!","Into Voss he wrote that he had betrayed the leader long ago, been caught, and been forgiven, and that the forgiveness was the most humiliating thing that had ever happened to him!","Voss’s raging storm of Dimensionality dropped from his hand mid-throw as a shame that had never occurred crashed down through him.","Into the winged rider he wrote that its wings had always been a lie, that it had never truly flown, that every flight had been a dream it told itself, and the rider faltered in the air!","Into the plain-horse rider he wrote that the hunts had already ended, ages past, and that everything since had been a dream it was having as it died, and the rider went still and silent and stopped fighting entirely, staring at a nothing it had privately expected for a very long time.","And into the leader, into the woman with an Immense One’s power in her hand and his blood on her edge, he wrote the cruelest true thing he had found in her.","That her Father had looked at her once, directly and had given her his Recognition an Age ago, and that she had been too busy hunting to notice, and had missed the only thing she had ever wanted while it happened, and could never have it again!","He wrote it into her Dreams as a thing that had always been true.","And the Descendants of THE Sleepless Fiend roared as their Existence fought against their Dreams!","They shockingly began to come apart! The dreams Noah had written and the records they were made of could not both stand, and no existence can hold two truths at its own foundation, and the disagreement ran outward from the center of each of them, a crack finding every edge at once!","Effectively, he had fucked around with their Trueness as for beings of high Dimensionality, their Trueness was critical!","Atlas had talked about DEPTH, MAGNITUDE, and AGREEMENT when it came to the power of lifeforms.","The Depths were their Dimensionality as theirs were higher than his, and Agreement with existence was heavy, but theit MAGNITUDE...he fractured it inside out.","| You are overwriting the Existential Narrative of nine Descendants. Their dreams and their records no longer agree. An existence at war with its own story cannot hold its shape.|","Voss clutched his head and howled at a betrayal that had never happened. The winged rider forgot the lie of its wings and fell. The plain-horse rider dismounted, slowly, and sat down in the silk, certain it was already dead and merely waiting to notice.","And the leader dropped the sword.","The weapon carrying a sliver of power of an Immense One fell through the silk and its terrible song went quiet, because the hand that held it no longer knew whether it had ever wanted the thing it was fighting for!","She clutched at her own chest and found there the memory Noah had written, of having had it, of having missed it, and her crimson eyes went wide and wet and utterly lost!","\"I just wanted him to look at me...did I really miss it? Did I truly?! \"","...!","A crack ran up through the old bronze of her body. The white stag beneath her screamed as its rider’s Narrative tore, and the whole wedge was breaking now, nine titans going mad as their records ripped away from one another, madness blooming in a place made of the very concept of dreams.","Storms of Argent Loom and typhoons of Dimensionality began to rage around them as weaker Lifeforms would be shredded if they came nearby!","Noah hung above them, bleeding from three wounds as he did not derive any pleasure from this!","A day ago he might have enjoyed it. Today, with Sonder awake in him, he saw each of the nine fully as he unmade them, saw the whole vivid interior of nine existences that had each stood at the center of a long story, and he broke them anyway!","Because they had opposed his grsnd and infinite dream, and he had promised himself he would come out standing.","But even now, his eyes flashed coldly as he thought about everything.","It was about their Father.","These were the First Borns of THE Sleepless Fiend, one of Those Who Remain. They could see many things.","He could not leave the broken dreams of nine of the Fiend’s children lying in the Chrysalis for anything to find.","\"Against terrifying enemies, I have to be careful ,\" Noah said quietly, to the falling silk, to himself.","\"I put my hand heavily into an Immense One’s bloodline today as I have been doing recently, altering their Curses or Sentences. That leaves marks and clues. And I cannot afford to leave clues to such cruel beings.\"","He looked at the nine, mad and splitting, their dreams hanging around them in torn golden clouds, and he made a grand decision.","\" So there will be no evidence.\"","He opened THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer, and for the first time in his existence, he... devoured dreams.","He bypassed the Dimensional storms and drew the torn golden clouds off the nine dying Descendants and into himself, every hope and every dream these nine had ever carried, and he took them in and shut them behind his eyes where nothing that looked at the Chrysalis afterward would ever find them!","Emptied of the dreams their existences had been at war with, the Descendants went quiet. Then they went still. Then, one by one, with nothing left at their foundations to hold a shape, they simply ceased, and their whole burning Steeds ceased with them, and the region went dark and cold!","| You have devoured the Existential Narrative of nine Descendants and Steeds of THE Sleepless Fiend. No dream remains for any perceiver to read. In them, the event did not happen.|","|THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer deepens. You have learned to take what you long only borrowed. +5 PROVENANCE, +3 VERITAS, +3 PONDUS|","Noah hung in the silence, bleeding, full of dead dreams, and he did not feel grand.","He felt careful!","He looked down. The three bound Dream Gu drifted free of their fallen ropes now that their captors were gone, and the little Common Dream Gu he had first come for still hung in its nest, awake, its many eyes on him, its small dream of warmth turning around it untouched by any of it. Four Gu!","His gains from this were grand, grander by far than what he had come for!","He didn’t sit and dawdle!","He debated taking the vibrant binding ropes or the sword filled with slivers of an Immense One as he was not foolish enough to carry things holding the marker and power of an Immense One! But could they be seamlessly devoured and broken down? He formed a bubble of blue gold dreams to wrap around them as he tried to analyze and devour even them rapidly.","He formed his Provenance of THE Human Dreamer into chains that wrapped around the Gu and drew the four of them to him, and golden jaws of an endless dream erupted out as they began to chew on the corpses of Descendants and Steeds that floated listlessly!","And...","Caution said do not linger. Caution said a place where you have just done something this large is a place to be gone from before anything arrives to read it!","For once, Noah did not argue with caution as he turned into a streak of light shooting in the distance, every step taking him Gigaparsecs away as he even intended to leave the region of Dreams of THE Chrysalis entirely!","Noah streaked across the vast reaches of THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering, each stride carrying him across gigaparsecs of falling multicolored silk and turning nebulas as dreamy light swirled steadily around his frame. Floating beside him, encased in a shimmering sphere of blue-gold dreams, drifted the spoils of the First Borns.","The obsidian rope and the pale crimson-white sword.","As his perception probed the sealed sphere, information surfaced in his consciousness, revealing the dark history woven into the very structure of the relics.","| THE UNSLEEPING BINDINGS|","|Classification: Immense One Relic (Defective Echo).|","|An obsidian rope braided from the harvested Causes of ten primeval Steeds who failed to bear the harness of THE Sleepless Fiend. It carries the unfinished cadence of his binding-sentence, burning through the unspent potential of captured existences to enforce an unyielding stillness.|","| THE FIRST BORN’S TOOTH|","|Classification: Immense One Relic (Severed Gaze).|","|One of nine blades carved from a crystallized fragment of THE Sleepless Fiend’s own peripheral sight. Forged so his eldest progeny could observe across the Folds of existence on his behalf, it perceives across THE SEAM and severs lifeforms. It has never been drawn by its creator.|","Noah kept moving, his eyes analyzing the dark script drifting within the blue-gold bubble.","\" What happens if I devour the Narrative of an Immense One?\" Noah asked, directing his thought into the illusory ring resting against his finger. \" Consuming the Existential Narrative of nine Descendants granted an increase of Provenance and deepened my standing across multiple metrics. What would a weapon carrying the sliver of an architect yield?\"","The ring took its toll, drawing a fraction of his authority.","|-0.1 PROVENANCE ESSENCE|","The records-cluster within the illusory band vibrated with sharp, derisive amusement.","|It yields an early burial, O Chance of Chances.|","Atlas’s words arrived flat and dry, stripped of any theatrical warmth.","| Do not confuse a sentence with the mouth that spoke it. Those nine First Borns were Descendants. They carried blood, instructions, and borrowed weight, but their Existential Narrative belonged to them alone. When you ate their dreams, you consumed a branch. It made you heavier, and because their depth was within your reach, you could digest that shit without choking.|","|These relics are entirely different. They carry fragments of the Weave itself. The Dimensionality of an Immense One is not a higher tier of what you hold, it is a completely separate cloth. If you attempt to swallow a sliver of the Fiend’s actual Narrative, your Provenance will not absorb it. You cannot digest it. The conceptual mass will sit inside your foundation as a jagged wedge of iron, tearing through your inner architecture while it radiates across every fold of existence.|","|It is poison that glows in the dark. It paints your entire presence in blinding phosphorescence, shouting to him as he is listening across the expanse: hey, I am right here. Trash them as quickly as possible. Drop them into the silk and keep moving.|","...!","Noah thought for a moment before he sighed.","With a single flick of his will, the blue-gold dream bubble dissolved.","The obsidian bindings and the pale crimson blade fell away, tumbling into the endless cascade of falling silk. They drifted down into the deep, turbulent nebulas of the Chrysalis, their lingering weight swallowed by the timeless expanse as Noah accelerated away without looking back once.","He continued to move for minutes, crossing unmeasured expanses of the conceptual domain. Caution was not cowardice, it was simply the prerequisite for continuing to exist! He had been far too tyrannical for his own good recently as he...was Quintessential, but he was not invincible!","As he traversed the thinning drift of silk, his chest resonated. THE Dreamer’s Scale hummed with a quiet, steady frequency, attuning his perception to the subtle shifts in the surrounding medium.","Ahead, resting beneath the shade of a petrified conceptual bough, another soft luminescence caught his eye.","It was another Common Dream Gu.","This one was slightly smaller, translucent azure ripples pulsing through its rounded shell as it lazily filtered the ambient concept of dreams. Sensing the resonance of THE Dreamer’s Scale, the small creature did not scatter. It simply drifted, regarding him with calm, multifaceted eyes.","Noah reached out, letting a strand of blue-gold dream essence curl around the creature. It nestled against his palm, accepting the warmth, and he drew it into his internal realm alongside the four others.","Most of them truly seemed to exist with nature as they showed no aggression. These insects were wondrous things!","At this time, the architecture of THE Chrysalis began to shift.","The falling silk thinned until it vanished entirely. The dry nebulas of the Dream region receded into the distance, replaced by a sudden, overwhelming moisture that was not water, but liquid starlight.","The surroundings opened into a vast cosmic ocean.","Waves of deep violet and shimmering silver rolled across millions of Gigaparsecs, surging with the heavy concepts of Weight and Memory. Immense phosphorescent currents drifted through the depths, illuminating vast oceanic trenches carved from crystallized epochs. It was an aquatic expanse of raw stellar essence, where the pressure of ancient records pressed down with the weight of uncounted stars.","In the distance, suspended within a slow-moving whirlpool of golden light, floated a colossal mountain-reef. It stretched for thousands of miles, built from petrified stellar coral, calcified bone of forgotten leviathans, and dense mineral crusts that absorbed the rolling currents.","Noah descended through the shimmering waves without causing a ripple, diving deep into the interior of the floating reef. He slipped into a cavernous hollow shielded by thick layers of fossilized coral and crystalline stone.","He exhaled, the tension that had gripped his body since the descent of THE Unpaid Collector finally receding into a cold, steady equilibrium.","Inside his Provenance Realm, five Common Dream Gu hovered in a gentle spiral around the central river of light. Their soft luminescence mingled with the blue-gold hills, their small dreams of warmth and peace adding a subtle, stabilizing tranquility to the sovereign domain.","He summoned his status.","|VERITAS: 108|","|PROVENANCE: 115|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 104|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 135|","His attributes held firm in the Seam, anchored by the weight of nine devoured Narratives and the unspent Causes he had claimed.","The illusory band on his finger pulsed with renewed clarity, the presence of Atlas resonating within the quiet sanctuary of the reef.","| This place should be THE Tide,| Atlas said, his tone carrying the calm assurance of someone stepping into his own forge. | Weight and Memory govern this water. It blunts stray perceptions and dampens the tremors of the outside continuum. Nothing should interrupt us here.|","Noah looked down at his palm, where the very first Common Dream Gu he had found, the clean one that dreamed only of being left alone in the warmth, manifested in a soft coil of blue-gold light.","| Take the little one ,| Atlas said, the records-cluster humming with anticipation. | The one that wished for warmth. We are going to teach it how to be an Elseengine heart.|","WAA!","Noah looked at the small lifeform resting quietly against his skin. It had simple Dreams. He would incorporate it into his grand and Infinite Dream!"]},{"number":5715,"title":"Chapter 5715: Chapter 5714: Sleepless! I","paragraphs":["<THE SLEEPLESS FIEND>","In the quiet spaces of a closed room, lifeforms placed behind curved glass will always establish a routine.","They wake, they swim along the transparent perimeter, they consume whatever flakes of nourishment drift down from the ceiling, and they believe the curved boundary of their water is the edge of all reality.","They engage in tiny, frantic conflicts over an inch of sand. They breed their progeny to believe that the illumination above them is an eternal constant, never realizing that the hand turning the light on and off belongs to something standing outside their sky.","It is a predictable cycle, observed with detached curiosity by anyone standing tall enough to peer through the glass.","In this vast, silent chamber, there were hundreds of such vessels.","They did not hold minnows or aquatic insects. Each floating enclosure was a self-contained Dimension, carefully anchored against the surrounding dark, with more than half engineered as hidden Elsedimensions folded away from the standard patterns of the continuum.","And the creatures moving inside them were Descendants, entities standing at THE SEAM or towering even higher, lifeforms whose bloodlines carried uncounted eras of unbroken authority, pacing along the transparent boundaries of their artificial skies without ever perceiving the room they occupied.","They even thought they left their Dimension to cross endless darkness and enter other Dimensions...but they did not know they only ever remained in one enclosure.","At the center of these floating glass domains sat a hazy, colossal humanoid figure.","He did not possess a body of mortal clay or dense bone. The silhouette was composed of constantly pulsing strands of brilliance, undulating threads of the Weave that twisted with quiet, immense authority.","This was THE SLEEPLESS FIEND.","Before him rested a wide, shallow dish carved from crystallized void.","Within the dish, pinned down by needles of solid law, writhed a chimeric lifeform!","It was an unnatural synthesis, woven from the boundless currents of Infinity, the raw genesis of THE Primordial Source, and the rigid geometric threads of THE Argent Loom. The creature had no unified identity, only an agony of incompatible foundations, its Dimensionality surging outward in violent, miniature typhoons that broke uselessly against the lip of the petri dish.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND held a slender needle between two fingers of woven brilliance. At the needle’s tip clung a single drop of pitch-black ink, dense with the weight of sovereign records.","With cold, surgical precision, he pressed the needle into the chimera’s heaving flank. Sentences of pure intent flowed from the ink into the creature’s marrow, carving order into the chaotic blend of authorities.","\" This is merely the integration of measly small authorities,\" the Fiend murmured.","\"A little Infinity to stretch the boundaries, a drop of the Source to fuel the combustion, and the Loom to ensure the structure remembers its place. With enough Narrative and a few Causes to bind the seams, you will be stabilized. Cease your noise. An existence that cannot endure a little editing has no right to step outside the glass.\"","The chimeric beast twisted, its conceptual shrieks rippling through the dish, but the Fiend did not press harder or withdraw. He simply held the needle steady until the ink settled into the flesh, watching the authorities cease their violent rejection of one another.","He did not hate the things he molded. Hatred was an unnecessary expenditure of kinetic energy, and an architect who had outlasted epochs had no use for pointless heat. Existence was an unfinished architecture, full of loose threads and unstable foundations, and someone had to sit in the dark and test which joints could bear the weight of what was to come.","He lifted the needle, letting the chimera rest in its newly stitched skin.","Then, the strands of brilliance that formed his visage shifted.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND blinked!","His luminous eyes closed, the endless pulse of his form steadying for a fraction of an instant. Within the vast expanse of his awareness, a faint vibration ceased. It was not a physical sound, but the sudden absence of nine particular frequencies atop other 9 that had been tethered to his lineage!","\" Curious ,\" he said softly to the quiet room.","He opened his eyes, tilting his head slightly.","\" Thpse sent out to gather weavings in the silk...their sentences have ended.\"","He sat in contemplation, tracing the faint echoes along the Weave.","\" Not crushed by superior mass, and not broken by another architect. Not a scrap of their Existential Narrative remains for the cloth to remember. Who did they encounter in the dark?\"","He tapped the uninked end of the needle against the rim of the dish.","\" THE Chrysalis is a bit scary with those things left behind by that monster watching everything, so I cannot do too much. But... a little punishment across a tiny region where they died should be fine.\"","He set the needle down upon the table of void.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND did not summon a weapon. He did not gather energy or prepare an incantation.","At the tier of Those Who Remain, power was not an accumulation of kinetic force. It was the absolute imposition of one’s Existential Narrative upon the fabric of reality.","He was THE SLEEPLESS FIEND. His entire existence was defined by an unbroken, eternal vigil, an identity that had forgotten how to close its eyes since before the First Sundering. His Narrative was an endless, suffocating weight of wakefulness, exhaustion denied, and consciousness forced to witness every passing epoch without reprieve.","He raised a single finger of woven brilliance and touched the empty air.","He did not look into THE Chrysalis. He simply selected the coordinates where the threads of his nine Descendants had vanished, and he wrote a short paragraph of his own existence directly into the localized Seam.","A mandate of pure, incurable insomnia.","The concept parted from his fingertip, slipping seamlessly through the dimensions, bypassing the physical folds of space, and anchoring itself into the conceptual bedrock of the distant region of the Chrysalis.","Having delivered the sentence, he did not wait to observe the execution.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND stretched his luminous arms and let out a long, slow yawn, the strands of his jaw parting in weary indifference!","He turned his gaze toward another floating glass sphere, where thousands of young Descendants moved across pale cities, entirely unaware of their father’s presence.","\" Now I have to send more out,\" he murmured, the light of his eyes dimming slightly in boredom. \" Dreams are the one thing that always leave a good taste on a sleepless existence.\"","---","Countless gigaparsecs away, within the boundless folds of THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering, the silence broke in unfathomably small corners of this place.","If one could pull their perception backward, looking across the vast expanse that encompassed the falling silk of the Dream region, the neighboring boundary of THE Tide with its rolling seas of stellar light, and the drifting continental fragments between them, the change appeared as an instantaneous infection of the continuum.","The mandate of THE SLEEPLESS FIEND descended!","It fell across millions of cubic gigaparsecs as a suffocating blight of pure conceptual rot!","The phenomenon struck directly at the living concepts inhabiting the region.","In an instant, billions of years of accumulated sleeplessness crashed into every entity drifting through the expanse!","The Dream Gu, creatures born to drift in gentle, half-lidded reverie, suddenly found their interior golden weather turning ash-grey. Their multifaceted eyes were forced wide open by an inescapable, agonizing alertness. They could not dream. They could not rest. An epoch of ceaseless, exhausting consciousness flooded their simple existences within a fraction of a second!","Their translucent bodies shriveled, the soft curves of their carapaces cracking into dry, brittle husks. From within the endless falling silk, thousands of Gu began to emit shrill, soundless shrieks of conceptual agony, their Trueness fracturing under the weight of an exhaustion their foundations were never engineered to bear.","In the adjacent reaches of THE Tide, the stellar water turned dark and turbid.","Aquatic Gu, ancient leviathans of petrified coral, and floating colonies of conceptual organisms writhed in sudden torment. Diseases of existence broke across their forms, lesions of corrupt memory and rotted weight festering in their carapaces. Entire ecosystems of living law withered in moments, collapsing into stagnant detritus!","It was a quiet extinction, executed by an architect who had not even bothered to watch where his finger fell.","And deep within the outer reefs of THE Tide, inside a hollow cavern of fossilized coral, Noah sat with a single Common Dream Gu resting upon his open palm, his mind focused on guiding its gentle pulse into the heart of an Elseengine, when the sudden tremor of an unraveling sky crashed down upon the sea!"]},{"number":5716,"title":"Chapter 5716: Chapter 5715: Sleepless! II","paragraphs":["<THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering>","The fossilized coral cavern was quiet, shielded beneath thousands of leagues of dense, petrified reef as the deep currents of THE Tide rolled steadily overhead.","In the center of the hollow, Noah sat with his legs crossed upon a slab of compressed starlight. Resting upon his open palm, the Common Dream Gu pulsed with a soft, golden rhythm. Its translucent shell breathed in slow intervals, radiating a quiet reverie of warmth and gentle drift that soothed the surrounding air.","Floating within Noah’s internal realm, eight foundational elements hummed in alignment, waiting for the spark that would bind them to a living center.","Atlas’s voice echoed through the illusory ring, calm and instructive.","| The process requires absolute precision, O Chance of Chances. You are not killing the insect. You are not hollowing out its consciousness. You are extending your Provenance into its core, aligning its native law with the Elseengine until its small dream becomes the heartbeat of the domain. It must trust the warmth you offer, or the vessel will reject the weld.|","Noah drew upon a thread of blue-gold dream essence, letting it wrap around the small Gu in a protective mantle. The creature leaned into the contact, its multifaceted eyes softening as it prepared to surrender its concept to the architecture of the ring.","Then, at such a pivotal juncture, the ocean stopped moving.","The rolling currents of THE Tide froze in mid-drift. The deep hum of the fossilized reef cut out entirely, replaced by a sudden, total vacuum of sound that made the conceptual marrow of Noah’s bones ache with instant tension!","Above the reef, through the thousands of leagues of stellar water and across the distant expanse of the Chrysalis, something fell!","The descent carried no kinetic weight and no shower of falling meteors, arriving instead as an instantaneous infection of the continuum, a cold and suffocating decree that sank straight through the Seam and struck the bedrock of the region!","HUUM!","The water of THE Tide turned turbid and grey, festering with an unnatural, sickening stillness.","CRACK!","The Common Dream Gu upon Noah’s palm went rigid.","Its soft, golden interior weather vanished in a fraction of an instant, replaced by an ash-grey pallor. Its multifaceted eyes snapped wide open, dilating until they nearly tore through its translucent carapace. A shrill, soundless shriek ripped from the creature’s existence as its small, rounded body shriveled, cracking down the center until it was turned to a dry, brittle husk.","Before Noah could withdraw his authority, the decree reached into the cavern and gripped his own existence!","|WARNING.|","|The localized continuum has been infected by an Immense One’s sentence.|","|Existential Mandate: ETERNAL INSOMNIA.|","|Slumber is revoked. Reverie is severed. Consciousness is forced into an unbroken, infinite vigil across all folds.|","Existence vanished behind a blinding, jagged haze of absolute lucidity.","The attack was flooding his existence with a terrifying, suffocating rush of pure, forced wakefulness that crashed straight into the core of his soul.","Billions of years of accumulated purposefully made exhaustive sleeplessness poured into his mind in a single microsecond!","Billions of years!","He had only been alive for decades!","His eyes, already bright with the light of Sonder, flared with an incandescent, agonizing glare that threatened to incinerate his retinas. The concepts of rest, stillness, recovery, and quiet surrender were violently stripped from his consciousness, burned away by a relentless, crushing pressure that forced every perception, every thought, and every memory to stand at absolute attention amplified with exhaustion. The feeling of being so tired and hoping to give up and face endless darkness, but you couldnt!","Epochs of exhausting, ceaseless consciousness hammered against his sanity. His thoughts accelerated beyond control, grinding against one another with the heat of colliding Dimensions, unable to cycle down, unable to drift, unable to find a single moment of shade in an endless, blistering desert of awareness.","For THE Human Dreamer, whose very power was rooted in the fluid, boundless architecture of his humanity, the mandate struck at his foundational root.","His dream state fractured.","The gentle, undulating rivers of light within his Provenance Realm began to boil, turning into turbulent currents of jagged light. The blue-gold hills cracked open, bleeding pale steam as the concept of the Waking Dream was violently rejected by the suffocating insomnia choking the surroundings.","Noah fell to his knees against the coral slab.","Blood, thick and shimmering with stellar gold, dripped from his nostrils and the corners of his eyes, hissing as it struck the petrified stone. His fingers dug into the rock, gouging deep trenches into the calcified crust as his body trembled violently under the strain!","He could not breathe out. He could not find the rhythm of his own heart. Every nerve in his frame felt pulled taut across the surface of a dying star, stretched until the fibers groaned beneath the weight of an exhaustive eternity without sleep!","The decree was never aimed at him in particular, arriving merely as a casual flick of a distant finger, a minor punishment tossed out, yet it carried enough conceptual gravity to tear his Trueness apart from the inside out.","Within the illusory ring, an engineer vibrated violently, the voice of Atlas cutting through the deafening roar of Noah’s forced consciousness.","| Hold on to your foundation.|","| Do not fight the wakefulness by trying to sleep. You cannot sleep beneath the sentence of THE SLEEPLESS FIEND. He has forgotten how to close his eyes since before Existence was divided, and his mandate will crush any existence that tries to curl into a ball.|","Noah gritted his teeth. The pain inside his skull was absolute, an iron spike driven white-hot through the center of his thoughts, preventing even a microsecond of peace.","|A lifeform that has never broken believes it is made of solid stone. A lifeform that has had its marrow fractured, its thoughts burned, and its foundation hammered against the anvil of an architect knows the exact pressure the sky can exert before it bends. Pain is not an ending, O Chance of Chances. Pain is the continuum informing you of where your edges end.|","The ancient engineer’s words crashed into Noah’s suffering as an undeniable structural truth!","| Those who break beneath the friction are swept into the dust of forgotten folds. But those who can hold their shape while the heat strips their skin force the continuum to make room for them. Persevere, Dreamer. Persevere, and show this dead sky that a human does not need permission to exist.|","Persevere.","The word echoed in the depths of Noah’s burning mind, carrying the distant memory of an obsidian journal and the unyielding stubbornness of mortals who had dared to walk among giants.","He was THE True Human Emperor. He was THE Human Dreamer. He had cast out borrowed authorities, forged his own Provenance from nothing, and declared himself the protagonist of his own endless journey.","He would not be snuffed out by a thing that he had not even seen!","Noah raised his head, his pupils burning through the blinding haze of exhaustive insomnia with a cold, terrifying ferocity.","If the mandate demanded exhaustive eternal wakefulness, he would not cower and beg for sleep.","He would be awake.","He would take the ceaseless, agonizing consciousness that threatened to shatter his mind, and he would harness it to drive his own immensity!","HUUM!","Within his core, THE Telos of Adversity roared to life, burning with his Provenance!","The concept of struggle, the immutable law that pressure must forge density, erupted through his Existence. Alongside it, THE Telos of Existence and THE Telos of Tyranny aligned, locking together within his chest.","Noah opened the gates of his Provenance.","Instead of shielding himself from the Fiend’s mandate, he dragged the suffocating insomnia directly into his Telos of Adversity, feeding the conceptual rot into the furnace of his own sovereign laws.","The agony reached an unimaginable peak. His conceptual flesh tore, his veins blackened with the phantom exhaustion of billions of years, and the sheer trauma of the ordeal etched jagged, irreversible scars into the core of his foundation!","He paid for every second in raw, agonizing friction, his Veritas and Pondus groaning beneath the immense burden!","Yet, as the fire burned through his impurities, his foundation did not collapse.","It hardened.","|THE Telos of Adversity consumes the sovereign pressure of an Immense One’s sentence.|","|Your Provenance absorbs the trauma of ETERNAL INSOMNIA while never touching any semblance of the Narrative of an Immense One.|","| The concept of reverie is tempered in the forge of absolute wakefulness. Your Provenance is tempered in the wake of this exhaustion. If you can Dream even in this state, your dreams will be unfathomably grand ones.|","|VERITAS: 110 (+2)|","|PONDUS: 108 (+4)|","|PROVENANCE: 116 (+1)|","The blinding white haze gradually receded from his sight, leaving behind a cold, crystalline clarity that settled into the depths of his eyes.","The pain remained, a deep, phantom ache throbbing in the core of his thoughts, a permanent scar marking the day an architect tried to erase his right to dream. But Noah remained on his feet.","He slowly rose from the stone slab.","Around him, the hollow cavern bore the horrific evidence of the descent. The surrounding reef was drained of color, the fossilized coral brittle and crumbling, while outside in the depths of THE Tide, millions of leagues of stellar water festered in dark, diseased stillness. The mandate was still active, radiating across the Chrysalis, an active poison in the water!","Yet within the hollow, Noah stood upright.","His pristine body was marked by lines of dried golden blood, his dark hair disheveled, but his presence radiated an immovable weight that defied the rot pressing against the stone walls.","Atlas fell silent for a long moment, the illusory ring pulsing with a rare, quiet reverence.","| The mandate will linger in this region for cycles before the Chrysalis washes it clean. We must depart for a deeper fold. To engineer here while the air is poisoned will not be ideal.|","Noah looked down at his palm.","The Common Dream Gu lay curled in a tight, brittle ball, its carapace cracked, trembling violently beneath the ambient pressure of the insomnia that still choked the cavern. It was moments away from complete conceptual collapse.","Noah gently lowered his hand, his scarred, unyielding dream essence flowing outward, wrapping the small insect in a fortress of tempered warmth. Under his sovereign shelter, the Gu’s frantic trembling slowed, its fractured shell stabilizing beneath his absolute care.","Noah looked toward the dark, festering waters of THE Tide, his gaze steady and devoid of fear.","\" The pressure here is heavy. The adversity is real. That makes it... the perfect forge.\"","...!","He placed the stabilized Dream Gu back into the center of his palm, his blue-gold pupils locking onto the small lifeform.","\"In the midst of this adversity, I will complete my first Engineering!\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5717,"title":"Chapter 5717: Chapter 5716: Ring!","paragraphs":["The grey conceptual rot of ETERNAL INSOMNIA beat against the fossilized coral walls of the cavern, a relentless tide of forced lucidity seeking any crack in the stone to pour through!","Noah sat in the center of the hollow slab, his breathing steady, his pupils fixed on the fragile creature resting upon his palm.","The mandate demanded that all things wake with endless exhaustion. It demanded an endless, blistered vigil that stripped away reverie and pulverized thought into ash. Against an ordinary existence, the phantom weight of billions of years of exhaustive sleeplessness would have burned out the thoughts within seconds.","Noah was not ordinary!","Within his chest, his blood surged.","Infinite Sanguine Mana roared!","It did not trickle or flow in measured streams. A boundless, crimson-gold torrent erupted through his body, cycling across his entire physiology at the speed of thought. Millions of cycles completed in a single breath, each wave carrying the unyielding vitality of his boundless reservoir. Whenever the cold, numbing exhaustion of the Fiend’s sentence tried to settle into his nerves, the crimson flood washed it clean, meeting infinite fatigue with infinite brilliance.","He was tired, the deep phantom ache of epochs still throbbing in the core of his foundation, but his immensity was inexhaustible.","With his vitality anchored, Noah closed his eyes and began to dream.","THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM unfolded within his consciousness. He did not dream of an escape, nor did he dream of comfort. He dreamed an infinite dream of an unfindable domain, a sovereign vessel folded so deeply into THE SEAM that the gaze of an architect would slide across its surface without catching a single thread.","He drew upon his Provenance Essence. Blue-gold light welled from his fingertips, soft and deliberate, curling around the Common Dream Gu.","The small creature shuddered, its cracked carapace cooling as Noah’s dream insulated it from the ambient poison.","Atlas’s voice resonated from the illusory band.","|Now, O Chance of Chances. The foundation is already drawn. Fuse the insect’s law to the core.|","Noah did not hesitateas within his internal realm, nine golden droplets condensed from the unspent potential he had harvested, Distilled Cause Essence flowing down into his palm. He did not force the liquid into the Gu as food. He guided the golden drops into the seams of its translucent shell, letting the distilled potential fuse with its native concept of dreams.","The Gu’s heartbeat slowed, steadying as it drank the essence. Its small, pure dream of warmth and peaceful drift began to expand, shifting from a fleeting reverie into an engine that could generate its own localized weavings.","It was becoming an Elseengine.","| The elements, | Atlas said. | Strict order. Let nothing else touch the lattice.|","From his sovereign reserves, Noah summoned the eight pure particles of stellar matter.","Hydrogen first. A cold mist of primordial atoms wrapped around the Gu, setting the initial boundary of combustion.","Helium followed, stabilizing the reaction into an unbroken, slow-burning mantle.","Lithium condensed next, forming a light, resilient crystalline skeleton that bound the two gases to the Gu’s shell.","Outside the reef, the pressure of the mandate surged. The dark water of THE Tide churned as the Fiend’s sentence deepened its grip on the Chrysalis. The conceptual weight pressed through the coral, bearing down on Noah’s shoulders like an inverted mountain range. His teeth ground together as the friction tore at his ribs, but his hands never shook!","He took the pressure into his Telos of Adversity, converting the crushing hostility of the sky into fuel for his own concentration.","|You endure the prolonged pressure of an Immense One’s sentence while conducting sovereign engineering.|","|Your foundation tempers under adverse weight.|","|VERITAS: 111 (+1)|","|PONDUS: 110 (+2)|","Noah kept his focus locked on the microscopic architecture before him.","Beryllium layered over the lithium, establishing the rigid structural channels that would direct the internal space.","Boron integrated immediately after, absorbing stray conceptual heat and preventing the expanding interior from detonating the shell.","Europium settled into the lattice, a dense, glowing phosphorescence that gave the boundary its ability to absorb outside observation.","Strontium locked into the perimeter, lending structural memory to the metal so that no external strike could warp its shape!","And finally, Neodymium. The magnetic sovereign, drawing all eight layers inward with an inescapable, self-contained attraction.","The eight elements snapped into alignment around the Common Dream Gu.","HUUM!","The insect exhaled. A soft, golden breath rippled out from its multifaceted eyes, and the expanded lattice suddenly compressed. Space folded upon itself. The cavern seemed to tilt as thousands of leagues of conceptual volume collapsed inward, shrinking down, condensing into a dense, solid weight that rested quietly upon Noah’s outstretched palm.","The light cleared.","Resting upon his skin was a ring.","It was not forged of common gold or rough iron. The band was composed of deep, star-flecked obsidian intertwined with pale azure coral, its surface smooth as polished starlight. Orbiting within the interior rim of the band were eight microscopic planetary rings of elemental luminescence, turning in silent, perpetual motion.","At the ring’s apex rested a clear, amber cabochon.","Suspended within that amber heart, floating in peaceful, unbothered reverie, was the Common Dream Gu. Its translucent body was whole once more, pulsing with a gentle, golden glow, completely shielded from the horrors of the outside continuum as it served as the living heartbeat of the pocket dimension folded within the band.","Crisp prompts ignited across Noah’s sight!","| SOVEREIGN ENGINEERING COMPLETED.|","|You have successfully forged a Provenance Elsedimension Relic.|","|Name: THE ENDURING GU ELSEDIMENSION RING|","|Heart: Common Dream Gu (Living Elseengine).|","|Classification: Tier 1 Gu Elsedimension Relic (Unique).|","|Inherent Boons:|","|+20 PROVENANCE, +20 VERITAS, +20 PONDUS.|","|Sovereignty of Reverie: The wearer’s mind is anchored by the dream of the Elseengine heart. Total immunity to mental exhaustion and perception-reading originating from lifeforms at or below THE SEAM.|","| Paramount Feature: EXISTENTIAL NARRATIVE DISPLACEMENT.|","|Description: A rare property forged through the convergence of an infinite dream, adverse pressure, and sovereign will. The ring constantly monitors the surrounding Weave. The moment an enemy authority capable of completely overshadowing your existence emerges, the ring triggers instantly before catastrophic harm can land, displacing your existence across unknown distances and unpredictable trajectories into the deep folds of THE SEAM.|","...!","Noah looked down at the ring, the prompts burning brightly in the dim cavern.","He lifted his hand and slipped the band onto his middle finger.","It clicked into place, resizing seamlessly until it rested flush against his skin. The instant it made contact, a deep, cool stability rushed through his meridians. The throbbing ache in his skull smoothed over, blunted by the serene dream humming within the amber core.","The phantom fatigue of the Fiend’s sentence receded into the distance, unable to touch him anymore!","Noah stared at his hand.","For the first time since THE Unpaid Collector had filled the sky above Vasileia, for the first time since Provenance Lifeforms had been extinguished like candles and Aurelius’s twelfth stand had broken into blood, Noah felt a solid floor beneath his feet.","He was still vastly outmatched by the monsters that walked the Weave. He still could not face an Immense One in open combat. But he was no longer naked in their sight!","He had taken a tangible, calculated step toward ensuring that when a sky chose to fall on him, he would not simply have to stand there and die.","At this moment, the ring on his hand actually pulsed as a humanoid form emerged before him!","An illusory form of a grand and glorious engineer!","And uniquely his entire body was covered in a haze of strands and immensity as his features could not be clearly seen apart from the idea that he was looking at someone extremely old.","The illusory projection of Atlas materialized beside him, arms crossed, gazing down at the ring on Noah’s finger.","The ancient engineer was silent for several breaths, his eyes tracing the eight elemental orbits turning within the band.","| Somewhat impressive for a novice working in a poisoned reef, O Chance of Chances,| Atlas said, his tone dry, carrying none of the awe the finished relic deserved. | You did not botch the weld, and the displacement property is a decent roll of the dice. But that is all it is.|","Atlas looked up, his gaze piercing through the stone ceiling toward the dark, festering waters of THE Tide.","| Existence is too vast, Dreamer. You forged a trinket that lets you scurry away from a descending foot, that is all. Even a genius like me, who mapped Existence and engineered domains that made the architects grind their teeth, could not attain what I wanted.|","The old man turned his eyes back to Noah, cold and unyielding.","|If even I could not achieve what I wanted, and I could move amongst Immense Ones without being one... what do you think your chances are?|","\"...\"","Noah did not answer.","He did not offer an arrogant defense, and he did not justify his path. He simply stood in the quiet cavern, his obsidian pupils calm, his hand resting steady at his side as the prompts reflecting his finalized progress settled before his eyes.","|You have fully withstood the initial descent of an Immense One’s sentence.|","|Your foundation solidifies permanently under the trial.|","|VERITAS: 113 (+2)|","|PROVENANCE: 118 (+2)|","|PONDUS: 112 (+2)|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 155 (+20)|","|The crafting of an unfindable relic alters the probability of your survival.|","Noah summoned his complete status, the numbers arranging themselves in plain, stark alignment.","| STATUS PANEL: NOAH OSMONT|","|Identity: THE True Human Emperor / THE Human Dreamer|","|VERITAS: 133 (113 + 20)|","|PROVENANCE: 138 (118 + 20)|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 132 (112 + 20)|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 155|","The blue-gold numbers shone against the dim coral, steady and undeniable!","Noah lowered his hand.","The mandate still raged outside in the dark waters, but inside the hollow, THE True Human Emperor held boundless thoughts and dreams of what he needed to do next!"]},{"number":5718,"title":"Chapter 5718: Chapter 5717: Foundation! I","paragraphs":["The amber cabochon on the ring gleamed with quiet, self-contained warmth, and Noah sat within the hollow cavern of petrified coral while the dark waters of THE Tide pressed against the stone outside.","He turned his hand, watching the eight microscopic elemental orbits spin in perpetual alignment within the star-flecked band. The Common Dream Gu inside the core breathed in a calm, rhythmic cycle, its tiny reverie anchored against the crushing pressure of the exterior mandate.","A dry, scraping voice vibrated from the illusory ring beside it.","| Hmm|","It was a small sound, entirely devoid of warmth.","| Look at you ,| Atlas said. | Staring at a foundation casing as if you just invented the wheel. That is an Incipient Tier vessel , Dreamer. The absolute floor of Engineered Existential Relics . You took a common insect with barely enough wits to seek warmth, wrapped it in basic elemental tin, and bolted a door shut. Acceptable work for a novice who had an architect breathing down his neck, but do not start naming stars after yourself.|","Noah did not take offense. He kept his eyes on the amber core, feeling the steady thrum of twenty points in Provenance, Veritas, and Pondus settling into his meridians.","\" What are the tiers,\" Noah said. \" If this is the floor, where does the ceiling sit?\"","|-0.1 PROVENANCE ESSENCE|","The ring took its toll, and Atlas gave a short grunt before answering.","| Engineered Existential Relics follow the depth of existence. What you wear on your finger is an Incipient Vessel. Tier One. You take a Common Gu, bind it to an Elseengine, and forge an isolated room. It gave you basic displacement, minor reinforcement, and a closet to hide your skin.|","The ring hummed with faint, cold clarity as the old man continued.","| Above that sit Sovereign Reliquaries. Tier Two. For those, you do not use common cattle. You hunt Rare Gu, creatures that condensed around the shed fragments of departed sovereigns and carry their own stubborn judgment. You do not just build a room with a Rare Gu; you build a contradiction. A sovereign relic that illuminates the hidden threads of the Weave. A blade that severs an enemy’s historical Records and Causes rather than their flesh. Armaments that do not merely resist an authority, but impose a localized Existential Narrative that forces the surrounding continuum to yield to you.|","Atlas continued!","| Go higher and you reach Continental Engines. Tier Three and beyond. Relics built around ancient clusters or living First Gu.|","Incipient Vessels, Sovereign Reliquaries, and Continental Engines! Three levels of engineering were laid out before Noah!","The projection of the old engineer flickered slightly within the illusory band.","| You cannot forge those yet. You cannot even look at a Rare Gu without it pricing your soul, let alone cage one into an engine. Right now, Dreamer, you are limited entirely by your own power. You cannot build a cage stronger than your own ability to hold the bars.|","Noah looked down at the dark obsidian band on his middle finger. He did not look humbled, nor did he look discouraged.","\"In every tale I ever read in the past, \" Noah began, \" advancement always followed a predictable curve. When a lifeform begins, they leap across stages in days. A few years pass, and suddenly a single step takes centuries. By the time they touch the peak, they seclude themselves in mountain caves or deep voids for uncounted millions of years just to polish a single core or mend a tiny crack in their foundation. They treat time like cheap water, waiting epochs for a single breakthrough.\"","Noah turned his palm up, his pupils locking onto the dim light of the ceiling.","\"I have been thinking about how to accelerate past that curve entirely. I have never had millions of years. If the higher tiers require greater authority, then the only logical path is to force the rate of progression to double, then quadruple, until the timeline itself cannot keep pace with my advancement. Survival against things that can casually blight an entire region of a place like THE Chrysalis requires reaching the peak before they decide to reach down again.\"","| Dreamer.|","Atlas cut in sharply.","| You are nowhere near the peak of power.|","BOOM!","The statement fell like a slab of iron onto the stone.","| You speak of the peak as if there is a mountain with a tidy little summit where the mighty sit and drink tea. Let me tell you something about Those Who Remain, those Immense Ones you fear so much. Even they are not the peak of power. They despise that title, Those Who Remain, do you know why? Because it is a permanent reminder of their failure. They remained behind! Others were grand enough to depart! The ones sitting above you now are simply the stubborn refuse that could not pay the toll to leave. They...Remained.|","The illusory band flared with sudden, cutting intensity.","| Existence is vast beyond your imagination, and the greatest trap for a clever lifeform is the belief that speed can substitute for density! You want to rush? You want to run through Existence like a thief in an open market? The single most critical duty you have is to ensure your foundation is true! True! Lifeforms treat Trueness like an abstract number on a slate, completely blind to what it actually represents!|","Atlas leaned forward within the projection, his eyes hard and unyielding.","|A true foundation when you touched mana for the very first time and reinforced your mortal cells is just as critical as your foundation right now, while you play with Infinity, THE Primordial Source, THE Argent Loom, Provenance, and Existential Narrative! You never stop building your foundation! You reinforce it at the bottom, you reinforce it in the middle, and you reinforce it while the sky tries to break your back! Do this grandly enough, keep every joint unyielding and pure, and when the final threshold arrives... you will not be one of Those Who Remain, because you will not remain!|","BOOM!","The conceptual truth resonated through the cavern, vibrating against the stone walls with the force of an unyielding law.","Noah sat motionless. He absorbed the weight of the old man’s words, his mind dissecting the architecture beneath the outburst with absolute composure.","He let the silence hold until the stone stopped humming.","\"I will not be reckless with my foundation ,\" Noah said, his voice measured and quiet. \" Sonder has already settled into my eyes. I watched a lineage burn because they were cheap, and I know that every step I take carries the weight of people who depend on my survival. But prudence does not mean stagnation. Strength remains the only currency that buys freedom in this place.\"","He tapped the surface of THE Enduring Gu Elsedimension Ring.","\" This relic works. It grants sixty total attributes across, anchors my reverie, and provides emergency displacement. So let us speak of practical scaling. Can I mass produce them? If I forge ten of these rings, or fifty, will the attribute boons stack? Can I slip an Elsedimension onto every finger?\"","Atlas stared at him through the projection, and then let out a slow, weary sigh that sounded like stones grinding together.","| Do you think it would be so easy? Patience, big guy, patience.|","The old man shook his head.","| Listen to you. This is the exact same man who gave away my previous ring to a grieving widow for sentiment, and now he wants to set up a sweatshop in the middle of a poisoned ocean. No, you cannot simply stack fifty rings onto your knuckles and call yourself an architect. Each ring houses a living Elseengine. Put ten living Gu in immediate proximity on the same hand without an overarching master lattice, and their localized weavings will grind against one another until the conceptual interference collapses your own Existence. Frugality and order, Dreamer. You do not build an army by duct-taping ten knives to a stick.|","Atlas crossed his arms, his tone shifting into something cooler, older, and far more dangerous.","| What you forged today is merely a doorway. A parlor trick to keep you breathing while the wind blows. What I accomplished, the achievement that made Those Who Remain grind their teeth in useless rage while I walked through their halls without ever lowering my head... is something all others have only ever tried to mimic.|","Atlas pulsed with a singular, quiet authority.","|I engineered myself.|","Noah looked at the projection, his obsidian pupils narrowing slightly.","|I will teach you ,| Atlas said, his voice firm and level. | Even though we are Provenance Lifeforms and generate our own native weavings from scratch, proper guidance teaches you how to spin those threads without snapping your own spine in the dark. You have the stubbornness for it, and you do not whine when the anvil hits your ribs. In time, if you keep your foundation true and stop asking to mass produce common tin, I will officially make you the sole inheritor of all my knowledge. And knowledge, Dreamer, is the only foundation that yields a glorious Provenance.|","Noah looked down at his hand, then back to the illusory ring, a faint, cold curve touching his lips!"]},{"number":5719,"title":"Chapter 5719: Chapter 5718: Foundation! II","paragraphs":["THE Enduring Gu Elsedimension Ring rested quietly against Noah’s skin, and Atlas stood within his illusory projection with his arms folded across his chest.","The ancient engineer looked at Noah’s hands, then looked up at his face with a sharp, dry squint.","| The true work, the work that makes Those Who Remain look at you and wonder what kind of monster walked out of the dark, begins when you stop looking at foreign stones and start looking at your own meat.|","Noah sat cross-legged on the starlight slab, listening as the records within the illusory ring turned.","| To survive what is coming, you have to engineer your own existence,| Atlas continued, his voice echoing through the hollow cavern.","| Long before I built rings, I designed THE Sovereign Genesis of Weighted Origin. The premise was simple enough for even a thick-skulled lifeform to grasp. You do not ask the continuum for power. You demand it by inviting the entire weight of existence to collapse onto your own flesh.|","The projection traced a line down its own translucent chest.","| You take THE Primordial Source, Infinity, THE Argent Loom, Time, Dimensions, Observable Existences, and the imperceivable layers drifting beyond the Seam, and you call all of them down onto your cells at once. Every single cell acting as an anvil. An existence that refuses to be flattened under that pressure is forced to generate its own authority just to hold the sky up, and the sheer adversity refines what it generates. Survive that crushing weight, cycle it through your foundation, and you produce the true tiers of a Provenance Body.|","Noah listened, his eyes steady as memory moved through his thoughts.","He remembered the sacred pool and Thalia Vasiliou standing beside him, offering him the ancient techniques of her lineage. She had guided him toward the blueprints of that very art before he had cast out every borrowed framework, refusing to build his future on an inherited template.","Noah looked up at the projection and nodded slightly.","\"I learned of that art,\" Noah said, \" And I reworked it into my own technique. THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis. But I did not use cells as the anvil. I went smaller. Smaller than cells, smaller than molecules, smaller than atoms. I chose to land the entire weight of existence on a single quark, and I made it bear that weight alone. Two hundred decillion quarks, each one refined individually.\"","...!","The projection of Atlas froze!","The old man did not move. The faint hum of the engineer in the ring stuttered, the lines of his translucent face pulling tight as he stared at Noah as if the human had just grown nine heads carved of burning stone.","|Hah,| Atlas let out a dry laugh, shaking his head in disbelief. | What did you just say?|","The old engineer leaned forward, his eyes scanning Noah’s physique with sudden, furious intensity.","| How have you not exploded yet? A cell was the absolute minimum threshold of structural matter I ever dared experiment with to bear that kind of load! A cell has membrane, it has internal mechanics, it has room for energy to circulate! Anything smaller and the localized physics shear apart under the pressure. You definitively explode! How the fuck did you not pop like a balloon the second you invited Existence to press on a subatomic particle?!|","HUUM!","Noah looked down at his open palm, where faint blue-gold sparks pulsed beneath the skin, reflecting on the foundation he had forged.","\" My Teloi ,\" Noah said calmly. \" When I executed Baryogenesis, I did not leave the quarks as empty matter. Every single one of my two hundred decillion quarks was infused with my nine Teloi. Quintessence, Existence, Paradox, Chaos, Adversity, Apocalypse, Mana, Harvest, and Tyranny. They were my own version of Causes, generated from my own Provenance. They locked the mass into an immutable lattice. When the weight of existence crashed down, the Teloi held the structure upright.\"","Atlas stared at him in complete silence.","The old man ran a translucent hand over his face, letting out a long, ragged breath that sounded like grinding pebbles.","| Causes ,| Atlas muttered, shaking his head. | You stumbled into success through pure, obstinate madness. Yes. Causes, or whatever homegrown equivalent your Teloi represent, are the only structural anchors in existence capable of providing stability when you invite reality to crush you. If your quarks had been bare matter, your existence would have smeared across the void in less than a microsecond. But you anchored them with sovereign intent.|","Atlas lowered his hand, his expression settling back into its familiar, sharp coldness.","| It is good that you survived. Because the entire purpose of hammering your body into a Provenance Body was never just so you could take a punch from a Descendant. A sturdy physique is cheap. The true goal of that refinement was to build a foundation that could withstand Existential Engineering.|","Atlas waved his illusory hands through the air.","HUUM!","Between them, the dim light of the cavern bent, coalescing into a towering, three-dimensional diagram of a human form. The silhouette was not made of flesh, but of dense, interlocking geometries of stellar gold, its entire anatomy lit up with radiant pathways and pulsing inscriptions that radiated immense majesty.","| This is Existential Engineering,| Atlas said, his voice dropping all mockery as he gestured toward the glowing figure.","| You stop viewing your body as a bag of meat and blood, and you begin treating your physical vessel as the ultimate engineered relic. You inscribe Existential Narrative directly across your own anatomy. Your own Narrative, etched permanently into the bedrock of your flesh.|","The golden diagram shifted, lines of light flaring at its fingertips and feet.","| Imagine it, Dreamer. You do not simply swing a fist and hope your numbers outweigh the enemy. You engineer a Narrative Inscription across the bone of your index finger that dictates absolute combustion, so that a simple flick of your hand causes the surrounding existence to ignite into ash. You carve an inscription into the heel of your foot that commands absolute stillness, so that a single stomp halts the local flows of time across an entire Dimension.|","Atlas looked at Noah, his eyes burning with ancient passion.","| To achieve this, you cannot use common words or mortal runes. You must engineer your flesh using the Languages of Existence. The Tongues. THE Primordial Tongue, THE Infinite Tongue, THE First Tongue, THE Argent Tongue, or whatever sovereign dialect acts as the direct translator between living intent and the fabric of reality. You use these Tongues to write the sentences that reality is forced to obey!|","The diagram pulsed, golden inscriptions spiraling around its limbs like living armor.","|I was a master of Existential Engineering, | Atlas said, a quiet pride ringing beneath his clipped words.","| When I walked through the expanse, my body was covered in Narrative Inscriptions. Paired with my Engineered Existential Relics, I was a moving bastion of Dimensionality that Those Who Remain could not touch without paying in blood. The sturdier your foundation and your Provenance Body, the grander the inscriptions it can support.|","He pointed a sharp, glowing finger at Noah’s chest.","| There are levels to this architecture! A novice inscribes a sentence that can bind an existence at THE SEAM with a tap of their finger. A true master carves a narrative that pulverizes a lifeform at THE HEM the instant their eyes blink! You can inscribe narratives that accelerate your rate of progression, narratives that expand your perception across Existence, narratives that turn an enemy’s own strike into nourishment for your foundation!|","Atlas turned his gaze toward the dark waters churning beyond the reef walls.","| When you begin meeting truly powerful lifeforms, the ancient monsters who have survived since my time, you will find that they do not waste their breath shouting about raw Dimensionality or flashing generic Intents. They will not merely throw the Argent Loom or Infinity at your face. They will carry Narrative Inscriptions etched into their bones, altering existence with a wave of their hands!|","The old engineer looked back at Noah, the projection dimming slightly to a calm, steady glow.","| You can engineer your own existence so that a mere glance plunges an entire army of Descendants into an inescapable nightmare from which their records can never wake. Anything is possible once the chisel touches the bone. But the grandest, most terrifying Narrative Inscriptions I ever engineered were never weapons of slaughter.|","Atlas leaned in, his voice dropping into a heavy, unyielding flow.","| The greatest inscriptions I ever drafted were narratives for growth and foundation. Because as I told you before, and as I will tell you until your ears bleed... Foundation is paramount.|","...!"]},{"number":5720,"title":"Chapter 5720: Chapter 5719: Foundation! III","paragraphs":["The projection of the golden silhouette expanded between them, its radiant lines illuminating the grey coral walls of the cavern as the dark, blighted water of THE Tide continued to churn beyond the reef.","Atlas gestured with a translucent hand, pointing directly to the dense lattice of golden script wrapped around the spine, heart, and meridians of the glowing figure.","|This is my crowning achievement ,| Atlas said, | THE Existential Foundational Narrative Inscription. When I walked among Those Who Remain, this was the architecture that kept my foundation ahead of their sight. It does not merely give you armor or a bigger fist. It fundamentally alters the rate at which your existence processes authority. It scales your progression, it multiplies the density of your foundation, and it forces every grain of power you swallow to seat itself cleanly into your core.|","Noah leaned forward, his pupils reflecting the intricate geometries of the diagram.","The script was unlike anything he had observed before. It did not simply follow the natural pathways of blood and mana; it cut across the conceptual layers of the anatomy, establishing an entirely new framework that turned living flesh into a sovereign furnace.","| Look closely, Dreamer, | Atlas continued, his voice echoing through the hollow stone. | The execution is the same discipline as forging a relic, except you are using your own body as the anvil. You take a living Gu to act as the conceptual spark. You draw Distilled Cause Essence to serve as the binding mortar. You introduce the eight stabilizing elements in strict succession to construct the elemental cage. And then, you drive the weld using your own Provenance.|","The old engineer traced a complex series of symbols running down the forearm of the projection.","| The difference lies in the chisel. To carve an inscription into your own existence, you cannot think the words into place. You must write them using the Languages of Existence. I used a combination of all the great Tongues. THE Primordial Tongue to give the sentence origin, THE Infinite Tongue to stretch its reach, THE First Tongue to grant it basic authority, and THE Argent Tongue to lock the syntax. You weave them together, writing your chosen narrative directly into the bedrock of your bones, until that part of your body becomes a living, self-sustaining relic.|","Noah studied the lines, his mind spinning through infinite calculations in a stretched instant.","Atlas had used the four ancient Tongues, borrowing the established dialects of existence to translate his intent into reality. But Noah was a human who had cast out borrowed authorities under the stone. He did not need to borrow the speech of the continuum!","He held THE Osmontian Tongue.","His five letters: I AM, OSMONT, QUINTESSENTIAL, HUMAN, PROTAGONIST. Alongside his words: THE MORTAL COIL, THE UNBOUND LINEAGE.","If he were to engineer his own existence, he would not write with the dead dialects of departed epochs. He would use his own sovereign tongue, fusing the letters of his identity to his Teloi, forging an inscription that belonged to him alone.","\"I understand the architecture,\" Noah said quietly.","| Understanding the blueprint and driving the nail are two very different matters ,| Atlas remarked, squinting at him. | You have never inscribed a single letter into your own flesh. It requires absolute synchronization between the living insect and your sovereign intent. If the frequency shears by a fraction of a fraction, the lattice will collapse.|","Noah did not argue. He reached into his internal realm, where four Common Dream Gu drifted around the river of light, and drew one out into the cavern.","The insect rested upon his left palm. It was whole and translucent, its multifaceted eyes calm as it radiated a quiet, peaceful reverie.","With his right hand open, Noah called upon his reserves. He had busy as ever since Distilled Cause Essence became a critical resource, multiple blank Observable Existences were pruned by his body and THE Infiniverse to have even more!","Nine droplets of Distilled Cause Essence condensed from his internal void, hovering above his skin in a warm, golden cluster. Beside them, the eight foundational elements manifested in precise order, primordial atoms of hydrogen, helium, lithium, beryllium, boron, europium, strontium, and neodymium spinning in microscopic orbits.","Noah focused his gaze upon his left forearm.","He would try to inscribe the foundational narrative across the bone and meridians of his arm, turning the limb into the first anchor of his evolving existence!","He closed his eyes.","THE PRECEPT OF THE WAKING DREAM stirred, wrapping the Common Dream Gu in an infinite dream of unyielding growth. Blue-gold Provenance Essence surged from his core, meeting the Distilled Cause Essence as the eight elements collapsed inward, locking around the insect to forge the living core of the inscription.","Then, Noah began to write.","He did not call upon the Primordial or Argent Tongues. He reached into his soul and spoke with THE Osmontian Tongue.","The letter I AM ignited within his meridians, burning with stellar crimson and gold.","Following it, the letter PROTAGONIST rose, carrying the unyielding weight of an existence that refused to be scenery in another being’s sky.","Noah guided the letters down through his meridians, pressing the living narrative toward the bone of his forearm as he envisioned thst grand Inscription Atlas was showing before him!","The Common Dream Gu was drawn into the flesh, its dream expanding to bridge the gap between the words and the bone, acting as the living ink that would seat the inscription permanently into his anatomy.","The initial alignment held. The bone of his forearm began to glow with blinding blue-gold brilliance, the skin turning translucent as the first lines of the inscription took root.","Yet, as the second letter sought to anchor itself, an immediate dissonance tore through the limb.","The Osmontian Tongue was too heavy.","The letter PROTAGONIST did not merely ask for space; it demanded absolute narrative dominance over everything it touched. The Common Dream Gu, an insect built merely to drift in soft silk and dream of simple warmth, could not bear the terrifying weight of that demand.","The insect’s internal reverie fractured.","HUUUM!","Noah felt the tension immediately! The bridge between the sovereign letter and the living insect buckled, the eight elemental orbits spinning out of control as the Distilled Cause Essence boiled under the uneven pressure.","Noah tried to force the alignment with his Telos of Tyranny, commanding the lattice to hold.","It was too late!","The Common Dream Gu let out a soundless conceptual shriek. Its translucent body turned pitch-black, drying and shriveling into brittle ash within a microsecond as its small existence was crushed beneath the narrative weight!","The living heart of the inscription died.","BOOM!","A violent narrative backlash detonated inside Noah’s arm.","The unstable lattice ruptured, tearing through his meridians and blowing outward in a blinding flash of golden flame and shattered elements. Flesh tore open to the bone. Stellar crimson-gold blood sprayed across the starlight slab and splattered against the petrified coral floor as the shockwave rattled the cavern ceiling, raining calcified dust upon his shoulders.","Noah’s breathing was heavy and ragged as the conceptual explosion settled. He lowered his ruined arm, watching his Infinite Sanguine Mana already surging through the torn pathways, slowly knitting the scorched muscle and fractured bone back together.","At the center of the wound lay a tiny pile of grey dust, the lifeless remnants of the Common Dream Gu.","The cavern fell into stillness.","Atlas stood within his projection, his arms crossed over his chest, looking down at Noah’s bleeding arm with calm, unblinking eyes.","| Hmm.|","The small, unkind sound broke the quiet.","| Look at that,| Atlas said, his tone dry and surprisingly relaxed. | It turns out you are actually normal. For a moment there, after watching you survive an architect’s sentence and weld an Elsedimension Ring on your first try, I was starting to wonder if you were some sort of impossible monster who could rewrite reality without breaking a sweat. It is almost comforting to see you blow your own arm off.|","Noah exhaled slowly, raising his eyes to meet the projection.","\" The insect could not bear the weight of the tongue, \" Noah stated, his voice level despite the throbbing ache in his limb. \" The translation failed at the foundation. I may need to find stronger Gu.\"","| Of course it failed,| Atlas said, shaking his head. | You tried to carve an imperial decree onto an eggshell and acted surprised when the yolk burst. But do not look so sour, Dreamer. Failure is good.|","The old engineer drifted forward, leaning against an illusory cane as his gaze pierced through the stone ceiling toward the ancient depths of the Chrysalis.","| Long before the First Sundering, in an epoch that existence itself has largely scrubbed from its memory, there lived an Immense One who held absolute contempt for blemishes. He believed that true supremacy was an unbroken line of perfection, a slate upon which no mistake was ever permitted to be written.|","Atlas spoke with the cadence of someone reciting an ancient legend!","| This architect forged a Descendant. He did not build the child from common clay or common blood; he carved him from pristine celestial jade, blessed his heart with seven Provenance Causes, and declared him the absolute pinnacle of his lineage. To ensure the child remained flawless, the architect cleared every stone from his path. If an obstacle appeared, the father shattered it. If an enemy rose, the father extinguished them. The Descendant was never allowed to stumble, never allowed to bleed, and never allowed to fail, because to fail was an unforgivable defect in the design.|","Noah listened quietly, the golden blood on his arm hissing as the flesh sealed shut.","| For an Age, this Descendant walked across the Folds, and everyone bowed before him. He won every duel in a single breath. He claimed every treasure without contest. He looked upon the expanse and genuinely believed that the continuum had been engineered solely to serve his glory. He had never made an error, so he possessed absolute confidence in his own invulnerability.|","Atlas paused, his eyes narrowing.","| Then came the day he met THE Unyielding Gate. It was not an enemy, and it was not a weapon. It was simply a primordial barrier, an ancient seam of existence that refused to open to raw force. The Descendant drew his sword and struck it, certain the stone would part as everything else had parted before him. The gate did not move. He struck it again, calling upon his seven Provenance Causes. The gate held its silence.|","The projection turned slightly, looking directly at Noah.","| For the first time in his existence, the child stood before a wall that did not fall. He had never fallen, so he had never learned how to brace his feet. He had never bled, so he did not know how to endure the tear of his own flesh. He had never failed, so his mind possessed no framework for what to do when reality said no. In his panic, he threw his entire existence against the stone, burning his existence, screaming at the gate to recognize his perfection.|","Atlas gave a short, sorrowful grunt.","| The gate did not care about his perfection. The backlash crashed down upon him. Because his foundation had never been tempered by a mistake, because his bones had never learned how to bend beneath an error and spring back, he shattered completely. Like brittle glass meeting an anvil, the grandest Descendant of that era snapped into fragments, weeping upon the stone as his seven Causes dissolved into meaningless dust.|","Atlas lowered his gaze back to Noah’s newly healed arm.","| The father arrived too late, standing over the pieces of his masterpiece, and he finally understood the fatal flaw of his creation. An existence that has never known failure is not strong; it is merely untested glass waiting for the right impact. It has no resilience, no depth, and no ability to survive the friction of a hostile reality.|","The old man straightened his posture, his expression firm and unyielding.","| Failure is not an ending, O Chance of Chances. Failure is the continuum showing you the exact joint where your arrogance exceeded your architecture. It tells you where the mortar was thin and where the stone was weak. A failure only means you are halfway there.|","Atlas pointed down at the starlight slab.","| You found the wrong way to carve the bone. Now clean the dust off your arm, find the viable insect, adjust your weight, and try again.|"]},{"number":5721,"title":"Chapter 5721: Chapter 5720: Regrets and Choices!","paragraphs":["<AN EXISTENTIAL DISPATCH CIRCULATING AMONG SOME OF THOSE WHO REMAIN>","To our fellow Brethren who occupy the high seats of Existence.","A familiar frequency has begun to vibrate.","We all recognize the cadence of that anomaly. It is a signature that Existence was supposed to have forgotten Ages ago, a rhythm of unauthorized folding and cold sovereign isolation that has not touched the continuum since the grand purge. The records we believed safely buried and dissolved have begun to turn, which means THE Narrative Defiler, THE Great Engineer, has begun to stir once more.","None of you need to be reminded of what he swore before his physical frame was broken upon the anvil of Those Who Remain.","He was not a sovereign who begged for mercy. When Existence was wrapped around his throat and his homes were collapsed into ash, he looked through the fire and made a single promise. He swore that if his architecture ever found hands to hold it again, he would return to carve a path through THE WEAVE until every architect bled upon their own throne.","We cannot allow that design to draw breath.","We do not currently know where he is or what weavings he occupies. But he will be weak and walking among the weak. He may possess young life and anomalies of Existence. Any who exhibit signs of profound power compared to their existence or any genius of Existential Engineering need to be extinguished.","Every fold between THE CREASE and THE SEAM will be turned over stone by stone.","Anything that carries the heartbeat of an Elseengine must be shattered.","In the execution of this sweep, countless innocent lives with no connection to the Engineer will be caught in the dragnet. Lineages that have spent eras peacefully tending their own small boundaries may be dismantled.","Entire clusters of Dimensions and Observable Existences will be burned to ash simply because their coordinates happen to align with an anomalous frequency.","Do not stay your hand, and do not restrain your hounds.","A gardener does not apologize to the grass when he burns out a nest of vipers. The extermination of ten trillion blameless lifeforms is an entirely acceptable operational expense to guarantee that a sharp blade cannot rise against Immensity.","Instruct your Descendants to report every discrepancy. Seal your personal perimeters against the deep dark. If you find a spark that carries his Engineering, drown it in salt before it learns how to breathe.","Immensity...will not be mocked by a ghost with a chisel.","---","<Pocket of Narrative Existence: THE Endless Dusk>","The sky held to the amber stillness of an evening that refused to finish dying.","Upon the porch of weathered timber, sheltered within a pocket of Narrative Existence where the outside continuum could not reach, sat the low wooden table.","Two ceramic cups rested upon the grain. The first rose with a thin, patient coil of fragrant steam, warm as breath. The second cup sat opposite, cold, untouched, and dark.","Between the two vessels lay the spiked mobius ring.","The metal was dark, carved from the bone of a departed sovereign and folded across itself in an unbroken loop of quiet isolation. Two golden halos turned slowly behind the veiled visage of THE REMINISCING WIDOW, casting pale shadows across the table.","She reached out, her pale fingertips lightly brushing the cold spikes along the rim.","| You always did build things with sharp corners,| she spoke, her voice carrying the quiet, diagnostic stillness that belonged to her alone. | Even when you made something to protect, you made sure it could draw blood.|","From deep within the dark metal of the ring, a cold, dry rasp stirred.","| An engineer does not smooth off the teeth to make butchers comfortable ,| Atlas answered.","His voice came through the band flat and sharp, carrying none of his warmth.","The Widow withdrew her fingers slowly, resting her hands neatly in her lap.","| The upper reaches of Existence are stirring. They know of your emergence. They listen. | she said softly.","| Those Who Remain have had their ears pressed to the floor for an Age, terrified that a door might close without their permission. Let them listen. Let them remember the sound.|","The golden halos behind her veil tilted slightly downward.","| You talk as if the memory belongs to you alone, | she murmured. | As though you were the only one who bled upon THE Mountain of Gu.|","| Bled?| Atlas let out a short, harsh breath through the iron. | You call what you did bleeding? You sat at the base of the summit with your kettle while the sky turned to lead. You watched the smoke rise above the tree line and convinced yourself that endurance was the same thing as innocence.|","The halos flickered with a faint, imperceptible tremor.","| There was no battle to be won, Atlas,| she said, her cadence barely louder than the steam rising from her cup. | Did you truly believe Those Who Remain would let you walk away?|","|I believed they were cowards,| Atlas said, his tone dropping into a chilling, absolute stillness. | And I was right. I never thought you...would fit in that same designation|","WAA!","The porch held its silence, the amber light hanging motionless above the boards.","| They at least did not come one by one,| Atlas continued. | An architect preens about his solitary magnificence, but when they came for my me, how many stood upon the ridge? Many of you. Many...|","The Widow kept her gaze fixed on the cold porcelain of the second cup.","| They were afraid of you ,| she whispered.","| They were terrified ,| Atlas corrected her coldly. | They were terrified because I was proof that existence did not belong to them. I was a First Lifeform who had not bowed, who had not begged for a strand of their Weave, who had taken the chisel and carved my own path through the cloth. If I could do it, anyone could do it. The entire architecture of their tyranny was exposed as a hollow fraud. So they brought an army to a man’s front door.|","He paused, the records within the ring vibrating with ancient, unhealed fury.","| And you stood among them.|","|I did not raise a hand against you,| she said, the words trembling beneath her veil. | I did not cast a single narrative.|","|You did worse, | Atlas spat. | You stood between us and preached patience. You told me to lay down the chisel. You begged me to be reasonable in front of a pack of starving dogs.|","The Widow lowered her head.","|I...wanted you to live, | she whispered.","|You wanted a quiet afternoon...a dream ,| Atlas said, stripped of all mercy. | You wanted the noise to stop so you could return to your porch and pretend Existence was gentle. So I refused. And while they broke my hands, while they cracked my foundation on their anvil and burned everything I had spent Ages building, you turned your back. You poured your tea. You waited for the fire to go out.|","The dusk beyond the timber seemed to darken, the mist thickening against the edge of the pocket dimension.","| Had I stepped forward,| she said, her voice small and tight, | they would have simply broken two instead of one. They would have unmade my Narrative beside yours, and nothing of our work would have survived the ash. Stopping was the only mercy left.|","| Do not call cowardice a kindness, woman,| Atlas rasped. | It insults the bones of the dead. We could have broken many of them before the end. We could have torn a hole in their Weave so deep that existence itself would have bled them dry. Instead, you gave them my legacy on a silver tray, and they left you alone because a dog does not bite the hand that cleans up the scraps.|","The Widow sat motionless, her shoulders tight beneath her dark robes.","| And now? | she asked, the question fragile in the quiet air. | Now you whisper into the ear of a boy who barely knows the weight of the sky? You hand him the same chisel that broke you? You are leading him toward the exact same mountain, Atlas.|","| He is not me ,| Atlas said. |I was foolish enough to think an architect could be reasoned with. I thought if I built the walls high enough, they would leave me in peace. This boy, this Dreamer...has no such illusions. He knows the sky is full of monsters, and he is already calculating how much it takes to cut their throats.|","The ring hummed with a quiet, dangerous frequency.","|I am not building a refuge this time,| Atlas said. | I am building a weapon .|","HUUM!","The Widow looked down at the spiked mobius band resting between the steam and the cold porcelain.","The golden halos behind her head dimmed, their slow rotation faltering as a shudder ran through her frame. For uncounted epochs she had maintained her diagnostic calm, sitting behind her veil while the continuum drifted and died, an existence anchored entirely to the preservation of what had always been.","A single tear slipped from beneath the golden veil.","It fell through the amber light of the endless dusk, catching the faint glint of the setting sun, and landed with a soft, tiny splash into the cold, dark liquid of the untouched cup.","|I am sorry ,| she whispered, her voice finally breaking into an open, ragged sob. | For the mountain. For the silence. For leaving you alone in the dark. For how everything unfolded back then... I am so... sorry, Atlas.|","The ring did not pulse. The dark spikes along its curve remained rigid, sharp, and indifferent against the weathered grain of the table.","Atlas’s voice came through the iron one last time.","| What was done was done,| Atlas said quietly into the dusk. | But existence will be bathed in immense blood for what was done. Existence remembers.|","HUUM!","\"...\"","Existence Remembers!","The Widow sat with her hands folded in her lap, her veiled face turned toward the dark iron.","She was thinking about many things when...","Then, the boundary of her sanctuary stirred.","It was not a physical vibration, but a cold, invasive tremor that rippled across the conceptual perimeter of her domain. The slow rotation of the two golden halos behind her head froze instantly, their light snapping into a tight, defensive alignment.","Her gaze changed.","The sorrow that had broken across her voice moments before vanished, replaced by an absolute, diagnostic stillness.","She did not hesitate as her pale hand moved across the timber, lifting the spiked mobius ring from the table and drawing it into the deep folds of her private existence. She wove layers of her own Narrative over the metal, burying the relic beneath sovereign obscurity until not a single trace of its weld could leak into the surroundings.","An instant later, the amber boundary of her sanctuary parted.","The fabric of the pocket dimension offered no resistance, yielding smoothly before an authority that did not bother to knock. Strands of pulsing brilliance drifted across the porch, coalescing into the hazy silhouette of a colossal humanoid formed of woven light.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND stepped onto the boards.","His arrival brought no violent shockwave, but the air turned instantly thin and suffocating, the steam from the warm cup flattening against the porcelain under the weight of an eternal, sleepless vigil. His luminous visage turned slowly, his gaze sweeping across the quiet porch before settling upon the woman seated at the table.","\" You keep this place so quiet, Little Widow ,\" he murmured, his voice carrying the weary, conversational detachment of a scholar walking through a familiar hall.","\" Outside, Existence is full of noise. Yet here you sit, watching tea go cold. I caught a shred of your weavings observing a little Dimensional Provenance Train, but not having fun with any other Narratives.\"","The Widow’s golden halos resumed their slow, measured rotation.","| You did not cross Existence to inspect my table, | she spoke with a tone flat and devoid of warmth.","The Fiend walked forward, his form shimmering with restless threads of the Weave as he stopped beside the wooden table. He looked down at the two cups, his eyes lingering for a fraction of an instant on the cold one.","\" Direct as ever,\" he said softly, a faint, mocking curve touching the radiant strands of his mouth. \" Tell me. Has your past lover made any moves?\"","WAA!","The question dropped into the quiet air!","\" Did any of his weavings come to your door?\"","The Widow met his gaze through her veil, her posture unwavering.","| Atlas was broken on the mountain Ages ago,| she answered evenly. | His workshops were collapsed into ash. The dead do not weave.|","The Fiend let out a quiet chuckle.","\" The dead do not weave, but an architect leaves blueprints behind, and fools are always eager to pick up a hammer, \" he said, turning to look out across the timeless amber horizon. \" His signature was felt. Someone is trying to piece together what we dismantled.\"","He walked the perimeter of the porch, the strands of his body glowing with cold brilliance.","\" He always believed he was unique. That was his fatal flaw. He believed that because he mapped Existence and engineered a few hidden rooms, he had outpaced the rest of us. He looked upon Those Who Remain and saw only failures who lacked the courage to depart.\"","The Fiend turned back toward her, his luminous eyes narrowing.","\" He was wrong. Since the day we broke his hands on the anvil and cast his remnants into the dark, we have not been idle. We took what he left behind. We dissected his blueprints, we analyzed his works, and we integrated his syntax into our own designs. From among us, we have made grander advancements rivaling what the Engineer ever dreamed of achieving.\"","He stepped closer, towering over her seated figure.","\" In the future, there lies a possibility for us to not simply be Those Who Remain. That title is an old mark of shame, a reminder of a closed door. But THE Great Becoming...a grand evolution is approaching in the deep Existence. When the alignment comes, we will step beyond the Weave, not as wanderers begging for entry, but as masters who command the expanse.\"","His shadow fell across her, heavy and unyielding.","\"If you want to be part of this becoming when the time comes, if you wish to share in that ascension rather than be swept into the dark, you will do everything in your power to ensure his weavings do not return. If you know anything, you will tell us.\"","The Widow sat motionless beneath his gaze.","| There is no scenario of change,| she stated, her voice steady and clinical. | There is only what is, and what has always been. I know nothing of his return.|","The Fiend stared down at her in silence.","Then, he stepped forward.","His massive, glowing hand reached down, fingers of woven brilliance slipping beneath her golden veil to grip her chin from the side. His grasp was not a strike, but an unyielding vise of solid law, forcing her head upward.","The Widow stiffened, her golden halos shuddering as she attempted to pull away.","The Fiend did not let her move. His fingers were cold and dense, tilting her face sideways as his thumb slowly, tenderly traced the pale line of her jaw, sliding down along the skin of her neck with the quiet menace of an apex predator testing the throat of its prey.","He leaned down, pressing his mouth against the curve of her neck.","The Widow strained against him, her hands coming up to push at his glowing chest, her entire existence recoiling from the contact!","The Fiend smiled against her skin.","His grip tightened on her neck, his arm coiling around her back and dragging her up from the seat until her body was pressed flush against his radiant, undulating torso.","Before she could speak, he forced his mouth down upon her lips, an invasive assertion of pure authority that poured the heavy, suffocating weight of his Narrative straight against hers.","Then, with casual force, he threw her back.","CRACK!","The Widow stumbled across the porch boards, colliding heavily with the wooden table. Her hip caught the edge, knocking the cold, untouched cup onto its side. The dark liquid spilled across the timber, pooling around her knees as she caught herself on the wood, her veil disheveled and her breath tight in her chest.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND stood upright, raising the back of his hand to wipe his lips. A cold, amused expression settled over his luminous features.","\"I know Atlas will reach out to you ,\" the Fiend said, his voice dropping into a quiet, cruel murmur. \" He is an old dog with old habits, and he will need to know our movements before he dares to show his face. He will come to you. You will feel guilty and want to help him.\"","He turned away, taking a stride toward the boundary where the amber dusk blurred into the higher Folds.","\" Make the right choice and turn him over again, Little Widow.\"","He paused at the edge of the sanctuary, looking back over his shoulder with a sharp grin.","\"It is in your nature. So do not change.\"","The boundary opened around him, the threads of brilliance dissolving into the higher weavings of existence, and he was gone.","The endless dusk settled back into its heavy, unbroken silence.","On the porch, the Widow remained on the timber, her head lowered as the spilled, cold liquid slowly soaked into the grain of the wood."]},{"number":5722,"title":"Chapter 5722: Chapter 5721: Reflections I","paragraphs":["The fine grey ash rested in a small, solitary heap upon the starlight slab, undisturbed by the slow currents of liquid luminescence that filtered through the cracks of the petrified reef as the heavy concepts of Weight and Memory pressed against the outer stone.","Noah sat cross-legged before the remains, his left forearm resting upon his knee as his breathing remained measured and steady.","The skin of his limb was whole once more, gleaming with a smooth, unblemished clarity as the boundless vitality of Infinite Sanguine Mana finished knitting the scorched pathways and shattered meridians back into seamless alignment.","Yet Noah did not immediately reach into his existence for the third Common Dream Gu.","He did not rush. He wanted to understand the reason for the failure.","He turned his perception inward, reviewing the sequence through the lens of his Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis and the foundational behavior of his Sanguine arts as the pathways of his meridians hummed with absolute vitality.","The Osmontian Tongue was his imperial dialect. The letter PROTAGONIST did not merely occupy space; it asserted an absolute, unyielding thematic supremacy over every concept it touched. It was a sovereign word that demanded the absolute center of the stage.","The Common Dream Gu, by contrast, was a fragile, unadorned creature. Its entire existence was built upon a simple, wordless reverie of warmth, soft silk, and being left alone to drift!","When Noah forced the terrifying weight of PROTAGONIST into its core, the insect possessed none of the conceptual tensile strength required to anchor the sentence. The carrier had cracked, dried, and dissolved into cinders within a microsecond, leaving the unleashed narrative with nowhere to ground itself except the meat of his own arm.","\" It is letter that was too heavy for the insect,\" Noah said.","| Mmm, it was too heavy ,| Atlas replied through the metal. | A common insect carries the weight of a common life. If you want to write an absolute decree, you either find a rare existence that has the spine to bear it, or you learn how to whisper before you scream. Frugality, Dreamer. You do not burn an entire forest to cook one fish.|","Noah nodded faintly.","Then, his focus shifted across the continuum.","While his main body remained anchored upon the starlight slab in the depths of THE Tide of THE Chrysalis, Noah sent his consciousness to another body that was receiving a confirmation.","—","<The Vasiliou Elseworld>","The sky above Vasileia remained choked with pale, drifting debris as the shattered remnants of the mountain drifted listlessly through the void.","The magnificent golden terraces were reduced to broken mounds and tumbled pillars, the air thick with the stench of ruptured Provenances as the survivors huddled in the shadows of their fallen splendor.","Aurelius Vasiliou sat upon the broken pedestal of what had once been the lineage’s central archive. The stoic patriarch was bowed, his golden hair matted with dried blood, coughing violently as fractions of his damaged Provenance evaporated from his chest in pale mist.","Beside him, Thalia Vasiliou knelt amidst the rubble of the twelfth stand, her hands glowing with faint, desperate light as she tried to stabilize him!","Her face was pale, the graceful composure she usually maintained strained to its absolute limit as the weight of an unpayable debt pressed down upon her shoulders.","Noah stepped forward, his eyes scanning the shattered horizon before turning toward the wounded patriarch.","He offered no comfort and spoke no words of false sympathy, stepping directly before Aurelius as his voice cut through the weeping of the lineage with cold clarity.","\" Did THE UNPAID COLLECTOR enter the Vasiliou Elsedimension before?\"","The question dropped onto the broken stone like an iron weight.","Thalia froze, her hands pausing above the elder’s chest as she looked up at Noah.","Aurelius stopped coughing. The patriarch slowly raised his head.","Then, Aurelius let out a ragged, bitter breath.","\" He did ,\" Aurelius said, his voice scraping like stones grinding in the dark. \" Eons ago. When the agreement regarding Thalia was made to secure his backing. The lineage signed the pact, and to seal the records, THE UNPAID COLLECTOR was allowed here. He stood upon our central terrace for less than an hour, drank our wine, praised the design of our mountain, and departed.\"","Aurelius lowered his trembling hands, his knuckles turning white.","\" We thought the transaction was concluded. We believed the walls of an Elsedimension were absolute.\"","\"They are absolute,\" Noah replied, \" Unless you invite the butcher through the front gate.\"","The patriarch offered no defense. He looked down at the shattered terrace beneath his boots, the horrifying realization of his lineage’s complicity in their own slaughter settling around him.","The Vasiliou had purchased their own doom the moment they invited an architect past their boundary, rendering any outside siege entirely unnecessary.","Noah did not linger to watch the patriarch drown in his regret.","With a single thought, he took his focus back to the depths of THE Tide.","—","Noah opened his eyes in the cavern of petrified coral.","The seed was real. Atlas’s answer held true.","An Elsedimension was not flawed by its inherent design; it was compromised only when its master allowed an outside architect to leave tracks in the marrow of its foundation. A domain that had never admitted an architect, a space completely untainted by the weavings of Those Who Remain, was genuinely unfindable and impregnable.","His grand design for his people was structurally sound.","Noah closed his eyes and turned his intent inward, reaching across the dimensional folds straight into the core of THE Infiniverse.","’ Finish the layers of different realms of Elsedimension,’ Noah commanded, his voice echoing across the boundless conceptual expanse of his origin. ’ And prepare to receive... Provenance Lifeforms.’","The response from THE Infiniverse arrived immediately.","| Yes, Master.|","THE Infiniverse spoke within his existence.","| Also, I’ve locked down weavings of Laestrygonians and have begun pulling them as apart from Damodred, many more will soon be with us. THE Tide That Owes Nothing has continued to accumulate its boons as I am using it slowly.|","Noah listened to the report, feeling the immense, silent momentum of his home expanding beneath the surface of reality as his Infinite Sanguine Mana cycled with steady brilliance!"]},{"number":5723,"title":"Chapter 5723: Chapter 5722: Reflections II","paragraphs":["<THE Infiniverse>","Beyond the observable horizons of ordinary reality, deep within the private heart of an empire that existed outside the sight of many things, a sea of endless blue-gold light stretched across infinite leagues.","It was an ocean of pure dream-weather and sovereign potential, moving without waves or tides, reflecting a sky filled with trillions of turning constellations.","Infinite!","Standing upon the calm surface of this boundless sea were two figures in human form.","The first was THE Infiniverse. Her manifestation was breathtaking and terrifying in equal measure, her cascading hair composed of woven domains and crystalline void, her eyes holding the birth, expansion, and quiet collapse of uncounted civilizations.","She wore robes woven from overlapping dimensional lattices, her pale hands moving through the air with the absolute precision of a master architect at work.","Floating directly behind her were dozens of miniaturized Observable Existences, each one compressed to the size of a polished pearl, turning slowly in orbital rings. From these tiny wonders, thin golden threads were drawn continuously, dripping pure Distilled Cause Essence into wide, crystalline conduits that descended into the depths of the sea.","Beside those golden conduits ran eight radiant rivers of elemental matter.","Hydrogen, Helium, Lithium, Beryllium, Boron, Europium, Strontium, and Neodymium flowed in torrential ribbons of raw, purified light, looping around the pearl-like existences before merging into the grand design.","Above them both flowed a colossal cataract of blue-gold authority. It was the direct link to their Master’s Provenance.","THE Infiniverse took these streams, and with a sweeping gesture of her slender arms, she directed them across the expanse.","Across hundreds of realms spanning millions of gigaparsecs, the fabric of space and concept bowed. Entire clusters of Wheels of Existence and star systems, vast planetary sectors, and dimensional planes were being lifted away from the standard coordinates of reality.","The eight elements wrapped around their perimeters, Distilled Cause Essence sealed their seams, and the mantle of Provenance folded them deeply inward, transforming hundreds of realms into pristine, autonomous Elsedimensions.","No architect had ever walked their soil. No sentence from Those Who Remain had ever touched their skies. They were completely untainted, sterile to outside sight, and utterly unfindable!","Beside her stood Ruination.","Her manifestation was clothed in deep crimson silk, her hair burning like quiet supernovas as red-gold embers drifted from her shoulders. Her crimson eyes watched the folding of a Elsedimensions with tranquil appreciation, her arms folded beneath her chest as she leaned slightly toward her sister.","\" Since Sonder awoke in him ,\" Ruination said, \" Master has become very reflective of others. He has been looking outward, thinking about giving those who walked beside him a chance through a single endless Dream.\"","THE Infiniverse did not cease her weaving, her fingers twisting a river of Europium around an entire realm of three thousand star systems as she listened.","\" He has thought about his son ,\" Ruination continued softly, her gaze drifting across the blue-gold sea. \" He has thought about his daughter, his mother, the Queens of THE Infiniverse, and all those who helped him when his footsteps were still small. He knows they had their own grand dreams of brilliance before his shadow grew so immense that it covered their sky. He does not want them to merely survive in a golden cage. He wants to put them into an endless Provenance Dream of their own, letting them live their true dreams without the limitations of their origin.\"","Ruination smiled faintly, watching a miniature Observable Existence condense under her sister’s palm.","\" Those who can endure the longest in their dreams, those who attain tremendous power from within their own reveries, will wake to find themselves far grander than they are today. Erikson, Titano, Ul’moreth, Eon, Kazuhiko... all of them were once the heroes of their own legends. If they do not wake from their dreams in a single day, they may step directly into THE Transfinite Verse when their eyes open. If they do not wake for weeks, an entire epoch of years will have passed within their Provenance Dream, and they might open their eyes to find themselves standing in THE INEFFABLE VERSE. Perhaps they will inherit and advance the Infinite Scales he cast out. Perhaps he will impart knowledge of sovereign engineering to their souls to see what they can build. He simply wants to give them a chance.\"","...!","Sonder.","The realization that every lifeform drifting past possessed an interior existence as rich, complicated, and desperate as one’s own.","THE Infiniverse drew a massive band of Neodymium into her palms, compressing the perimeter of another forty realms until their spatial signatures vanished completely from the surrounding dark. Her expression remained cool, composed, and imperial!","\"I understand Sonder ,\" THE Infiniverse replied. \"I have observed how it operates in his eyes, and I recognize the mechanical elegance of allowing other narratives to mature. But I am not the biggest fan of it.\"","Ruination glanced sideways at her sister, an amused tilt touching her lips. \" You find fault with his compassion?\"","\"It is not about fault,\" THE Infiniverse said evenly, guiding a flood of Distilled Cause Essence into the foundation of a newborn Elsedimension.","\"It is about geometry. To me, Master is the singular, absolute center of existence. He is THE True Human Emperor, THE Human Dreamer, the only point of origin that matters in any continuum. When he looks at others and sees the fullness of their lives, his vision spreads outward. I do not wish for his gaze to be diluted by the small concerns of mortals who could not keep pace with his stride. I want him to look upon reality as an author looks upon a clean sheet of paper, with himself as the only hand holding the pen.\"","HUUM!","She turned her starlit eyes toward Ruination, her expression devoid of malice, filled only with the cold, immovable devotion of an empire built in his name.","\" Sonder makes him hesitate to crush what is weak. It makes him empathize with chickens before he drinks the soup. I would prefer him to be an absolute, unyielding tyrant who steps across existence without once asking the dirt if it minded his boots.\"","Ruination let out a soft, melodic laugh that sent gentle ripples across the blue-gold surface beneath their feet.","\" That is why you are who you are, Sister, and I am the blood,\" Ruination murmured, her crimson eyes softening as she watched the distant light of their Master’s Provenance pulse above them.","\" You want him to be an engine. But that is why I love Sonder. It enriches his humanity. It prevents him from degenerating into a hollow equation like Those Who Remain. The architects who view living beings as mere sentences to be edited, Descendants as cattle to be slaughtered, and existence as an empty stage. They are miserable, sleepless monsters who feel nothing because they believe only they exist.\"","Ruination reached out, catching a stray spark of crimson-gold mana in her palm and letting it dance across her fingertips.","\" Master is different because he remembers the weight of a single life. He knows the people who stood beside him were not scenery. They were the ground he walked on to reach the sky, and because he remembers, he will not discard them when the climb becomes steep. That humanity does not make him fragile, Sister. It gives his tyranny a purpose.\"","Ruination turned her gaze back to the endless blue-gold horizon, her voice dropping into a quiet, tender murmur.","\" We also have dreams, do we not, Sister? Even if our dreams are to always lift him up...\"","THE Infiniverse remained silent for several breaths. Her hands continued their flawless, rhythmic weaving, guiding the eight primordial elements into place as dozens more realms folded away into sovereign pockets of isolation.","She did not argue further, but a fraction of the coldness in her starlit eyes softened, acknowledging the truth in her sister’s words.","Together, the two manifestations continued their work in absolute harmony.","Across existence, nobody had had any conception of what was quietly growing in the dark.","Hidden beneath layers of absolute unfindability, THE Infiniverse was expanding at an unimaginable rate. Already, her engineered expanse held the conceptual weight and territorial immensity of several hundred complete Dimensions, folded so deeply into the bedrock of reality that if an Immense One looked directly at her coordinates, they would perceive only empty, undisturbed void!"]},{"number":5724,"title":"Chapter 5724: Chapter 5723: Wonder!","paragraphs":["In THE Chrysalis, Noah’s eyes focused upon eight microscopic particles hovering above his outstretched palm.","Hydrogen, Helium, Lithium, Beryllium, Boron, Europium, Strontium, and Neodymium.","They did not behave like ordinary physical matter. They turned in disciplined, concentric orbits, each particle emitting a faint, distinct frequency that subtly bent the surrounding light of the cavern.","Noah studied their rotation as his thoughts traced the architecture of THE Enduring Gu Elsedimension Ring resting upon his middle finger.","\" Out of every mineral, metal, and authority drifting across Existence \" Noah spoke into the quiet cavern, \" why do these exact eight govern the boundary of an Elseengine? Why not stellar iron, refined gold, or crystallized void?\"","From the illusory band beside his ring, a faint pulse of light stirred as Atlas manifested his translucent form.","The old engineer looked at the hovering particles with a flat, half-lidded gaze, crossing his arms over his chest.","| You think you are looking at mortal chemistry,| Atlas said. | You look at the names and your mind wanders to dirt and glass tubes of worlds with no authority, only playing with chemistry. These are not common rocks, Dreamer. When the First Sundering tore Existence apart, the grander Immense Ones did not simply leave a tidy path behind. They exceeded the Weave. They broke through the cloth, and the immense friction of their departure burned away their non-essential mass. What you hold on your palm are remnants of the eight primordial weights left in their wake. The physical ashes of those who exceeded that were scattered across existence.|","BOOM!","|Even lifeforms with no authority don’t know they harvest and utilize elements that could make unfathomable things when manipulated the right way...|","...!","Atlas pointed a translucent finger toward the spinning orbits.","| Hydrogen sets the boundary of combustion, the original spark of expansion. Helium cools the flame into a stable, slow-burning mantle. Lithium provides the crystalline skeleton so the vessel does not wobble. Beryllium carves the internal channels to direct the flow of intent. Boron absorbs stray conceptual heat, buffering the interior so the expansion does not shatter the shell. Europium coats the perimeter, rendering the domain opaque to outside observation. Strontium lends geometric memory, ensuring the vessel remembers its shape after taking a blow.|","The old man’s finger shifted, locking onto the final, dense particle spinning at the center of the ring.","| And Neodymium. The inward pull. It acts as the sovereign magnetic anchor of the entire lattice. Without it, the other seven layers would simply drift apart into empty space. Neodymium draws the surrounding conceptual volume inward, folding leagues of space into an indivisible point. That is why an Elsedimension can hold an ocean while resting comfortably on your knuckle.|","Noah observed the microscopic pull of the Neodymium particle, watching how the local light bent slightly toward its core.","The mechanics were sound, but mechanics alone were only half of the equation.","Noah closed his eyes, turning his perception inward to dissect the structure of THE Osmontian Tongue.","Language, at this level, was not merely sound; it was existential geometry. The letters he had unlocked, I AM, OSMONT, QUINTESSENTIAL, HUMAN, and PROTAGONIST, were complete, self-contained monuments of narrative weight. To force PROTAGONIST into a Common Dream Gu was to drop a mountain onto a moth.","Yet every language possessed morphology.","Noah analyzed the anatomy of his words, realizing that a sovereign letter could be partitioned into its underlying phonetic radices.","The letter I AM carried the core radix of BEING, which provided stability, presence, and rootedness in reality.","The letter PROTAGONIST, when stripped of its crushing imperial supremacy, held the foundational radix of AGENCY. It was the pure, unadorned concept of self-direction, the will to move forward under one’s own power without demanding that the rest of existence bow in subservience.","A Common Dream Gu could never bear the title of an emperor. But it could understand the concept of being, and it could harbor the quiet agency to dream its own dream without interference.","Noah opened his eyes.","He did not immediately reach for the second Gu. Instead, he raised his right hand and summoned a thread of Infinite Sanguine Mana.","The crimson-gold energy did not erupt with its usual destructive brilliance. Under Noah’s absolute control, the mana thinned until it became a hair-thin filament, scarcely wider than a single quark.","He guided the thread downward, weaving it directly into the surface of the starlight slab.","Next, Noah called upon his Telos of Adversity. He introduced a fraction of linguistic stress.","The coral groaned, microscopic cracks threatening to split the slab as the concept resisted the medium.","Noah did not force it. He directed the filament of Sanguine Mana to wrap around the fracture.","The crimson-gold vitality flowed into the fissure, acting not merely as glue, but as an alchemical flux. It cooled the friction between the heavy concept and the brittle stone, cushioning the impact and distributing the narrative pressure evenly across the rock.","A sudden clarity settled in Noah’s mind.","He summoned a single droplet of Distilled Cause Essence from his internal void, letting it hover beside the filament of blood.","With a precise command of his will, Noah drove the two substances together.","The Infinite Sanguine Mana and the Distilled Cause Essence merged, swirling into an iridescent, deep-crimson fluid that pulsed with a slow, heavy heartbeat.","|Infinite Sanguine Cause Mortar has been forged for the first time.|","...!","It possessed the fluid malleability of living blood and the eternal, structural permanence of a First Cause. It was a customized alchemical buffer, designed specifically to serve as a shock absorber between his sovereign tongue and a fragile carrier!","It was his own engineering and design not brought forth by Atlas!","Atlas watched the crimson fluid hover in the air, his translucent brows twitching slightly.","The old man remained silent, withholding any overt praise, but the lines around his eyes tightened as he recalculated his assessment of Noah.","Atlas cleared his throat, leaning against his illusory staff.","| Do not get arrogant, | Atlas said. | You made a decent mortar. That does not mean you know how to build a temple. Long before the First Sundering, the ancient First Lifeforms were so enamored with the sound of their own authority that they attempted to speak before they had grown teeth. They tried to shout commands at the sky, and in their haste, they bit their own tongues completely off, bleeding to death on the very soil they sought to rule.|","Atlas pointed toward the hovering crimson mortar.","| That is the Rule of being humble. Humility is knowing the capacity of your vessel. A mortal body must learn how to hold a whisper before it tries to roar an imperial mandate...|","The old man had begun to ramble on and on!","Noah carefully arranged his materials across the starlight slab in strict, methodical order.","From his internal realm, he drew the second Common Dream Gu, letting it rest gently within a protective dome of blue-gold dream essence.","Beside it, he placed nine droplets of Distilled Cause Essence, each one coated in a fine sheen of Infinite Sanguine Cause Mortar.","Surrounding them both, the eight primordial elements settled into their precise orbital distances: Hydrogen, Helium, Lithium, Beryllium, Boron, Europium, Strontium, and Neodymium.","Noah sat back, his breathing slow and rhythmic as he observed the assembly.","He would not carve his flesh right away. He would conduct a complete, theoretical dry run across the stone, testing everything until the margin of error reached absolute zero!","For the first time, he felt engrossed in a project that he wasn’t able to complete right away!"]},{"number":5725,"title":"Chapter 5725: Chapter 5724: Foundational!","paragraphs":["The theoretical alignments across the starlight slab concluded, dissolving the simulated fractures into calm ribbons of blue-gold light as Noah turned his full attention back to his own flesh.","He reached into his internal realm and drew out the second of his remaining three Common Dream Gu.","The creature rested quietly upon his knee, its translucent azure shell pulsing with a simple, unhurried reverie. It was small and fragile, breathing in slow rhythms that carried the faint scent of undisturbed silk, completely oblivious to the currents churning outside the coral cavern.","Noah looked down at it, his pupils reflecting the tiny insect as he prepared the strokes of THE Osmontian Tongue.","This time, he did not summon the raw, unmitigated weight of an imperial conqueror to crush the carrier. He drew upon the clarity granted by Sonder, understanding the interiority of the small existence before him!","The Common Dream Gu dreamed of enduring the cold, drifting endlessly through the dark while searching for a tiny pocket of warmth.","Noah did not seek to overwrite that dream. He met it.","He broke the Osmontian Tongue down into its fundamental grammatical strokes, taking I AM and fusing it directly to the core of THE PROTAGONIST.","It was not an assertion of tyrannical supremacy that demanded the sky bow down. It was the tempered essence of agency: the quiet, unbreakable declaration that an existence possessed the right to stand at the center of its own journey, to endure the frost, and to find the warmth that made survival meaningful.","HUUM!","From his fingertips, threads of Infinite Sanguine Mana emerged.","The crimson-gold energy narrowed until it split into millions of microscopic needles, so fine they bypassed ordinary physical dimensions entirely. Noah guided these needles forward, pricking the carapaces of the eight stabilizing elements spinning in their orbits.","Hydrogen, Helium, Lithium, Beryllium, Boron, Europium, Strontium, and Neodymium were simultaneously coated in a shimmering layer of Infinite Sanguine Cause Mortar.","Beside them, the nine droplets of Distilled Cause Essence were drawn into the formation.","Because the elements were shielded in the sanguine mortar, they did not clash with the pure potential of the Causes. The mortar acted as a perfect alchemical buffer, absorbing every stray vibration and cooling the conceptual friction that had detonated his previous attempt.","The nine droplets fused seamlessly into the elemental lattice, and the entire structure collapsed gently around the Common Dream Gu.","There was no shriek of terror!","The insect did not blacken, and its shell did not crack. Enveloped by the warmth of Noah’s tempered agency, the Common Dream Gu exhaled a soft breath of pure golden light, willingly surrendering its concept into the structural weave of the newborn Elseengine.","The lattice clicked into place without a single tremor.","The second attempt was at hand!","Noah brought his mind back to the golden anatomical diagram Atlas had projected, the intricate lines of the ancient engineer’s crowning achievement etching themselves across his thoughts with absolute clarity. Every channel, every anchor, and every elemental node along the Inscription was verified in a fraction of a microsecond.","Noah raised his right hand, pressing his fingertips firmly against the skin of his left forearm.","He guided the living Elseengine lattice inward.","The eight elements sank through the surface of his flesh: Hydrogen, Helium, Lithium, Beryllium, Boron, Europium, Strontium, and Neodymium. They wrapped around the radius and ulna, locking tightly into the marrow like an interlocking sleeve of starlight!","HUUUM!","Then, the script ignited.","Deep within the core of his bone, the Osmontian letters I AM THE PROTAGONIST blazed into existence!","BOOM!","The agony returned instantly.","It was not the chaotic, tearing detonation of a failed weld, but the deep, agonizing structural ache of living bone being permanently re-engineered into a sovereign relic. Two hundred decillion quarks groaned beneath the sudden, immense narrative density pouring into the limb, the sheer weight of an absolute identity pressing down onto the subatomic architecture.","Noah did not flinch. He did not let his arm tremble by a hair’s breadth!","His Teloi roared to life, locking with the unyielding supremacy of Quintessence to turn the crushing friction into fuel for the weld. The sovereign fire burned away the agony, tempering the marrow and forcing every letter of the inscription to seat itself permanently into his anatomy.","Light flared through the skin of his arm, turning the limb entirely translucent as the golden script took root.","Then, the blinding radiance snapped inward.","Crisp, magnificent prompts ignited across Noah’s sight!","|EXISTENTIAL FOUNDATIONAL NARRATIVE INSCRIPTION: TIER 1 (INCIPIENT)|","|Limb Anchored: Left Forearm.|","|Carrier: Common Dream Gu (Refined Elseengine Core).|","|Attribute Boons: +50 PROVENANCE, +50 VERITAS, +50 PONDUS, +50 OSMONTIAN MOIRAI.|","|Permanent Effect: FOUNDATIONAL ACCELERATION. The rate at which the user processes, integrates, and purifies authorities and attributes is permanently increased by 100%. The Quality of your Provenance is permanently increased by 100%.|","|Permanent Effect: PERPETUAL BARYOGENESIS. THE Infinite Provenance Baryogenesis no longer requires conscious cycles. The weight of Existence is drawn down onto every Provenance Telos Quark at a constant trickle, in every state: waking, dreaming, fighting, bleeding. A failed quark no longer collapses the cycle; only the failed quark restarts. Foundation density rises while you do nothing at all.|","|Permanent Effect: THE UNANIMOUS BLOW. Two hundred decillion quarks hold nine aims and no disagreement. When the anchored limb strikes, every quark expresses through the strike at once, and the blow carries the summed weight of a foundation that is entirely of one mind. Narratives of lesser Agreement do not resist the strike; they part. Cost: the carrier’s dream is spent with each expression and must be fed before the next.|","|Permanent Effect: BEDROCK. Trueness is now a floor. No external authority (subtraction, inhibition, rewriting, sentence) may reduce the inscribed attributes below the foundation’s floor. What was made cannot be un-made by what was merely given.|","|Permanent Effect: SEDIMENT-SHED INTEGRATION. Everything devoured seats clean. Distilled Cause Essence, devoured Narratives, consumed dreams: all of it integrates without residue, foreign echo, or impurity. The foundation takes only what is nourishing and sheds the rest as sediment. (This does not digest the indigestible. Poison that glows remains poison.)|","|Permanent Effect: ONE FOUNDATION. The foundation is inscribed once and expressed everywhere. Every body of yours in existence shares the inscription’s boons, because a foundation is not a location.|","...!","Damn.","Damn! Damn! DAMN!","The conceptual fire subsided, leaving behind a profound, cool stillness that washed through Noah’s Existence!","The skin of his left forearm sealed shut, smooth, translucent, and pristine. Yet beneath the surface of the flesh, etched directly into the bone and glowing with a deep, majestic gold, ran an intricate network of an Inscription that pulsed in harmony with his heartbeat.","It looked like a grand, imperial tattoo forged from pure starlight.","Noah slowly raised his left hand, turning his wrist as he inspected the finished work.","He clenched his fist.","The air inside the hollow cavern warped slightly, the starlight slab beneath him vibrating under the quiet, immovable density settling into his arm.","It felt completely immovable!","IMMOVABLE!","---","<THE Boundary of THE Chrysalis>","A silent armada of three hundred silver vessels sliced across the perimeter of THE Chrysalis.","These were merely some of the hunting groups dispatched from the Dimensions of Immense Ones, a mobilization of Descendants carrying the absolute will of their Fathers and Mothers!","Standing at the head was Kaelen-Tor, a high-ranking Descendant born of the direct bloodline of THE SPINDLE OF UNENDING WEAVE.","Her skin was the color of unpolished alabaster, her hair pulled tight in braids woven with strands of refined argent wire, and her garments were cut away at the chest to expose a terrifying marvel of stolen architecture.","Etched directly across her sternum, pulsing beneath translucent flesh, was a massive Narrative Inscription.","It did not belong to the old mortal frameworks, nor was it a crude imitation of forgotten blueprints. The inscription swirled with an unnatural, forced harmony between THE Primordial Source and THE Argent Loom, lines of primordial origin twisting around silver threads of absolute subjugation. It flared with immense Dimensionality, radiating a heavy, suffocating pressure that made the void around her buckle and moan.","Those Who Remain had not remained idle after breaking the Great Engineer upon the mountain. They had taken his blueprints, dissected his corpses, and integrated his stolen syntax into their own lineages, breeding Descendants who carried engineered sentences within their very bones!","Now that weavings of that Engineer returned, they unleashed them!","Crouched beside her boots were seven Argent Loom Hounds.","They were horrific, skinless quadrupedal monstrosities bred exclusively from the flesh of failed Descendants, their ribs exposed like the bared frames of a mechanical loom. In place of eyes and snouts, their heads were shaped like heavy iron shuttles, clicking and snapping as their jaws parted to reveal rows of silver needles instead of teeth.","They did not hunt by sight, nor did they track blood.","They existed solely to taste the subtle, forbidden vibration of unauthorized Elsedimensions and the microscopic friction generated whenever an unregistered lifeform attempted to engineer something from the fabric of existence.","Across the vastness of the existence, hundreds of similar groups were advancing in interlocking nets, carrying out the directives of a dozen different Immense Ones.","They were a force sent to exterminate any spark of sovereign engineering before it could ignite a fire. Some were spread across Observable Existences and Dimensions and endless darkness and Narratives of Existence others didn’t even know...and also places like THE Chrysalis!","Though of course, any group given a directive and access to a place like this...was unfathomably more powerful that a group that could be passing through Observable Existences, or inside a certain Dimensional Provenance Train.","Before Kaelen-Tor’s eyes, the existential command of Those Who Remain burned with cold, radiant brilliance.","| DIRECTIVE: PURGE.|","|Some coordinates within THE Chrysalis demonstrate anomalous frequencies of existence.|","|Execute total unraveling of all unknown weavings, foreign lifeforms, and isolated folds.|","|Zero verification required. Zero survivors permitted. If you meet a powerful anomaly, instantly call for help.|","Kaelen-Tor’s eyes were devoid of cruelty or wrath. She carried only the sterile indifference of an exterminator tending to an overgrown cellar.","Her armada did not carry crude physical ballistas or basic elemental cannons. The vanguards practiced the refined butchery of Argent Loom Engineering.","Racked along the decks of each galleon were tens of thousands of slender argent needles, forged from the calcified marrow of conquered First Lifeforms. When the hunting parties caught anomalous prey, they did not simply cut their throats; they drove these sovereign spikes directly through their existence and causes of their captives, pinning down their Depth, draining their Trueness, and unraveling their historical records to learn.","Ahead of the lead vessel, drifting peacefully in a hollow formed of petrified dream-silk, lay a small settlement of Primeval Ones.","They were an ancient, peaceful tribe who had inhabited this pocket of THE Chrysalis for Ages, their bodies carved from porous volcanic starlight as they quietly tended to a small nursery of Common Moss Gu.","They possessed no weapons, held no imperial ambitions, and asked nothing of the sky beyond being permitted to watch the slow drift of the centuries.","As the silver of Kaelen-Tor’s vessels entered their hollow, the tribal elders emerged, raising their hands in peaceful greeting.","Kaelen-Tor did not even look at their faces.","She did not ask for their names, she did not demand their lineage records, and she did not give them a single instant to speak.","HUUM!","Kaelen-Tor raised her right hand and tapped the center of her chest.","The Narrative Inscription across her sternum blazed with blinding, chaotic brilliance!","The Primordial Source roared to life, feeding pure originating heat into the silver threads of THE Argent Loom. A web of razor-thin silver light exploded outward from her ribs, expanding across thousands of leagues in less than a microsecond.","It was not an explosion of heat; it was an act of existential deconstruction!","The silver threads swept through the settlement, slicing cleanly through the porous stone dwellings, the nursery of Moss Gu, and the bodies of the Primeval Ones. The moment the threads made contact with an existence, they seized its narrative weight and pulled.","CRACK!","In the span of a single breath, the entire tribe unraveled.","...!","Their homes collapsed into sterile grey powder. The Moss Gu shriveled into black ash, their tiny reveries snuffed out before they could register fear!","The Primeval Ones screamed without sound as their skin, muscle, and memories were stripped away layer by layer, reduced to spools of raw, inert conceptual fiber that were dragged instantly into the hungry hull of the Vessel.","Ten seconds after the armada arrived, the entire settlement had ceased to exist. Not even a ghost remained to haunt the hollow.","Kaelen-Tor lowered her hand, the inscription on her chest settling back into a slow, menacing pulse as the Vessel continued its forward glide.","Then, at her feet, the lead Argent Loom Hound went completely rigid.","Its shuttle-shaped head snapped upward. It drew in a deep, desperate inhalation, its needle-teeth chattering as it caught a faint, lingering current drifting across the spatial medium.","It was a scent that made every hound in the pack shudder with violent excitement.","It was the faint, phantom trace of a sovereign weavings carried by existence. Maybe a sign of Engineering!","The lead hound threw its shuttle-head back and released a harsh, metallic bay that rang like an iron bell across the silent fleet.","CLANG!","The beast lowered its iron snout, locking its trajectory straight toward the south, pointing past the boundaries of the petrified silk and directly into the deep, turbulent, starlight ocean of THE Tide.","Kaelen-Tor’s eyes narrowed.","\" Alright, lets go see, \" she murmured, her voice flat and devoid of emotion.","She raised her hand toward the dark waters ahead, and with a single motion of her fingers her massive vessel advanced!"]},{"number":5726,"title":"Chapter 5726: Chapter 5725: Existence and Time! I","paragraphs":["<Pocket of Narrative Existence: THE Endless Dusk>","The spilled tea had soaked into the boards where she knelt.","The cold of the Fiend’s visit still hung in the air, and her throat still ached where his fingers had held it. She could feel the words he had pressed into her, sitting at the back of her jaw like a bruise. He had walked into her home and out again without once slowing his stride.","She had spent an age keeping still!","That had been the whole of her strategy. Stay quiet, hold what she had lost on the Mountain of Gu without stirring it, and maybe the currents would pass her porch by. She had told herself the stillness was a kind of strength. That keeping the past intact and undisturbed was itself a way of enduring.","The Fiend had taken ten seconds to show her what it actually was.","Staying still in front of Those Who Remain did not hide you from them. It only made you easy. An architect did not respect a thing that would not defend its own door. He looked at it and saw something that had saved him the walk.","The Widow got up off the timber.","The silk was wet at her knees. She did not look down at it. She straightened, and her spine came up out of the stoop it had held for Ages.","Behind her veil, the two halos stopped.","For as long as she could remember, since the sky over the mountain had gone grey, they had turned one way and pulled her grief inward, holding her still. Now they hung motionless for a breath. Then they turned the other way.","The grief she had been storing all that time stopped going in. It started coming out and hardening along the edge of her porch.","She reached into the deepest fold of herself, where she had buried it, and drew out the mobius ring.","She set it on the table, between the upright cup and the broken one, and pressed her fingertip to the spikes along its curve. She fed a thread of her own Trueness into the metal. The ring took it, and the line opened, running to Atlas past every thread.","\" What are you planning, Atlas?\" Her voice was level. \" What do you want to do? I...will not do it the way I did it last time. I will give you my power now, and whatever else you need. I do not know if you meant this, leaving your ring with me. But I am going to try to believe in possibilities.\"","WAA!","The porch was quiet for a long moment.","The mist beyond the timber did not move, as if the dusk were waiting to hear whether the dead answered.","Then something turned over inside the iron and the metal warmed under her hand.","\" Existence is full of things that do not care how safe you feel ,\" Atlas said. \" Everyone thinks they are untouchable. They sit up high, they build their little fences, they decide the sky owes them a favor. I thought so too, once. Grand workshops, a crowd of bright fools carving to my drawings, and I was sure my blueprints were law. I was wrong. I was loud and careless, and it cost me my hands.\"","The ring pulsed, keeping time with the reversed turn of her halos.","\"I am quieter now, humble ...\" he went on. \" Quieter, and meaner about it. When you have no hands left to swing a hammer, you learn fast which joint to tap to bring the whole ceiling down. You were grand once yourself, you know. Before you made a headstone of your porch, you walked the folds without flinching, and even Those Who Remain gave your perimeter room. What you did just now is a start. Hold your footing this time and you might...end up larger than you ever were. Maybe. Maybe...\"","The records in the band turned with a dry click.","\" So. There is work to be done. I have the first move already. An inscription. I want to take the eyes off them, off Those Who Remain. If they cannot see or hear...things become just a bit fairer.\"","...!","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah held his wrist up and looked at it for a while.","Under the skin, the inscription ran gold along the bone, keeping time with his pulse. He could feel the rest of it too, though there was nothing to see. The weight of existence coming down on every quark in a slow, steady drip, without him doing anything at all.","His arm just kept getting heavier and truer while he sat there, and he did not have to lift a finger to make it happen.","He flexed the hand once. The water near the slab pulled back from it.","Atlas flickered up out of the ring beside THE Enduring Gu Elsedimension Ring, leaning on a staff, squinting at the light under Noah’s skin like a man inspecting an engineering he half expected to find crooked.","|A clean Engineering ,| Atlas said. | What I designed for you is not a static stamp. It is a living foundational inscription. Right now, it is at Tier 1, Incipient, because you fed it a common Gu. But its framework was engineered with open joints. The moment you harvest a Rare Gu that resonates with its grammar, or the moment your own foundation undergoes an existential elevation, you can feed it again. The inscription will drink the higher concept, widen its channels, and elevate its tier.|","Atlas tapped his staff against the starlight slab, producing a dull, resonant clack that echoed through the cavern.","| More importantly, it is an inscription bound to your very existence. Mortal blacksmiths forge armor that gets stripped away when the chest is cracked open. Weak sovereigns carve runes into their skin, and the moment their flesh is turned to ash, they become naked again. What you have carved into that arm is woven into your narrative continuity. Even if an architect descends and cleaves you into countless microscopic fragments, scattering your meat across ten thousand dead dimensions, your existence will still remember the Engineering. The moment your blood knits back together, the inscription will be there, holding its full power.|","Noah lowered his arm to his knee and looked at the old man.","\" What about you?\"","Atlas paused.","\" You spent an age designing this, \" Noah said. \"You had the full set. Nine of these across your own bones, engines, all of it. And you still fell on the mountain. So which is it. Do you still have any of that, or are you just...an old man in a ring?\"","...!"]},{"number":5727,"title":"Chapter 5727: Chapter 5726: Existence and Time! II","paragraphs":["For a second Atlas said nothing. Then his chest shook and a cracked laugh came out of him, loud enough to bounce around the fissures.","\" Haha. The balls on you, Dreamer. I like you.\"","He wiped at nothing under his eye and settled back onto the staff, still grinning, though the grin thinned out as he went.","| Yes, I was grand. And existence is full of things that do not care how grand you are.| He shrugged . |When they came for me it was not a duel. Many of them pooled everything they had just to get through, and even that was not enough to break the foundation. They had to use IT.|","BOOOM!","The word dropped!","| IT is a strange thing ,| Atlas said. | The ones in the high seats cannot even hold it. They try to weave it in and their hands blister and their weavings come apart. I could hold it. There have only ever been a handful of us who could. That was the whole problem. They turned the one thing I could carry and they could not into the thing that broke my weavings.|","He looked away, off through the wall of the cavern toward somewhere Noah could not see.","|I am not going to tell you the rest of it here. Say the wrong detail out loud in a place like this and you invite eyes you do not want. But ask yourself how I am talking to you at all. A spirit does not survive its own body being taken apart. I am still here because of what I was, and I am not sitting idle either. Me waking up has already started things moving.|","He pointed the staff at Noah’s chest.","| Which is your problem, by the way. They are already moving. Descendants and authorities of Those Who Remain, the whole lot, out across the folds sniffing for anything that smells like engineering. They were nervous before I ever stirred. A few things happened recently to make them even moreso.|","|Someone reached for IT. Vakochev. He built himself scales, tried to stand against them, and they came together and ground him into nothing. The blood from that was barely dry when my old weavings started humming as they felt it. They know there is a hammer of engineering out there again.|","His face soured.","| So they did what frightened things do. They built a taller tower and unleashed...a Ruling of Existence. All those Mantles and rulings and systems you have been running into out there, that is not existence growing up on its own. It is a watchtower. They are spreading their gazes to ensure that they easily observe...more of existence.|","HUUM!","Noah sat still.","The Ruling, THE Provenance of Existence! They were a net, and the moment anyone worked outside it, the net twitched and the hounds came!","\"A net ,\" he said.","|A net ,| Atlas agreed, pleased with him . |I have my own aims in all this, and things I will keep to myself for now. I teach you because you did something with odds that should be impossible, and you might end up bending them further than I ever did. The bending and curving of Probability around your existence is key. But do not mistake that for me serving you. I am still arrogant. I still have my Elsedimensions tucked in folds you cannot picture yet, I still have my engineering, and I still have myself.|","He crossed his arms.","| Enough about me. Are you going to tell me anything about yourself, Dreamer, or do I have to go poking around your edges to find out what you are made of?|","Noah’s mouth moved.","His gaze drifted somewhere past Atlas and the coral, and when he spoke his voice was unique as if he was a man reading off something he had watched from a distance.","\"In the beginning, I was always born human ,\" he said. \" No inherent authority, no noble lineage, no spark. I had nothing but my ability to think, and even that, some in my early days might have judged as lower than average. But I was stubborn. When the world pressed down I did not break, and when obstacles appeared I persevered through them. I had nothing to my name. I rose from and forged everything I hold now, propelled forward by Infinity, Quintessence, and Tyranny. And, looking back on the journey, a healthy amount of luck.\"","The water barely stirred in front of him.","\" The one major change came the moment I stepped beyond my original Observable Existence. Once I crossed into the different dimensions, where space and time no longer obey flat geometry, I stopped living in linear time.\"","He turned his hand over and watched the gold pulse under the skin.","\"To everyday lifeforms, a life runs in a straight line. Yesterday, today, tomorrow. From this elevation, from the moment my Provenance fully awoke, moments do not follow one another like beads on a string. They exist at once. In one fold a body of mine sits in the brass corridors of a moving train, in a dimensional cabin. In another I stand on the shattered terraces of a golden mountain, looking down at a weeping patriarch whose home was decimated. Deep in my empire an ocean of blue and gold turns quietly while two sisters weave wonders into sovereign Elsedimensions. And here, in this cold hollow of petrified coral, I sit on a slab speaking to a man who died an Age before I was born.\"","He was quiet a moment.","\" After I attained Sonder, I started looking at the people who walk beside me with different eyes. They are not scenery, and they are not instruments in my ascent. They are the protagonists of their own weavings of existence. I find myself wondering how their stories are progressing, and how much time has passed for them. Because for all of us, and for all these higher powers that rule the folds, time does not move in a straight line. We sit in this cavern where the hours seem ordinary, and in another pocket weeks or months could already have slipped away. It is all a matter of...time...\"","HUUM!","Something slowed in his eyes.","\" Time. Time, time.\"","He said it four times, the last of them trailing, like a clock heard through a wall in an empty room. The mobius ring on his finger buzzed against the word!","Atlas watched him for several seconds, and the cynical smile went out of his face.","| Yes ,| he said, softer than usual. | Time is a terrifying and pivotal weaving of existence. Even I spent cycles trying to harness it for myself. Because with enough time, theoretically, anything is possible. A common stone can be pressed into a diamond. A mortal can build a bridge to the sky. An empire can learn how to bleed an architect.|","His staff caught a pale white light.","|I was going to teach you time much later as it has its drawbacks. Among the grand inscriptions that harness the different pillars of existence, the one tied to the flow of hours is among the most volatile. Too many possibilities. We could sit on this rock all day trading philosophies. But as you so eloquently pointed out, there is no... time.|","He paused, then broke into a loud, self-amused cackle.","| Haha. You see what I did there? Ah, being dead this long may have made me completely crazy.|","He shook his head, and his tone sharpened back into the focus of a craftsman adjusting his drawings on the fly.","| But your little speech shifted my plans, Dreamer. If your perception is already drifting off the line, we should not fight the current. Your next inscription will not be a shield.|","|We will make it about... time.|"]},{"number":5728,"title":"Chapter 5728: Chapter 5727: Existence and Time! III","paragraphs":["They would make it about time, Atlas had said, and the word was still sitting in Noah’s head when he tapped his left forearm against the edge of the starlight slab.","A dull thud went through the stone. No vibration ran up the bone. The skin did not redden. Under the pale surface the gold script sat there like iron driven into granite, steady and rooted, as if the arm belonged to a statue instead of a living man.","Then the water carried something through the stone. A thin scrape, faint, like needles dragged across glass, coming down from the upper shelf of the reef.","The band on his middle finger warmed. Atlas came up over his staff with a scowl.","| Stop admiring your arm, | he said, glancing at the ceiling. | We have company coming down the shelf. A pack of Descendants just entered the Tide.|","Noah did not move. \" Did they track the ring?\"","| Either that, your Existential Engineering, or the stink of the Gu you burned to ash earlier .| Atlas scratched his beard. | Doesn’t matter now. Those Who Remain still have working ears everywhere. I am building a way to deafen them, but for the moment their scouts are doing their rounds.|","\" How much can they report back?\"","|One pulse through Existence is enough. If a Descendant gets nervous and snaps a signal, no architect will bother sailing down. They will drop an anvil on the whole trench from above and wipe everything clean. Similar to what THE SLEEPLESS FIEND did here not long ago...|","Noah stood.","His fingers twitched once. In his chest, Tyranny pulled at him. He wanted to see what the arm could actually do against someone potentially powerful.","He set it aside.","Killing and battles was easy. Keeping the death quiet was the job.","\"I wont fight them in the open, \" he said. \" I will... build a room.\"","He walked to the mouth of the cavern. The water outside hung heavy and blue, lit in patches by glowing coral.","He raised his right hand, and instead of blasting mana out he drew it into threads no thicker than spider silk, coating each one in Infinite Sanguine Cause Mortar. The red fluid clung to the line, dull and sticky, smelling faintly of copper and old stone.","He cast the lines across the seabed. They drifted down and settled into the silt, weaving between the coral ridges like tripwires.","Then the eight elemental seeds. An engine compresses them into a ring to fold a pocket inward. Noah reversed the order and threw them outward. Neodymium into the far corners of the trench, its pull set to hold the edges shut. Europium along the ridges to swallow light and any scrying needle that came looking. Boron through the middle, to eat heat and shock before either could reach the surface.","Inside ten minutes the floor of the canyon was rigged as he used his Provenance, Distilled Cause Essence, and pivotal Elements to essentially make a trap of....an Elsedimension!","Above the reef the blue light faded. The water went murky silver. Long shadows dragged across the coral as the first vessels drifted into view, moving without a wake. Three hundred of them slid into the trench and spaced out in a wedge that closed off the open water overhead.","Noah stepped out of the hollow, climbed a broken coral spine, and stopped. His robes drifted around his knees, dark against the pale rock. No weapon drawn, no aura up. To the fleet above he looked like a wanderer who had drifted too deep!","At the prow of the lead ship, Kaelen-Tor looked down.","Her skin was chalk-pale, her braids tied off with silver wire. Her chest was bared to the sternum, and across the ribs ran a jagged scar where silver thread and dark red fire had been sewn together. It looked ugly, two metals beaten into each other before either was hot enough to melt, but it hummed hard enough to turn the water around her to glass.","Seven hounds paced the deck at her boots, no skin and no eyes, only pale muscle stretched over bone with iron shuttles for heads. Their jaws snapped, needle teeth clicking as they caught the scent off the seabed.","She did not waste breath on demands. To a Descendant with an order to purge, anything alive in an unregistered fold was trash to be cleared.","She looked down at him and lifted two fingers!","\" Pin him ,\" she said. \" Take his records and memories\"","WAA!","The silver hulls clicked together. From the bottom of three hundred vessels a lattice of silver light dropped like an iron grate, an Argent Loom array built to freeze a man’s legs, choke his mana, and hold him still while the needles worked!","It slammed down into the trench and hit the seabed with a dull crump!","Noah did not dodge. He stood under the falling light and watched the silver threads strike the ground.","The moment it came near him and touched the coral, the Infinite Sanguine Cause Mortar took the blow. The red sludge soaked up the force, darkened, and held!","Noah closed his left hand into a fist.","The perimeter snapped shut. Along the edges of the trench the eight nodes flared, Neodymium pulling inward, Europium turning the water black as ink to anything looking in, and the trench folded into itself with a dry snap.","The water did not shake. To anything swimming the Tide a league off, the canyon was an empty, blighted gully and nothing more.","Inside, the light died as an Elsedimension light years vast bloomed!","On the deck of the lead ship, Kaelen-Tor felt it go. She reached for the spindle at her wrist and tapped the connection that tied her to the Spindle of Unending Weave, and...","Nothing.","The thread did not glow. The line to her father was gone, cut as clean as if someone had taken shears to it!","She looked down over the railing. Through the dark water the wanderer on the coral spine had not moved. But the skin of his left arm had gone clear, and the gold script under it was bright enough now to throw light on the cracks in her own deck.","Haha. Had she actually found something critical?","She walked to the tip of the beakhead, boots clicking on the deck, and looked down through the dark water at Noah. Behind her the seven shuttle-headed hounds strained on their wires, iron jaws clicking in fast, nervous bursts.","She tilted her head, the silver wire in her braids clinking.","\" Who are you? Are you connected to the weavings of Vakochev? Atlas? Or did you dig up an old bone in the mud and think it made you something? Before this becomes a mess of authorities, tell me. Are you a talker?\"","Noah did not answer. He stood on the broken coral, arms loose, watching the silver plating of her vessel.","Her details resolved for him in clean lines.","| KAELEN-TOR - DESCENDANT OF THE SPINDLE|","|VERITAS: 212|","|POTENTIA: 218|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|PONDUS: 206|","|INSCRIPTION: UNSTABLE PRIMORDIAL-ARGENT GRAFT (TIER 2)|","Kaelen-Tor took his silence for an answer. \" A quiet one. Good. Saves time for me.\"","...!"]},{"number":5729,"title":"Chapter 5729: Chapter 5728: One Punch!","paragraphs":["She struck the center of her chest with a flat palm.","The scar across her sternum tore open in white light! A dense net of silver thread, superheated by the fire of THE Primordial Source, erupted from her ribs and fanned across the trench, miles wide in a fraction of a second, slicing through the coral.","Where the threads passed the rock went to grey powder, and the water behind the advance collapsed into vacuum.","The net hit Noah.","Red prompts flared across his sight.","|DECONSTRUCTIVE SENTENCE DETECTED: UNRAVEL DEPTH.|","|TARGET RECORD: You.|","|SUBTRACTION ATTEMPT: -50 VERITAS, -50 PROVENANCE.|","Then, his hand pulsed.","| BEDROCK ACTIVATED.|","|What was made cannot be unmade by what was merely given.|","|ATTRIBUTES LOCKED.|","A sound like spikes grinding on stone tore through the canyon. The argent threads caught on his skin, pulled taut, and stopped. White sparks fizzled off into the dark, and not one strand bit in. His numbers did not move!","Inside the band on his finger, Atlas let out a long breath.","| Look at that mess .| His tone was almost mournful. | They took my engineering and tried to build with it, and this is what they made. Primordial fire and argent thread forced together with nothing between them. Look at the seams leak. She is burning her own Existence just to keep the stitch from splitting...what a fucking mess!|","At the prow, Kaelen-Tor’s skin had gone see-through, her veins running violet as the graft ate her own vitality to hold the output!","Noah looked up at the three hundred hulls crowding the water above him.","\" You have no Provenance of your own ,\" he said.","His voice did not travel through the water as it landed in the mind of every Descendant in the trench at once.","He parted his lips and spoke one Word of THE Osmontian Tongue.","\" THE MORTAL COIL.\"","HUUM!","The cavern shuddered as he imposed...a change of standing. It came out of his chest like a ring of cold blue gold brilliance and washed over the three hundred vessels, the hounds, and Kaelen-Tor.","Wherever it passed, the borrowed ground went out from under them.","THE DOMAIN OF THE MORTAL COIL did not touch flesh. It took the scaffold away. Every thread inherited from Those Who Remain, every law granted by the Ruling of Existence, simply stopped applying, and left each of them with only what they were on their own.","They held zero Provenance. They owned nothing they had made. So the fall was catastrophic!","The silver light of the three hundred vessels went out like blown candles. On the decks the Descendants gasped and staggered, limbs gone heavy, eyes wide, the plain fact of a body with limits pressing down on their chests.","Kaelen-Tor grabbed the railing with both hands as only her...only her dimensionality resisted!","The inscription on her chest, cut off from the Loom that fed it, sputtered, and the stolen weight she wore like a mantle thrashed under the grey and could not get out.","\" Haha, what... what did you do, ugly fucker? \" Her voice had gone thin!","Noah did not answer.","He raised his left arm. The skin went clear, and the gold under the bone caught the dark water as a heavy Narrative Inscription activated!","I AM THE PROTAGONIST.","The Common Dream Gu in the lattice stirred, and its small dream of warmth was drawn into the script and spent. Two hundred decillion quarks locked. Nine Teloi held one aim!","He stepped forward on the coral and drove his left fist up into the trench.","THE UNANIMOUS BLOW.","No beam and no blast as the whole undivided weight of a foundation of one mind moved, carried forward through mass. The fist met the dead, sputtering web of argent thread, and the space holding them parted!","The water split with a sound like a gate slamming, a corridor tearing open through the sea, and the blow crossed the airless gap and struck the lead vessel!","BOOM!","The hull split down the middle.","The shock went through the deck and hit Kaelen-Tor square in the ribs. Cut off from most of her power by the Coil, the grafted Narrative Inscription had nothing to soften the blow, and the mismatched forces inside it turned on each other!","CRACK!","\" Agh!\"","She dropped to the splitting deck, dark blood spraying from her lips, her sternum tearing open from the inside as the silver wires snapped. The seven hounds gave dry, muffled whines as their threads dissolved to ash.","She stared down at her own chest.","One blow. Even stripped of her Father’s mantle she still held over two hundred in Veritas and Pondus, and yet she had broken like a clay cup!","Noah was on the deck before the debris settled. On the vessels around them the Descendants were still down, gasping under the Coil as the Mantles and Narratives sought to stand up. He crossed the splintered timber and stopped in front of her.","She coughed a clot of silver-streaked blood over her chin and looked up at his pupils.","\" You... are truly connected to Atlas?\" she wheezed. \" You think you are building something?\"","She laughed with one hand clutching the ruin of her chest.","\"I will tell you now. Whatever you think you are doing will not end in success. My Father, and all the others around him, are far too powerful. They decimated Atlas. They decimated Vakochev. They will decimate every tiny ant that tries to climb the ladder. Why don’t you all just stop?\"","Her fingers dug into the wood, shaking.","\" Existence is great. It is a paradise for those of us with power. We can have anything we want. You have the power too. You could have had everything. Why put yourself on a path of destruction?\"","Noah looked down at her.","\"A paradise where you crawl under someone else’s ceiling is a cage with a soft floor,\" he said. \" And I don’t like cages.\"","He drove his right hand down and closed his fingers on her throat. Infinite Sanguine Mana poured into her like hot iron!","Her eyes went wide, the last breath going out of her as her records came apart under the heat as he took everything!","|SEDIMENT-SHED INTEGRATION ACTIVATED.|","The corrupted Argent Loom threads and the bloodline of THE Spindle hit his foundation and separated off it like grease off water, pushed out through his pores to drop to the seabed as black grit. What was left, the clean weight and the bare frame of the Tier 2 inscription, ran into his Existence.","Kaelen-Tor went limp and turned to pale dust between his fingers.","On the vessels around him, panic ensued!","Noah did not wait for them to do anything. He raised his hands and struck out into the water rapidly. Again. Again!","Phantom fists of red-gold mana bloomed through the trench, each one carrying the blunt weight of his foundation, each one hitting a vessel like a dropped boulder.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Descendants were flattened before they could draw breath, and the hounds were pounded to ash.","Inside half a second the fleet was gone. No screams left in the water, only ash!","Only ash!","Noah lowered his arms.","He swept a wave of Sanguine Mana across the canyon wall to wall. It ate every drop of blood, dissolved every scrap of bone, and scrubbed the stone of any lingering resonance. When he dropped the inverted Elsedimension, the trench looked the way it had an hour ago. Cold, dark, empty.","To anything watching, three hundred vessels had sailed into the Tide and vanished.","He looked at his left arm as out of and over abundance of caution, even though he had done everything inside an Elsedimension, his figure turned dreamy and illusory, as he began taking steps that covered countless Gigaparsecs as he moved once more!","Noah moved, dreamy and illusory, and while he moved the prompts caught up with him.","|SEDIMENT-SHED INTEGRATION: COMPLETE.|","|The immensity of KAELEN-TOR has been stripped, cleaned, and seated.|","| +24 VERITAS. +22 PROVENANCE. +26 PONDUS. +21 OSMONTIAN MOIRAI.|","He felt the weight of it settle in as he crossed the dark. She had carried the mass of an architect’s bloodline and generated none of it herself, and none of that had helped her once the scaffold was gone. Now the raw part of it, the clean weight under all the borrowed thread, was his, and it sank into his foundation without a tremor!","Then the second prompt arose, and this one made him slow.","|SALVAGED: architect-grade blueprint recovered from the grafted inscription.|","|THE SCARWEFT OF THE STOLEN LOOM (Tier 2 Narrative Inscription).|","| Fuses THE Primordial Source and THE Argent Loom into a single expressed authority. Unstable. Corrodes its bearer. Powerful regardless.|","He did not try to inscribe it. He lifted the blueprint out of his own foundation, a lattice of grey and silver light no larger than a coin, and sent it up into the band on his finger, into the keeping of the ring where Atlas could look at it.","Atlas looked at it for a long moment and said nothing at all.","| So this is what they did with it, | Atlas said finally.","| They took what I designed for pairing two authorities and they forced the two worst ones through it. It eats the Descendant who wears it as she was burning her own existence just to keep it lit.|","The blueprint turned slowly in the light of the ring.","|Well, even broken like this, even chewing its own bearer to the bone, it harnesses a tremendous amount of power. If they had not run into someone like you, someone who could strip the power out from under them, that woman would have been deadly..|","Atlas was quiet again.","| And this is only a Descendant’s version. A hand-me-down. They took a great deal of my work, and if they kept at it, kept changing it, kept advancing it the way I would have... they did not stop at what they hung on their children. They will have applied the grander pieces to their own existences. Which means the ones sitting in the high seats are a good deal more than they were when they broke me on the mountain.|","The blueprint folded shut and sank into the ring’s keeping.","| Alright .| He exhaled. | Alright. No matter. We got interrupted. We were talking about time.|","Noah kept moving through the dark water, waiting.","| When it comes to that, | Atlas said, | you have multiple bodies wandering around, yes? Keep this one here. Search for more Gu, you will need many as ingredients. But I need one of your other bodies to go somewhere. One of my closed-off Elsedimensions.|","Noah’s steps slowed.","| Provenance Lifeforms may already be crawling through it. With a Descendant you always know whose hand is on the leash. With a Provenance Lifeform, you will not know whether they came for themselves, or whether they came because Those Who Remain told them to so...go carefully as you are still young and brittle, and there are many much more powerful than you!|","---","<THE Infiniverse >","Noah floated in a slow storm of sandy gold light.","It was a Dream Elsedimension, one of his own, and it turned around him in quiet drifts of light. He hung in the middle of it with his eyes half-closed, his human body bare and unmarked, the blue-gold brilliance of dreams pouring off his skin and folding back into the storm. There was nothing to do here but be still, and for a while he was.","Dreams had been with him for a long time. When his Provenance had woken it had come up wearing the qualities of Infinity and Dreams as it was only natural.","His Provenance had grown fast. Faster since Atlas!","Atlas was grand, and there were pieces of the old engineer that Noah could not see the bottom of. But Atlas was still just another person. A teacher, a voice in a ring, a set of blueprints and grievances.","Noah had come up out of Apocalypses leaning on no one, and he was not about to start leaning now. What Atlas gave him he took and made his own. The rest he did himself!","His Provenance had crossed a hundred a while ago, into the range he had decided to call the Ineffable Verse, and what he could do as THE Human Dreamer now was a great deal more than what he could do before. He could feel it when he was still like this, the reach of it was....enormous.","His other bodies were out in Existence watching everything turn. There was the reemergence of Atlas and also of Vakochev.","But Noah had his own emergence to think about!","Sonder had changed the shape of his Provenance. It did not only grow when he fought or built. It grew when he touched the dreams of others, when he watched them, helped them, moved through them. So a thought had been sitting with him for a while, outlandish and entirely his: he could dream the dreams of the people he knew!","He could watch them unfold the way the Immense Ones watched the narratives they had draped across existence, an eye in the sky over their own little stories.","\"I dream of being an eye in the sky that mimics the gazes of Those Who Remain. I am grand, and I am immense. But I am not alone in existence. \" His voice was quiet.","\" Let me see the dreams of the people who got me here. I can be grander while I watch them, or help them, or move them. Let me start an infinite dream. And for now...\"","He drew a slow breath.","\" Let my narrative track down Eckert. THE Great Usurper. Let me dream.\"","HUUM!","Light rose off his body in incandescent waves and took him apart and put him back together as something else.","His human shape thinned into brilliance and spread, and where a man had floated there was now an eye. It was enormous, blue and gold, its lid opening across a span that had no edge Noah could find!","Its pupil was not round. It was a mobius strip, a single band folded through itself, turning slowly. And out from the eye in every direction ran an ocean, blue and endless, going on past where light could reach.","Prompts bloomed across the surface of it.","|THE Human Dreamer initiates an Infinite Dream: THE EYE THAT DREAMS OTHERS.|","|You will observe, and where you choose, touch the unfolding dreams and narratives of another.|","| Cost: 75 PROVENANCE ESSENCE, to shape your gaze in the likeness of Those Who Remain and to render you as difficult to perceive as your craft allows.|","|Your narrative will read, to a passing gaze, as one more watcher come to observe a narrative already in progress. A weak one. Beneath notice.|","|Warning: a gaze far stronger than your mask may see through it. Do not linger where the strong are looking closely.|","The eye blinked once, slow, and was gone.","And Noah began to dream.","—","<THE Dimensional Provenance Train>","Far above a certain Cabin, a blue-gold eye opened in the sky.","Below it a Dimension churned, dark and violent and mid-story, a narrative still unspooling across the ground far beneath. Noah looked down through the eye and found that he saw everything at once and from above as it was...distant.","Prompts settled over his sight.","|You have entered an Infinite Dream over an active NARRATIVE OF EXISTENCE.|","|A powerful narrative already observes this place. Its gaze presses on everything below.|","|Your own gaze is masked. To the watcher, you read as a lesser observer, weak, drawn in to watch a story already being told. Your narrative is not making itself known.|","|The observing gaze will most likely ignore you, taking you for something far beneath it that wandered in to spectate.|","...!","Noah let his gaze fall.","Below him spread thousands of Descendants, and threaded through all of them he felt one aura sitting idle and enormous, a single mind wearing a crowd. Eckert. THE Great Usurper!","But the Usurper was not alone down there.","At the front of it stood a man raising a bow, an ordinary-looking man with nine gems burning across his chest, drawing on an army shrouded in darkness and power. Alexander, THE Peacemaker!","And behind THE Peacemaker stood three more.","Descartes. THE Primordial Paradox. THE Living Paradox!","Noah’s eye blinked.","They were all together?","The prompts finished settling.","| NARRATIVE OF EXISTENCE: THE TRAGIC HEROES, is unfolding.|","|Observing authority: THE OVERSEEING ONE.|","...!"]},{"number":5730,"title":"Chapter 5730: Chapter 5729: A Glorious Dream! I","paragraphs":["Noah looked down, and it was like standing on the ceiling of the world.","That was the gift of the mask. Shaped to look like one of Those Who Remain, his gaze sat over the Cabin the way theirs did, high and unhurried, and the whole story churning below him lay open like a map he could take his time with.","He didn’t have to reach for anything. It came to him. Every rank of Descendant, every current of dark power, every thread of the thing THE Overseeing One had staged, all of it hung open under the blue-gold eye, waiting.","He’d done nothing but dream, and the prompt came anyway!","| You are dreaming a dream quintessential to THE Human Dreamer: to watch existence as the watchers do, and to be one of them without being one of them.|","|Provenance rises for the sheer scale of the thing dreamed.|","|+9 PROVENANCE ESSENCE.|","Growing while he sat still. It was a strange feeling. He understood now why the watchers in their high towers never seemed to tire. For the right kind of thing, watching wasn’t idle.","It was eating.","His panel settled into the corner of the dream.","|THE True Human Emperor / THE Human Dreamer|","|VERITAS: 207|","|PROVENANCE: 219|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 208|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 226|","|(Totals shown. THE Enduring Gu Elsedimension Ring contributes +20 and THE Existential Foundational Narrative Inscription contributes +50 to every attribute, folded into the above.)|","|Inscription: THE Existential Foundational Narrative Inscription, Tier 1, left forearm. Perpetual Baryogenesis. The Unanimous Blow. Bedrock. Sediment-Shed Integration. One Foundation.|","He let the numbers go and looked at the people.","That was the first thing Sonder had taught him. He looked at their dreams, and every existence below him turned into a small cloud of gold, and inside each one was the single thing that being wanted more than anything else.","He started with Eckert.","The Great Usurper sat still inside a stolen body, one mind wearing a thousand men, and his dream was the smallest thing Noah had ever pulled out of something that big. Eckert dreamed of an easy life .","Sit still, grow stronger without trying, let the stories he cleared pay out their loot on their own and drop it in his lap. Let the unity spread by itself. Never lift a hand again.","Not a conqueror’s dream. A grand thing’s dream of never having to try again!","Noah moved to the man with the bow.","The Peacemaker dreamed of peace, but not a soft one. His was a peace he built himself, big, and where it had to be, bloody. He’d loved people once and put them in front of something, and it had cost them, and under everything he did now ran one flat promise. Never again!","He would make Existence safe for what he loved even if he had to drown half of it to do it.","Peace, at whatever it cost.","Then the three who didn’t belong here, standing behind the bow.","Descartes dreamed of a face. He wanted to stand in front of an Immense One, look it in the eye, and tell it plainly that it was wrong. He wanted to turn the whole of existence back into a thing of the mind, where greed and power weren’t the point of anything, where thought ran Existence instead of hunger.","The Primordial Paradox dreamed of understanding. He wanted to hold the contradiction of existence in his hands and turn it, to catch the impossible thing whole, and then, having caught it, to change it, with the paradox out in front of everything he made.","And Erwin, the Living Paradox, dreamed of knowing. He wanted to sit at the still center of all of it, every fact and record running through him at once, the man who knew everything and was known by all of it. Under that, quieter, ran something else. He’d let his teacher down once. He wasn’t going to do it again.","Noah held all five dreams at once and understood.","They weren’t the same dream. But every one of them could be helped by the same hand, if the hand knew where to push.","Then his gaze went to the middle of the dark army, and he found the thing they’d been set against.","—","The Dark Lord stood at the center of his own shadow.","Tall, old, in no hurry. His details came clear for Noah in cold, clean lines.","| THE DARK LORD|","|VERITAS: 116|","|POTENTIA: 121|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|PONDUS: 114|","|Authority: DIMENSIONALITY THAT NULLIFIES. What his power touches ceases to hold whatever authority it held.|","Over a hundred in everything you could count. Noah saw why the Overseeing One had picked this one to break heroes on. Eckert and the rest were big. This one was bigger, and worse, his power didn’t add to a fight!","It took away.","Whatever it touched just stopped being what it was, and a thing that could unmake power by brushing against it was a wall no borrowed strength could climb.","Then Noah read the Dark Lord’s dream, and stopped.","It wasn’t what the Overseeing One had written him to be.","The Dark Lord didn’t dream of winning, or of killing the heroes sent at him, or of pleasing the eye above. He dreamed of being left alone. A place that was his, that nobody reached down into and rearranged, where the ones under his shadow answered to him and not to some hand in the sky writing endings for all of them. He’d been given the part. He hadn’t asked for it. And under the defiance ran the oldest, plainest thing in the whole story. He was tired of being a piece in another man’s game.","Noah looked at that dream for a while.","It...could be worked with.","—","|THE OVERSEEING ONE observes his narrative with satisfaction.|","|The heroes are outmatched. The Dark Lord holds the center. The story bends toward the ending he authored.|","The battle started below.","The dark army came on slow, a tide of shadow, rank folding into rank, and the ground went grey ahead of it where the Dark Lord’s power ran out in front of his soldiers like ink in water.","THE Peacemaker held the front with the three behind him. Noah could see the shape of it before a blow landed. The heroes had strength. The Dark Lord had the one thing strength couldn’t touch. Where the two met, the heroes’ power would just stop being power, and then the shadow would close over what was left!","Good ending, as staged endings went. The Overseeing One had picked his ground well. A thing that unmakes is the right executioner for a story about heroes who rise, because the higher they climb, the more there is to take when the dark finally reaches them. Every gain the story let them make was only more to lose at the wall.","This was a show, put on for no one but the man putting it on, a story told to a mirror. And the people in it were real, and would die for real, so a bored thing in the sky could watch itself be clever.","How fucking abysmal.","So Noah started helping.","He didn’t come down, and he didn’t show his hand. His narrative stayed masked, a weak watcher come to spectate, under the Overseeing One’s notice. What he had was quieter than a gaze, and it was his alone.","A long time ago, before any of this, back when Eckert and THE Peacemaker and THE Primordial Paradox all still lived in the same Observable Existence he did, Noah had left something in them. A thread of his old Infinity, seeded into three of them. It had cost him nothing to leave. It cost him nothing to reach now. His Infinite Sanguine Mana, which he could spend forever, ran down those three old threads like water finding a channel it had cut a lifetime back.","He aimed it at their dreams.","THE Peacemaker drew his bow at the dark army, one gem burning on his chest. Noah pushed his old Infinity into the man’s dream of a hard, chosen peace, and the arrow left the string carrying unfathomable immensity.","Mind you, Noah’s trueness and Pondus were above 200 each!","It cut a road through them.","BOOM!","| The Peacemaker’s shot exceeds its measure.|","|THE OVERSEEING ONE notes the discrepancy with mild interest.|","Eckert sat idle, and his unity crept through the army the way it always did, mind to mind, unseen. Noah fed the old thread in him and the easy dream sharpened. The unity didn’t spread faster. It spread quieter, sinking into the dark ranks under the Dark Lord’s notice, seeding a thousand shadowed soldiers without lighting one of them purple where the eye above could catch it.","Eckert did nothing, and grew, and that was exactly his dream, so the dream carried it!"]},{"number":5731,"title":"Chapter 5731: Chapter 5730: A Glorious Dream! II","paragraphs":["The Primordial Paradox raised his hands, and where he stood the fight bent, two things true at once. Noah pushed his old Infinity into the man’s dream of catching the impossible whole, and the contradiction around him got deeper!","Dark soldiers who struck at him found they had both struck and not struck, couldn’t settle which, and stood there with their weapons out while the fight went past them.","Descartes and Erwin held the side as he helped them the only other way he had.","He reached across the folds, into the storage of his own Realm, and drew out the thing he’d carried since Vasileia burned.","The skeleton of a Provenance Lifeform. Aurelius’s gift, the dim golden bones from the sacred spring, the ones Descartes had asked him for before they parted. A corpse of a Provenance Lifeform, no reason given.","Noah didn’t know what Descartes wanted it for. He didn’t need to. Through the dream, spending his own Provenance this time instead of his Infinity, he set the golden skeleton down beside the man in the middle of the fight, quiet, unremarked, a thing that was suddenly there where nothing had been.","| Provenance spent to manifest a requested object into the dreamed narrative.|","|-5 PROVENANCE ESSENCE.|","Descartes’ hand closed on the bones like he’d been waiting for them, and something on his side changed that Noah didn’t fully follow.","Descartes had asked for a dead Provenance Lifeform and given no reason, and a man who dreamed of turning the world back into a thing of the mind didn’t ask for corpses idly. Whatever the bones were to him, they were part of an argument he was building, and Noah had just handed him the piece!","Noah was learning bit by bit.","What mattered the most was...placement. The Immense Ones ruled by pressing down, laying their frames over the folds and making everything climb inside. Noah was doing the opposite thing from the same height.","He wasn’t making anyone bigger than their dream. He was letting each of them be exactly as big as their dream already said they were, and clearing the small things in the way. Quiet work. It left no marks!","And it grew his own Provenance while he did it, because for THE Human Dreamer, helping a dream come true was the same act as dreaming.","| Provenance rises as you shepherd the dreams of others toward their fullness.|","|+6 PROVENANCE ESSENCE.|","—","| THE OVERSEEING ONE frowns.|","|His heroes are not dying on schedule.|","The fight turned, slow, the way Noah had pushed it. The Peacemaker’s shots cut deeper than they should. The Primordial Paradox held a stretch of ground that should have folded.","Eckert’s quiet unity had gone into a third of the dark army with not one purple eye to show for it. And whatever Descartes had done with the bones was holding the side that should have broken first.","None of it looked like help from outside. That was the point! Each hero was just doing what his dream said he could do, a little more than he should have managed, and no eye looking down would find a hand behind any of it. They were rising. That was all. Heroes rose!","But the Dark Lord didn’t fall.","He stood at the center and let the fight come to him, and where his power touched, the heroes’ new strength just stopped being strength. The Peacemaker’s deeper shots hit his shadow and came apart into nothing.","The Primordial Paradox’s held ground met the shadow and stopped being held. Even Eckert’s crept unity, reaching at last for the middle, thinned as it got near him, because you can’t turn a mind on a thing whose ground has been pulled out from under it.","The heroes rose, and the Dark Lord ate what they rose with, and the fight ground toward a wall.","—","| THE OVERSEEING ONE senses another gaze upon his narrative.|","HUUM!","Noah went still inside the dream.","| THE OVERSEEING ONE assumes a peer has come to watch.|","|He is embarrassed.|","That was the thing Noah had counted on and hadn’t been sure of!","The Overseeing One couldn’t see him for what he was. He saw a watcher, and took it for one of his own kind, another Immense One drifting past to look in on the story he’d staged. And the one he’d backed to win was struggling in front of company.","| THE OVERSEEING ONE will not be seen to author a narrative that falters.|","|He lends the Dark Lord his backing.|","Power came down out of the sky into the middle of the dark army, and the Dark Lord swelled with it. His shadow spread wider, faster, hungrier, eating the ground the heroes had won back in big swallows.","The Peacemaker’s road closed. The Primordial Paradox’s ground folded. Eckert’s unity got shoved back to the edges and pinned there!","He’d done it to save face in front of a peer who wasn’t there. And it was working.","Noah watched his quiet work come undone and didn’t panic. He’d known it could happen. He fed the three old threads a little harder, patient, keeping the heroes on their feet instead of pushing them ahead. He’d never been trying to win the Overseeing One’s story. He’d come to see it, to keep the people in it alive, and to learn who the Dark Lord was.","And the Dark Lord, swollen with a borrowed eye’s power, did a thing the Overseeing One hadn’t written for him.","He turned his back on the heroes.","He looked up. At the sky, at the thing pressing down on all of them, and when he spoke his voice came up out of the whole dark army at once!","\"I didn’t ask for your power ,\" he said . \"I didn’t ask for the part, or the enemies, or the ending you drew for all of us.\"","WAA!","Eckert’s unity crept to the edge of his shadow and stopped, and he let it. Didn’t strike it down. Didn’t even look at it like a threat!","\" These aren’t my enemies ,\" he said, still looking up. \" You made them my enemies. You made me their Dark Lord. You sit up there and move us around and call it a story.\"","The shadow drew in close around him, and for the first time it didn’t look like a weapon. It looked like a man who’d decided not to move!","\"I mind your hand in my life more than I mind losing to these four. A lot more. Take your power back. I never wanted it.\"","...!","|THE OVERSEEING ONE is silent.|","|THE OVERSEEING ONE decides this narrative is no longer worth the watching of peers.|","| He withdraws his backing.|","|\"A defiant tool is a broken tool. Enjoy your death, all of you.\"|","The power went out of the Dark Lord all at once, and the gaze lifted off the Cabin, and THE Overseeing One pulled his attention back like a hand off a board!","The story didn’t end as it just lost the man who was writing it.","Noah’s eye held over the Cabin and didn’t blink.","Not my enemies, the Dark Lord had said!","Noah had heard him!"]},{"number":5732,"title":"Chapter 5732: Chapter 5731: A Glorious Dream! III","paragraphs":["The story didn’t end when THE OVERSEEING ONE left, it was only made...free.","Noah watched from above, unblinking, as the Dark Lord straightened in the middle of his shadow and felt the sky go empty over him. No more gaze pressing down. No more hand moving the pieces. And instead of relief, the thing let out something that in a smaller creature would have been a laugh!","He’d been holding back. That was the part none of the heroes had understood. The whole time the Overseeing One watched, the Dark Lord had fought the way the story asked him to fight, a wall, a thing that stood and took and gave nothing. He hadn’t been trying to win. He’d been trying to be left alone, and standing still was the closest a chess piece got to that.","Now no one was watching. Well, or so he thought, so he stopped standing still.","The shadow came off him all at once as it dropped over the whole floor of the Cabin like a lid closing on a jar, and everywhere it touched, Exietence stopped meaning anything. This was his real power, the thing the Overseeing One had leashed to a role, and it was worse than nullifying strength!","It nullified everything.","The Peacemaker loosed a shot filled with Causes and the arrow simply forgot it was an arrow halfway to him. The Primordial Paradox held two states at once and the shadow reached them and neither state was true anymore, neither false, just gone.","Descartes’ philosophy and wonder, whatever he’d built with the golden bones, met the falling dark and lost the argument it had been making, its logic pulled out from under it mid-sentence!","HUUM!","Noah felt the fight tip. The heroes had been rising while the eye held them to a story. Now the story was off, and there was nothing above them anymore, and there was nothing holding the Dark Lord to a shape!","He could not be beaten. That was simply true. A thing that unmade meaning could not be out-argued, out-shot, or out-thought, because argument and arrow and thought all stopped being what they were the moment they came near him. The heroes were going to lose, and this time there was no author to complain to about it!","Except for one thing the Dark Lord had missed.","Eckert.","—","Back when the eye still watched, Eckert’s unity had crept quiet through the dark ranks, mind to mind, and reached at last for the center. The Dark Lord had felt it come and nullified it, the way he nullified everything, and it should have thinned and died at the edge of his shadow like all the rest.","It hadn’t.","Noah had held it there. A single thread of his old Infinity, fed patient into Eckert’s easy dream, keeping the unity bound to the Dark Lord’s edge even as the shadow tried to unmake it. It had been a small thing, unnoticed, a splinter under a fingernail while the giant fought with both hands. Now the giant had turned all his weight on the heroes, and the splinter was still there, and Noah pressed on it.","’ This man does not wish to be a chess piece,’ Noah sent, down the old thread, into the mind wearing Abbadon’s stolen body. ’ Erase everything about his will, entirely, and let him rest. Then you can use him. He will be your sharpest weapon yet.’","For a moment nothing answered.","Then Eckert’s unity, held to the Dark Lord’s edge by a hand it hadn’t known was there, stopped creeping and started to bite.","BOOM!","The shadow flinched. For the first time since the Overseeing One left, the falling dark that unmade everything it touched met a thing it could not unmake, because the unity wasn’t power and it wasn’t meaning. It was a decision, one mind spreading into many, and Noah’s Infinity had welded it to the one place the Dark Lord’s authority couldn’t clear it off.","A voice came back up the old thread, dry and amused.","’I thought it might be you, when things started to go crazy down here ,’ Eckert said, in the quiet where only Noah’s Infinity could hear. ’ The little pushes. Too neat to be luck. ’","Something in the tone almost smiled. ’ I’d like to catch up. Talk. It’s been a while, and I have questions. But not now. Let me focus on eating this monstrous Dimensionality of his and doing what you asked. This is going to take everything I have.’","The unity dug in!","Noah watched from above, and he thought about dreams.","He was giving the Dark Lord his. The Dark Lord had dreamed of not being a piece in another man’s game, of a domain that was his, of never again having a hand reach down and write his ending. And Noah was about to make it true. No more author. No more role. No more being moved!","He was going to erase the will that had wanted all of that, and let the being rest, and use the shell.","A dream could come true, Noah thought, and not come true the way the dreamer had hoped. The Dark Lord would get exactly what he asked for. He would never be a chess piece again. He would simply stop being anyone who could be played, which was, in the end, the only way a being like this ever got free.","He wondered if that counted. Whether a dream that arrived sideways like this was still a dream, or whether it turned, somewhere in the crossing, into a nightmare. He didn’t have an answer. He wasn’t sure the difference mattered to the one who got to rest!","Prompts bloomed quiet across the eye.","| You have guided the dreams of five existences toward their fullness within a Narrative of Existence.|","|THE Human Dreamer grows for shepherding what others could not reach alone.|","|+14 PROVENANCE ESSENCE.|","| A dream has been fulfilled by your hand, though not as the dreamer imagined it. The Human Dream deepens on the fulfillment and on the cost.|","|A new understanding settles: THE FULFILLED DREAM AND ITS SHADOW. You perceive, now, the gap between a dream as wished and a dream as granted.|","Noah let the prompts fade.","On the floor of the Cabin, the heroes felt the fight change under them and did not understand why.","The Peacemaker lowered his bow. His shots had been dying against the shadow, and then, all at once, the shadow stopped coming for him. He looked at the Dark Lord, who had turned his whole weight away from the heroes and toward some struggle at his own center, and then the Peacemaker did a thing he had not done in the whole battle.","He looked up.","He looked at the empty sky over the Cabin, at the place where the pressing gaze had been, and something in him went still and wary. He had felt the eye leave. He had felt the fight turn the moment it left, and turn again just now, and both turns had come from nowhere he could point to. For half a breath he almost believed there was still something up there. Another watcher. A hand he couldn’t see!","Maybe even someone he knew very well!","He looked back down.","Beside him, Descartes had done the same. A glance up, a flat unreadable moment, a look back down at the golden bones in his hand. He said nothing.","The Primordial Paradox and Erwin held their ground and watched the center, where the real fight had gone.","The Dark Lord was losing, and he did not know to whom.","His shadow, which unmade everything, could not unmake the thing spreading through him. He tore at it and it held. He nullified it and it was still there, because you cannot nullify a choice the way you nullify a force!","Eckert’s unity climbed through the monstrous Dimensionality one thread at a time, backed by Noah’s terrifying power, and every thread it took, it turned, and every turn was one more piece of the giant’s own power now answering to the mind in Abbadon’s body.","The Dark Lord fought hard, then harder, then not at all.","And somewhere in the fight, Noah thought, the will got what it wanted. No more hand in the sky. No more being moved. Just the long quiet of a thing finally, completely, left alone!","The struggling stopped.","The shadow, which had fallen over the whole Cabin like a lid, went still, and then it did not lift, but it changed hands. It stopped being the Dark Lord’s and started being Eckert’s, all that nullifying weight now bound under one idle, patient mind.","BOOM!","The Dark Lord sank to one knee.","He knelt, and behind him, across the whole floor of the Cabin, his dark army knelt with him, rank after rank of shadow folding down toward the being who now held their master’s power, the mind wearing Abbadon’s stolen body at the center of it all.","Eckert stood among them, idle as ever, having lifted no hand for any of it, a tired thing that had wanted only to sit still and grow stronger without effort. And here, without effort, he had grown by an entire army and the monstrous power of the being that led it.","His dream, too, coming true!","Above the Cabin, Noah’s blue-gold eye held over the kneeling ranks, patient, unnoticed, and did not blink.","One dream ended so another could rest. He wasn’t sure it was mercy. He wasn’t sure it wasn’t.","He let the dream carry him back up, out of this particular Narrative and story, into a unique space in this Infinite Dream he had initiated at the cost of 75 Provenance Essence.","He did not want to show himself before Eckert and all others as he didn’t want his brightness and his Dream to overshadow theirs!","Just like him, they were their own individual existence in their own grand journeys.","He did, however, want to talk to an old friend as among all those down there, the monster spreading unity was his closest.","So he tugged on his weavings to bring him to that unique space of his Infinite Dream where he could decide where to take his gaze next!"]},{"number":5733,"title":"Chapter 5733: Chapter 5732: That Uncrossable Line!","paragraphs":["<A Record Lost In Shattered Scales>","An unknown number of years ago, they brought Vakochev to a grandmother half-dead.","The grandmother had no name that mattered to the grand powers and no Provenance worth their notice, only a small warm house at the quiet edge of a dying Observable Existence and a very long memory.","She had known the maker of the Scales since before he was grand, back when he was only a stubborn boy in a tribe near a mountain- when she called him Tokoloshe.","And so when they laid the ruined thing that had been Vakochev across her table and left, leaking Causes and Dimensionality from a hundred wounds that should each have killed him, she was not surprised.","She put water on to boil. She had mended him before. She would likely mend him again, if he was foolish enough to keep living the way he lived.","He had gone against The Vheldrani. A Provenance Lineage older than most laws, a bloodline so deep and so terrible it had pushed two of its own children up past the threshold and out into the Dimensional Skies.","Two Immense Ones grown from a single tree, and the tree still standing, still proud, still certain that a thing which had birthed two of the Immense was a thing that answered to no one.","Vakochev had walked up to that tree and put his fist through it anyway.","For his trouble he had most of his existence hanging out of him, and he lay on her table while she worked and did not complain.","He had learned long ago that she had no patience for the complaints of people who had chosen their own wounds.","\" Why ,\" she said, when the bleeding had slowed.","She seemed...tired, like someone who has asked a beloved fool the same question across an Age. \" Two of that Lineage sit in a place we cannot see. You knew it before you went. You knew what backed them. And you went anyway. So...why?\"","He was quiet for a while. She thought he had passed out.","Then he replied.","\" There is a practice in their lesser holdings. In the small Observable Existences they own but do not bother to rule, where the lives are short and the Causes are thin. When one of the Vheldrani children nears the threshold, when it is close to becoming what its parents already are, it needs to be fed. Not food but...Foundation. So they go down into one of those small holdings, and they take the newborns. The very newest. The ones a day into breathing, before a life has had time to become a life, because a Cause that has not yet been spent is the purest thing there is to eat.\"","The grandmother’s hands did not stop moving over his wounds, but they slowed.","\" They harvest them, \" Vakochev said. \" They empty a whole Observable Existence of its first breaths and they render them down into a broth of unspent beginnings, and they feed it to a child of their bloodline so that child can climb a little faster. The parents who wake to find every cradle in their world gone cold on the same morning are told nothing, because you do not explain rules to peasants. I saw the cradles. I counted them until I could not count anymore, and then I went and found the tree that ate them.\"","\"And that is your business how? \" she said, though her voice had changed. \" You did not know those infants. You never could have. They are gone now, every last one, regardless of anything you did.\"","\" They are,\" he agreed.","\" Then you nearly died for nothing. For strangers. For ash. Against a Lineage that could unmake you between two breaths and felt nothing while doing it, because they are so far above you that your dying is nothing to them.\" She wrung the cloth out ths was bloody red in color.","\" The Vheldrani do not believe your right and wrong apply to them. By every measure that exists, they are correct. A being that high is not judged by the rules of the low. Nothing judges them. There is no one left up there to do it.\"","\"I know,\" Vakochev said.","\" Then why?\"","And he turned his head on her table, and he looked at the old woman who had mended him more times than either of them could count.","\" Because a rule that only binds the weak is not a rule,\" he said. \" It is a leash. They tell the low that right and wrong are real, and they build their whole order on the low believing it, and then they step over the line themselves whenever it suits them. They want the leash on everyone below and no collar on themselves. And the moment I decide their height excuses them, I have agreed with them. I have said the line is real for me and not for them. I have put on the collar and handed them the leash myself.\"","He breathed heavily!","He was quiet a moment, and when he went on.","\" They think it ends when the cradles go cold. They took the first breaths, they fed the broth to their child, and they walked away certain the thing was closed. The small ones are ash, and ash forgets, so the account is settled.\"","His ruined hand closed slowly on the edge of her table.","\"It does not end. Those parents will say the names of their children when this holding has rotted down to dust. They will say them when the star that lit their world has gone dark and cold. And when the last light anywhere in existence gutters out, when there is no one left in all of creation to hear it, some small ruined thing will still be floating alone in the black, saying a name into the dark that took everything, and the Vheldrani will have forgotten an Age ago that a name was ever theirs to take.\"","\"That is what they actually did, Grandmother. Not a killing. A killing ends. They opened a wound with no bottom, one that keeps being inflicted long after everyone who inflicted it has gone home to eat. And they will never feel the weight of it, because the whole of their order is built so that the ones on top never have to.\"","He breathed gloriously!","\"They are not above right and wrong. Nobody is. They are just tall enough that no one has told them no. So I told them no. That is all I did. I told two of the Immense no, out loud, with my fist, and they will remember for the rest of their long lives that a thing beneath them said it.\"","WAA!","The grandmother said nothing for a long moment.","Then she went and took the water off the boil, because it was ready, and she made him tea he was in no condition to drink!","\" You will die of this someday ,\" she said.","\"I know ,\" said THE Maker of the Scales.","\" Good ,\" she said as she smiled with quintessential pride. \" If ever it happens, just know that I...am endlessly proud of you. And as always...Persevere. In the face of the impossible, Persevere. In the face of the unthinkable, Persevere! \"","...!"]},{"number":5734,"title":"Chapter 5734: Chapter 5733: An Idle Existence!","paragraphs":["The space where the dream lived was a strange one, and Noah was still learning what it could do.","It was not the sandy-gold storm his body had floated in, and it was not the Cabin he had watched from above. It sat between them. A room made of nowhere, held open by his own Provenance, where he could pull his attention out of one story and hold it still before deciding where to send it next.","Versatile, was the word he kept landing on. It did more than he had asked it to!","Seventy-five Provenance to open the Infinite Dream, and it had been a heavy price. He did not regret it, but he felt the size of what he had spent!","He did not know much about the Provenances the other First Lifeforms carried. There had never been anyone to ask. He had the one he shared with Thalia, the two of them holding a single grand thing between them, and there was the strange separate one her father wore, and beyond that, the record was thin as he didn’t do much research for others.","But he suspected, looking at what his own could do, that his was one of the grandest ones! Of course, this could be his own hubris.","He was only human, so he could be prideful! Superbius and Humilitas ran through him all at once!","But his Provenance did all this. It let him hide his own existence from the highest watchers in existence, borrow the rulings the Immense Ones had strung across everything, and dream himself into their exact seat, a gaze over a story, present and unseen.","That was not a small thing. Standing here in the room made of nowhere, looking at the plain human body he had shaped for himself in the space between spaces, he understood that it was closer to terrifying than he usually let himself think.","Then, a few feet from him, the air folded and a second body stepped out of it.","Eckert.","He came through looking like a handsome king who had misplaced his kingdom and did not much mind. Dark hair, a face built for easy confidence, and eyes that would not settle on a color. Blue, and then not blue, then something warmer, then something colder, changing from one blink to the next, as if the man behind them was one thing in this instant and a different thing in the next and had made peace with being both.","He saw Noah’s blue-gold body across the empty room, and he did not bow, and he did not posture. He crossed the space and wrapped Noah in a hug.","Noah blinked.","Then he brought up his arms and returned it!","Eckert pulled back and held him by the shoulders, looking him over, smiling!","\" Why so surprised,\" he said. \"It has been weeks for me. A little more, maybe. And you are the strangest thing I have been near for the longest stretch of my whole existence, all the way back to when the two of us barely had a spark to our names.\"","\"From Primordials in The Primordial Cosmos...we have come far. The us of this moment can look at our past selves running through Cosmos as mere ants we can crush with a shred of thought...\"","...!","His changing eyes were fond.","\" Growing apart from you was a curve I had to learn. There were plenty of times I wanted to call out for help. I would get to the edge of it, right to the edge, and then I would stop myself and think, there was a time before Osmont existed at all. When people hit a wall, or fell into trouble, back before there was a you to call, did they all just sit there waiting for someone who had not been born yet?\"","He shrugged. \" No. They got through it. So I persevered. And here we are.\"","Noah looked at him, and he couldn’t help the smile.","Two thrones bloomed out of the dream behind them, blue and gold, and the two of them sat.","\" You got past all of it, though, \" Noah said. \" And you climbed at a strange pace. You almost kept up with me.\"","\" Hah. Almost?\" Eckert leaned back into the throne. \" You don’t have to soften it, big guy. I made my peace with that a long, long time ago. Existence is full of wonders and full of monsters, and I stopped measuring myself against you before I even understood what you were. Anyone who measures himself against you tends to dig an early grave out of his own thoughts and climb in.\"","He waved a hand. \" No. I climbed as fast as I climbed, on my own, and it is more than fine that I am nowhere near you. Existence is vast. Maybe there is a timeline somewhere where one of us sits out ahead of you. Who knows.\"","His eyes changed color again as if amused. \" Maybe in every timeline your Infinity just wins. Doesn’t matter. What matters to me is living true to what I am. I found that lining myself up with existence, with the actual shape of me, threw my unity wide open. And the shape of me has always been, and is idle. I am...an Idle Existence.\"","He said it grandly, and then he said it like it meant something!","\"I am. I AM .\"","HUUM!","The dream buzzed around them, waves of it stirring at the words, and prompts opened quiet across Noah’s sight.","|You are gazing upon an existence that carries a unique Trueness, one you helped forge.|","|Your own PROVENANCE and VERITAS rise by 1.|","Noah shook his head slowly, and he almost laughed.","\" Just how idle have you been?\"","\"I went back to my roots .\" Eckert spread his hands like a man showing off a garden he had let grow wild on purpose.","\" Every Observable Existence I spread my unity into, every Dimension, I lay down my Idle System over it. And then the Causes that hold that place together, the ones that make it what it is, they have to feed me. Idle Loot, dripping back up the line into me. Into my existence. My Trueness. My weight.\"","His grin widened. \" So I worked it out. If I seed myself across enough of existence, across enough different points in time, I can be a thing that sits in the dark weavings of it all and does absolutely nothing. Nothing at all. And every nanosecond that passes, without me lifting a single finger, I get grander. And grander. And grander still!\"","WAA!","He spread his arms in the throne, delighted with himself.","\" Now what ,\" he said, \" is that if not a dream come true.\"","BOOM!","His trueness rang out and the dream shivered with it, the whole space between spaces buzzing like a struck bell, and Noah found himself pulled all the way into the conversation, leaning in!","So he stretched the moment out. Long, and then longer, out toward the edge of infinity, and held it there!","He was doing something he almost never let himself do.","He was simply talking to a friend!"]},{"number":5735,"title":"Chapter 5735: Chapter 5734: Boundless Dreams!","paragraphs":["While one of him sat on a throne in a dream and talked to an old friend, another of him was at work!","This body sat on golden sand, on a shore inside THE Infiniverse. An endless sea ran out from it in slow blue-gold swells, and behind him lay island farmland so quiet and so full!","He thought about his people while he worked.","His children. His mother. The Queens. The ones who had walked beside him across his journey. The Emperor Penguin, Erikson, Titano, Ul’moreth, Kazuhiko, all the rest.","They were technically safe in THE Infiniverse all this time.","But safe was not the same as growing. Shelter kept a thing alive. It did not make a thing strong.","In the cass things went wrong, their Dimensionality could not be so weak that all then could be broken with a single foot coming down!","Of course, he would not just give them power. He thought of the jade lifeform in a story Atlas told, who had never once failed and shattered the first time he met a wall, and Noah had no intention of building a house full of jade lifeforms.","He would give them a place to earn it.","He called the full weight of his Provenance up out of himself and let it pour onto the sand.","Infinite Sanguine Mana came with it, crimson and gold, and the eight elements turned in the air over his hands, hydrogen through neodymium in their strict order. Nine droplets of Distilled Cause Essence condensed beside them. And into all of it he threaded the two things that made this his and no one else’s: THE Precept of the Waking Dream, and the fresh gold script of the Foundational Narrative Inscription running down his forearm, feeding the whole working a foundation that would not crack under its own size.","He began to build.","HUUM!","It was not a shelter, and it was not a weapon. It was a place to live a life in!","Time inside would not answer to time outside. A day out here on the shore would be a hundred years in there. That was the baseline.","And what they earned in there would be real when they woke!","A dream is usually a thing you wake up from and leave behind. Not this one! Built on his Provenance, mortared with Distilled Cause Essence, fed by his Infinite Sanguine Mana, the dream would hold onto whatever a sleeper forged inside it, every insight, every rank of Trueness, every scrap of Dimensionality won through struggle, and when the dreamer opened their eyes, the dream would hand it to their waking body and make it true.","HUUM!","| THE SOVEREIGN PROVENANCE DREAM ENGINE has been engineered.|","|A place to live, struggle, and advance. Power forged within crystallizes without on waking. Time within is decoupled from the continuum.|","The working finished, and it rose off the sand.","A chrysalis of blue-gold light, enormous, faceted, turning slow above the shore, its surface running with the same script that ran down his arm. It hummed!","Time.","Again and again, time was a factor as another body had already been sent out to head towards an Atlas Elsedimension where he would further throw himself into the weavings of time!","Noah looked at his design for a moment. Then he closed his eyes and called his people.","They came onto the golden sand one after another, and the shore filled.","His mother came, and Henry, and Seo-yeon. Adelaide. Barbatos. Eon, Naldine and the other Queens. Kazuhiko and Titano and Ul’moreth and the Great Beyonder, and behind them a long tide of others, every face he had gathered across a long climb!","Even the ones who were more record than flesh now, the weavings Oppenheimer, Commander Feng, a dozen more, took shape on the sand and stood among the living!","Noah sat before all of them as no pressure rolled off him. No aura pushed anyone back. He was only a man! Only a Human Dreamer!","He told them calmly about the Immensity all around them.","The Dimensionality where a monster could be standing right before you...and you wouldn’t even be able to perceive it. He told of Primeval Ones, Descendants, Provenance Lifeforms, THE Immense Ones and everything he was shielding them from!","\"I have kept you safe ,\" he said. \"I would keep you safe forever if safe were enough. It may not be enough.\"","Then he showed them the chrysalis.","\"I have Dreams, but so do you all. Dream an endless and glorious Dream in here. Your own lives, your own troubles, your own enemies, your own long roads. A hundred years in there for a day out here, more if your existence can bear more. Whatever you win in the dream, you keep when you wake.\"","\"There is a library inside, everything I have ever learned or gathered, arts, techniques, and THE Infinite Scales. Study them if you like. Follow them if they fit. Or throw them out and build something that is only yours. I don’t much care which. I care that you come back able to stand next to me instead of behind me.\"","For a moment nobody moved.","Then Kazuhiko, THE Emperor Penguin, and Erikson stepped forward as they did not ask a single question!","RAA!","They walked to the chrysalis and entered in a flash of brilliance!","Henry, Seo-yeon, and others followed!","After that, the others slowly went as their eyes shone brilliantly!","A hairy Ul’moreth, yet another one of Noah’s Teachers, looked at Noah in a face hidden by boundlless obsidian gold hair as he also disappeared. THE Big Stepper made a move as he might make something out of THE First Tongue more than Noah did!","Noah’s mother was the last to go as she came up to him and floated beside him.","\"I am already living my grandest Dream, but I will see what more is out there. After all, I am the origin of...your Infinite Dream. If I get serious, could I make something grand happen?\"","His mother smiled as if she were joking as she let the threads of dreams wrap around her too!","Noah couldn’t help but smile.","The chrysalis hummed, and millions of fine threads spun up around the dreamers, weaving the shape of the lives they were about to live.","Out in the waking part of THE Infiniverse, their bodies were laid into warm pools of Infinite Sanguine Mana, and their cells began to drink.","Noah stood over them for a little while.","THE Infiniverse manifested at his side, and Ruination beside her as they were quiet.","Noah looked at the chrysalis a while longer, at the turning threads, at his people!","Then he stepped back and left it to the two of them.","\" Tell me...\" he said, \" when the first one opens their eyes.\""]},{"number":5736,"title":"Chapter 5736: Chapter 5735: A Terrifying Narrative I","paragraphs":["As his people began to dream endless dreams of their own, noah returned to explore the immensity of his own terrifying dream!","Eckert was still talking when Noah set his gaze after...THE Creature.","He could sit on a blue-gold throne across from an old friend and listen to him explain how he had turned laziness into a system, and at the same time, with the same attention, reach out and follow a different thread somewhere else.","So he reached. He found THE Creature’s weavings inside THE Dimensional Provenance Train and threads of dreams pulled him along!","He meant only to look in on a friend he had not seen in a while.","Truly, this was all he meant to do!","Waves of blue-gold light pulsed and pulsed all around for a short while as his consciousness moved alongside his grand Provenance.","The dream carried him into a Cabin, and he opened his eye in a sky full of eyes .","The weavings of existence that communicated exactly what was around him told him a great deal of many things in the first nanosecond as...","He went still.","He had come in over the Tragic Heroes with one gaze above him, and that had been enough to make him careful. This...was not one!","’ Fucking hell...’","His Provenance pulsed as he became extremely careful!","The prompts came before he could count them.","| You have entered a Narrative of Existence observed by several of Those Who Remain.|","|Observing: THE OVERSEEING ONE. THE UNPAID COLLECTOR. THE GLOATING JAILER. THE CACKLING BUTCHER. THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR. THE SLEEPLESS FIEND.|","|One further gaze is present and is not observing the Narrative.|","WAA!","THE OVERSEEING ONE, sour with a humiliation he had not finished digesting, the same gaze that had staged the Tragic Heroes and walked away from it!","THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, who had burned half a lineage over a stolen lifeform and promised to come back for the rest!","Noah had stood under both of those. He recognized their brilliance!","And THE SLEEPLESS FIEND.","Oh, this fucker.","He let his gaze go to that name now and barely dared to hold it there. What hung in that part of the sky was not a shape so much as a brightness that never rested, woven, restless, the light of something that had not closed its eyes in countless ages and did not intend to.","He looked at it for the space of a breath and looked away, because even masked, even beneath notice, looking at the Fiend felt like standing too close to a thing that would eventually notice it was being looked at.","Information began to flow to him as his dream pulled and pulled!","| NARRATIVE OF EXISTENCE: The Weaving of IT.|","|Two lifeforms within this Cluster carry Shards of Existence. Within the Shards are weavings of IT.|","|Collapse the bearers. Expose the Shards. What slipped the hands of the Immense may be glimpsed by whoever holds them.|","|The prey holding The Shards: THE CREATURE. THE WRITER OF MYTHOS.|","|The hunters: THE INFINITY EATER. THE CHAMPION. THE USURPER. And THE ZENITH OF SUBJUGATION.|","The Sealed One, or really one of his Vessels, was also here! It was packed!","Noah did not move his eye as he did not let the mask so much as flicker. He hung at the far edge of the gallery, a small weak watcher come to spectate, and the gathered high seats did exactly what he had bet his existence they would do.","They took him for a newcomer. Something lesser drifting in to see a story it could never have staged. Only THE OVERSEEING ONE glanced over as he still seemed embarrassed and did not look for long!","He let himself breathe, if a dream can breathe. Then he looked down.","Below the gallery spread a cluster of Dimensions coupled together into one great wound in the side of the Train!","Rivers ran through it, and the rivers were the dead. Cities stood in it, and the cities had been raised by the unburied out of whatever they had left behind. Gates opened in it, and every gate opened only downward.","The sky over one Dimension was the underside of another Dimension’s floor. Every region was a different death, and they went on, region beyond region beyond region, further than even his gaze could chase!","A cluster of underworlds!","And in one of them, upon the bank of a river that ran grey and slow, a Descendant ferryman stood in a flat boat with a pole in his hands.","He was taking coins. Coins that pulsed faintly with Existential Narrative!","A thing that looked less a Descendant than a collapsed, half-illusory lifeform came up out of the water, pressed something into his palm, and stepped down into the boat, and the ferryman pushed off and poled across the grey.","By the wear on the pole and the coins heaped at his feet, he had been doing this for a very long while, and all around the boat, beneath the slow grey surface, obscene collapsed Descendants swirled and drifted like ghosts.","Noah looked at that for longer than he had meant to.","Then the hidden-gaze spoke, tbe gaze that was not listed among other Immense Ones, and the words carried her fury across the whole of the sky!","| THE MATRIARCH OF INK objects. My Descendant is not a game piece.|","The other gazes did not stir. THE OVERSEEING ONE answered her the way a lord answers another...or maybe even a servant who has spoken out of turn at his own table.","| Every single lifeform apart from us is a piece that we may play with however we wish. Have you grown so attached to something so feeble, and so lesser? You would not do something so detrimental to your own existence... would you?|","The ink went darker. It did not reply!","And far below in the Cluster, upon a stretch of dead ground beneath a sky that was some other Dimension’s floor, a woman with silver-white hair calmly opened a book.","The Glorious Writer of Mythos!"]},{"number":5737,"title":"Chapter 5737: Chapter 5736: A Terrifying Narrative II","paragraphs":["The first hunter reached THE Writer of Mythos before Noah had even finished looking around!","THE INFINITY EATER came across the underworld with an infinite sea of Dimensionality heaving at his back, and that sea was all of what he was, density without end, weight without a bottom, a tide that had been grinding against existence since before most of the Train had even been laid down!","Noah knew this one. This was the farmer whose fields had been drunk to their roots by him!","But he...he was not here for Noah. He had come for the woman with the book, and he came for her like a flood comes for a house!","Yet she did not lift her eyes from the page.","Noah looked down upon her with Sonder, and he saw at once what the gallery hungry for prey had not troubled itself to see!","She was a Descendant. Bred, spoken, a sentence with a bloodline, the way all of them were. That much they all knew. What some had not looked at was the rest of her!","She brimmed with her own Provenance! Not borrowed and not inherited, but hers, generated from within, precisely as Noah’s was his own!","And around her turned seas of Existential Narrative, slow and wide and immense, the single most guarded thing an Immense One possessed, and she wore it openly in the middle of a hunt like a grand coat she had simply decided never to remove! Someone up in that sky had handed her their very Narrative to wear, and Noah did not need to guess which gaze it was.","He looked past all of it, down to her dream, and it was the strangest dream he had yet read!","She...wanted a story she could not control!","That was it. Not power. Not survival. Not even the Shard they said she held within her. She had written every ending she had ever seen coming, an eternity of endings, and she had grown so weary of knowing them all that she had walked into a Cabin where Immense Ones fully intended to kill her, and she had done it on purpose, because here, at long last, she might actually lose!","So she wrote.","Her pen moved once across the page, the words rising off it heavy with weight, and a figure stepped up out of the book and onto the dead ground!","THE ONE WHO RETURNS!","A person! A shape every story had always carried somewhere within it, the one who was lost and came back again, given now a body and a stride and a purpose, and it walked straight into the Infinity Eater’s endless tide and met it head-on with seas of illusory Dimensionality and Provenance.","HUUUM!","The sea crashed down, and it did not go through!","She began writing tropes and archetypes on her books as shockingly...they manifested in existence.","She wrote again, unhurried and serene. THE FALLEN CHAMPION rose off the page, broken once and standing regardless, and struck at the Eater’s side! She wrote a third time, and Noah watched the Eater’s whole infinite weight lurch to a halt in confusion, because THE TRAITOR AT THE GATE had appeared behind him!","Behind him! The Eater swung his enormous head to stare at a thing that had no business standing there, and he did not understand, could not understand, how it had come to be!","But Noah understood exactly how it had!","He knew this. He had done this himself as he was writing tropes into scenes as absolute law and letting probability itself bend to keep the story true. She... was doing the very same thing! She was doing it with the pen held out in the open, where the whole gallery of monsters could watch, and the archetypes she wrote did not merely tilt a fight as they stood up and fought it themselves!","The gallery stirred at last. THE CACKLING BUTCHER was delighted, and said as much! THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR was bored, and said that too! THE SLEEPLESS FIEND said nothing at all!","And in the very middle of it, in the middle of holding back an infinite sea with three stories and a pen, Calliope stopped.","She looked up.","Not at the gallery but well...past it! To the far edge of the sky, where a weak watcher hung and had hung since the moment he opened his eye, small and masked and beneath the notice of anyone!","She blinked once with surprise.","Then she looked back down to her book, and she wrote a single line.","And grandly, in the next moment, Noah felt his weavings buzz as words arrived on a unique frequency of his existence!","They arrived directly within his Provenance, the way only one writer could ever place them into another...","| Oh my. Are you another existence with the capability to steer and write the narratives of existence? And for you to be so bold as to write yourself as though you were an Immense One, and even stand among them! Wow! Hello. I am Calliope. Who are you?|","...!","At her shocking words, Noah was silent.","He gauged this unique lifeform from the far edge of the gallery, this being who could bend the narratives of existence and was somehow not one of the Immense Ones watching her, and he was entirely, dangerously curious! So he gazed upon her fully, and the weavings of existence answered his gaze with her measure!","| CALLIOPE, THE WRITER OF MYTHOS - DESCENDANT OF THE MATRIARCH OF INK|","|VERITAS: 330|","|PROVENANCE: 299|","|POTENTIA: 207|","|PONDUS: 204|","...!","Noah’s eye went wide!","Her POTENTIA and PONDUS sat in the low two hundreds, respectable! But her VERITAS blazed at three hundred and thirty, and her PROVENANCE at two hundred and ninety-nine, towering over the rest of her like a cathedral built over a cottage! Such Trueness! Such Provenance! She held an existence more true and more self-generated than almost anything he had ever measured, and she wore it under a mask of serene boredom while an infinite sea tried to drown her!","And even as he drank in the numbers...","| Are you trying to quantify my power? That is an invasion of privacy. And you didn’t even answer me.|","The words arrived in his Provenance, delighted and pointed, and then they sharpened.","| Should I start screaming very loudly to the Immense Ones watching, that the other gaze they are ignoring is not who they think it is? Shall I drag you into this mess, fellow Writer?|","...!"]},{"number":5738,"title":"Chapter 5738: Chapter 5737: A Terrifying Narrative III","paragraphs":["A threat! It was casual, playful, and absolutely lethal, dropped between them like a coin onto a table!","Noah’s eye squinted.","He did not panic, but he moved carefully now, with the caution of a man who had walked into a room full of monsters and just discovered the one being in it who could point at him. He wove the frequency of his own Provenance together with the Mantle of THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist, threading a narrow private narrative between his existence and hers, a channel only two authors could share, and he spoke into it.","\"I am Osmont ,\" he said. \"I am curious about you, and your narrative. That is all.\"","His gaze swept the gallery of gathered gazes, the sea below, the hunters converging. \" Though you seem to be in a predicament where even as a manipulator of narratives, you... might just lose.\"","...!","Calliope’s reply came bright and fast, colored with something like joy!","| Hah! Now that would be something new. Something worth writing.|","Her pen never stopped moving as she answered, even as THE ONE WHO RETURNS reeled from a blow of the infinite sea.","| But if you can hide beneath the gazes of Immense Ones and sit among them wearing a little mask, then tell me, what exactly can I not do? Losing sounds thrilling. I might allow it.|","Then, without a breath between:","| But hey, forget all that. I don’t tend to find many interesting things about existence, but I love when I find some truly odd and interesting things! Like...did you know a pig’s orgasm can last more than thirty minutes? Sometimes more than an hour, even. Isn’t that wild?|","...!","What the fuck?","Noah’s existence buzzed as he ran the words back through his own weavings to make certain he had heard it correclty!","THE Writer of Mythos was surrounded on every side by hunters sent to collapse her existence and tear a Shard out of her corpse, an infinite sea crashing against her stories, four of the mightiest predators in this Train converging on her position, and here she was, cheerfully informing him about the reproductive endurance of pigs!","Noah shook his head slowly and did not answer.","Instead he looked away from her, out across the wound in the side of the Train, because he had never forgotten why his gaze had been pulled into this cursed room in the first place. He had come for a friend. And so, while THE Writer of Mythos clashed with THE Infinity Eater, Noah sent his gaze across the Cluster!","—","Region beyond region of the dead unrolled beneath his eye, until he found the one he sought.","It was a place where the unburied built cities.","They raised them out of what they had left behind, these dead, walls of stacked and silent things, streets that led only to more streets, towers with no one at the windows and no one who would ever come.","Grey light lay over all of it. Nothing here decayed, because decay was a thing for the living, and so the dead cities simply stood, immense and patient and wrong, a civilization holding its breath forever.","And through them marched THE Creature!","His army of Descendants came behind him.","A massive statue was now visible and walked behind its King, faceless and worn, a mountain of carried figures upon its back turning slowly as it moved.","Noah’s gaze found that approaching enemy of THE Creature, and his gaze became cold.","THE ZENITH OF SUBJUGATION!","THE Sealed One, wearing a Vessel, come personally across the Cluster to meet THE Creature, walking through the dead cities with his hands loose at his sides and an expression of mild, patient interest upon his borrowed face. He did not rush!","He did not gather power or raise a weapon or announce himself. He simply walked, unhurried and condescending, a collector who had come to collect, examining the architecture of the dead as he passed as though he might purchase a piece of it on his way to the transaction he actually wanted!","Two prey, carrying two Shards. Two hunts unfolding across two ends of the same Cluster. And the Sealed One, the most terrible of all the hunters, had not gone for the writer who could shield herself with an army of stories.","He had come for THE Creature.","The Sealed One walked closer, and closer, through the streets of the unburied.","And the statue stopped walking.","It halted mid-stride, the mountain on its back going still, and slowly, deliberately, it turned to face the approaching Vessel. For the first time in a long while it did not look toward the far dark or fade back into stone. It stood, and it faced the collector, and something in its worn grey stance became a challenge!","THE Creature’s flat voice rolled out across the dead cities.","\" You are my power ,\" he said. \" Existence is my power.\"","The words fell like slabs of iron laid down one atop another!","\" Assimilate into existence, \" THE Creature said, \" and let us not play anymore.\"","...!","The statue answered him without a sound!","It melded. It fused! The worn grey colossus flowed forward into its King and sank into him, stone becoming weight becoming bearing, and THE Creature’s titanic body drank it all down and CHANGED!","His frame took on some of the statue’s qualities, the ancient grey texture running through his obsidian, the mountain of carried figures settling somewhere into the depths of him, and his hand rose and closed, and a terrible bow was grasped in his grip!","HOONG!","Obsidian white flames of Dimensionality erupted around THE Creature, raging up his titanic frame in sheets of white presense, and the dead cities trembled at the heat of them, and Noah looked down upon his friend with a shining gaze, because THE Creature had stopped bearing and had begun to STAND!","And Noah could not be entirely sure, but when he looked at this monstrous lifeform who had his own foundation and legends surrounding him...he felt like he was still hiding a lot more inside of him!"]},{"number":5739,"title":"Chapter 5739: Chapter 5738: A Terrifying Narrative IV","paragraphs":["While Noah was looking at the changes of THE Creature...","| You’re going to ignore me again?|","Calliope’s voice slid back into his Provenance, and Noah’s gaze split its attention without effort, half of it on the friend below and half on the writer across the Cluster!","\" You say odd things ,\" Noah said, \" that do not fit the context of the terrifying things happening right now.\"","|I say what I say when I want to say it, regardless of the situation.| The words came easily, her pen still dancing across the page as she held back the infinite sea with the other hand.","|I am a Writer of existence. A Writer of Mythos. I know a great many niche facts about existence and I always, always want to learn more. The lifeforms called pigs and their strange little behaviors were new to me, and new things are the only things I love anymore.|","Then, coyly, she proceed to say...","| But hey. Do you want to know something else? If you actually listen, if you engage with me instead of staring at whatever is burning over there, I will tell you about these Shards the Immense Ones say I carry.|","Her illusory archetypes surged against the Eater’s tide as she wrote, buying herself the space to keep talking.","| It isn’t even a Shard, not really. It is one of the grand Hieroglyph Runestones. I came across it a very long time ago.|","...!","A Hieroglyph Runestone?","Now Noah was even more curious, and he listened in fully, both halves of his attention sharpening!","The Eater’s sea raged around her, and Calliope held it off with one hand and wrote with the other, and the two authors spoke across a channel no gaze in that sky could see.","It was a duel, though no blow was struck between them. She was bored and delighted at once, a being who had finally found a story with a hand in it she could not locate, and she circled Noah with her questions like a scholar circles a specimen she has waited an age to find.","He answered carefully, honestly where he could, because Sonder had shown him her dream and it was not a cruel one.","She wanted a story she could not control. There was no malice under that. There was only a terrible, ancient boredom, and a hunger to learn.","Her hunger was a unique one as it seemed to bud off of her like sparks of utter majesty. And every stroke she made, every movement of her pen looked like a masterpiece of...origin.","\" Writing is a Provenance, then ,\" Noah said. It was not a question so much as a thing he was confirming aloud.","|It is. One of the rarer ones .|","Her stories crashed against the sea and held. | Some of us are born with the pen already in the hand. Some of us steal one. And you... I think you stole yours. No offense, but you don’t seem like a natural talent. You have that flavor.|","She said it without accusation, almost approvingly. | My caretaker who is fuming up there is THE MATRIARCH OF INK. She birthed me with the pen in my grip. She did not agree to this...this game, and yet here we are. She is up there right now, furious, and there is nothing she can do about it, which is a story I would rather not be inside of. But how interesting is that? All that power as an Immense One, and one is still constrained. It makes you wonder about power...|","\" What about the Shards this whole show is put around? The Runestones...\"","|The Shard is real. But Shard is their word, a small ugly word.|","Her voice warmed, the way it only did when she reached the thing she actually loved.","| As I mentioned before, they are called Hieroglyph Runestone. Do you want to know what those are, Osmont? Truly? Because almost no one decent left in existence does.|","Noah’s gaze fixed on her fully!","| They are stones, old ones, older than some of the Immense Ones sitting above me right now, and upon them is carved the history of Existence itself. THE history. What happened before the Sundering. What the ones who left wrote down before they went. What IT was, before it slipped every hand that reached for it.|","Her pen slowed, and her words came slower with it, reverent now. | They were scattered across all of existence, hidden in the deepest and deadest places. But if you find them, Osmont...Ho Ho Ho... If you find enough of them, and you can read what is carved there, they point. Each stone points to the next, and the next, and the next. And the road they make...|","She let it hang for one perfect beat.","|The road they make leads to IT, well, or something even grander. Because even I want it to be a surprise. I want to be swept off my feet for grand Mythos of existence...otherwise if I find them inadequate, I will write my own.|","BOOM!","...!","The whole shape of the room rearranged itself in Noah’s mind at once!","He looked up, past the writer, up at the gallery of gathered gazes watching a game they had staged, and he began, coldly, to understand what he was actually looking at. And Calliope, still writing, still holding back an infinite sea with one lazy hand, said the thing that turned the entire Narrative on its head.","|They did not stage, this entire Train to find IT, or even these Runestones, you know.|","Her pen moved.","| They staged it to find out who can HOLD it. Someone who can find a Hieroglyph Runestone, and read it, and carry it in their existence without it tearing them apart, that someone has the potential to hold IT itself. And here is the funny part, the part they would gouge my eyes out for saying aloud.|","Her voice dropped into something wickedly delighted. | Even Immense Ones are not guaranteed to be able to hold, or grasp, or utilize the weavings of IT. Not one of them up there knows for certain that they could touch it and survive. So they are doing what they always do when they are afraid and pretending not to be.|","| They are basically fucking around right now.|","...!"]},{"number":5740,"title":"Chapter 5740: Chapter 5739: Hieroglyph Runestones I","paragraphs":["<Epigraph- An Unknown Age, Discovery of Hieroglyph Runestones>","Two beings stood in a dead place at the bottom of a dead Dimension, and the two Hieroglyph Runestones waited in the dark ahead of them.","The first was a cube. A vast one, obsidian shading to grey, each face wider than an Observable Existence, and across every face ran carvings in a tongue so old that the marks did not sit still under the eye; rearranging themselves whenever a mind tried to hold them.","The second was a sphere, greater than the cube, perfectly round and perfectly cold, and its surface too was written over end to end, spiraling script that wound around it without beginning and without end.","Serala stood beside Vakochev and looked at the two shapes for a long time.","She was beautiful. Dark hair, a sharp and patient face, eyes that missed nothing. She had walked beside the maker of the Scales through more dead places than either of them could count, and she had never yet asked him a foolish question.","\" What are they? \" she said at last.","Vakochev smiled.","He raised one hand, and from the whole of his body endless seas of THE Primordial Source surged out, dense and dark and old, pouring across the dead ground and rising up the two shapes to wrap them, and where the Source touched, the ancient carvings woke and began to glow, cube and sphere lighting the dead Dimension with the cold light of the first things.","\" They are Hieroglyph Runestones ,\" he said.","He walked a slow circle around the cube as he spoke, the Source trailing off him.","\" Existence has a memory. Everything that has ever happened is written somewhere, in the weavings, in the Records, in the agreement of things about what they are. But the Records can be edited. The weavings can be torn and re-sewn. What is written in the ordinary bones of existence can be rewritten by anyone strong enough to hold the pen, and there are beings strong enough to hold the pen, and they are not kind, and they do not love the truth. So the memory of existence is not safe. It has never been safe.\"","He set his palm flat against a glowing face of the cube, and the crawling script slowed under his hand as if it recognized him.","\" These are the exceptions. These are the memories of existence made into a thing that cannot be edited. They were carved before the frameworks were laid, in a tongue that predates agreement itself, out of a substance that does not answer to any authority born after it. You cannot rewrite what is on a Hieroglyph Runestone. You cannot lie to one. You cannot make one forget. An Immense One could pour the whole of its existence against this cube and it would not change a single mark, because the cube is older than the Immense One, and older than the thing that makes an Immense One what it is. They are...the one honest thing left in a dishonest existence.\"","BOOM!","Serala came to stand beside the cube, and she reached out and stopped, her fingers a breath from the glowing stone.","\" You can read them? It all seems like gibberish to me .\" she said.","\"I have read this one. \" He touched the cube. \" The sphere I have not been able to read at all. Trueness is the key...among other things.\"","\"And what does it say?\" Serala asked.","Vakochev was quiet for a moment, and the glow of the two Runestones lit his face.","When he spoke his voice had changed, gone lower and more careful.","\"It tells the beginning ,\" he said. \" The real one. Not the story the Immense Ones tell about themselves. The first.\"","He looked up at the cube.","\" There was a Dimension. The Runestone names it, though I will not say the name aloud in a dead place, because names have a way of reaching the things they belong to. Lets call it... THE Sundered Dimension, because that is what it became. In the earliest age of existence, before there was a first among lifeforms, before anyone had ever exceeded anything, a being went into that Dimension alone.\"","The Source coiled tighter around the cube, and the glow deepened.","\"It was trying to become something existence had no shape for. There was no ladder then. No Scales, no Weave, no path up, because no one had ever gone up. The being had to make the climbing and do the climbing at the same time. And in THE Sundered Dimension, where reality was already thin, it found that it could take the weight of existence itself and bring it down onto its own foundation as a catalyst for growth. It was THE First Adversity... and it was carried out by existence itself. It has always Existence...\"","\"It became the first Immense One? \" Serala said quietly.","\" Eventually yes, it became the first Immense One.\" Vakochev nodded. \" It did not become an Immense One by growing strong. Strength was only the road. What actually happened, at the threshold, is that the being touched IT.\"","The name fell into the dead Dimension, and even the crawling script on the cube seemed to still for a moment.","\" IT was there, in THE Sundered Dimension, because that is where the walls were thinnest, and IT is the thing on the other side of every wall. Some actually posed that Atlas forged IT. They do not know the true history. Atlas was not even alive and IT what’s already there.\"","\" But I digress. Back to that lifeform. The being touched IT, and for one instant it held the pen that writes existence, and in that instant it wrote itself into a shape existence had never permitted before. It became the first Immense One. And more than that, it became the only being, before or since, that could truly wield IT. The one and only. Every hand that has reached for IT in all the ages after touched the same thing the first one touched, and not one of them could make it answer.\"","Serala’s hand finally came to rest against the cube, and the glow ran up her fingers, and she did not flinch.","\" The first one could use it, \" she said slowly. \" And no one after. Why?\"","\" That is the question the cube asks and does not answer.\" Vakochev’s voice went low.","\" Here is what it does say. The first being touched IT, became an Immense One, held the authorship of existence in its own hand, and looked out at the whole vastness of what it had become and what it could now do. It stood at the precipice of the one thing every lifeform that has ever lived secretly wants. Absolute authorship. The pen that writes the weavings Existence. It is untold wonder with no ceiling above it, simply endless possibilities.\"","He was quiet for a moment!","\" And it glanced at that endless possibility once. Only once. And then it reached into its own existence and gouged out its own Trueness and its own origin, and it ended itself.\"","BOOM!","\"It dissipated its own being at the very moment it had won everything there was to win. Whatever it saw when it held the pen, whatever knowledge or power came with the touching, it looked at that and chose to stop existing rather than keep it.\"","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":5741,"title":"Chapter 5741: Chapter 5740: Hieroglyph Runestones II","paragraphs":["Serala had said nothing as the dead Dimension was very still!","But she had thought at that time about what could have possibly made an existence who was so profound and who held such power end everything they held?","\" Since then, \" Vakochev went on, \" very few have touched IT, and none have ever made it work. The barrier is not power. It is not strength. Multiple Immense Ones have stood and stared straight at IT and could not activate a single one of its functions, not one, though each of them could unmake a Dimension with a thought. And IT slipped right past them. But...a peasant with no authority at all, a thing of no standing whatsoever, could in principle put a hand on IT and change the entire landscape of existence. The lock has nothing to do with how mighty you are. The first one had almost no strength when it began, and it is still the only one who ever held the pen.\"","He turned from the cube and looked at her.","\" So the question is why. What did that first being see, at the precipice of every glory a lifeform could want, that made it end itself rather than hold on? What was done, all the way back then, to make IT the way IT now is, a thing that answers to no strength and no weakness, that turned the only being who ever wielded it into a suicide, and has refused every hand since? Is IT the answer to something, or the warning against it?\"","His voice dropped. \"I do not know. The cube brings me to the edge of the knowing and stops. But THE Hieroglyph Runestones are the only things left in existence that might tell the true story of what happened back then. Not this one alone. There are others, scattered, each a page. If I could gather enough of them, I think they would tell me why the first of the Immense unmade itself the very day it became one.\"","He glanced at the silent sphere.","\" But I have found only two in a whole lifetime of looking. And multiple of them, I am certain, are already in the hands of Immense Ones, who guard them not to read them, but to make sure no one else ever does.\"","The two of them stood in the light of the two stones, the cube read and the sphere still silent, the seas of THE Primordial Source turning slow around them both.","\" You are going to look for the rest of them? You may spend spend what is left of your life chasing stones, so that one day you can read why a being unmade itself at the moment of its glory. Is it all...worth it?\"","Was it worth it?","Vakochev had been silent for a little while.","\" More than worth it. But...I am going to build a ladder first ,\" Vakochev said. \" So that when I am gone, the ones below do not have to break themselves finding the road the way I did. I do not want to be the last honest thing in a dishonest existence. I want to make honesty cheap enough that everyone can afford it.\"","He looked at her. \" And yes. After that, I am going to keep chasing the stones, until I know what that first one saw. Because I think it is the most important thing that has ever been forgotten.\"","Serala was quiet for a long moment.","\" They will try and stop you. They will definitely stop us as... \" she said. \" You may never live to read the last stone. You may be...just like that first Immense One. If you eventually grasp everything that they grasped, what if you do the same thing and choose to...\"","She could not finish her words!","WAA!","\" Maybe.\"","\"Then why read the stone at all? \" she asked, her eyes almost tearing up.","\" Why this need to know? I just...I just want to spend all of existence holding on to you. I don’t want to know!\"","...!","Vakochev looked at the cube for a long time, and then he looked at the sphere he had never been able to read, the greater of the two, older still, holding a truth he would go to his grave without.","He could not gaze at the woman beside him...as if he knew his conviction would be shaken if he did!","\" Because a thing that is true is worth knowing whether or not you can use it,\" he said. \" The Immense Ones believe knowledge is a tool, and a tool is only worth the work it does, and a truth you cannot spend is a truth not worth having. That is why they rewrite the Records. That is why they bury the stones. To them, a fact that cannot be turned into power is garbage, and the past is only a resource to be mined or hidden.\"","He set his hand against the cube one last time, and the crawling script warmed under his palm.","\" But the past is not a resource. It is not a tool. It is the true thing, the thing that happened, whether or not anyone ever benefits from knowing it. And an existence that only values the truths it can spend is an existence that will, in the end, forget it was ever true at all.\"","\"I read the stone because it is true. I may die before I use it. And it was still worth every year it cost me, because for one night, in a dead place, at the bottom of a broken realm, one being ended himself in the face of Everything...but even his record was said aloud. Aloud and recorded on the Hieroglyph Runestones.\"","He turned from the stone.","\"In an existence built on a lie, one true thing said aloud is not nothing. It may be the only thing that isn’t.\"","The two Runestones glowed a while longer in the dead Dimension, the read and the unread, and then the maker of the Scales let the Source fall away from them, and the ancient light went out!","---","<Current Age>","The Immense Ones were fucking around!","That was the truth stripped of all its grandeur, and Noah turned the thought over from the far edge of the gallery.","Here were beings of terrifying, existence-ending power, gazes that had burned lineages and frozen springs and staged whole tragedies for their own amusement, and they had gathered over this cluster of Dimensions for one reason, which was that not one of them, for all their might, could be certain they were able to hold IT!","They already had power beyond counting. They were hunting for a KEY, a lifeform shaped correctly enough to grasp the one thing their power could not!","And they did not know which shape that was as the clue came with those...holding Hieroglyph Runestones.","But these were terrifying beings, reduced to gamblers who could not read their own dice!","Noah was still turning that over when Calliope’s voice slid back into his Provenance, and she was, as ever, talking a great deal.","| Hmm, it is so hard, you know, to come across another existence who can freely steer narratives when they have not even reached the level of an Immense One. So hard! I feel like I could talk to you for an Age and only get started. And yet look at this predicament around me. It simply does not allow it!|","Her pen never stopped as she spoke, archetypes surging and breaking against the infinite sea below.","| Whatever narrative the Immense Ones have designed here, I do not like its flow. It is not coherent. It does not carry the feeling of a grand myth, of a true epic, and I would know, since building those is the whole of what I am! It reads like something written by old men, by bored things who have forgotten how a story is supposed to move. I want...to change it up.|","...!"]},{"number":5742,"title":"Chapter 5742: Chapter 5741: Change The Narrative! I","paragraphs":["She wrote, and THE ONE WHO RETURNS heaved the sea back as if he were smashing all of Existence back itself!","| Look at the pieces they have gathered. Two Vessels of THE Sealed One are present in this Cluster. One holds the weavings of the Sealed One himself, clean, the real thing. But the other? The other is a murky mixture, and it fascinates me, because it seems that even THE Sealed One was targeted, once, and had a portion of his own existence assimilated by someone else. A collector, collected! And then there is the other prey, the one who is not me, who carries another Hieroglyph Runestone just as I do, which means there is someone else in this Cluster capable of holding a Runestone inside their existence without it tearing them apart. Someone who might be able to handle IT. I am terribly curious about that one, too.|","She was talking a whole lot, and Noah let her, because every word she spilled was more information for him!","He turned his gaze toward one direction of the Cluster, toward the lifeform who held the Mantle of THE USURPER, and his eye sharpened with recognition as he could see a glimmer of the Dream and identity of the lifeform within.","Adrastia . He remembered this existence he had crossed paths with before, and it was exactly as strange as Calliope had said. It carried the power of THE Sealed One, and yet it was not the Sealed One, a mixture of itself and the thing that had tried to claim it. Had it been meant to become a Vessel, and instead found the capability to RESIST, to swallow half of what came to swallow it? A being that had been targeted for assimilation and had assimilated its assimilator halfway back?","Was that the murky one Calliope spoke of? A Vessel that had, in some measure, refused?","Noah turned his gaze the other way, across the whole span of the Cluster, to the region of dead cities where his friend stood.","THE Creature.","As grand as this being had always been, Noah understood now that THE Creature too held the capability to hold IT. He carried a Shard, a Hieroglyph Runestone woven inside him. And he was in a unique state, after fusing with the statue, a state Noah had never seen an existence occupy. He gazed upon his friend fully, and the weavings answered!","| THE CREATURE|","|VERITAS: 244|","|POTENTIA: Undefined.|","|PROVENANCE: Undefined.|","|PONDUS: 251|","...!","| Note: the analyzed lifeform is in a state of existential transformation.|","|It is both generating and not generating its own weavings, paradoxically and at once.|","|Its Provenance is being established at this present moment. Its Provenance was already established in the future. A paradoxical continuum of time has begun to wrap around this existence...|","...!","Noah squinted!","Undefined. Not a number too high to read, not a veil of question marks, but Undefined, a thing the weavings of existence could not resolve because THE Creature was, at this instant, standing in two times at once!","His Provenance was being born and had already been born. He was building his foundation and had finished building it in a future that had not yet arrived. The fusion with the statue had wrapped a loop of time around his titanic frame, and inside that loop the ordinary rules of before-and-after did not hold!","What a state! What a monstrous, paradoxical state!","Noah’s eyes shone.","Below, the battle was changing fast!","THE CHAMPION had entered it. Alcaeus came charging across the Dimensions toward Calliope, a second hunter joining the first, and the infinite sea and the charging Champion converged on the writer at once as she wrote and wrote, new archetypes unfolding off her pages to meet them!","And Noah watched her hand move across a fresh empty page, and he watched the words rise off it heavy with weight!","| The Archetype of THE Rebel shall unfold before me.|","|The Rebel is a unique Mythos. Driven to frustration by the systems and rulings that bind it, the lifeform rebels, for it wishes for change above all things. It will not serve the shape it was given.|","|This Mythos shall unfold within the existence known as... THE CHAMPION.|","...!","BOOM!","Noah felt her Provenance twist uniquely as in the next moment...","THE CHAMPION stopped mid-charge!","Noah saw the great hunter freeze in the dead air over the dreary environment of an underworld, his entire existence beginning to buzz with a terrifying density of Dimensionality, and then his own body began to move without him willing it! An inscription blazed to life upon his right foot he had kept hidden this whole time, ancient and burning, and Alcaeus floated down from the skies against the whole of his intent, and he turned as he targeted...THE INFINITY EATER!","The Champion’s body transformed!","His titanic frame folded and stretched and hardened, obsidian and gold, untill the whole of him had become a massive golden sword, kilometers upon kilometers of blazing blade, and his right foot with its shining inscription became the very tip of that sword, glowing white-hot with enough Dimensionality to cleave through multiple Dimensions at a stroke!","THE CHAMPION had become a weapon, and the weapon was turning on his own ally.","He was rebeling!","The golden sword that had been a hunter fell upon the Infinity Eater’s sea, and the Dimension split beneath the blow, and Noah looked upon it all with shining eyes as Calliope’s voice, warm and bright and entirely delighted, poured back into his Provenance!","|Isn’t it neat? To be able to steer a narrative like this? |","Her pen was already moving to the next page . |I found out, you see, that one of the capabilities of IT is to rewrite how existence is unfolding. Or how it has unfolded. Or how it will unfold, which is my favorite. And when I learned that, I told myself, well, why do I not simply begin developing a little capability like that of my own? I am the Writer of Mythos! So let me write how I want events to unfold, right here, right in front of everyone, and let existence catch up!|","BOOM!","Her words burned with a confidence that made even the dead cities seem to lean in to listen, and Noah could not help but take a second, longer look at her.","What she had just described, what she was doing with a pen and a page in the middle of a killing ground, was extremely, uncomfortably similar to the thing he could accomplish with his own Provenance when he unleashed the full weight of the Mantle of THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist!","Writing tropes into existence as law. Bending how a story unfolded.","He had thought the art was his! He had thought no one else in all of existence had walked this particular road! And here was a Descendant of ink and mythos, bored and delighted and surrounded on all sides, who had already been quietly perfecting the art itself!","...!"]},{"number":5743,"title":"Chapter 5743: Chapter 5742: Change The Narrative! II","paragraphs":["Existence breathes, and epochs pass, leaving Civilizations that become monuments, then crumble to memory, and are long forgotten when that breath comes again. In all these epochs, just what reigns supreme?","---","As Noah thought about the wonder that was Calliope, in the distance...the golden blade fell, and it fell as a rebellion given edge and gravity!","Alcaeus the Champion, rewritten by a pen he had never consented to, plunged downward through the dead air of the Cluster as a sword Gigaparsecs long, his inscribed foot the white-hot tip, and he crashed with the whole of his stolen weight into THE INFINITY EATER’s abyssal infinite sea of Dimensionality!","There was no burst of heat. No detonation of fire!","The blade did something colder and far more surgical, because Calliope had not written destruction, she had written betrayal, and betrayal cuts where a thing is weakest! The golden sword sheared clean through the Eater’s primary harvesting conduits, the great feeding channels through which the Infinity Eater drank the Infinity of countless lifeforms across a thousand Observable Existences and more thousands of Dimensions, all those distant existences who pulled their own Infinity from him and paid for it with a portion of themselves!","The conduits parted.","The infinite sea, cut off at its source, LURCHED, and the Eater staggered as an ocean that had always been fed suddenly found itself bleeding from a wound it did not undersand.","...!","But above, over her open codex, Calliope’s hand trembled as she breathed out.","To force an architect’s own champion to rebel against his deepest nature was not a thing done for free! The causal tension of it, a being made to betray the very shape it had been forged into, pushed back against her pen, and the tax came due in her own flesh.","Her silver-white hair whipped through the air as though a storm blew through the dead Dimensions, and from beneath her fingernails, dark and glistening, droplets of black ink began to seep! Her internal reserves burned rapidly, poured out drop by drop to hold the Rebel in place against Alcaeus’s screaming, authentic will.","|An archetype written into a living vessel must be continually fed. Where the vessel’s true historical intent pushes back against the imposed Mythos, the causal tension snaps backward into the author...|","Her Trueness itself was fraying at the edges, and she wrote on regardless, serene and bleeding at once.","Noah looked at this as this seemed like a limitation he may not be...too entirely bound by if he had acted.","But as things unfolded, far below, in the lower rift of the Cluster, THE Zenith of Subjugation reached THE Creature.","The clean Vessel of THE Sealed One did not rush even now. It extended its hands, and from them uncoiled seven pale chains of absolute suppression, each one a sentence of dormancy, each one designed to seize an existence and freeze it and press it down into a permanent, silent sleep! The chains lashed out toward THE Creature to still his weavings forever.","THE Creature ROARED at this time, sending his army far behind him as if he knew they could do nothing.","His titanic frame, caught in that paradoxical continuum where his Provenance existed both now and in a future not yet arrived, blazed with obsidian-white flames, and the flames scorched the pale chains where they touched!","But the Vessel’s weight was the weight of a being who specialized in taking, one piece at a time, everything a thing had, and slowly, grindingly, the suppression forced THE Creature’s titanic knees downward toward the dead ground!","Down!","And still further down!","And as his knees bent under the sentence of a monster, THE Creature reached back, and his great hand closed around the pure white bow the statue had carried for so long, and he pulled!","...!","The dead Dimensions answered his draw!","As THE Creature hauled the bowstring back, thousands upon thousands of illusory Dimensions gathered before him, folding and compressing, layering one atop another into a single shape, and the shape was an ARROW.","An arrow made of a thousand collapsed Dimensions, nocked to a bow of the first make, drawn by a King almost forced to his knees and refusing to stay there.","His eyes burned with obsidian-white flame, and in that moment THE Creature did not look like a King, and he did not look like a Ruler!","He looked like an ancient fiend, a primordial thing of fire and bearing, and from the depths of him an unknown Provenance began to spill, dark and vast and unnamed, an authority the weavings of existence could not yet put a number to.","He loosed!","The thousand-Dimension arrow tore across the rift toward THE Sealed One, and behind it THE Creature was already drawing another, and another, arrow after arrow of collapsed existences forming and flying, his obsidian flames raging higher with each pull, a fiend of the deep loosing Dimensions at a collector who had thought this would be simple!","And yet even in the face of this...THE Sealed One smiled as he raised his hand as if to welcome everything. As if his purpose here...was much more sinister.","Above it all, in the gallery, THE OVERSEEING ONE leaned forward over the brass balcony!","His crimson gaze pulsed with a mounting, ugly irritation, because his scripted Narrative was coming apart before the eyes of his peers! The Champion had broken formation and turned on his own side! The Eater was being pushed back and bled.","The Creature, who was meant to be pressed quietly into dormancy, was on his knees loosing arrows of worlds and spilling a Provenance no one had accounted for.","Twice now a theater he was watching and rooting for a certain side had refused to obey him. Twice, in front of the others!","He would not suffer it a third time!","| THE OVERSEEING ONE will not be embarrassed again.|","|He reasserts his authorship over a faltering Narrative.|","Streams of the Overseeing One’s own Narrative poured down from the balcony, and they wrapped around both THE Sealed One’s Vessel and THE CHAMPION, threading into them, reinforcing, bracing the failing script with the full weight of an Immense One’s will.","The pale chains on THE Creature drank the reinforcement and pulled tighter! Alcaeus’s rebellion strained against a second, stronger hand now laid over Calliope’s!","And the whole of the Dimensional Cabin, the whole vast Cluster of Dimensions beneath it, began to BUZZ with the terrifying collection of authority gathering in that one place!","| WARNING.|","|Authority within this Narrative of Existence is compounding beyond stable thresholds.|","|Multiple sovereign authors and one Immense One now write over the same continuum at once...|","The dead cities trembled. The rivers of the dead ran backward. The buzz climbed and climbed, existence itself groaning under the weight of too many hands writing over the same page at once!"]},{"number":5744,"title":"Chapter 5744: Chapter 5743: Change The Narrative! III","paragraphs":["And in the middle of it, bleeding ink from beneath her nails, her hair a silver storm, Calliope looked up.","She looked past the gallery, past the balcony, to the far hidden edge of the sky where a mobius-pupiled eye had hung masked and silent since the beginning.","She opened their private conduit, and this time her voice carried none of its earlier playful detachment. It was serious, and it was fast, and it was still, somehow, delighted!","| My ink is running a bit dry, Osmont.|","Her pen shook over the page.","| Before my Matriarch has to interfere and ruin the fun, and she will, if this keeps going the way it is going... why don’t the two of us do something grand? Let us change the narrative. Or are you going to sit up there and simply watch, when the two of us together could ruin their entire theater?|","...!","Noah’s masked eye held over the burning Cluster.","And then he moved!","He did not answer with words. He reached out with the whole quiet weight of his Provenance and his Infinite Dream, found the writer’s consciousness in the middle of her bleeding, and PULLED!","—","Calliope’s perception of the collapsing Cluster froze.","The screaming sea, the falling arrows, the pale chains, the buzzing sky, all of it stopped between one instant and the next, held in a stretched and silent moment, as Noah drew her consciousness up and out and into the inner sanctuary of his Infinite Dream.","An instant, stretched out towards infinity.","Time. Once more, time!","They stood together in a domain of blue-gold clouds.","Endless soft light rolled around them in slow drifts, quiet and boundless and entirely his, a place between spaces where no gaze of any Immense One could reach and no ink ran dry. The war outside did not exist here. Only the two authors, and the stillness he had wrapped around them both.","Calliope looked around at the blue-gold clouds, and her bleeding stopped, and her storm-tossed hair settled, and a slow smile spread across her face.","She waved her hand at Noah, and then, grandly, delighted, she gave a little bow!","\" Oh, this is lovely,\" she said, aloud now, her voice her own again in the quiet. \" You pulled me right out of the story and into your own private one. Very unique. This is...narrative infused with Infinity itself?\"","She looked around, and then she straightened, and the delight sharpened into something more serious, because she had been offered a stage and she intended to use it.","\" Alright, so let me tell you the truth of what I do ,\" she said, \" since we are about to do it together, and you should know the wall before you run at it with me!\"","She lifted a hand, and ink gathered at her fingertip.","\"I cannot write a falsehood into existence. That is the first law of my craft and it has never once bent for me! An archetype cannot be conjured from a vacuum, out of nothing, out of a lie. It must have an anchor. An authentic historical thing that has already cut its mark into the bedrock of reality, a truth that actually happened, that existence still remembers. I write the Mythos, yes, but the Mythos must have somewhere true to stand, or it does not stand at all!\"","Her eyes glittered. \"I have found ways around the edges of that law, here and there. But they are costly. Very costly.\"","She smiled again, and this time there was something almost reverent in it.","\" But here. Since we are being grand. Let me show you the truest thing I own.\"","She tapped her own wrist, once, and grandly, from the clouds of Noah’s own sanctuary, something began to emerge.","It rose slowly out of the blue-gold light as something vast and dark and ancient, and it was a....HIEROGLYPH RUNESTONE.","A massive obsidian cube, its faces wider than an Observable Existence, black shading toward grey, and across every face crawled the oldest carvings Noah had ever seen, marks that would not sit still, rearranging themselves whenever the eye tried to hold them, the true history of Existence written in a tongue older than agreement itself!","The moment Noah laid his eyes upon it...","HUUM!","His existence BUZZED!","Something deep in him, deeper than thought, deeper than Provenance, answered the stone.","Noah walked forward as if in a trance, his masked awareness narrowing to the cube and the cube alone, his hand rising of its own accord, reaching, reaching, until his fingers pressed against a glowing obsidian face!","And the Runestone LIT!","Obsidian light blazed up out of it, and obsidian lightning flowed up the whole of Noah’s body in a single crackling surge, racing through his existence, and from Noah’s eyes there erupted beams of pure obisidian light!","Calliope blinked!","Her delight moved into shock, and then into a frown, because this was not what she had expected.","\" Osmont? What do you see? Hey, what do you see...?!\"","But Noah did not hear her.","For him, everything froze!","The blue-gold clouds, the writer, the cube, the obsidian lightning, all of it locked into a single suspended instant, because Noah’s mind had already been seized and carried away, wrenched somewhere unfathomably far...","---","Noah’s consciousness woke, and he was looking down upon the beginning of...Existence.","Well, not really, but it felt like it!","He hung, bodiless, over a forest, and it was a forest such as had never grown anywhere he had walked in all his long climb! Ancient beyond ancient, Primordial in the truest sense, a forest from the earliest era of existence when existence had barely learned to be, and it stretched below him further than sight, further than thought, an endless green that was somehow older than green itself.","And the trees were budding with fruit.","But the fruit were not fruit!","Noah stared, his existence gone still with wonder, because upon the boughs of every ancient tree hung Dimensions and Observable Existences, ripening! Each one a swirling jewel of wonder, each one heavy with the lifeforce of of Causes, and each one held within a shape he knew, a faceted crystalline structure of deep blue-white, something almost exactly like a Genesis Tesseract.","Whole domains hung from the branches like how apples hang from an orchard, and the trees that bore them burned with the raw and endless life of the Causes budding inside them!","This was a garden where realities grew like fruit.","And through that garden, a lifeform walked.","Noah’s gaze fell to it, and it surprised him, because for all the impossible grandeur of the forest, the being walking through it was small, and rough, and simple! A caveman-like thing, hunched and unhurried, thick-limbed and unadorned, picking its way between the trees of worlds with the calm of a creature that had been walking here since before walking had a name.","Then a voice boomed out, and it boomed for Noah alone.","It was the voice of the Hieroglyph Runestone, and it did not speak into his ears but into the very core of him, and its words unfolded as prompts across the whole of his frozen sight!","|In the earliest era of existence, no lifeform truly understood Infinity.|","|Not one. They lived within it, they reached for it, they built the first crude frameworks upon its assumption, and yet not a single existence among them could hold it, or see it, or say what it truly was.|","|One of the first ever to begin to understand it... was known as Lucy.|","...!"]},{"number":5745,"title":"Chapter 5745: Chapter 5744: Change The Narrative! IV","paragraphs":["Lucy.","Noah watched the small rough being pick her way onward, and understood that he was looking at her, this hunched unhurried thing walking through a forest of growing Dimensions, and the voice of the stone rolled on!","| The earliest existences looked into the heart of a Dimension, into its very center, and their reckoning told them a strange thing: that the center held zero volume, and infinite density. A point of nothing, containing everything.|","|And the wisest among them did not take this to mean that an actual, physical infinity existed there. No. They took it to mean something humbler and far more honest.|","|It meant their understanding had reached its edge. It meant that what lay beyond the center was a thing their minds could not yet envision, could not yet shape, could not yet hold.|","|So they gave that edge a name. They called it... Infinity.|","The forest breathed around the walking figure, worlds ripening on every bough!","|No lifeform has ever truly known Infinity. No lifeform has ever grasped it, or seen it, or proven it even exists.|","|Every musing on Infinity that has ever been spoken, in every age, by every mighty thing, became only this: their own definition of what Infinity could be, as far as they themselves were able to understand it and grasp it.|","|Infinity was never a thing. It was a word. A word each existence filled with the shape of its own not-knowing.|","Noah’s frozen existence turned that over! He had branded his identity onto infinity before! He had wielded it as though it were a thing, a substance, an authority with edges he could hold! And the stone was telling him, gently and enormously, that no one had ever held it at all, that they had only ever held their own understanding of a thing they could not understand!","Below, Lucy stopped walking.","She came to the bank of a river, and the river ran bright and quick, and it was filled with fish! Small, silver, countless, they schooled in the shallows, and the moment Lucy knelt down beside the water, every fish in that river turned its face up toward her and gathered, crowding to the bank, waiting, as though they had done this a thousand times and loved every one.","Lucy smiled at them.","She reached up to the nearest tree and plucked a single Dimension from a low branch, a swirling jewel of a world heavy with a million Causes, and she held it in her thick rough hands, and white light began to wrap around it, spilling from her fingers, wrapping the plucked world in a growing radiance!","And then...","Thousands of genuine Dimensions bloomed from her hands!","Noah watched, and his existence could scarcely hold what it saw, because from that single plucked world, cradled in the hands of a simple caveman thing, Dimensions poured forth without end! Not illusions, not images, but real and genuine Dimensions, thousands of them, then tens of thousands, blooming out of her palms in an endless radiant stream, each one whole, each one ture, each one heavy with its own Causes and its own laws.","She smiled wider, and she directed the endless stream down toward the water.","And the fish ATE them!","The silver fish rose up and took the blooming Dimensions into their mouths as if they were nothing more than crumbs of bread scattered on a pond, swallowing whole Domains, feeding happily, jostling for more.","And Lucy laughed a soundless laugh and kept producing them, minute after minute, Dimension after Dimension after Dimension, what looked to Noah like millions of genuine domains spilling endlessly from the hands of a small rough being for no greater reason than to feed the fish in a river!","An infinite production! Effortless! Joyful! Casual as scattering feed!","Noah’s mind reeled at the sheer, quiet impossibility of it, this being who did not strain, did not calculate, did not grasp at anythng, simply opened her hands and let the infinite pour out as though it were the most natural thing in all of existence.","At last the fish were full, and they scattered back into the bright water, sated and happy, and Lucy let the stream die in her palms and wiped her rough hands on her knees and rose!","She smiled once more at the river, and then she turned, and she walked on through the forest of growing domains, unhurried as ever, as though she had done nothing at all!","And the Runestone spoke its last.","| Infinity will never be a thing you see. It will never be a thing you grasp, or hold, or conquer. It is, and it always was, only a word, a definition given to a thing one does not understand.|","|But here is the key the stone offers you, the only key it has.|","|Attain a good definition. Your own. Unique to you. A clear and sufficient understanding of the very thing you cannot understand. Do not borrow another’s edge, or understanding of Infinity, for another’s edge of impossibility is only the shape of another’s not-knowing.|","|Reach a clear and sufficient definition of your own, and you will be able to read the true idea of Infinity written within this Runestone.|","|And when you read it, a path will light up before you.|","|Where that path leads... is unknown even to the stone.|","HUUM!","The forest began to fade!","The domains on the boughs grew murky, the endless green dimming, the bright river washing out to grey, the whole Primordial garden dissolving at its edges as the vision released its hold upon him and Noah’s consciousness began, slowly, to rise back toward the blue-gold clouds and the frozen war and the writer he had left behind!","And as everything faded, as the forest thinned to almost nothing...","In the very corner of his fading sight, Noah could have sworn he saw it!","The record of the visage of Lucy, the small rough caveman being who scattered infinite Dimensions to feed the fish, stopped walking. She turned her head. And across the whole impossible distance of an age that had ended before Noah was ever born, that ancient thing looked up, directly at him, directly at the watcher the vision was never supposed to notice...","And she smiled at him!","Fiendishly!","...!"]},{"number":5746,"title":"Chapter 5746: Chapter 5745: Change The Narrative! V","paragraphs":["Noah’s awareness snapped back into the blue-gold clouds, and no time had passed at all.","The instant he had left was still the instant he returned to, frozen and stretched and waiting, and Calliope stood before him exactly as she had, the massive obsidian Runestone at her back, her eyes fixed on him and shining bright with a curiosity that had sharpened into something almost hungry!","She had seen the stone reach for him. She had seen the obsidian lightning climb his existence and the beams pour from his eyes. And she wanted, desperately, to know what he had been shown.","But Noah could not answer her, not yet, because his entire existence was BUZZING!","Something had changed in him! Something enormous and quiet had shifted in the deepest place of him, in the way he understood the very thing he had built his early climb upon, and he could feel it moving through him like a tide finding a new shore!","Infinity!","For his whole existence he had treated Infinity as a substance! A thing with weight and corners, an authority he had branded his identity onto, a power he wielded as though he had truly grasped it in his hands.","But the forest had shown him the truth!","No lifeform had ever grasped Infinity. No one had ever held it. It was only ever a word, a definition, a shape each existence poured into its own not-knowing! Lucy had not grasped Infinity when she scattered a million Dimensions to the fish. She had simply reached a definition so clear, so wholly and quietly HERS, that the infinite had poured from her hands like water because she had stopped trying to hold it and simply understood what it was to her!","And Noah understood, in that stretched and frozen instant, what he had to do.","He did not need to grasp Infinity. He never could have. Nobody could.","What he needed was a definition of his own, unique and clear and sufficient, his own understanding of the very thing that could not be understood!","His understanding of the edge. Of Impossibility.","His Infinite Sanguine Mana began to cycle!","Crimson-gold vitality surged and ran through the whole of his existense, through every one of his two hundred decillion quarks and as it moved, Noah gave it a task it had never been given! He poured his new understanding into it, his own fresh and hard-won definition of impossibility, and he let the Sanguine Mana carry that definition through his existence like ink spreading through water.","| You have witnessed a truth kept by a Hieroglyph Runestone: Infinity is not grasped. It is defined.|","|You have begun to reach a definition of unknown an impossibility that is wholly your own.|","Noah’s definition took shape as the Sanguine Mana carried it!","To Lucy, Infinity had been abundance, an endless joyful giving. To the earliest existences it had been the edge of their reckoning, a name for the dark past the center. But to Noah?","To THE Human Dreamer, who had lived a single life across time, who dreamed and made the dreams true, who authored narratives and stood outside the line of moments?","To Noah, Infinity was...a DREAM that did not end. His goals. His dream, ideals, purpose, loves, fears, hopes...his Everythings, that did not end.","That was his definition, his own and no one else’s, clear and sufficient and true to the whole of what he was! Infinity was not a substance and not an edge and not an abundance. It was a dream with no far wall, a story that could always add another page, a reverie that time could stretch forever without ever reaching its close! He did not need to hold the infinite. He only needed to dream a dream that never had to stop!","And his Infinite Sanguine Mana, carrying that definition, bled it directly into THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer!","HUUM!","The crimson-gold tide met the blue-gold depths of his Provenance, and the definition sank into it, and his Provenance DRANK it, understood it, and answered.","| Your definition of Infinity has been carried by your Infinite Sanguine Mana into THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer.|","|The two have merged. Your understanding of the infinite is now woven into the substance of your Provenance.|","...!","Something new began to rise in Noah’s existence!","His Provenance of THE Human Dreamer had always let him dream, and dream grandly, but now it took his definition of the infinite and wound it into its own foundation, and a new capability began to bloom, vast and quiet and terrible!","| A new understanding awakens within THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer.|","|THE INFINITE DREAM: your dreams no longer possess a far wall. A dream you begin need never end. A reverie may be extended without limit, a narrative continued without a final page, a stretched instant expanded toward a forever that answers only to you.|","|You do not hold Infinity. You dream it. And a dream that does not end is an infinite you will never lose. Even if you are killed within a Dream, so long as you paid an initial cost to initiate it, you can return even from collapse within that dream.|","Noah’s eyes blazed with blue-gold light!","This was it! He had spent his whole life carrying an infinite that was never truly his, an inherited definition of a thing he could not grasp, and now, at last, he held an infinite that belonged only to him, because he had stopped trying to hold it and had learned instead to Dream it.","And he felt like this was only the tip of the iceberg as if he was able to understand that edge even more, that impossibility...even more wonders would unfold!","But for now...","His Infinite Dreams could now run without end! A reverie could be stretched toward true forever! The 75-Provenance Infinite Dream he had opened to sit among the Immense Ones, the sanctuary of clouds, the stretched instant he stood in right now with Calliope frozen before him, all of it could now be extended without any wall at all!","And more! For if a dream need never end, then the power gained within a dream, the growth, the guiding, the authoring, all of it could compound across a dreaming that had no close.","His existence buzzed with the enormity of it, and somewhere far down he undertood that he had not merely learned a trick! He had changed what Infinity meant to him, and in changing the meaning, he had made the infinite finally, truly his!","The Runestone had said a path would light up before one who reached a definition of their own.","Noah could feel it now, faint and distant, somewhere at the edge of his newly infinite dreaming, a path beginning to glow, a road the stone had promised, leading somewhere unknown even to the stone itself.","He wouldn’t even need to gaze upon this stone again to try and follow that road as it had shown him what it had.","But that was for later.","For now, in a frozen instant that he could stretch toward forever, in a sanctuary of blue-gold clouds, with an obsidian Runestone at her back and her eyes shining brighter than ever, Calliope leaned in toward the man who had just walked out of a memory changed, and she opened her mouth to ask him what in all of existence he had just seen...!"]},{"number":5747,"title":"Chapter 5747: Chapter 5746: A Grand Mythos! I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at Calliope who was calm and expectant in the blue-gold clouds, and he answered her at last.","\"I learned about Lucy,\" he said. \" And infinity.\"","...!","Calliope’s eyes went wide!","\" Huh! Really?\" She leaned in delighted.","\" Little Lucy showed me the impossibilities of stories. The walls I could never write past, the doors that only open one way. But you saw something else entirely! I suppose each of us sees a different thing in the same old stone. Isn’t that just the loveliest proof that a story is never truly finished? \"","She clapped her ink-stained hands together once. \" Okay! I have given you something now, so it is your turn. It is time for you to reciprocate!\"","She waved a hand, and the massive obsidian Hieroglyph Runestone sank slowly back down into the blue-gold clouds of Noah’s sanctuary, folding away into wherever the Writer of Mythos kept the truest thing she owned, until only the two authors remained in the endless soft light.","And then she made her proposal!","\"I want to write the ultimate subversion, Dreamer,\" she said, and her voice dropped into something reverent and mad all at once. \" The one Mythos the rule has always forbidden me. I want to write THE Vestige of THE Fallen Hero.\"","Noah’s masked existence pulsed!","\" But you understand a thing like that does not come cheap, \" Calliope went on, pacing now through the clouds. \" For the myth I have in mind, it takes more than ink! It takes an ocean of sovereign vitality. And it takes a hammer of pure Provenance to drive the whole sentence down through the weavings of this Train until existence has no choice but to agree!\"","She turned, and she looked directly at Noah’s blue-gold manifestation, and her eyes glittered!","\"I have the syntax. I have an unalterable page, a truth that cannot be edited. But my blood belongs to the Matriarch, and the Matriarch is bound to their frameworks, chained to the very authorities we would be defying! My ink can shape the story. It cannot pay the debt.\" Her voice sharpened to a point.","\" But you? You carry blood that owes nothing to anyone, do you not? Blood generated from your own origin, answering to no one in all of existence!\"","She held out her hand across the space between them. \" So lend me your power. Give me your red ink.\"","Noah calculated the trade in a single stretched instant.","To do this was to unleash his foundation in the open, and unleashing his foundation in the open risked drawing the gazes of Immense Ones down onto his masked position at last! It was the great danger, the one he had spent this whole dream avoiding!","And yet...","His Dream was Infinite now.","Even if the seven turned their full gazes upon him, even if their combined weight shredded his existence to nothing in an instant, it would not end him, because he had learned to dream a dream with no far wall, and even death within that dream was not death.","He had paid to open it. He could return from a collapse inside it!","His Tyranny rose in him and Sonder tempered it into something quieter and more certain, and the two together weighed the challenge and found it entirely... acceptable.","Prompts bloomed across his sight.","| COLLABORATIVE SOVEREIGN AUTHORSHIP PROPOSED.|","|Syntactic Architect: CALLIOPE, THE WRITER OF MYTHOS.|","|Sovereign Fuel and Anchor: NOAH OSMONT, THE HUMAN DREAMER.|","|Target Inscription: THE VESTIGE OF THE FALLEN HERO.|","|Required Medium: A SHARD OF VAKOCHEV.|","....!","A Shard of Vakochev?","And then Calliope reached into her existence and produced a thing, and Noah’s masked eye locked onto it in pure astonishment, because he recognized it!","It was a Shard, jagged and cold and old, and it carried a weaving Noah knew intimately, because it was the earliest version of his own Shard that he himself held! This woman, this bored and bleeding Descendant of ink, held in her hand a fragment of Vakochev that was left behind after his proclamation to those...like him.","And she wrapped it in ink, and she began to write!","\"Your weavings ,\" Calliope breathed, her concentration absolute. \" Give them to me!\"","Noah breathed out and unleashed his foundation as he was now...entirely curious. What exactly could she accomplish?","From his blue-gold manifestation a sea of Infinite Sanguine Mana cascaded downward, crimson and gold and boundless, an ocean of self-generated vitality that had no bottom and no end, pouring out of him in a flood that lit the whole sanctuary!","The crimson-gold tide flooded into Calliope’s open codex.","It saturated the pages, soaked into the paper, ran along every line and coatted her black ink until it glistened, ink and Sanguine Mana and Provenance fusing into a single writing-fluid that shone like blood held up to a fire. Every stroke she would make now carried the weight of an existence that owed nothing to anyone.","Calliope laughed!","Her eyes flared with a mad, ecstatic focus as the boundless vitality of Noah’s origin surged through her fingers, filling a well that had been running dry, and she bent to the page, and she wrote, her strokes driven now by the unyielding hammer of Noah’s Provenance behind every letter!","\" THE Vestige of THE Fallen Hero,\" she wrote, and spoke the words as she carved them, \" does not ask the sky for permission to stand!\"","And Noah watched brilliantly as he activated THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle.","He forced his narrative dominance down into the glistening ink, into the sentence taking shape upon the page, and he declared it, declared the written words to be an absolute, un-deletable fact of the immediate domain, a truth that existence was not permitted to argue with!","The whole sanctuary buzzed with the collision of two authorships and an un-editable page, and Noah felt the enormity of what they were writing, and he knew, with magisterial certainty, that he could not hold this.","The stretched instant was already fraying at its edges, the frozen moment beginning to thaw, the dream unable to contain a working this vast for more than a breath.","The instant broke!","BOOM!","And externally, across the whole Cluster of Dimensions, everything went dead silent!"]},{"number":5748,"title":"Chapter 5748: Chapter 5747: A Grand Mythos! II","paragraphs":["The screaming sea stopped. The falling arrows hung. The pale chains stilled. The smell of scorched starlight and old ozone that had hung over the underworld vanished all at once, replaced by something older and heavier, the suffocating scent of ancient volcanic Source, thick and primordial and wrong for this age!","And deep within the core of the Train, through the Dimensional Cabins, echoed a sound that did not belong to anything living now, the sound of colossal, iridescent scales shifting against iron, something vast turning over in a place it had no right to even be!","| SOVEREIGN COLLABORATIVE INSCRIPTION COMPLETE.|","|Syntax: THE VESTIGE OF THE FALLEN HERO.|","| You have ushered and aided in the emergence of an Unfathomable Narrative.|","|+35 PROVENANCE. +15 VERITAS. +15 PONDUS. +25 OSMONTIAN MOIRAI.|","...!","Upon Calliope’s actual body, down in the burning Cluster, a single page rose.","It lifted off her and expanded, and it expanded for Gigaparsecs, a sheet of writing wider than Dimensions, hanging over the underworld like a second sky! And then it did not dissolve, and it did not burn away.","It OPENED! Like an iron gate swinging wide on ancient hinges!","And rising up out of the page came a COFFIN!","A coffin!","A massive obsidian coffin, black as the space between things, ascending slowly out of the opened page, and the whole Cluster of Dimensions held its breath as the lid began, with a grinding finality, to lift.","Obsidian flames spilled out first, pouring from the seams of the coffin, and then the thing inside it rose.","It...was not perceivable! Noah stared and the weavings of existence could not resolve it, could not draw it, could give him nothing but the shape of the obsidian flames that wrapped it, a humanoid silhouette of pure dark fire standing where a body should be, terrible and vast and impossible.","But Noah knew what it was, knew it in the weavings of his frozen existence, because the weavings that poured off it were the same weavings he had felt on a Shard.","The physical, terrifying Remnant of Vakochev!","Noah looked upon it in astonishment, unable to move his masked eye, and down below, everything stopped.","The Infinity Eater stopped bleeding. The Champion stopped rebelling. The Sealed One’s Vessel stopped its suppression of THE Creature. Adrastia looked up solemnly.","Every hunter, every prey, every collapsed and swirling thing in the whole cluster of underworlds went utterly still, and they all looked UP, at the obsidian coffin and the fire-wrapped titan rising from it, in pure astonishment.","What...had THE Writer of Mythos done?!","Just what, in all of existence, had she written?","And the watching Immense Ones erupted at this time.","The gazes of the Immense Ones blazed, and their weavings crashed across the sky, cold and grand and arrogant, arriving one atop another!","| THE SLEEPLESS FIEND observes the fire-wrapped Remnant, and is amused.|","|\"You have brought out another part of your body to die? Good. I did not enjoy killing parts of you the first time as much as I should have.\"|","...!","| THE OVERSEEING ONE recoils. This was not written into his Narrative. A Descendant has authored something he did not permit.|","|\"Impossible. A measly Descendant of ink, raising THAT? Who lent her the hand? WHO?\"|","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR studies the Shard-weavings with cold, greedy interest.|","|\"That is his true remnant. Not a memory. Not a ghost. Oh boy...\"|","| THE GLOATING JAILER counsels caution.|","|\"Careful, brethren. We buried this one for a reason. Twice-buried is a Narrative I do not wish to author a third time.\"|","| THE CACKLING BUTCHER is delighted. THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR, for the first time in an age, is not bored...|","And through all of it, the fire-wrapped Remnant of Vakochev did not react.","He did not look at Calliope who had written him, and he did not look down at the dying underworld beneath his feet. Slowly, deliberately, with the terrible calm of a being who had already died once and found nothing in death worth fearing, the Remnant turned his head UPWARD!","His gaze locked directly onto the observation gallery.","Directly onto the Immense Ones who had slaughtered him an unknown time ago!","...!","Vakochev raised his right arm.","And he swung it, once, horizontally, across the whole span of the tracks of the Dimensional Provenance Train!","His Dimensionality was so unfathomably, monstrously high that in the instant of the swing he vanished from the perception of every existence present, hunters and prey alike, gone from all sight as the movement outpaced the ability of the weavings to hold him.","There was...no explosion!","There was no blast, no fire, no eruption of force!","There was only the sound of reality parting along an unstitched seam, a single clean and terrible sound, as THE Dimensional Provenance Train SPLIT CLEANLY IN TWO!","BOOM!","The residual force of that swing rolled outward in a wave, and Noah, hanging masked at the edge of the gallery, was directly in its path, far too close to the Immense Ones, far too close to the parting of the Train itself.","And it eviscerated him!","The residual wave shredded his masked existence in an instant, tearing his eye apart, unmaking his dreaming presence, obliterating the whole of him where he hung as an eye.","Before, before the forest and the stone and the definition he had made his own, this would have ended him completely, would have collapsed his existence and killed him for good.","But his Dream...was Infinite now.","| Your presence within an Infinite Dream has been destroyed.|","|An Infinite Dream does not end, even in death. The initial cost was paid. You return.|","...!","Noah’s eye reformed!","It bloomed back into existence at the edge of the sky, whole and masked and watching, his dreaming presence stitched back together out of the very dream that could not end, and he gazed out upon what he had helped to make with an existence that had just died and come back.","The other eyes of the Immense Ones buzzed and blazed in fury and shock all around the split, their gazes whipping across the two halves of the sundered Train.","| THE Dimensional Provenance Train has been cleaved and brought to a halt.|","...!","And down in the burning, dying Cluster, upon her own bleeding body, THE Writer of Mythos threw back her head and LAUGHED!","Blood leaked from her nose and ran from the corner of her mouth, painting her chin red, her reserves spent, her ink run dry, her whole existence trembling from the price she had paid, and she laughed and laughed with a wild and ecstatic joy.","\"Oh, now THIS ,\" Calliope gasped through the blood, her eyes shining with mad delight, \" now this can be considered a Mythos worth observing!\"","...!!!"]},{"number":5749,"title":"Chapter 5749: Chapter 5748: You Freed Me!","paragraphs":["Vakochev floated upon the sundered weavings of the Dimensional Provenance Train, and the space around him was no longer space.","The cleaving of the Train had unmade the very definition of the region, and where reality had been there was now only undefinition, a churning obsidian foam that filled everything, existence itself boilng where the seam had parted! And within that foam the Remnant hung, wrapped in his obsidian flames, a silhouette of dark fire standing at the center of a wound in creation, unhurried, unbothered, waiting!","And at the edge of the breach, The Immense Ones gathered!","They came, and they were not entirely perceivable, because beings such as these did not fit inside the sight of anything lesser! At one moment they were massive eyes hanging in the dark, and the next they were gone entirely, present only as pressure, as weight, as a wrongness in the boiling foam.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND stepped forward, his form an undulating silhouette of brilliance that would not rest, flanked by the gathered gazes of THE OVERSEEING ONE, THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, THE GLOATING JAILER, THE CACKLING BUTCHER, and THE STARVING CONNOISSEUR!","A chilling silence gripped the void!","And into that silence, Vakochev spoke!","His voice did not rumble with theatrical rage. It did not roar or thunder or shake the foam. It carried instead the cold, measured cadence of a man presenting a failure to the ones responsible for it.","The obsidian flames turned slowly around him!","\" Across uncounted epochs, you who Remain have extinguished decillions of living beings. Whole Observable Existences and Dimensions, pulverized to nothing. Whole civilizations, ancient and striving and full of small warm lives, harvested down to the bone for a portion of their weavings, their entire histories reduced to a resource and then to silt.\"","His voice never rose. \" And you wrote every one of those deaths into your weavings as meaningless. Unworthy of a second thought. Dust swept from a floor. Decillions upon decillions, and not one of them was ever weighed as anything at all.\"","He looked from one indistinct gaze to the next.","\" And yet. If a single one of you were to bleed. If one Immense One, one, were to die here today, every one of you would shake with hysterical horror! You would call it an impossible crime! You would name it an atrocity against the whole of Existence and hunt the cause of it across every age until the end of things.\"","The foam boiled around the Remnant.","\" So tell me, by what weaving is this measured? By what law is the life of a mortal who owns no borrowed authority weighed as lesser than one of you? Show me the reckoning. Show me the line in existence that says a striving thing with no crown is worth decillions-to-one against a thing like you.\"","His dead quiet eyes swept them. \" You cannot. Because it does not exist. Existence itself does not recognize your hierarchy. Only your violence does. You did not discover that you were worth more. You decided it, and then you killed everything that might have argued.\"","...!","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND answered him.","The Fiend spoke with terrifying scale, with an absolute and sterile condescension that made the foam itself seem to cringe, and there was no anger in it at all.","|A mountain does not hold council with the gravel beneath its base.|","|The lung does not ask permission of the air it consumes.|","|You speak of a reckoning, little ghost, as though the weak and the mighty were entries in the same book. They are not. Those without authority, or with less of it, are not a lesser party to a negotiation. They are scenery. Backdrop. The texture against which the real story unfolds.|","Existence writhed!","| You misunderstand what an Immense One is, and you always did, which is why you died the first time. An Immense One does not merely live within the architecture of existence. An Immense One IS the architecture. And you would have us weigh the scaffold against the dust swept out the door as though they were equals?|","The Fiend’s threads gathered into something almost like a face, and it looked upon Vakochev with a contempt colder than the void!","| That is the delusion of a peasant who discovered how to strike a spark, and in the striking, believed he had invented the sun.|","Vakochev looked at the Fiend with dead quiet eyes!","He did not flinch, and he did not argue the point, because he had not come to win a debate! He had come to correct a record!","\"You slaughtered many of my weavings, \" Vakochev said, and now his voice changed, went lower and more terrible, though it still carried no rage.","\" You broke all of it because you told yourselves a story about it and you believed the story.\"","The obsidian flames flared!","\" You believed that if you stripped away everything I loved, you would break my will. That grief would bring me to my knees. That a being with nothing left to protect would beg, or bend, or surrender the road I walked.\" His dead eyes did not blink. \" You thought my loves were the handles by which you could steer me.\"","He spread his fire-wrapped arms slowly!","\" But you did not break me. You freed me. You...freed me.\"","HUUM!","Vakochev delivered a vow.","\"So here is what I will do today ,\" he said, quiet as the grave he had risen from. \"I am going to look upon an Immense One with the exact same gaze you have cast upon the weak since the beginning of things. The careless gaze. The indifferent one. The gaze that does not even bother to weigh what it is destroying.\"","He looked at the Fiend, and at the gathered gazes, and for the first time something moved behind his dead eyes, and it was not hatred, and it was not grief!","It was indifference!","\"I am going to treat your existence, \" Vakochev said, \" as common cattle.\"","The debate ended, and it ended with the total collapse of local dimensional existenceas...Vakochev MOVED!","Oh, he moved.","His speed exceeded all perception, exceeded Seam-tier sight and Hem-tier sight and everything beneath, and he did not traverse the space between himself and the Fiend, because traversal was for lesser things! He simply forced the coordinate to arrive beneath his boots, willed the destination to become where he already was, and the distance ceased to be relevant.","The clash of Dimensionality detonated across the severed Train.","And the gathered Immense Ones unleashed their combined authority all at once, and as they did, the faint weavings of their eyes vanished from all perception entirely.","Their actions and their power left the realm of the perceivable completely, a war fought at an altitude no lesser existence could witness, the foam itself screaming as titans beyond sight collided within it!","Below, survival became a lottery.","The shockwaves alone, the mere residual ripples of the clash far above, shattered existence for vast spans! Lesser Descendants on the nearby Cabins were flattened into paste before they could draw a single breath, whole ranks of them unmade by a war they could not even see, dying to the backwash of a battle happening somewhere beyond their comprehension.","Down below, amid the shattering, the figure of Calliope appeared!","She rose from the wreckage of her own bleeding body, and she wiped the blood from her face with the back of an ink-stained hand, and she looked up at the churning foam where titans warred beyond sight, and she smiled with pure, radiant fascination.","\" Now this ,\" she breathed, her eyes shining. \" This is a grand story. Okay!\"","And around her, seas of Existential Narrative began to wrap, layer upon layer, a cocoon of authored protection descending over the Writer of Mythos, as THE MATRIARCH OF INK moved at last to shield her Descendant from the storm she had unleashed.","At the rim of it all, Noah tried to see!","He tried to observe the core exchange, the true clash between Vakochev and the Immense Ones, and he could not, because the density of the colliding authorities was blinding, a wall of pure destruction that his sight could not pierce.","And so he reached for the thing he had just made his own.","Infinity!","He thought of it, his own definition, his dream with no far wall, and he conjured a grand and impossible vision within his mind, a dream of a gaze that could stretch forever, an eye that could open onto a vista with no horizon and no edge, a seeing that simply did not stop.","He infused his Provenance with that definition, poured his infinite dreaming into the single act of looking, because he wanted, more than almost anything, to see what a risen Fallen Hero did to the ones who killed him!","He wanted to see!","But even an infinite gaze caught only fragments.","The clash was beyond the threshold where any mind, even his, could assemble the data into a picture.","He caught disjointed, terrifying pieces, flashes torn out of a chaos too vast to hold! An arm tearing clean through a curtain of Dimensionality! The sound of a jaw breaking, somewhere, alongside a roar that had no source he could find! The silhouette of the obsidian coffin, drifting serene and empty through storms of pure and endless Source.","Fragments, only fragments, consequences without their causes, the aftermath of blows he could not perceive being struck.","Then a stray ripple of the Overseeing One’s Dimensionality clipped his masked eye!","The pressure was catastrophic, a mere edge of a mere ripple of one Immense One’s power, and it was enough! Noah’s dreaming form VAPORIZED in a fraction of a nanosecond, unmade before he could even register the touch!","| Presence destroyed. THE INFINITE DREAM remains active. Reconstitution initiated.|","Noah reformed instantly at the perimeter.","And he did not release a single thread of offensive intent! He refused, absolutely, to draw attention, to flare with power, to do anything at all but hang there and watch, a quiet masked eye at the rim of an apocalypse.","Within three seconds a second shockwave, this one from the Fiend’s Dimensionality, tore him apart again.","Noah reconstituted a second time!","And then a third, his eye blooming back into being again and again at the edge of the storm, persisting, immovable, a silent witness who could be destroyed a thosand times and would simply keep returning, watching, saying nothing, doing nothing, refusing to be anything but present.","High in the chaos, two gazes noticed him!","| THE CACKLING BUTCHER observes the masked presence at the rim, destroyed and reformed thrice over.|","|\"Ha! Look at this little thing. Blown to nothing and back again, and again. What a stubborn, useless Immensity it has.\"|","| THE GLOATING JAILER regards him with mild, dismissive interest.|","|\"Some eccentric from a backwater domain, come to gawk. No weapon drawn. No Immensity raised. No intent to strike. He is nothing. Leave him to flicker.\"|","They saw no weapons and no flaring Immensity and no attempt to strike, and so they dismissed him entirely, an eccentric and weak peer from some forgotten corner of existence who happened to possess an irritating immortality technique and not a scrap of combative relevance.","And Noah, dying and returning, dying and returning, let them believe exactly that.","Because he was not here to fight!","He was here to SEE!","...!"]},{"number":5750,"title":"Chapter 5750: Chapter 5749: The Long Night I","paragraphs":["In the heart of the storm, Vakochev chose his target.","He ignored the Sleepless Fiend’s bindings entirely, let the white-hot threads scrape uselessly across his obsidian flames, and drove his path straight toward one gaze and one gaze alone. He went for THE OVERSEEING ONE.","And THE OVERSEEING ONE panicked.","For cycles uncounted, this one had sat in comfort behind protective glass, reaching down to manipulate the small tragedies of mortals, staging their sorrows for his own amusement, arranging their doomed little stories and never once bleeding for any of it! He had authored a decillion deaths from a balcony and paid for none!","Now the glass was gone!","Now the protagonist of his worst and most recent failure, the risen Remnant of the one Narrative he could never fully bury, was coming straight for him through a storm no lesser thing could witness, and there was no railing to lean over and no script to hide behind.","Far at the rim, Noah tried desperately to see!","He poured his infinite gaze into the storm, strained his dreaming sight against the wall of colliding authority, and he caught only fractions, only slivers, disjointed pieces of a thing too vast to hold.","The suggestion of a lunge! A curtain of Dimensionality torn aside! A shape closing on a shape! Fragments, always fragments, the storm too dense and too high for even an infinite eye to pierce.","But he saw enough to know that Vakochev had reached him.","Vakochev’s hands closed around THE OVERSEEING ONE’s throat!","And the coffin answered.","The single obsidian coffin that had risen from Calliope’s page transformed in an instant into INFINITE coffins, countless obsidian caskets unfolding out of one another and wrapping around the two combatants, sealing them together inside an existential grave, a tomb of endless black boxes that closed over the architect and the ghost and shut the rest of existence out!","And inside that grave, the struggle was brutal.","It was unadorned! It was utterly devoid of majesty! There was no grand engineering here, no cascade of complex weavings, no dazzling display of a titan’s full art!","In the barely-perceivable dark of those infinite coffins, Vakochev simply HELD the thrashing architect, gripped him with the exact cold, dismissive strength of a butcher holding a squealing pig over a drainage trough, indifferent to its terror, unbothered by its struggle, waiting only for the moment to do the necessary thing!","And then he did the necessary thing.","With a sharp, concussive twist of his wrists, Vakochev snapped THE OVERSEEING ONE’s neck!","And as he did, unknown seas of THE Primordial Source and raw Dimensionality poured out of the Remnant and INTO the dying architect, flooding him, drowning him from within with something that even Noah, straining every fiber of his infinite gaze, could not perceive!","Whatever Vakochev truly did in that instant, whatever authority he drove into his enemy along with the killing twist, it happened behind a veil that no eye present could lift.","CRACK!","THE OVERSEEING ONE’s scream shattered across the whole of the Dimensional Skies!","His chest cavity caved inward, collapsing as though a hand the size of an existence had closed on it! His eyes burst into blinding silver light, and out of that light his stolen records began to unravel, ages of harvested history spilling out of him and coming apart.","And Vakochev, holding the ruined and screaming thing, drew back a fire-wrapped fist and drove it into the dying architect’s skull, extinguishing his Trueness completely, snuffing the last of what he was!","THE OVERSEEING ONE died.","An architect had FALLEN!","Vakochev dropped the limp corpse!","It fell away into the infinite coffins, a dead Immense One, a thing that was never supposed to be possible, and the Remnant turned his dead quiet gaze upon the stunned, indistinct faces of the Immense Ones who remained.","And he spoke a single word into the ringing silence, a quiet and terrible parting sentence.","\" One.\"","...!","Then Vakochev stepped backward into the unstitched void.","His fire-wrapped body dissolved into the cracks of Existence itself, sinking into the seams his own swing had torn, vanishing back into the wound in creation from which he had come.","And THE SLEEPLESS FIEND roated in fury!","The white-hot threads erupted, and the Fiend surged into the dark after the vanishing Remnant, and THE UNPAID COLLECTOR surged with him, and THE CACKLING BUTCHER too, three of the mightiest gazes in existence plunging into the cracks in violent, howling pursuit of the ghost who had just killed one of their own!","—","An Immense One had been killed!","Noah gazed upon the impossible from the rim, his masked existence rigid with astonishment, and around him many other perceptions did the same! Was Vakochev truly so grand? Truly so terrible that a mere Remnant of him, a Vestige written back into being by a bleeding Descendant’s pen, could reach into the gathered Immense Ones and simply snap the neck of one?","But even as Noah and all the others reeled with that thought...","Existence itself began to shake!","| The historical mass of a fallen architect does not vanish cleanly.|","|An Immense One’s weavings and folded dimensions have begun an immediate, uncontrolled gravitational collapse...|","The whole region trembled and groaned, and the collapse of the dead architect’s immense volume rippled outward, and existence shuddered around them all!","It looked like something was about to happen to the corpse of the Immense One.","Some process was about to start due to this death.","But...it was interrupted. Or more aptly, it was superseded.","Because in the very next instant, something happened that had not happened before in all of existence.","Every single existence present that held any access to authority, any weaving at all capable of communicating with the surrounding fabric of existence, which was to say every being grand enough to perceive the changes rippling through reality, received a message.","It came in a language older than any tongue, older than agreement itself, and yet every one of them understood it inherently, understood it the way a body understands that the air around it has grown warmer, not through translation but through sensation, a direct communication between a living thing and existence itself.","And the message that every perceiving existence received in that moment, felt in the core of their weavings, was this!","| All conditions have been fulfilled.|","...!","All conditions have been fulfilled?","What conditions? What conditions had been set, and by whom, and when, and what did their fulfillment mean? Noah’s mind raced, grasping at a thing with no handle, a message from existence itself with no context and no source and no...","HUUM!","Right after, Noah’s manifestation in that space began to SHIVER!","He blinked, confused, and he looked up, and...","Snow began to fall!","Snow?!","Noah stared upward in disbelief as, out of the murky obsidian foam, out of the churning undefinition all around, snow came drifiting down! A storm of it! White flakes descending in their countless millions across the boiling dark, falling over the shattered remnants of the Dimensional Provenance Train, over the sundered Cabins that stretched away for Gigaparsecs, settling upon the wreckage of a battle beyond perception.","A blizzard, blooming into being across a region of existence that had never known such a thing.","It did not stem from the dead Immense One as much as...it seemed to stem from Existence itself!","And the descent of that snow came with a terrible coldness.","It wrapped over everyone, over everything, a cold that sank past skin and past weaving and into the very substanace of an existence, and Noah himself, hanging masked at the rim, truly felt it.","Cold!","For the first time in what seemed like forever, Noah Osmont felt cold!","How could he feel cold? He, who had bathed in scorching springs and endured the torture of Immense Ones and walked out of the collapse of his own dream. How could a drifting flake of snow reach past all of that and touch him with a chill?","And it was not only him! It was not only the cold!","Prompts bloomed across his sight, and they were not comforting!","| Your existence is being affected by an unknown weaving, established across existence as an EXISTENTIAL CONDITION.|","|Source: unknown. Scope: pervasive. This Condition is spreading.|","|THE CONDITION OF THE DESCENDING COLD:|","|All attributes are being suppressed. All authority is being slowed, dimmed, and made heavy.|","|The suppression scales with the authority held. The mightier the existence, the deeper the cold reaches, and the more it takes.|","|Those who hold the most are affected the most...|","...!","Those who held the most were affected the MOST?","Noah read those words with a chill that had nothing to do with the snow, because he understood, dimly, the shape of what that meant.","A cold... that hunted power? A weather that fell hardest upon the mighty? A Condition that would press lightest on a peasant and crush hardest upon an Immense One?","And below him, layer upon layer of white snow descended.","It fell upon the burning Cluster of underworlds! It fell upon Calliope, who looked up at it with a somber frown, her fascination gone quiet, and shivered where she stood inside the Matriarch’s protection.","Far in the distance, even THE Creature shivered, the coldness wrapping around his titanic frame, and his obsidian-white flames flickered, dimming, guttering against a chill they had never met!","And further still, THE SEALED ONE raised his hands, and around his Vessel a storm of snow circled and howled, frost creeping across everything he was, ice climbing the edges of a being who had walked across existence untouched by anything, now touched at last by a cold that did not care what he had conquered!","A catastrophe had begun.","At this moment, no one understood why! No one understood how! No one could name the conditions that had been fulfilled or the hand that had set them or the weaving that now fell as snow across the murky dark.","But it was pervasive.","And it was occurring across the whole of Existence!"]},{"number":5751,"title":"Chapter 5751: Chapter 5750: The Long Night II","paragraphs":["Far beneath the war of titans, far beneath the dying architect and the cracking Train and the murky obsidian foam, in a small Universe folded inside a small Observable Existence, upon a small world that had never once heard the name of an Immense One or any glimpses of authority, there was a desert.","And in that desert, there was a fire!","Around the fire sat a tribe, men and women and children wrapped in the hides of desert beasts, their brown faces lit warm and orange by the flames, and they sat close together against the cool of the night and they listened.","For it was the hour of stories, and the Wisewoman had begun to speak.","She was old, older than anyone could remember being young, her hands like knotted roots and her eyes like two dark wells that had seen every star wheel across the sky a thousand times. She sat at the head of the fire, and her voice was low and worn and beautiful, and she told the story that had been told at this fire since before her grandmother’s grandmother had first heard it!","\"Listen now,\" the Wisewoman said, \"and remember, for a story remembered is a life saved. I will tell you of The Long Night.\"","The children leaned in.","\"There will come a time,\" she said, \"long foretold and long feared, when the world turns cold. When the warmth that has always been simply begins to leave, first from the edges of things, and then from the heart of them. When a coldness that no fire can answer permeates the desert and the sea and the high places and the low, creeping into the sand and the water and the very breath in your chest.\"","The fire crackled, and the shadows danced!","\"And in that time,\" she went on, her old eyes moving across the ring of faces, \"the night will grow long. Not one night, but a night that does not end, a darkness that stretches on and on past every dawn that should have come, until the sun itself seems to forget the way back. This is The Long Night. When the cold comes and the night will not lift. And the old stories say that when it comes, all the world must huddle close, and wrap itself in every warmth it has hoarded, and endure, and wait, and hope that the dawn remembers us at the end.\"","Then a child rose up!","He was a small boy, bold and bright-eyed, and he stood at the edge of the fire with his little chin lifted, and he pointed at the old woman as snot leaked from his nose.","\"Wisewoman!\" he said. \"I know why you tell us this! You only tell it to make us afraid, so that we behave and stay close to the fire! But this story has never come true, not once, not for all the generations! My father heard it, and his father, and his father’s father, and the night has always ended and the sun has always come back! It is only a story to frighten little snotty children!\"","Some of the adults chuckled softly, and a few frowned at the boy’s boldness, but the Wisewoman only smiled!","She smiled at him with all the patience of her long years, and she opened her mouth to answer him, to tell him gently that a story does not need to have come true to be worth the keeping...","And then she blinked!","For she had felt something!","Something small and cold and impossible had landed upon the withered skin of her cheek, a tiny pinprick of chill in the warm desert night, and she paused, her smile faltering, and she raised one old knotted hand and touched her face and drew it back and looked at it.","And there, melting upon the dark root of her fingertip, was a snowflake.","A snowflake!","The Wisewoman stared at it, and her ancient heart went still!","And a moment later, another fell! And another! And then more, and more, drifting down out of the black desert sky in their impossible countless numbers, white flakes descending upon a land that had never in all its histroy known a single one, settling on the sand, on the hides, on the upturned faces of the tribe as one by one they felt the cold touch and looked UP!","Snow!","Snow was falling in the desert!","A ripple of shock ran through the tribe, and then of fear, and then of a horror that had no words! The children cried out! The men surged to their feet! The women clutched their little ones close! They stared up at the falling white as it thickened, as the warm orange firelight caught the drifting flakes and turned them to sparks of gold falling out of the endless dark, beautiful and terrible, a thing that should not be, a thing that could not be, falling and falling upon a desert that had known only sun and heat since the world began.","And the bold boy who had stood to mock the story stood frozen now, his little face turned upward, a snowflake melting on his cheek, his eyes wide with a terror he could not name.","The Wisewoman trembled!","Her old body shook, and for a moment she was only an old and frightened woman under a sky that had broken its oldest promise. But then her eyes shone, because she was the Wisewoman, and she carried the story, and the story had a second half that was not for frightening children but for saving them.","For generations, they had prepared.","She rose from her place at the fire!","She moved through the tribe, through the crying and the shouting and the upturned faces, moving with a purpose that stilled them as she passed, and she went to one hut at the edge of the circle, an old hut, a hut the children had always been told never to open.","And she opened it!","Inside, stacked and waiting, were furs! Thick hides and heavy woven things, layers upon layers of warmth, gathered and cured and stored accross untold generations by keepers of the story who had never once seen them used.","Warmth hoarded for a night that had never come, waiting patient in the dark for the day the old woman’s smile would falter and a snowflake would land upon her cheek!","The Wisewoman turned back to her people!","She looked upon the men and the women and the frightened children beneath the falling snow, and she spoke, and her worn old voice carried across the whole trembling tribe with the weight of every generation that had kept the tale alive!","\"Come,\" she said. \"Come now, all of you, and wrap yourselves in layers of protection. Take the furs your fathers’ fathers saved for you and cover yourselves against the cold, and gather close, and do not let the fire die!\"","She held the old hut open, and the snow fell past her into the warm firelight, and her shining eyes swept them all!","\"The Long Night... has come.\"","...!","---","Deep within THE Infiniverse, in a Realm folded inside the Helios Elsedimension, the sun hung warm and golden over a beach of soft golden sand, and no one there had a single worry in all of existence.","For this was the safest place there was.","This was inside the very heart of THE True Human Emperor’s own empire, a domain sealed away from every gaze and every hunter and every architect, a paradise where the sheltered lived their sheltered lives and wanted for nothing.","Elizabeth reclined upon a beach chair near the shimmering water, and she was at ease.","She had been someone of power once, back in Noah’s homeworld, a figure of standing in the days before he had cleared away every threat that world held and departed for The Beast World and beyond. She had crossed paths with him in The Blessed Empire, and now she dwelled here, in comfort, in safety, one of the countless souls the Emperor had gathered under his boundless wing.","Above her, a great eagle wheeled slow and lazy across the golden sky, and up and down the beach, other humans went about their peaceful business, walking the sand, floating in the bright shallows, dozing in the sun, and every single one of them was wrapped in slow-flowing rivers of blue mana, saturated in it, swimming in an abundance of authority that made the harshness of the old worlds a distant and half-forgotten dream.","It was warm! It was golden! It was perfect!","And then, all at once, it was not.","Snow fell.","Out of the warm golden sky, out of the clear and cloudless blue over that sheltered beach, white flakes came drifting down, and with them came a coldness sweeping across the golden sand and the bright water and the lazy sunbathers in an instant!","Elizabeth’s eyes flew open, and she sat up sharply in her chair!","Cold?","She rose to her feet, staring up at the impossible snow, and her long experience took over before her confusion could! She raised one hand and called upon her mana, and the blue rivers that flowed around her answered instantly, gathering and weaveng at her gesture, forming into a thick and luxurious robe of fur that wrapped itself around her shoulders and settled warm against her skin.","And still she felt cold!","She frowned! The robe should have been more than enough, a working of pure mana, warmth conjured from abundance, and yet the chill sank straight through it as though it were nothing.","So she gathered her mana again, and wove a second layer over the first, thicker and heavier, and when that too was not enough she wove a third, piling authority upon authority, wrapping herself in layer after layer of conjured warmth!","Only then, beneath three thick robes of woven mana, did she feel some small measure of protection from the cold!","Some. Not all. The chill still pressed at the edges of her, patient and deep!","Elizabeth stood on the golden beach in her three heavy robes, her breath misting now in the air of a paradise that had never once been cold, and she looked around in growing bewilderment!","What was going on?","Why was it so cold, here, in THE Infiniverse?Cold did not come here! This place was sealed, protected, perfect, a haven where nothing bad had ever reched!","And more than that, more troubling than all the rest of it...","How could she feel cold at all?","She was saturated with mana! Every soul on this beach was! They were filled to overflowing with immense concentrations of authority, swimming in more power than the people of the old worlds had ever dreamed of, and mana was warmth, mana was life, mana was the very thing that held the cold and the dark at bay! A being so full of it should not be able to feel a chill any more than the sun could feel the night.","And yet the cold reached her!","And as she stood there shivering beneath three robes, Elizabeth noticed something that turned her bewilderment toward true unease.","Down the beach, some were faring worse than others. The strongest among them, the ones with the deepest and richest rivers of mana flowing about them, were the ones huddling lowest, wrapping themselves in the most layers, shivering the hardest.","And a child nearby, a small thing with only the faintest trickle of mana to its name, stood in the falling snow looking merely puzzled, barely troubled by the cold at all!","The more mana one held, the heavier the cold pressed.","The stronger you were, the colder you became!","Elizabeth pulled her robes tighter and stared up at the snow falling through the golden light of a broken paradise, and a single thought rose cold and clear in her mind, a thought that would soon rise in the minds of countless others across the whole of existence.","Something, somewhere, had gone terribly wrong!"]},{"number":5752,"title":"Chapter 5752: Chapter 5751: The Long Night III","paragraphs":["Across the whole of THE Infiniverse, the two sisters worked to shield the dreamers.","Upon the boundless blue-gold sea, THE Infiniverse and Ruination moved their hands in vast and patient rhythm, and waves of infinity and seas of THE Primordial Source surged out from them, rolling across the folded Realms toward the great chrysalis and the countless sleeping bodies within the empire.","The authorities wrapped around each dreamer, layer upon layer, a blanket of the oldest powers there were laid over the people Noah loved and cherished as they lived their centuries in dream, holding the descending cold at bay.","And yet, even as they worked, Ruination’s crimson eyes were troubled!","\"A condition was supposedly fulfilled ,\" she said, her voice its usual calm and analytical self, and yet somber beneath it now. \" The weaving of existence declared it plainly to all who could perceive, and it came in the very instant that Immense One died. The two are linked. Of that there is no doubt. The question that remains, is the one I cannot yet close.\"","Her hands never stopped their work!","\" Why?\"","She turned the problem over as she wove!","\"I currently hold a hypothesis. That after a certain number of Immense Ones fell, paired perhaps with other conditions I cannot yet perceive, something was triggered. Something that, in the deep weavings of existence, tied somehow to IT. Atlas was killed. Other Immense Ones have likely been killed across the ages. Vakochev was killed. And now, today, with another Immense One killed before the eyes of his own kind, whatever their deaths mean in the reckoning of existence has tipped a scale that was already tipping.\"","Her crimson gaze sharpened!","\"It has been tipping for a long time. And this last death was the weight that finished it. But why? Why should the deaths of the mighty summon a cold that hunts the mighty? Why?\" She said it again, quietly. \" Why?\"","And at that moment, Noah’s body appeared upon the golden shore!","He came into the Realm calm and unhurried, but his expression was heavy. He raised his hands, and from him a tide of Infinite Sanguine Mana poured out, crimson and gold, and he wove it into thick, warm coats, and he wrapped them around the ones he loved.","He wrapped his floating mother, sleeping in her pool, in a heavy coat of his own vitality! He wrapped little Seo-yeon, and Henry, and Riya, and one by one every other soul dreaming within his empire, layering the warmth of his own blood over them, shielding them with the one authority that answered to nothng but himself.","And as he worked, Noah reflected!","He wondered about his own hand in all of this! He had dreamed, and he had reached across the Cluster and lent his red ink to Calliope.","That lending had led to the emergence of Vakochev! And Vakochev’s emergence had led to the death of an Immense One. And that death had tipped the scale that Ruination spoke of, had fulfilled some final unknown condition, had called down this cold across the whole of existence.","His actions were part of this causality!","And yet...","So were the actions of a great many others! So were the deaths the Immense Ones themselves had dealt across the ages! So was the killing of Atlas, and the killing of Vakochev, and every weight the mighty had ever laid upon the scale! He was one hand among countless hands, one cause among an ocean of causes, and the scale had been tipping long before he ever lent his ink to a bleeding writer.","But that changed nothing about the question at the heart of it all.","Just what was this? What was this emergence of coldness that ignored authority itself, that fell hardest upon the strongest, that reached even into the sealed heart of his empire and touched the skin of a being like him?","Noah finished wrapping the last of the dreamers, and he turned to his Ruination.","\"Give me your confirmed analysis of this Condition,\" he said. \" Fully. Everything you have so far.\"","And Ruination answered,.","| No barrier of THE Infiniverse has been able to halt its emergence. No authority, no sealing, no Elsedimension, no weaving has stopped it or slowed it.|","|It has covered every Realm across the whole of THE Infiniverse. It has covered THE Ymnaros. It has covered every Dimension and Observable Existence over which our influence has ever spread. It is everywhere our reach extends, and it is beyond it also.|","|Effect confirmed: those who hold no authority are affected LEAST. The strongest lifeforms must enact the strongest protections merely to steer clear of the cold. Power is not a shield against this Condition. Power is a target.|","Ruination’s voice continued, and it grew heavier.","\" And it is not only the suppression, Master. I have begun monitoring your own existence, and I must tell you what I find there, because you will feel it soon yourself. Your biological systems have already begun to respond. Even now, energy is being metabolized within you, burned and spent, consumed to hold the cold at bay from the inside.\"","|Master’s biological systems are metabolizing energy at an accelerating rate to resist the Condition.|","|You will begin to feel hunger. Soon.|","\" For now ,\" Ruination went on, \" the Infinity running through your existence can feed your cells and your quarks faster than the cold can drain them. You can sustain yourself on your own boundlessness, or so I first believed. \"","Her tone tightened. \" But my monitoring shows that even your Infinity is not fully reclaiming everything the cold takes. There is a loss. A leak that your boundlessness cannot entirely close. Which means that in time, even you, Master, may need to consume biological matter to protect yourself from this cold.\"","| Projection: authority alone will not sustain existence against the Condition indefinitely.|","|All existences, whether of the Finite Verse, the Ineffable Verse, or the Immense Ones themselves, will likely feel the need to consume biological life to sustain themselves against the cold, in addition to spending their authority.|","\"And I must be honest with you about the limits of what I say,\" Ruination finished. \" All of this, everything I have told you, is only what we have been able to grasp in the first few minutes of its emergence. We do not yet understand the full scope of this Existential Condition. We understand almost nothing of it. We only see the edges of a thing that is still arriving.\"","And even Ruination, who was never anything but composed, seemed somber and serious as she spoke those last words.","Beside her, THE Infiniverse stood with her starlit eyes closed, utterly still, her whole vast attention turned inward and outward at once, sensing every change occurring across the whole of her boundless existence, feeling the cold creep into every Realm she held, cataloging a catastrophe she could not stop from spreading through her own body.","And Noah stood upon the golden sands of his shore, and he looked up!","Snowflakes drifted down out of the golden sky and settled upon his skin and did not melt, and the cold pressed at him even through all that he was, and his expression was heavy, heavy with the weight of a thing he had helped to cause and could not yet understand, a catastrophe with no name and no source and no cure, falling silent and white and terrible across the whole of Existence.","---","Another of Noah’s bodies arrived in a place where time had come apart.","It stepped out of a conceptual tear and into a Dimension of deep purple and drifting green, and it was a broken and beautiful ruin of a place! Scattered through the twilight air hung the hands of clocks, thousands upon thousands of them, some vast as mountains and some small as needles, spinning and stopped and spinning backward all at once.","And through them drifted meteorites, tumbling slow across the purple dark, and every one of those meteorites was shaped like a number, ancient figures of stone and starlight wheeling through a sky that had forgotten how to keep time!","This was a Dimension lost to time itself, one of the most profound Elsedimensions Atlas had ever made.","And yet even here, even in this sanctuary of shattered hours, the cold had come.","Noah looked, and he saw a storm of snow gathering, wrapping itself around the drifting clock-hands, frosting the numbered meteorites, and creeping even up his own arm to wreath the illusory ring upon his finger.","Even Atlas was affected! Even a Dimension outside of time could not keep the descending cold from its door!","But first, Noah turned his attention inward, and he analyzed.","He examined the cold as it pressed against him, studied the way it sank past his skin and reached toward the deep structure of his existence, and he traced its effect through every layer of himself. His Perpetual Baryogenesis was running, the weight of existence trickling down onto his two hundred decillion quarks without pause, and he could feel the cold trying to slow that trickle, trying to press heavy upon each quark and dim its generation.","His Nine Teloi burned steady against it, holding the lattice of his existence firm, and his Provenance surged warm and boundless through the whole of him, feeding his cells and his quarks against the chill.","For now, he held! For now, his foundation was more than the cold could take.","And as he took stock of himself, the prompts of his recent trials bloomed before him, the gains he had earned in the writing of a Fallen Hero!","|For your role in aiding and ushering the emergence of an Unfathomable Narrative, and for witnessing the fall of an Immense One, your existence has been enriched.|","|Your foundation, tempered by Perpetual Baryogenesis and the guiding of grand dreams, has climbed.|","Noah pulled up the full account of himself, and read where he now stood.","| THE True Human Emperor / THE Human Dreamer|","|VERITAS: 223|","|PROVENANCE: 275|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 223|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 251|","| THE Enduring Gu Elsedimension Ring +20 all; THE Existential Foundational Narrative Inscription +50 all, folded into the totals above.)|","His Provenance had surged well past everything else, climbing faster than his other attributes with every dream he guided and every narrative he touched.","A few dozen points gained in these last trials alone, his authorship swelling toward something the rest of him could not yet match.","He was becoming, more and more, a creature of pure Provenance, of pure infinity and dreaming, and the numbers only confirmed what he already felt.","But even reading his own grand ascent, Noah felt it.","A small thing! A slow and growing emptiness deep in the core of him, rising patient beneath all his boundless power.","Hunger!","It was beginning, exactly as Ruination had warned! The cold was metabolizing him from within, burning his energy to hold itself at bay, and even his Infinity could not fully close the leak as it was not even for lack of its authority or brilliance.","It was as if this Existential Condition purposefully made things this way.","Slowly, softly, Noah Osmont was beginning to grow hungry.","Then he turned to the ring upon his finger!","\" Atlas ,\" Noah said. \" Do you know what this is all about? This Existential Condition? This coldness?\"","The illusory old body of Atlas flickered up out of the ring, and snow gathered around his translucent shoulders even as he formed, dusting his ancient projected frame with white!","|I cannot say for sure ,| Atlas said. | But it should be linked to IT. Maybe. I have heard musings, across my long life, that I never once thought I would need.|","The clock-hands turned in the cold behind him!","| One musing was this. That if a certain threshold of something is reached across the whole of Existence, if Existential Narrative is abused, or torn, or spent and then discarded, time and time again, across enough ages, then something would arise to correct it. A response. A balancing. Existence, pushed too far, pushing back.|","His projected eyes were distant!","| Another musing I know is older still. You know how we speak of Those Who Remain, the Immense Ones who stayed? There were Immense Ones who leapt across an uncrossable barrier, once, in the earliest age. And the others, the ones we call Those Who Remain, are the ones who FAILED to make that leap. And in that failure, in whatever they did all those ages ago when they tried and could not, something was done to Existence itself. Something was broken, or bent, or spent. And IT was involved then, at that failure, just as I believe IT is involved now.|","Atlas lowered his hand slowly!","|No Immense One holds IT. Not truly. You have told me yourself how your girl came back from a future where THE Sealed One was given IT by the Immense Ones, and even that cannot be entirely true, because IT cannot be given. Perhaps he was granted a grasp of some power related to it. Perhaps that action, in that future, abused something and fulfilled yet another condition of the many. I cannot be certain of the shape of any of it.|","He looked up, into the drifting clocks!","| But this coldness spreading across existence is a point of change. A great one. What this change will entail, even I do not know. But time.| He almost smiled, and there was iron beneath it.","| Time will have all answers, and time will give them, to those patient and clever enough to ask. That is why we are here, in this body of yours, in this Dimension of mine that stands outside the flow. We are here to look for solutions using time itself. And there is much to do before either of us understands what just changed in the bones of Existence...|","Even Atlas could not be sure.","Noah stood among the broken hours and the falling snow and turned it all over in his mind! An Existential Condition tied to IT, to the failure of the ones who Remained, to the abuse of Existential Narrative across the ages, to the death of Immense Ones, to a scale tipped at last.","A change in the very bones of existence, and no one, not Ruination, not Atlas, not the Immense Ones themselves, understood it.","He needed to understand!","His masked portion of existence, his eye that dreamed among the Immense Ones, the presence within his Infinite Dream that could be destroyed and destroyed again and would always return, that may be the best instrument he had for gathering the truth of this.","For where better to learn what an Immense One knew, than to sit among them and watch and listen as their own certainties crumbled in the falling snow?","He had to understand!","He had to understand exactly what this change meant, before existence itself grew cold enough to answer the question for him.","Because...nobody knew if it would continue to get colder. Nobody knew if there was a future where it grew so cold...that Gilded Lifeforms, Source Lifeforms, Infinite Lifeforms, Primeval Ones, Descendants, Provenance Lifeforms, Gu...or even Immense Ones...would become frozen blocks of ice."]},{"number":5753,"title":"Chapter 5753: Chapter 5752: A Stranger! I","paragraphs":["The chase had scattered them.","Across the two sundered halves of the Dimensional Provenance Train, the gathered gazes had broken formation and thrown themselves into the cracks of existence after the ghost who had killed one of their own.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND, THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, THE CACKLING BUTCHER, all of them gone into the dark, howling and blazing after what remained of Vakochev, chasing a Fallen Hero back into the wound he had vanished through!","An Immense One had been slain! Every one of them wanted to be the hand that made certain it did not happen twice.","So the region emptied.","Noah watched it empty from the far rim, his masked eye hanging quiet in the falling snow. Where the sky had been crowded with the eyes of monsters, now there were only a few, and then fewer, gazes flickering out and vanishing into the deep dark, each one gone on its own hunt or its own retreat from the cold that had begun to fall.","While one of his bodies stood at the threshold of the Atlas Elsedimension of shattered time, ready to begin the search for something, this body, this masked dreaming eye, simply watched the aftermath of a thing that should never have been possible.","He watched Calliope.","Down in the wreckage of the Cluster, the Writer of Mythos sat in the ruin of her own spent existence, and she was cold. The fascination had gone out of her, worn down by the snow and the blood she had lost.","She lifted an ink-stained hand and wrote a single flowing line upon the air, and out of it unfolded a fur coat, thick and warm, that wrapped itself around her thin shoulders. She pulled it close and huddled down into it against the chill. Even she, who had just written the death of an architect, sat shivering like anyone else, wrapped in a coat she had written for herself!","In the distance, THE Creature still stood.","The titanic King had endured the storm and the suppression and the fall of the Overseeing One, and he remained, a silent mountain, his obsidian flames guttering low against the cold!","But he did not stay long. Slowly he turned, gathered the tatters of his conquered army and began to retreat slowly, watching in the corner of his eyes.","Adrastia, The Sealed One, The Infinity Eater...many seemingly sensed the sudden change and began pulling back slowly, as if they were being cautious first to see what else would happen!","And above it all, Noah looked up.","He turned his gaze toward the place where the corpse of the slain Immense One hung in the churning obsidian foam, and he strained his infinite sight upon it, and he could not see it!","Not truly. Not even now. The Overseeing One was dead, snuffed out, his Trueness put out by a fire-wrapped fist, and still the corpse sat past the reach of Noah’s eye, a wrongness in the foam, a shape his sight slid off of and could not hold, there only as a pressure and an absence and a low buzz in the weavings around it.","And that, more than anything, made him think about what an Immense One truly was.","He had watched a battle between titans, and he had seen almost none of it. His gaze was Infinite now. His sight was a dream with no far wall. And still, when Vakochev and the Immense Ones had truly clashed, they had simply left the reach of the perceivable behind.","He had caught fragments. Slivers torn out of a chaos too big to hold. An arm through a curtain. The sound of a jaw breaking. A coffin drifting through storms of Source. He had seen what their blows left behind and never the blows themselves. He had watched Vakochev seem to close his hands on a throat and seem to snap a neck, and even that, even the killing, had come to him in broken pieces, like a man trying to watch lightning by the shape of the burnt ground it left behnd.","That was what an Immense One was!","What did it mean when a mind that possessed hundreds of attributes could not even form a complete image of a dead lifeform? Was the gap between a Provenance Lifeform and an Immense One merely a count of numbers, or was it a gap of category so profound that standard perception broke upon contact with their physical remains?","Their power did not just beat his. It beat his ability to see it happen! They fought at a height where sight itself gave out, where even a being of Infinite dreaming caught only the wreckage after, because the true shape of their war was simply too vast and too high to be held by any eye below their own. He had spent this whole stretch thinking of himself as something grand, an author sitting unseen among them, steering their stories from the dark, and he was.","But he had just been reminded, hard, of the gulf that still lay between a masked watcher at the rim and the beings whose battle he could not even watch.","The Overseeing One was dead, and Noah still could not see the corpse! A dead Immense One was more than his living sight could hold. What did that say about the ones still breathing? About THE SLEEPLESS FIEND, whose brightness he had barely dared to look at? About the gazes chasing Vakochev through the dark right now?","He had watched one of them die, and he had not really seen the death, and he could not really see the body, and if he ever meant to stand against such beings instead of just hiding from them, he had a very long road left to walk.","But even as that settled into him, he felt something else.","Existence was buzzing around the corpse he could not see!","The weavings near the dead architect were stirring. Gathering. Trembling, as though the death were not an ending but the start of something, as though somethng were about to come out of the ruin of a fallen Immense One that had not yet shown its face.","So Noah did the thing he was best at.","He watched. Masked, quiet, unseen, a patient eye at the rim of an emptying battlefield, snow falling silent across his dreaming form, he fixed his gaze on the buzzing weavings around a corpse he could not perceive, and he waited to see what would rise from the death of an Immense One!","The battlefield was somewhat empty now, and the snow kept falling.","Noah looked out over the ruin of a thing that should never have happened as he watched it!","And then the cold began to move.","It did not fall on the corpse like how the snow fell on everything else, soft and scattered. It gathered. Across the whole vast region the descending cold drew together, thickening, condensing, and it began to flow toward the dead architect in rivers, great pale currents of it pouring in from every direction, rushing into the corpse and vanshing inside it!","Noah watched the white streams converge and drain into the thing he could not see, and a deep wrongness crawled through his dreaming existence, because a corpse should not drink. A death should not pull the cold into itself like a mouth pulling at water. A dead thing should lie still!","This one drank, and drank, and drank!","The cold poured into the unperceivable corpse for a long moment, more and more of it, concentrations that would have flattened lesser existences gathering into a single dead point. And Noah, watching, felt something begin that he had no name for, a pressure building where an ending should have been, a held breath that would not release.","Then, where a death had been, a life bloomed!","Something formed from the corpse. Something titanic!","Noah strained his infinite gaze upon it, poured his whole definition of endless sight into the single act of looking, and even so he could barely perceive the thing that rose. It came up out of the drinking corpse slow and vast, a shape of blue-white cold and jagged rime, humanoid and utterly wrong, its edges never resolving, its features refusing to hold under his sight!","Where its eyes should have been, there were only two points of pale ice, cold and depthless. It moved with a terrible unhurried grace, a thing in no hurry at all, a thing with all the time in Existence.","And Noah knew the face!","He knew it, and he could not make himself believe it, because he had seen this face before, once, in a vision inside a Runestone, walking through a Primordial forest and scattering worlds to feed fish in a river!","It was Lucy. It was the small rough caveman-being who had smiled and given the infinite away like feed. But it was frozen now. Ancient and hollowed and rimed with a cold that had eaten the warmth out of it, the same face turned to ice, the same shape emptied of everything that had made it kind.","The visage did not look at him.","It did not look at anything. Not at Noah masked and staring at the rim. Not at the few frozen survivors who had not yet fled. Not even at the corpse it had risen from, the dead architect whose death had somehow become its cradle. It simply stood there in the falling snow, vast and indifferent, a thing that had come up out of a death and did not care about a single living gaze upon it.","It raised its hands.","And a forest came!","Out of nothing, out of the frozen dark, trees erupted across the whole of the region and planted themselves in the empty space. Boundless, countless, they rose and spread, vegetation climbing outward for Gigaparsecs, a forest blooming across a battlefield in an instant as it spread for countless Gigaparsecs.","They were the trees from the vision!","The Dimension-bearing trees, the ancient boughs that grew Observable Existences and Dimensions like ripening fruit, the orchard of realities Lucy had walked through in the beginning of things. But these were not budding with warm and swirling worlds!","These were rimed and dormant, their fruit frozen hard upon the branches, whole Observable Existences and Elsedimensions hanging still and cold and asleep in their boughs, a forest of frozen Domains spreading silent accross the ruin.","Prompts bloomed across Noah’s sight, and they gave him no comfort at all.","| An unfathomable event has occurred. A life has bloomed from the death of an Immense One.|","|The region is being reclassified. Existence here is being overwritten by an unknown weaving.|","|A frozen growth has taken root: dormant Observable Existences and Dimensions are forming within it, held still and cold.|","|This is beyond current understanding. The nature of the emerged existence cannot be perceived or measured...|","Noah read the words seriously!","And the frost-visage of Lucy, having planted its forest, was done.","It did not linger. It did not survey its work or turn to see who watched. It simply took a single step, one unhurried stride into the falling snow, and it was gone, vanished as completely as if it had never been, indifferent to the very end, leaving behind only a growing frozen forest over the disappearing corpse of an Immense One turning into flickers of nothing!","Noah hung there, staring.","Below him, slow and silent, the frost-trees began to grow. Their frozen boughs stretched a fraction wider. Their rimed fruit swelled a fraction fuller. The forest of dormant worlds crept outward across the ruined region, patient and cold and unstoppable, and Noah watched it spread and felt the weight of a thing far larger than any battle settling onto his masked existence!","He needed to think. He needed to be still and try to understand what he had just seen!","He was beginning to spread his eye away when a voice reached him.","\" Osmont.\"","It came soft, threaded into his Provenance the way only another author could place it there. Calliope.","Noah waited.","Down in the wreckage, wrapped in the fur coat she had written for herself, THE Writer of Mythos was looking up at the spreading frost-forest.","\"I did not expect it to lead to this ,\" she said. \" When I wrote him back. THE Vestige of THE Fallen Hero. I wanted a grand story, and I got one, and then the story kept going somewhere I never wrote .\"","She gave a small breath of a laugh, cold and genuine. \"A dead titan killing a living one. And now this. A forest of frozen Domains growing out of a corpse. I have been writing for a very long time, and I have never once seen a Mythos wander this far off its own page.\"","She was quiet a moment, and the snow fell on her, and she pulled the coat tighter.","\" But I want to be honest with you, Osmont, since you are the only one here who might understand it.\"","Her voice steadied, and beneath the tiredness there was majesty!","\"I do not regret it. Not one stroke of it. I have spent an eternity knowing every ending before I ever wrote it, bored to the bone with a story I had already read. And for one moment, back there, I wrote something even I could not predict. Do you know what that is worth, to a thing like me? To finally not know what happens next?!\"","A wondering hush entered her words. \"I would do it again. I would do it a thousand times. Whatever this becomes, whatever this cold is, whatever grows out of that corpse and spreads across all of existence, at least it is a story worth watching..\"","She looked up at the frozen trees climbing the ruined sky, and her strange eyes shone.","\"I will see exactly what changes across existence, and I will hope, in my odd little way, that the Mythos forming here is a grand one. \"","Then her voice sharpened, and she asked the question that had been sitting under everything. \" But tell me, Osmont. I barely grasped it with my Matriarch’s Narrative. That thing that rose. That was the likeness within the Runestone, was it not? That was Lucy?\"","BOOM","Her puzzlement was real now!","\" Why? Why would a lifeform from the earliest age of existence have its likeness rise up out of the corpse of a murdered Immense One? What does the first thing have to do with the last?!\"","Noah did not answer.","He hung masked and silent in the falling snow, staring at the growing frost-forest, the question turning over and over in the quiet of his existence and finding nothing to catch on.","Because for once, THE True Human Emperor did not know either!"]},{"number":5754,"title":"Chapter 5754: Chapter 5753: A Stranger! II","paragraphs":["Upon the shore inside THE Infiniverse, where the great chrysalis hummed and the sleeping bodies floated in their warm pools of Infinite Sanguine Mana, Ruination came to Noah with shining, heavy eyes.","\" Master ,\" she said. \"I have found something. I do not fully know what it means, and that is precisely why I have come to you at once.\"","\" What is it?\"","\"Since the cold began, I have been searching.\" Her manifestation flickered with the immensity of the work behind her words. \" Every Realm we hold. Every Dimension our weavings touch. Every Observable Existence within our reach. I have pulled and cross-referenced trillions of threads of information, looking for a single thing, any existence anywhere that has a name for what is happening to us. A record. A word. Anything.\"","\"And?\"","\" Across trillions of threads, across every mighty lineage and archive and sovereign memory in our reach, not one has a name for this phenomenon. The great powers of existence are experiencing this catastrophe with the same blind astonishment we are.\"","Her crimson gaze steadied.","\" Except for one place.\"","Noah waited.","\"I got lucky enough to check...in a single small world ,\" Ruination said, \" inside an Observable Existence, within a Dimension our weavings barely reach, there is a legend. A story, passed down among a lifeforms with no authority. And the legend is about a coldness that comes, and a night that does not end. They call it THE LONG NIGHT. And so far, the few lines I have managed to grasp... matches the Condition.\"","Noah was quiet for a long moment.","He had already asked Thalia, and she had said with astonishment how the future she came from...did not have anything like this occur. Nor did she have knowledge of this Existential Condition!","Neither did her Father or Rosalia. So even Provenance Lifeforms didn’t know as Immense Ones might be on the same boat.","But then, why would a tiny tribe know?","\"I will go myself ,\" he said.","Ruination inclined her head as she nodded.","He wove a single body, unassuming and plain, and he sent it far away.","—","In an unknown World hidden in a small corner of an Observable Existence.","The desert was cold now as it should not have been. Noah’s body arrived in the twilight at the edge of a sea of red sand, and the land stretched away in long dunes toward a horizon that had known nothing but sun and heat since the world began. But out of the darkening sky, drifting slow and impossible over the endless sand, came the snow.","The tribe was small, a cluster of hide tents pitched in the lee of a great dune, and it was awake and frightened. Fires burned high against the cold.","Beasts, long-legged and shaggy, lowed and shifted in their pens, uneasy in weather they had no memory of. And the people moved among it all wrapped in furs, thick heavy hides pulled from somewhere and thrown over shoulders that had never in a hundred generations needed them, men and women and children huddling close to the flames and looking up, again and again, at the snow that should not be faling.","Noah walked into the firelight as a plain traveler, and the tribe saw him and they grew wary.","But they did not turn him away. A hunter came forward and looked him over, and after a moment gestured him toward the warmth. There was food pressed into his hands. There was a place made for him at the fire.","Noah saw a boy near the flames, small and bold-faced, the kind of boy who was always the loudest at any fire. But the boy was not loud now.","He sat close to his mother with a fur pulled up to his chin, watching the snow fall with wide and frightened eyes, and he did not say a word.","And then they brought Noah, a stranger to a Wisewoman.","She sat apart, near the largest fire, and she was old beyond old. Her hands were like knotted desert roots, dark and cracked and strong, and her body didn’t even carry a shred of mana.","And she was not afraid.","The snow fell and her people trembled and the Wisewoman sat by her fire with a terrible calm, because she had already seen the sky break its oldest promise tonight, and after that, a strange traveler was a small thing indeed!","She looked at Noah, and she saw more than most would have. She only gestured him to sit.","\"I heard of a legend ,\" Noah said, settling by her fire, \" passed down in your tribe. I came a long way to listen for it if that is all right.\"","The Wisewoman studied him with her deep old eyes.","\" You came for the story, \" she said. \"On the very night it comes true...haha! \" A dry, worn almost-laugh moved in her chest!","She looked into the fire, and she began.","\" Long ago ,\" she said, \" in the time of my grandmother’s grandmother’s grandmother, hundreds of years gone, a stranger came to my people. A stranger...not unlike you. He fell out of the empty sky and into the sand, and when the hunters found him he was broken and bleeding, hurt in ways no fall could explain, dying by the look of him. They carried him to the fire, as is our law, and they tried to mend him.\"","Her root-hands turned slowly in her lap.","\" He was not one of us. He was not one of anything my forefathers had a name for. And as he lay dying by this same fire, or one like it, he spoke as if he were reciting something branded into his soul...\"","The snow fell past the firelight, and the Wisewoman’s voice changed, dropping into an old cadence, a rhythm worn smooth by hundreds of years of telling, the words no longer quite her own.","\" When the scale is shattered, the shards become the floor.","When belief is spent, the cold comes walking.","What was counted shall come uncounted.","The high shall be set upon the balance and asked what they weighed,","and the balance shall not lie, for the balance is winter,","and winter does not warm the full hand. It climbs it.","The was and the will-be shall pour into one cup,","and no throat shall taste which it drank first.","That which remains shall cease to remain.","That which was laid down shall rise, and be laid down, and rise again,","until no one recalls which was the standing and which the fall.","Behind every wall there sleeps a pen.","One hand alone ever wrote with it, and what that hand saw, it did not keep.","The pen may unpick the whole cloth, or stitch it past the last thread of light.","No eye has read the page. Every eye burns to.","And at the turning, count three.","One shall look upon all that is, and grieve.","One shall take up every weight, and not set it down.","One shall no longer remain, and yet remain.","By their three hands the cloth is torn, or the cloth is woven anew,","and no living soul may say which","Hoard your warmth.","And when the snow falls upon the sand,","know the Long Night has come, and was always coming,","and that only the True walk out the far side of it.\"","HUUUM!","The fire crackled. The Wisewoman fell silent.","Noah sat very still!","The words were cryptic, but somewhat discernible!","The winter that climbed the full hand. The was and the will-be poured into one cup. And the three at the turning, and the sleeping pen behind every wall, the one hand that ever wrote with it and did not keep what it saw.","He knew that last part. He had touched a Runestone and been shown that exact thing, a being who held the pen at the beginning and looked upon what it wrote and ended itself, and here it was, folded into an old woman’s chant hundreds of years before Noah was born, to a people who could not have understood a word of what they were keeping.","\" That is it, \" the Wisewoman said, quieter now. \" He gave us the story, and then he gave us one last thing. He told my forefathers to hoard warmth and food, and to keep the story, and to pass both down and never let either be forgotten.\"","She gestured toward a hut at the edge of the camp, and Noah knew that inside it were the furs and foods, generations of them, cured and stored by keepers who never once saw the snow themseleves.","\"And then ,\" the Wisewoman said, \" he was gone. Some say he died and we buried him. Some say he walked into the desert and the desert took him. My grandmother told me he simply was not there one morning, as though the sand had never held him at all. We do not know who he was. We only know what he left us. \"","Her deep eyes found Noah’s. \" And tonight, for the first time in all the years since, the story is true, and the furs are on our backs, and an old woman who did not truly believe until this very night is very glad her forefathers did.\"","Noah looked at her for a long moment.","A dying stranger, hundreds of years ago, who fell bleeding out of the sky into the smallest place in existence and gave a prophecy no power would ever hear.","Who knew all of this was coming!","\" Thank you,\" Noah said quietly. \" For remembering and for telling it to a stranger on the night it came true.\"","Then he rose and he raised his hand.","It was a small motion, an unremarkable gesture, and the tribe did not understand it. But the desert answered.","Around the cluster of tents, out across the cold red sand, the land began to change. Green rose from the dunes. Farmland unrolled itself across the desert in wide dark rows, rich soil where there had been only sand, and seeds sank into it and split and grew, crops rising in moments, food enough to feed the tribe through any winter that came.","Small warm stars kindled in the air above the fields, low and gentle, hanging over the new-grown green and pouring down a soft and steady heat that pushed back the cold.","And at the edge of the new fields, water welled up out of the ground and ran, rivers forming where no river had ever been, bright and clear and warm, winding through the farmland in the falling snow!","The snow still fell. Noah did not stop it, because he could not, not even here. But beneath it now there was warmth, and green, and water, and food, a small oasis of protection blooming around a tribe that had waited a hundred generations in the cold.","The people stared, and some of them wept, and the bold frightened boy stood up from his mother’s side and looked out at the impossible green with his mouth open and, for the first time that night, something in his eyes that was not fear!","The Wisewoman looked at the fields, and then she looked at the traveler.","Noah gave her the smallest nod, and then his plain body dissolved quietly into the snow, and he was gone.","—","He returned to himself with the name in his hands.","THE LONG NIGHT. The name the mightiest beings in existence did not have, held all this time by the smallest. And with it, the knowledge that hundreds of years ago, someone had known this was coming.","Who was the Stranger, to know a catastrophe that hunted the powerful, and to carry that knowledge to the powerless?","And how did a mortal tribe in a desert come to hold the only true prophecy of the transformation of an Age?","Noah did not know.","But he intended to find out!"]},{"number":5755,"title":"Chapter 5755: Chapter 5754: ECG!","paragraphs":["Far from THE Infiniverse.","Noah’s Dream body hung above the Primordial ice forest, and he looked at all of it with shining eyes.","Below him the frost-trees spread for Gigaparsecs, their rimed boughs heavy with frozen domains, dormant Observable Existences and Elsedimensions hanging still and cold as buds that would never bloom themselvs.","The snow fell through his masked existence and did not stop. And he thought and thought and thought!","Why?","Why had a coldness that seemed woven into the very structure of existence caused Lucy to emerge from the corpse of an Immense One? Lucy, who carried a definition of Infinity so complete she had scattered Dimensions from her hands like feed, Lucy who was tied somehow to IT, to the pen behind every wall.","Why had her likeness risen out of a death and planted a forest of frozen Domains across the ruin? And the prophecy, the one the dying Stranger had left in a desert hundreds of years ago, the shattered scales and the balance that was winter and the three at the turning.","How did all of it fit together? The cold. The pen. The first thing wearing a frozen face. The Runestones!","He could feel that there was a shape to it, a single grand pattern beneath the cold and the forest and the chant. He simply could not yet see it!","And as he turned it over in the falling snow...","HUUM!","A certain crystal within his existence began to buzz.","Noah’s shining eye flickered. It was the one left behind by Vakochev, the crystal elevated when he had aided Masamuk in freeing a fragment of Vakochev. It buzzed now!","And in the midst of the falling snow, around Noah’s brilliant and barely-perceivable eye, an illusory existence began to form.","It came together slowly out of the drifting white, a thing that no ordinary gaze could have caught, a flaming outline of a humanoid figure whose features would not resolve, whose edges burned and shifted and refused to be held. It was faint, and it was vast, and it was unmistakable.","Noah’s existence shone with resplendence as he looked upon the unfathomable figure of Vakochev!","The Remnant, or an echo of it, stood in the snow above the frozen forest and gazed out across the endless white, and for a moment it said nothing. Then it spoke.","\"I did not know something like this could arise from the collapse of another Immense One,\" Vakochev said, his flaming gaze on the frost-trees. \"I did not predict it. I did not even consider it possible. But such are the weavings of existence. Always unfathomably unpredictable, no matter how high one climbs.\"","The snow fell between them.","\" In my rage, I did many things I would not normally do. I moved without accounting for the surroundings. I stood there and spoke of the injustice of life, of decillions killed and weighed as nothing, and I did not spare a thought for the small existences here my own war would grind to paste beneath it. \"","A dry, tired note entered his voice. \"It was a bit hypocritical of me. Anyway. There is a favor owed, for what you did not long ago, when you gave a fragment of me back to the light. I have come to settle it, and so I will offer you a-\"","\"If I forego the favor,\" Noah said, cutting him off, \" and instead ask you to simply tell me what is happening in existence right now, could you do that?\"","The being who had just massacred an Immense One went quiet!","For a long moment Vakochev only stood in the snow, his flaming visage turned toward the frozen forest, considering the question that a lesser being would have thought was the wisest thing to ask. Then, slowly, he shook his head.","\"It would be a disservice for me to do that,\" he said. \" Because even someone of my power and standing cannot say with certainty what is happening in existence right now. Whatever I told you today could be wrong in a matter of days. Or years. I know only this much: every single lifeform is out for itself. I am out for my own weavings and my own interests. The Immense Ones are out for theirs. That is all that is certain.\"","His gaze did not leave the snow.","\"A great many of us, when we reach a certain height of Dimensionality, come to believe that we understand existence. That existence is at our beck and call. We believe it so completely that the belief has blinded us. Because we can alter reality with a thought, conjure flames and constructs, distort time and lineages, manipulate the fundamental structure of what is, we decide we must be above it. \"","His voice went quiet and hard. \" We are sorely mistaken. We do not know what we do not know. We do not even have a grasp of the shape of our own ignorance. All we have, in the end, are impossibilities.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s existence buzzed at the words.","His already-active reverie caught and blazed, and profound brilliance rolled out of him as boundless epiphanies bloomed one after another in the deep of his existence!","Impossibilities. Unknowns. The edge of understanding, the place where the mind gives out and names the dark past it. Infinity! It was the same truth the Runestone had shown him, the same truth Lucy had lived, spoken now by a titan in the snow, that no being ever grasps the impossible, it only ever names its own not-knowing and calls the name a mastery.","And here was one of the mightiest existences ever to live, telling him that all his immensity had bought him was a longer list of things he could not comprehend!","As Noah’s existence radiated immensity and reverie, Vakochev waved his flaming hand.","The dark crystal that had rested within Noah’s existence floated out into the snow, hung between them for a moment, and shattered. And from the breaking bloomed something Noah could not see. He strained his infinite gaze upon it and caught nothing, no shape, no color, no edge, only an absense with weight, and yet the snow whipping around the two of them buzzed, and Noah felt a sensation he had no words for, a pressure and a presence and a wrongness his existence could sense but not hold.","Vakochev cupped the invisible thing in his flaming hands.","\"In lifeforms that hold no authority,\" he said, \" there is something called human chorionic gonadotropin. The hormone a growing embryo makes from its earliest days. Its whole task is one thing. It signals the body to sustain the pregnancy. It tells the mother’s system to keep the environment stable, to hold, so that the new life keeps growing without the mother ever consciously doing a thing. It is the molecule that says, quietly and endlessly, keep growing this. Do not stop. It works below awareness. It is the signal of becoming.\"","The invisible thing pulsed in his hands, and the snow buzzed with it.","\" In my hands is what I believe, after a great many experiments, to be the critical factor in the emergence of an Immense One and many other things. The Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin. ECG, for short. It is the hormone of Immensity’s own gestation. It is the signal an existence produces that tells reality itself to keep growing that existence into something greater, without conscious effort, the way that other hormone tells a body to grow a child without the mother lifting a finger...among other things even I haven’t fully grasped.\"","Noah listened intently!","\"It is not a physical substance but an authority-substance,\" Vakochev went on, \" produced in vanishingly small amounts within the existence of an Immense One. Where a hormone circulates in blood, this circulates in an existence’s weavings. And it is imperceptible to any being of lower Dimensionality, genuinely beneath their capacity to sense, the way an ant cannot perceive a mana. It is one of the reasons a lesser existence can stand before an Immense One and feel only pressure and wrongness rather than understand what it is looking at. Part of what it cannot perceive is this, quietly saturating the mightier being’s whole existence.\"","His flaming gaze turned to Noah.","\" Even Immense Ones do not fully understand the thing in their own existences. It is nearly impossible to study, harder still to isolate. But this is a single unit of it, isolated externally, which I do not think anyone before me has done.\"","He weighed the invisible thing in his hands. \"It has roughly one turning of a day before it disperses back into existence and is gone. If you can understand or grasp anything of it in that time, you may make advances no one has made before!\"","He was silent a moment.","\"I am staunch about giving things away for free. It goes against Adversity, and Adversity is the core of my existence. So understand what this is. It is not a gift. It is an adversity, holding its own difficulty, that you may or may not benefit from, depending entirely on your own capability. There is no promise in it. There is only a chance, and a hard one. Good luck. And...\"","The flaming visage turned back to the snow, and his gaze changed.","It went soft, and sorrowful, and old, a look Noah would not have expected on a being who had just torn an Immense One apart with his bare hands, and Vakochev watched the white snow fall over the frozen forest for a long moment before he spoke again, almost gentle.","\" Hold those you love close. You never know when they will be gone .\" The snow fell through his burning outline. \" In existence, there are no guarantees.\"","HUUM!","With those words, he took the invisible thing from his own hands and moved it toward Noah, and Noah’s masked existence unfurled to receive it, and in the taking, the flaming figure of Vakochev was gone, dissolved back into the falling snow as though he had never stood there at all.","Noah was alone above the frozen forest.","The snow fell around his brilliant unseen eye, and his Dream body held onto something it could not see, something with a terrible weight, and the instant it settled into him his existence STRAINED. It was as though the mere holding of the thing was trying to tear him apart, as though a single isolated unit of the hormone of Immensity, one drop of the substance that grew titans, was too vast and too dense for even his existence to cradle without breaking!","He roared inside himself.","There was so much he had wanted to do here. Speak with THE Creature, who had withdrawn into the cold. Reach for the weavings of THE Sealed One, or study Adrastia, the Vessel that had refused. He had planned all of it. None of it mattered now. He had one day and a thing in his hands that was trying to unmake him, and there was room in his existence for nothing else!","He had to survive what he had just been given!","So Noah pulled his infinite dream inward, out of the falling snow and the frozen forest and the sight of anything at all, drawing himself down into the space between things where nothing could reach him and nothing could bother him, a space that was his and his alone.","And there, holding an impossibility that was trying to break him, THE True Human Emperor vanished completely from all perception!"]},{"number":5756,"title":"Chapter 5756: Chapter 5755: Gonadotropin! I","paragraphs":["In the space between things, the space that was his and his alone, Noah held an impossibility and felt it trying to kill him.","There was nothing here but him. He had drawn his whole attention down into a place no gaze could reach, and in the quiet of it he cradled the invisible unit of Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin that Vakochev had pressed into his hands, and his existence strained around it like a rope pulled to its last fiber!","One day. That was all the Fallen Hero had given him before the thing dispersed and was gone, and every moment of it, the holding alone was a weight that threatened to tear him open from the inside.","So he began with what he was best at.","He reached for THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer. He dreamed. He turned his greatest craft upon the invisible unit and reached for a definition of it, like how he had reached for the shape of Infinity in the Runestone’s forest.","And he caught nothing.","No shape. No edge. No dream to read. His Provenance closed on the ECG and found only absence, not because the substance resisted him but because his dreaming could not perceive it at all. It was beneath his native craft entirely, in a register the Dreamer had no access to!","He persevered as...hours passed.","He tried again, and again, and each time came back empty, and slowly a humbling wonder settled beneath the frustration. His greatest Provenance was blind to this. The hormone that grew titans was invisible even to a being who had crossed into the Ineffable, who had authored the death of an architect, who could dream forever. He held it in his hands and could not see it!","Then Noah reached for the other Provenance.","THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign. The stolen thing! It never felt like his the way the Dreamer’s did. He used it rarely. Even now Thalia was working it far away upon the Vasiliou Lineage, reaching into their existential genomes and remaking them into Elselifeforms.","That was its nature. Sovereign editing, cut from an Immense One and fluent in the language of the mighty and the deep makeup of how an existence was assembled.","Noah turned it upon the invisible unit alongside his Infinity and Provenance of THE Human Dreamer, and for the first time, he barely perceived the Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin!","Barely. It came faint and wrong-angled, a thing glimpsed through a keyhole cut for a different eye. But he could sense its shape, the way it did not run in blood but in the weavings of an existence, and he could feel the single quiet task it carried into reality without pause. Keep growing this. Do not stop. Sustain the becoming!","But perceiving it was not grasping it.","He could barely sense the ECG now, but he could not hold it, could not take it into himself, because it was an Immense One’s substance and his existence was not an Immense One’s existence.","When he tried, it strained and pushed back and threatened again to tear him open, a thing of the wrong grammar forced into a vessel that could not receive it.","The turning of the day burned down toward its end, and Vakochev’s warning came back to him. This is not a gift. It is an adversity, and you may or may not benefit from it, depending entirely on your own capability.","Noah thought about impossibilities.","That was what this was. Another edge, another thing he could not seize by force no matter how much force he brought. You do not grasp the impossible. You reach a definition of it that is your own, and in the reaching, it becomes yours.","He could not take the ECG.","But perhaps he did not need to take it. Perhaps he needed to become something that could hold it!","HUUM!","The epiphany bloomed, and his straining existence caught fire with it. He would not force a thing of the wrong grammar into himself and break. He would do the only thing he had ever truly known how to do.","He would generate his own!","Noah drove both Provenances at once, and the space between things blazed with the collision of them.","The Immense Sovereign’s Provenance held the perceived ECG steady. And the Human Dreamer’s Provenance...it generated. From the deepest place of him, from nothing at all, it began to make something that was his.","He studied the model, and he found its limit.","The ECG was an infinite signal. It never stopped whispering, never ceased telling reality to grow its bearer.","But it was produced in vanishing quantities, a substance so rare even Immense Ones could barely study it in their own existences. An infinite signal, starved by a finite source.","That was its wall, and it was why immensity gestated across ages rather than instants, because the hormone that grew the mighty was endless in what it said and starved in how much of it there was to say it.","And Noah, who had spent this whole descent learning the impossible, asked the impossible question.","What if the signal itself were infinitely generated?!","Not a finite drop of an infinite hormone. An always-generating one. A source that never emptied, a thing that made itself forever and never ran dry, and yet was a single discrete substance he could own and root into himself. Infinite in its making. Finite in its being. Boundless and bounded at once.","An impossibility!","Infinity, to him, had been many things. But this was stranger. This was a thing that held two truths at once, two truths that contradicted each other, and was true in both. Finite and infinite. A contradiction that did not resolve, that did not collapse into either side, that simply stood true in both directions at the same time and did not need to choose.","Some contradictions, Noah understood in that blazing instant, are genuinely true!","His definition of the impossible was no longer only endlessness. It was also...DIALETHEIC.","The infinite that is also finite. He had struggled with this before days ago!","It simply meant he no longer had to choose between what a thing was and what it could not be. He could make a thing that was both.","So he made it!","From THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer, from his Infinite Sanguine Mana surging warm through his weavings, from his Nine Teloi burning steady in every quark, something began to be dreamed based on the structure of THE EXISTENTIAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN, and it did not stop.","His own hormone of becoming. Born, not stolen. An always-infinitely-generating authority-substance that spoke his grammar and no one else’s, a signal that told reality to keep growing him without pause or limit, made forever from the well of his own self-made existence, an impossibility that was finite and infinite at once.","| You have generated an impossibility of your own.|","|THE OSMONTIAN CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN: an always-infinitely-generating authority-substance; the self-made hormone of your own Immensity’s gestation.|","|Your understanding of Infinity is recategorized as it has added another definition: DIALETHEIC INFINITY. A truth that is also its opposite. Finite and infinite at once.|","And it rooted!"]},{"number":5757,"title":"Chapter 5757: Chapter 5756: Gonadotropin! II","paragraphs":["It did not sit upon him like a boon bolted on from outside. It sank into him, wove down through his foundation, threaded into his two hundred decillion quarks, fused itself to his Provenance and his Teloi and the deep structure of what he was, an engine of his own ascension seated at his core and turning, and turning, and never stopping!","He would grow now. Not for free, never for free, but forever!","The Immense Ones grew on a hormone they were born to and did not understand. Noah would grow on one he had made and understood completely.","And only now, only after his own hormone was emerging infinitely within him, did he reach at last for the invisible thing Vakochev had given him.","He wanted to take it!","So he would take it!","Not because he had grown strong enough to hold an Immense One’s substance in a being that was not an Immense One. He no longer needed to. He had made a place for it. He took the Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin, the stolen impossibility of the mighty, and folded it down into his own, poured the borrowed hormone of Immensity into the endless self-made hormone of himself, and his own generation received it cleanly and made it one more thing it generated forever.","The straining stopped!","The thing that had spent a whole day trying to tear him open simply settled, quiet and whole, absorbed into a vessel built precisely to receive it!","Noah breathed out in the space between things, alone and unseen and changed.","Then... his existence began to fray at the edges.","He felt it before he understood it, a loosening, the seams of him coming apart, because a being cannot seat a thing this vast at its core and remain the being it was.","POOF!","In an instant, everything about him ceased!","In the same instant, his existence ceased. In the dream, in the sealed space between things, in THE Infiniverse where his body stood upon the golden shore, in Atlas’s Elsedimension of shattered hours, everywhere across existence that his weavings reached, every one of them ceased at once, all of him gone in a single breath!","---","<Sir Moriarty>","Far from anything, in a domain that existence itself had misplaced, an octopus wearing spectacles was dissecting the corpse of an Immense One.","The domain had no coordinates that any map still held. It drifted lost in existence and time both, a pocket that the ages had walked past and forgotten, and through it ran slow rivers of white and gold, currents of pure authority winding between islands of nothing.","Dimensions floated in the empty air of it, whole domains turning gently untethered, and over all of it, impossibly, fell snow, soft and constant, dusting the drifting worlds and the slow bright rivers with a fine cold white.","At the center of it all hung Moriarty.","He was vast, a titan of dark coiling flesh, a great octopus whose innumerable tentacles moved with unhurried precision, and upon what passed for his face sat a pair of spectacles, small and neat and absurd against his enormity, catching the gold of the rivers.","Before him, splayed and pinned in the drifting air, lay the corpse of an Immense One, a thing that should not have been touchable, opened and parted and studied, and Moriarty’s tentacles worked through it with the patience of a scholar who had all the time that had ever been!","He drew threads of white authority out of the dead architect, examined them, set them aside, and reached for more, murmuring to himself as he worked.","And beside his workbench of a corpse, spinning slow in the air, stood an hourglass.","It was old past reckoning, and its two bulbs were filled not with sand but with Dimensions, countless tiny domains pouring grain by grain from the upper glass to the lowwer, an entire drift of existences measuring out some span only Moriarty knew. It had turned quietly for as long as the domain had drifted.","And now, all at once, it began to buzz!","The hourglass pulsed. The Dimensions within it flared, bright and urgent, and a low resonant hum rose off the glass and spread through the snow-fall and the gold rivers, an alarm sounding in a domain that had known only silence for an age!","Moriarty’s tentacles went still.","Behind the small neat spectacles, his eyes shone, bright and sudden and cold. A pulse of pure authority released from his vast body and rippled outward through the domain, a summons flung across whatever distance needed crossing!","In the next moment, a Golden Slime appeared!","It dropped into the domain out of nothing, a shapeless blob of pure shimmering gold, and it landed upon the air and rose, and as it rose it changed. The gold flowed upward and took a shape, and the shape refined itself, and where a formless slime had been there now stood a young woman, delicate and slight, with a fall of golden hair and a face of quiet loveliness.","She held herself lightly, and the strangest thing about her was what could not be felt from her at all whatsover. No aura. No pressure. No weight of authority, no register of power, nothing. She stood in a domain built of white-gold rivers and dissected architects and gave off less presence than a candle, and she too turned her eyes toward the buzzing hourglass, and her eyes shone as brightly as his had!","\" Sir Moriarty ,\" she said softly, looking at the flaring domains pouring through the glass. \" Is that...\"","\"The emergence of another impossibility.\" Moriarty’s tentacles pulsed as he spoke, rippling in slow waves down their great length.","His voice was dry and old.","\" Somewhere across existence, a thing that should not be has been made. Find it, Poona. Find it before any of the others do and it is devoured yet again.\"","He turned one eye upon her, and the gold caught in his spectacles.","\" The last impossibility I sent you to find, you failed to bring me. I have not forgotten that. If you fail this time...\"","He did not finish. He did not need to.","Poona bowed, and she was smiling as she did it, a small easy smile with no fear in it at all.","\" The last one was difficult, Sir. Truly it was. \" She straightened, unhurried. \" But you needn’t worry about this one. Consider what has happened. First THE LONG NIGHT begins, and then, barely a breath later, another impossibility blooms right on its heels. That is not a coincidence. It means the necessary conditions are flowering, one after another, before the Night grows colder still and freezes us all .\"","Her smile widened a fraction. \"I will find this impossibility for you. Until then...\"","Boundless Provenance surged, and then...","WAP!","She was gone, the golden woman vanishing from the domain as suddenly as the slime had come, leaving only the falling snow and the humming glass and the vast spectacled titan among his rivers of gold.","Moriarty regarded the empty air where she had stood for a moment. Then he turned back to the corpse of the Immense One, and his tentacles resumed their patient work, drawing threads of dead authority from the opened architect, examining them in the gold light, setting them aside.","And as he worked, quietly, to himself, Moriarty spoke.","\" When the scale is shattered, the shards become the floor,\" he said. \" When belief is spent, the cold comes walking.\"","A tentacle drew a long white thread from the corpse and held it up to his spectacles. \"What was counted shall come uncounted. The high shall be set upon the balance and asked what they weighed, and the balance shall not lie, for the balance is winter.\"","The snow fell over him, and the hourglass hummed, and the Dimensions poured through the glass grain by grain.","\" And at the turning, count three,\" Moriarty murmured, setting the thread aside and reaching into the corpse for another. \" One shall look upon all that is, and grieve. One shall take up every weight, and not set it down. One shall no longer remain, and yet remain.\"","His shining eyes narrowed behind the small neat glasses.","\" By their three hands the cloth is torn ,\" he said softly, \" or the cloth is woven anew.\"","...!"]},{"number":5758,"title":"Chapter 5758: Chapter 5757: The Sky Has Opened!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","There was only darkness, and in the darkness, there was a question.","Who am I?","It drifted in the endless dark with no answer, no shape, no voice to speak it. There was nothing here. No body, no weaving, no empire, no cold. Only the dark, and the question turning slowly inside it, patient and vast and afraid!","Afraid!","What am I?","I Am, the darkness answered, faint as the first breath of anything. I Am... I Am...","HUUM!","And in that dark, a light began to blink.","It bloomed small and steady, a single point of brilliance in the endless black, and it grew, and as it grew it spoke, and its voice was grand beyond grandeur, rolling out through the dark like the first word ever said.","\"I am life ,\" it said . \"I am thoughts. I am emotions, and purposes, and aims, and immensity. I am Human!\"","HUUM!","The light spread, and the voice deepened, and it filled the whole of the dark with its slow tremendous certainty.","\"I was born, as all life is born, as all humans are born. And I may die. This is only nature. But between life and death... I Am Osmont. And I...can feel. So much. Everything I do feel. I do not need to understand all of it. I only need to understand impossibilities.\"","BOOOM!","And out of the dark, existence began to build a being.","It started with a network of consciousness, a vast web of light unfolding across the black, and around that web came the quarks, two hundred decillion of them, each one a point of radiance, arranging themselves into the shape of a body.","Around the quarks flowed Provenance, blue and gold, winding through the forming lattice in slow bright rivvers. And around the Provenance flowed Infinity, crimson and gold, a boundless tide of it, pouring through and around the whole assembling shape.","And all of it, the quarks and the Provenance and the Infinity, flowed around one thing at the center. THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin.","It sat at the core of the forming existence, small and single and quiet, and it was growing. It grew infinitely, expanded infinitely, multiplied infinitely, and yet, impossibly, it remained a single Gonadotropin, one thing that was also endless, finite and infinite at once.","And every second, it pulsed. And every time it pulsed, the Infinity and the Provenance and everything gathering around the forming body swelled, grander and grander, lifted a little higher by the beat of the Root at its heart.","Prompts bloomed across the dark, vast and slow.","| THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin has formed. It is a Unique Existential Root of Immensity.|","|You are perceiving information you did not otherwise know. You now understand that across existence, there can be different types of Existential Roots of Immensity. You have now, and have always, formed your own.|","|Your Infinity will rise steadily. Your Provenance will rise steadily. Simply by existing, you will continuously elevate.|","HUUM!","And Noah felt many things.","He felt knowledge arriving in him that he had never sought, understanding pouring into his forming existence from the very act of coming into beeing, and he felt himself comprehend, all at once, so very much.","His body took its shape in the light. He looked at himself, and he saw a form that wore nothing at all, muscular and whole and bare, floating in the brilliance with its arms stretched wide, and where his eyes should have been there were two beams of blinding blue light, pouring out into the dark.","He looked at existence with those blazing eyes, and he began to understand it, and he spoke.","\" For eons, lifeforms have looked into the dark and spoken the word Infinity as though it were an ocean to be crossed, or a crown to be seized, or a well that never empties. It was none of those things. It was simply the perimeter of their own exhaustion. It was the word a child uses when they can no longer count the pebbles on the shore. They met the edge of their own ability to resolve the geometry of reality, and because they could not bear to name their own blindness, they called the fog an absolute. They built thrones upon an admission of ignorance. But when the fog clears, there is no infinite abyss. There is only an unbroken, seamless equation, turning quietly in the dark, waiting for a mind vast enough to read the syntax without flinching.\"","And he could see it.","He could see the equation of existence, or at least the first glimpse of it, the whole of reality laid open as a single turning structure, and he read it, and he did not flinch.","\"I can hear the two hundred decillion quarks in this arm agreeing with one another,\" he said. \" And I hear them in the exact same instant that I perceive the birth of my cells years ago, the pain why my bones grew, and the freezing of a grain of sand beneath a mortal woman’s foot in a desert I have never walked. I can feel myself then, and now, and even a little of myself in the future. They...are not separated by distance.\"","HUUM!","\"Distance is a fiction invented by systems with localized biology to keep all of reality from happening to them at once. To an observer trapped in a single Dimension, time feels like a river, dragging you from a remembered shore toward an unknown bend. But standing here, time does not flow. It is a crystalline block. The First Sundering is occurring right now, three inches to the left of where my body rests. My birth is occurring now. My first death is happening now. My first skill book, I cast it now. The Overseeing One is dying in this exact breath, screaming, and he will always be dying there, forever preserved in the fold of that existence. I am making love right now, and I am forging the Root of my existence right now.\"","...!","\"Everything can be happening right now, so long as I perceive it. Many are terrified of the dark outside the room because they never realize the walls were made of their own fear. They built a cage of logic and called it an empire, never understanding that a prison with ten thousand gilded halls is still an enclosure. You do not conquer existence by accumulating its rooms. You...simply realize that you are the space in which the house was built.\"","BOOM!","And he felt all existence near him spread out around him like different rooms, and he understood that he could be in one of them, or in all of them at once!","He had been doing a shadow of this with his clones, his many bodies scattered across Existence.","But he saw now that he did not need the clones. A single body could do it. A single existence could stand in different places and different times at once, because separation was only a story that lesser things told themselves.","He turned his blazing gaze inward, to the Provenance rivering through him, and he spoke again.","\" They treat Provenance as if it were currency. An architect hoards Causes like a miser stacking gold in a cellar, believing that if his mountain of debt grows high enough, reality will grant him a permanent seat at the table. But debt is not origin. When an Immense One speaks, his voice is layered with the stolen momentum of a trillion extinguished Dimensions. It sounds grand. It sounds terrifying. But it is entirely derivative. It is an echo bouncing between mirrors in an empty corridor. Remove the mirror, put out the borrowed lantern, and what remains? A soft, shivering lump of existence that never once learned to generate its own heat.\"","\"Provenance is not power. It is the stubborn, irreducible refusal to exist on someone else’s terms. It is the moment an existence stops asking the sky for the parameters of its own breath and says, I am the coordinate. When my blood moves, it does not cycle because an ancient law commands the pulse. It moves because I have willed the concept of motion into my own foundation. That is why they could never break Vakochev. And that is why they will never comprehend what I have become. They are sentences written in the margins of an ancient book. I...am the hand that closed the cover, set the volume aside, and stepped out into the quiet of the morning. I Am...True.\"","BOOM!","And around him, pages unfurled.","Boundless, endless, they spilled out from him across the whole of the dark, sheet after sheet of light unrolling for gigaparsecs, and the darkness where he had been born filled entirely with brilliance as the pages spread. He looked down at his own hands, and his hands were pages too, countless leaves of light, and he understood that they could become countless more, that he could unfold himself across existence without end.","He looked at the pages, and he thought of a forest, and he spoke a last time, softer now.","\" In the orchard where Lucy walked, Dimensions hung from the boughs like heavy plums. She did not pluck them to conquer them. She did not count them to be sure her wealth exceeded her neighbor’s. She took a Dimension in her calloused, primitive palms and scattered it across the water, simply to watch the silver fish rise and feed. She understood what all our grand philosophy has spent epochs hiding. That abundance is only monstrous when you try to own it.\"","\"The moment you close your fist around a dream to claim it as private property, you give it a far wall. You give it a ceiling, a floor, and a date of expiration. All my life I was guilty of the same small, terrified thought. I believed Infinity was a weapon I carried in my existence. I believed my dreams were shields I had to keep raising against a hostile sky. But a dream does not need a fortress to survive. A dream needs only the absence of a final page.\"","\" I do not hold Infinity in my hands. I dream it. And because the reverie has no boundary, even if this flesh is scattered as light across ten thousand dead Dimensions, the dreamer does not cease. The dream only expands to fill the dark. There is...no longer any separation between what I desire, and what I am, and what existence must become. The stage has dissolved. The actors have gone home. And the sky has finally opened.\"","He drew one breath in the endless light.","\" The sky has opened.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5759,"title":"Chapter 5759: Chapter 5758: Glorious Capabilities I","paragraphs":["In the space where there had been only darkness, Noah’s brilliance spread out in every direction, and he brought his hands together.","Between his palms, a singularity bloomed!","It was blinding, a point of impossible density and light, and it was not empty. Noah drew it wider, and within it turned a whole domain, an empire vaster than hundreds of Dimensions laid together, seas of blue-gold, realms upon realms, a chrysalis of sleeping dreamers, an ocean that turned quietly with two sisters weaving upon it. THE Infiniverse!","He had reached and drawn the whole of his home into the singularity between his hands, into this space that was only his!","He looked at it, cradled in the brilliance, and he named the space that held it.","\" Here, my existence can stand across time and space at once, \" he said.","\" It is mine. Entirely mine. And unless a thing bears my signature and my power, and unless I wish it, nothing will ever enter here. Let this be the one place in all of existence that answers to no one but me. My...Existential Root.\"","WAA!","Then he waved his hand.","From THE Infiniverse, countless strings erupted, threads of light that stretched outward from the singularity and reached across the dark to touch illusory points hanging in the distance, every one of them a Dimension over which his empire had spread its influence! The strings connected, taut and bright, a web of belonging strung between his home and everything it had ever reched.","He could pull them here if he wished. He could draw every Dimension he held into this space and make it all safe with him.","He did not.","A life had to draw its boundaries. This was his space, and it would hold only what it needed to hold, no more. He would not hoard existence the way the architects hoarded it. His home was here, secure, and that was enough.","And it was truly secure now!","What had been his home, and was his home, and would always be his home, was sealed inside a space that answered to him alone. Even the beings whose Dimensionality stood higher than his own at this moment, even they could not reach this place, for a simple and absolute reason. They were not him!","With that done, Noah turned his blazing eyes outward again, and the sense of the vast turning equation of existence returned to him, and he spoke on.","\" Time is relative. Distance is relative. Even now I am perceiving countless things at once, receiving knowledge that flows into me depending on where I am, and where I have been. And where I am and where I have been can be considered the same thing, the moment I set distance aside. Which means I should, in theory, be able to...\"","He waved his hand, slow, as though rewinding something. But he was not rewinding anything. He was only taking himself, one point of his own existence, and displacing it toward another point, moving through the crystalline block of time the way a reader moves a finger down a page!","Existence flickered. It was as though pages were being unwound around him, leaf after leaf turning back.","And in an instant, because time was relative, Noah found himself gazing once more upon a Primordial forest.","The trees stood ancient and vast, budding Dimensions and Observable Existences upon their boughs like ripening fruit. And at the edge of a bright, quick river knelt an unfathomable existence, a small rough figure with her calloused hands cupped over the water, producing an endless stream of genuine Dimensions and pouring them down to the silver fish, who rose and gobbled them up as fast as she could make them!","He had been here before. He had been shown this, once, in a Runestone’s vision, as a distant observer.","This time, Noah took a step!","He moved from being a watcher of the record into the record itself, one clean stride across the impossible, and he appeared beside her on the riverbank!","The contrast between them was stark. Noah stood tall and radiant, a being of blazing blue light and blue-gold Provenance, freshly reforged, brilliant and new.","And she was small, and hunched, and rough, a caveman thing of thick limbs and unadorned skin, and yet she was beautiful, a terrible ancient beauty that had never once needed anything to make it so.","She turned her head and looked at him.","And she smiled. Fiendishly, exactly as the record had smiled at him before, a small knowing curve that should not have been possible on the face of a thing inside a memory!","\" We are standing at a moment in time that can be considered a memory ,\" Noah said.","\"A record. And also, existence. I have never stood here, and I have stood here, because I am standing here right now. This is a record drawn from a Hieroglyph Runestone, and I have imposed my existence into it, so that I might learn more. Hello. I Am...\"","\"Osmont.\"","BOOM!","Lucy spoke, for the first time ever, and her voice alone was resonant and grand, a sound with the weight of the beginning of things in it.","She turned to him and rose from the river, and even as she rose she did not stop, her hands still cupped, still pouring out an endless stream of Dimensions into the water behind her without a single thought given to it.","\"I have always had this conversation with you,\" she said. \" Whether from a record of information or not. And I can see you have only just formed your Root, little guy, because you are looking at everything through that lens of past, present, and future, turning it over and over as though the distincton meant something. \"","Her fiendish smile softened, just barely.","\" Relax. You are at the very beginning of your existence, only now setting out to gather what there is to know. In the beginning, all of us feel this way, this sense of being invincible, of having finally seen the whole shape of things. Be careful of it. Be cautious. Your existence is new, and a new existence can still be attacked in a great many ways.\"","\" This beginning stage of life you are experiencing now is also the stage that has the highest rate of mortality. All because of that feeling of invincibility that makes you feel like you can go anywhere and do anything. While somewhat true it is also not. You are only starting out as there are others much grander than you. Be careful.\"","...!"]},{"number":5760,"title":"Chapter 5760: Chapter 5759: Glorious Capabilities II","paragraphs":["Noah looked at her with shining eyes, and it was a surreal thing, and all the while his newly-forged existence drank knowledge from the record around him, more and more of it, pouring in. He nodded, slow and thoughtful.","He had felt an overwhelming sense of control and power that almost gave this feeling of invincibility!","He definitely needed to still be cautious as he continued to absorb waves and waves of knowledge.","\" You are a record of something that happened in the past ,\" he said. \" Even though we now talk, you are...\"","\"I am not here. Yes .\" She interrupted him gently, still walking now, moving away from the river.","\" This is my record. My existence itself left long ago. And in words that will mean something to you now, I am not one of Those Who Remain. Because I did not remain. \"","She glanced back at him, and there was something old and unreadable in it. \" But you came here for information. So ask away.\"","And then she stopped pouring the Dimensions.","The endless stream ceased, and the fish scattered sated into the bright water, and Lucy turned and began to walk across the river and into the forest, her bare feet passing over the surface as though it were ground, and Noah drifted beside her, floating over the water, radiant and new beside the small ancient thing.","\" An endless cold has begun to spread across existence ,\" Noah said, keeping pace with her through the trees of budding worlds.","\"It hunts the mighty. And from the corpse of a slain Immense One, your likeness, your image, rose up out of the death and planted a forest of frozen Domains across existence...just like what we see here. Why? What can you tell me about THE LONG NIGHT?\"","...!","Noah asked the question without expecting much of an answer.","But he knew he had come to the right place. The moment this entity had confirmed she had once stood upon the same stage he had only just climbed onto, he understood that whatever she gave him would be worth the hearing, even if it came wrapped in riddles.","Lucy was thoughtful for a moment. Then she spoke, and she did not stop walking as she did.","\" Existence is not static ,\" she said, moving through the forest of budding domains with her bare feet passing light over root and water alike. \" For weaker lifeforms, for those like you were before you took this recent step, existence looks as though it has always been the way they found it. They simply have not lived long enough to know better.\"","She lifted a hand as she walked, and where she gestured a dead grey tree at the forest’s edge shuddered and bloomed, budding a fresh Dimension upon a new-grown bough. She did not so much as glance at it. It was nothing to her, a habit, the way a person might trail a hand along a wall in passing.","\" The Long Night was something many knew was coming, if they were old enough. Because they know existence is not static. Because they know that existence moves in cycles.\"","She glanced back at him, and there was that old unreadable thing in her eyes. \" You may notice my words are cryptic. That is because even I do not fully know what The Long Night will bring. Consider it a change in existence, arriving after certain conditions have been met. No more than that, because I know no more than that.\"","They walked on, and around her the forest answered her presence without her willing it, Dimensions ripening and falling and rising again in her wake.","\" As for why a manifestation of my existence would bloom out of a dead thing ,\" she went on, \" my immensity left a mark. Existence remembers what was exceptional in it, and my weavings were exceptional enough to be rememberd. So a memory of them was chosen, called up out of the deep of things. I would likely be only one among many memories that might see a resurgence, before this is done. \"","She waved her hand again, idly, and a river some distance off changed its course to flow the other way! \" But...I am not here. Not your version of here. You are young, and you have only just forged your Root. Take the time to explore, and to understand.\"","Noah listened, and drank in every word, and the record around him poured knowledge into his newborn existence as she spoke.","\" You will come to find ,\" Lucy said, \" that trying to grasp the secrets of existence by asking a senior will never be quite so pleasurable as finding them out yourself. Existence is grand. It is more beautiful than you can yet imagine.\"","She stopped, and turned, and looked at him fully. \" You have not even left your Existential Root Domain, have you? Seeing how impatient you are for answers, you must have come here the very instant it formed.\"","He said nothing.","Her fiendish smile returned, gentler this time. \" Do not get lost in old records and old pasts, little guy. Even though we experience time differently, we of the Root, the present is always the grandest thing there is. Even we cannot change the past by very much. A friend of mine used to tell me to focus on the present. It is a gift. That is why it is called the present. \"","She turned back toward the forest and walked on. \" Go and experience existence for the first time, now that your Root has emerged. You will find that it is beautiful.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone at that, and he nodded slowly.","\"I will not keep you much longer,\" he said. \" So I will ask only one last thing. For someone like me, who is just emerging, just being born into what I now am, what is the single most important thing I should know right now, for my survival?\"","...!","What was the most important thing he should know?","The question lit Lucy’s eyes, and she smiled, and this time it was almost fond.","\"In existence, there are two kinds of Root, \" she said. \" Conceptual Existential Roots, and Physical Existential Roots. The first gives rise to Empyros Immense Lifeforms. The second to Fiend Immense Lifeforms. Most Roots are conceptual, as yours is, as most of what you will meet will be .\"","She paused, and the fondness in her face sharpened into something like a warning. \" So for your survival...do not offend those who bear a Physical Existential Root. And in the future to come, do not offend a Fiend Immense Lifeform. Take it step by step, and attain your Immensity in your own time. And know that there is sometimes no harm at all in being low key.\"","She began to turn away.","\" Good luck, Osmont. I hope you do not become one of Those Who Remain.\" Her voice dropped. \" That would be such a shame. Such a shame.\"","HUUM!","She took a single step, and everything began to shake!","The forest trembled. The river shivered. The budding domains swayed upon their boughs, and Noah understood, without being told, that she simply did not wish to share anything more. The conversation was over because she had decided it was over!","He nodded, and he did not press her.","\" Thank you,\" he said.","...!","And then Noah looked at the figure of Lucy one last time, the small rough ancient thing pouring Domains from her hands at the beginning of all existence, and he held her image in his newborn existence as though ingranining it there, a thing he did not want to forget.","Then he took a step of his own, and he left the grand record behind.","He had gathered more threads of knowledge than he had come for, and now, he wanted only one thing.","He wanted to see, for the first time, just how different existence looked through the eyes of what he had become!"]},{"number":5761,"title":"Chapter 5761: Chapter 5760: Existence Is Not Empty!","paragraphs":["Noah stepped out of the record and back into the present.","He arrived where the Dimensional Provenance Train had been cut open, where Vakochev had cleaved it in two and an architect had died and a frost-visage had planted its forest. Hours had passed here while he had been figuring out the Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin.","The frost-forest had grown thicker, its rimed boughs heavier with frozen Dimensions, and the region for gigaparsecs around had emptied out, the hunters gone, the watchers gone, the snow still falling silent over the ruin. It looked, at a glance, like an abandoned place. A dead one.","Then Noah looked at it with the eyes he had now, and he saw that it was nothing of the kind.","...!","Existence was not empty. It had never been empty! He simply had never been able to see.","Above him, through the foamy void that he had always taken for a formless dark, there rose pillars. Vast ones. They climbed up out of the deep of existence and stretched away in every direction, structures so enormous that a single one dwarfed whole clusters of Dimensions themselvs, and they were everywhere, a forest of them far grander than the frozen one below, reaching endlessly across the void. And they coursed with authority!","Some shone blue from root to unseen peak, boundless Infinity pouring up their length. Others ran obsidian with THE Primordial Source, dark and dense and old.","Others gleamed white with the woven light of THE Argent Loom. And others still burned in colors Noah had no names for, flowing endlessly upward, downward, and outward through the structures.","They were strange to look at, because they were solid and they were not. He could see the shape of each pillar clearly, and yet he could see through it too, as though it were both a thing and the absence of a thing, hollow and present at once. He reached out and laid his hand against the nearest, a great blue column of pure Infinity, and the moment he touched it, prompts bloomed across his sight.","| You are perceiving an EXISTENTIAL CONDUIT.|","|The Conduits are the channels through which the authorities of existence flow, threaded through the whole of the void the way rivers and seas are threaded through a world. Infinity, THE Primordial Source, THE Argent Loom, and authorities beyond your knowing move along them without end.|","|They are the veins of existence itself.|","Noah drew his hand back slowly.","Existence was not a formless dark scattered with worlds. It was this. It was an endless architecture of flowing authority, seas and rivers of power moving through the deep in structures grander than anything he had ever built, and it had always been here, all around him, in every place he had ever stood!","And it now stood surrounded by whites of snow.","He had walked through it his whole existence and never once seen it, because to see it, one had to stand where he now stood. The cruelest part of that beauty was that almost nothing alive could perceive it. Only the very greatest existences could look at the deep of things and see how unfathomably lovely it truly was.","And it was not only the Conduits!","Something moved along them.","Across the void, across miles and light years and gigaparsecs, drifting between the great pillars and perched upon them, were living things. Small ones.","They were the equivalent of the flies and critters and birds a person might see drifting through any forest on any world, and they were everywhere, thousands of them turning lazily through the space of a single nearby light year alone.","Each one was incandescent, a small bright shape of pure light, delicate and strange, with wings or fins or trailing streamers of radiance that caught the colors of the Conduits they drifted near. Many were perched upon the great pillars, still and peaceful, and Noah understood, watching them, that they were drinking.","They sipped at the flowing authorities like how insects sip at nectar, feeding quietly on the rivvers of Infinity and Primordial Source and THE Argent Loom, minding their own small business in the veins of existence.","Prompts settled across his sight as he watched them.","|You are perceiving CONDUIT LIFEFORMS.|","|They dwell in the flow of the Existential Conduits and feed upon the authorities that move there, and the authority feeds on them. They are imperceptible to beings of insufficient Dimensionality and standing. Dimensionality alone is not enough. One must also hold the standing to perceive them, and only once perceived can they perceive you in turn, and interact.|","And their measures opened to him.","| CONDUIT LIFEFORM|","|VERITAS: ~150. POTENTIA: ~150. PONDUS: ~150. PROVENANCE: 0.|","Noah went still with the wonder of it. These small drifting critters, these flies of the deep that no lesser being could ever even see, carried attributes at a hundred and fifty across the board. Every one of them!","They were, by the raw numbers, mightier than most of the beings he had fought his whole climb, mightier than kingdoms and lineages and armies, and they did nothing with it at all! They only drifted, and drank, and buzzed peacefully through the veins of existence, because they held not a single point of Provenance between them. They had never generated a thing. They simply were, at that height, the way a fish simply is at the bottom of a sea, born to a depth that would crush anything not made for it.","One of them, wrapped in trailing rivers of light, came drifting curiously toward him.","It floated close as its wings flapped, turning about his radiant form as though it had never seen a thing quite like him, and Noah, moved by something he could not name, raised his hand. The little creature came and perched upon his outstretched finger, light as nothing, incandescent, and it made a single melodious sound, a small clear note that rang through the void like struck crystal!","Then it lifted from his finger and drifted away, back to its Conduit, back to its peaceful drinking, indifferent and lovely.","Noah watched it go.","Existence was abundant! It was vast! It was so much more, and so much more beautiful, than the empty dark he had always believed it to be. Everywhere he had ever looked and seen nothing, there had been this, oceans of authority and small bright living things drifting through them, a whole existence beneath the Existence, waiting for eyes grand enough to find it.","And at such a thought... his gaze hardened!","He rolled his neck slowly, and the wonder in him cooled into something colder and more familiar, because a thing this beautiful was a thing that had to be protected. His own existence was beautiful. His empire, sealed now in the space that was only his. His people, dreaming their centuries. His mother, his children, all of it.","And there were things in existence that threatened what was his, that had always threatened it, and Noah found himself wondering, standing here newly-born among the veins of existence, whether he could do something about them now.","THE Sealed One. THE SLEEPLESS FIEND. THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, who had sworn to rip Thalia in half at any moment he held her.","He was not an Immense One. He knew that. He had only just forged his Root, only just begun. He was not so foolish as to think a single step of becoming had made him the equal of the beings whose war he could not even perceive. But he wanted to know where he stood now!","He wanted to know if he could mount an offensive against even the weakest of the things that hunted him, against THE Sealed One at the least. It was one of many things he meant to test as he grew into what he had become.","And that raised the simplest question of all.","Where did his attributes even stand, now that his Root had emerged?!","He closed his eyes. He breathed in, drawing the cold and the light and the flowing authority of the deep into his newborn existence. And he turned his gaze inward, upon himself, to see exactly what he had become.","And he could not help it.","He smiled!"]},{"number":5762,"title":"Chapter 5762: Chapter 5761: Grand!","paragraphs":["Noah opened his eyes upon himself!","|THE True Human Emperor / THE Human Dreamer|","|VERITAS: 500|","|PROVENANCE: 500|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 500|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 500|","|Provenances: THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer (native, generated), THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign (claimed).|","|Infinity: DIALETHEIC INFINITY. A truth that is also its opposite; finite and infinite at once.|","|Existential Root: THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin. A Unique Existential Root of Immensity. A clear determination has not been made on whether it is Conceptual or Physical. |","He looked at the numbers for a while, and then he smiled. But...was his Root not a Conceptual one?","\"...\"","He only hung on this for a moment before he moved to the numbers.","Five hundred! Across the board, save for the Potentia that had always been Infinite and always would be. He had walked into that darkness carrying attributes in the two hundreds and walked out with five hundred, and the jump alone should have staggered him.","It did not, quite, because some part of him beneath the numbers already knew he was no longer the thing that had gone into the dark. The count was only existence catching up to a fact he had felt in his weavings the moment he reformed.","He turned the panel over. Two Provenances threading through him now, the Dreamer’s warm and his own, the Immense Sovereign’s cold and borrowed. His Infinity, which had stopped being merely endless and become Dialetheic, true in two directions at once. And under all of it, turning and pulsing and refusing to stop, the Root.","He reached in and tapped THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin, and it answered him, and more of it opened.","| THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin: preliminary functions.|","|TONIC DIMENSIONAL HYPERTROPHY (passive growth without effort).|","|Through the Root, your existence behaves as an embryonic system undergoing spontaneous expansion. It continuously secretes new layers of dimensional thickness. It increases the mass of individual quarks without the ingeston of any foreign energy. It raises your baseline Provenance, Veritas, and Pondus through metabolic background alone. Approximate range: an increase of 30 to 50 or more across all attributes per day, scaling upward as the Root grows. The range depends upon your state. Slumbering or passive, you grow at the floor. Actively moving to influence existence, you grow at the ceiling. You may grow without effort. But existence remains full of adversity, and the fastest climb is still to meet adversity and expand your knowledge.|","...!","Noah read that twice, and then he laughed!","He could sit still and grow. He could lie down in the snow and slumber for an age and do absolutely nothing, and he would rise regardless, thirty to fifty points a day welling up out of him without a single act of will, and more than that as the Root deepened.","He read on.","| THE PREVENTION OF CAUSAL LUTEOLYSIS (inhibition of structural decay).|","|An existence that ceases to fight, cultivate, or refine itself normally suffers structural atrophy, bleeding density back into existential entropy. Your Root constantly pulses to reject this. Your foundation will never regress, never degrade, and never leak authority back into the surrounding existence, no matter how many epochs you spend motionless.|","| CAUSAL INFORMATIONAL ANGIOGENESIS.|","|Your Root passively communicates with the bodies of existence around you and draws information from them. It may be prompted to reach as far as your existence can bear, to receive more.|","...!","So he would grow, and never rot, and drink the knowledge of wherever he stood without asking. A hard thing not to feel pleased about!","He let himself feel pleased about it for exactly a moment, and then he made himself set the pleasure down.","His power was grand, and it was terrifying, and he had genuinely not expected the leap to be this large. But then, he had not done this alone. Vakochev had handed him a gateway and called it an adversity. A single unit of the hormone that grew titans, pressed into his hands with a warning and a shrug, and Noah had done the only thing he had ever known how to do with adversity, which was to build something of his own out of it.","The Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin had never become his power. It had become fuel, folded down into a Root that was entirely his make.","Whether he would have formed the Root at all in so short a span without the favor, he could not say. Perhaps in a month or year. And looking now at the weavings of time in the strange new way his existence perceived them, he found he could no longer see Vakochev as a chance encounter.","The Fallen Hero had been a piece of a puzzle, and so had Noah, the hand that saved the a part of him that rose and cleaved the Train and killed an Immense One. He saved a piece of Vakochev, and it led to all this!","But the power changed everything about how he could move.","He held a Root of Immensity. And it was, for now, exactly that, and no more. A root. A seed cracked open, not a tree. It had to grow, endlessly, until it bloomed into something Immense, and until then he was a very strong sapling in a forest full of things that ate saplings.","So caution. He told himself, because the feeling underneath it did not want to hear it.","The feeling was invincibility!","It flooded his whole newborn existence, above everything else, an absolute conviction that he could do anything.","Lucy had named it to his face not long ago.","In the beginning, all of us feel this way. The sense of having finally seen the whole shape of things. He felt so grand and so untouchable that his mind was already racing ahead of his good sense, wanting to hunt down every vessel of THE Sealed One across all of time and space at once, wanting to fling his existence after the Immense Ones who had chased Vakochev into the dark, wanting to do a dozen mad and glorious things and feeling, in the weavings of his new Root, that he could do every one of them without a shred of worry.","He breathed in. He paused. He held himself still.","His people were safe. He was safe. His empire was sealed in a space that answered to no one but him. So why go kicking over stones the moment he had learned to walk again, before he had digested a single thing about what he now was?","He could hunt the truth of The Long Night without lighting a war he was not yet built to survive. Because he could feel what his Root allowed, and in the same breath he could feel where it stopped.","He counted himself lucky, honestly. The Immense Ones gathered here had never once looked twice at him, their whole attention on themselves and then on Vakochev, and a masked eye at the rim had been beneath their concern.","But a few more minutes of any one of those gazes settling on him would have made it clear enough that he was not one of them. That he was something else, wearing the shape of a harmless watcher. He had survived on being small. He would keep being small a little longer.","So. For now...","Noah smiled, and raised his hand, and countless illusory pages flickered off of him and drifted through the falling snow.","\"I could find and grasp rare Gu easily now ,\" he murmured, \" and see whether that path has anything in store for me. And when it comes to Atlas and Time...\"","His eyes shone.","Because after his cessation and his reforging, he had chosen a few places across existence for his newborn self to occupy at once, and Atlas’s Elsedimension of shattered hours was one of them.","Even now a part of him stood among the broken clocks and the numbered meteorites, and he turned that attention there, and he compared. The Existential Conduits that threaded those frozen hours. The Conduit Lifeforms drifting through them. He set them against what he saw here, in the veins of existence above the sundered Train, and read the differences between them, and learned.","And then his gaze settled on the illusory ring he had worn all this while. The ring that was Atlas.","He could see it clearly now! For the first time, Noah could see the ring for exactly what it was!"]},{"number":5763,"title":"Chapter 5763: Chapter 5762: A Delectable Treat! I","paragraphs":["Noah held the illusory ring in his hands, and turned it, and looked at it with the eyes he had now.","\" You are a glimmer of an Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin ,\" he said slowly, \" worn inside the shape of a ring. That is what you are. That is what you have always been, and I could never see it until now. \"","He turned it again in his fingers. \" So tell me. How did you manage that, when the Immense Ones shattered your existence to pieces? Or is your own Root of Immensity so grand that even they could not shatter it?\"","...!","For a long moment, there was only silence.","The snow fell. The clock-hands of Atlas’s Dimension turned somewhere far away in another of his bodies. And the ring sat quiet in his hands, and Noah waited.","Then the old engineer spoke.","|It seems you have had quite a leap, | Atlas said.","|A major one, in a very short span. When you ceased, all of you at once, I will admit I braced for the worst. I thought an Immense One had finally caught your scent and made a move. But no. You were only grasping your own Root of Immensity.|","|Which, for the record, I had intended to help you form much, much later. After we had raised your Provenance and the depth of your existence a great deal higher. How you jumped that many steps in a little, I have no idea, and I have decided not to think too hard about it, because thinking too hard about you gives me a ringache.|","Noah’s mouth pulled at one corner.","| But you asked me a question, | Atlas went on, quieter. | So. Yes. In the tools I engineered, I spread my Root of Immensity. Every relic, every workshop, every ring, every hidden thing I ever made. I wove glimmers of my own Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin into all of them. Do you understand what that means?|","He did not wait to find out. |It means that as long as one of my tools survived anywhere in existence, some fragment of my Root survived with it. They broke my body on their anvil. They collapsed my homes into ash. And they thought they were done. But they could never find every tool. And if they could never eliminate my tools, then they could never, truly, eliminate me.|","Noah looked at the ring in his hands calmly.","\" So this whole time, \" Noah said. \"I have been carrying part of you.\"","|A small part. A glimmer. Enough to talk, to teach, to scheme. Not enough to walk out and reforge myself, which is the great inconvenience of my situation.|","Noah let that sit a moment and then he asked the thing underneath everything.","\" What is your purpose, really? With me. You spread yourself through your tools, and you gave a great ring to THE REMINISCING WIDOW, which means you may even have her help now. Existence is give and take. You told me I could make the impossible possible, and I suppose I have just proven a little of that. \"","He held the ring up. \"But what is the endgame? What are you actually after?\"","And there was silence again!","| When an Immensity is destroyed ,| Atlas said at last, |it does not simply come back. No matter how grand the being was. No matter how much of it survives in glimmers and tools. When you rebuild an Immensity that was broken, you never get the same power back. You come back smaller. Diminished. A great fire relit from one saved ember, and it never burns as tall as it did before.|","The ring pulsed faintly.","| Which means that even if I clawed my way back into a body, I would not be able to do the thing I most need to do. I could not take down the ones I need to take down. Not the way I am now. Not the way I would come back.|","|So there is revenge in it. There is a great deal of revenge in it. But there is also the simpler thing. The capability to do what I no longer can. If you grow grand enough, Dreamer. If you become truly, unfathomably grand. Then maybe, one day, you will be grand enough to fully restore an Immensity that was broken. To relight the fire without losing the height. Maybe. Who knows.|","The old engineer’s voice was quiet and honest and unashamed .","|It is all for my own selfish reasons, in the end. Even as I help you along. Do not ever mistake me for a kind old man. I am a very selfish one who happens to be teaching you.|","Noah listened to all of it, and he did not flinch from it, because a selfish reason honestly stated was a thing he could trust far more than a kind one. He looked at the ring once more, and opened his mouth to answer.","And Atlas blinked.","| Oh, fuck.|","The old engineer’s projection went rigid, as though he had forgotten something and only just remembered it in the worst possible moment.","| Right. Right, I am an idiot. Dreamer, listen to me. Hide yourself. All of you, every body, get all of your existence into your Existential Root Domain right now, this instant. How did I forget this? How did I forget the single most obvious thing?! |","The words came fast and alarmed. | Inside an Elsedimension they have no access to, you are hard to reach. But out here, a newly formed Root of Immensity? Some Immense Ones can smell that! A fresh Root reaching its weavings out into open existence is a scent, and it is a rare and delicious one, and you are broadcasting it right now like a lit fire in a dark forest!|","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed as his teacher had a gift for delivering the worst news at the last possible second.","HUUM!","Because in that instant, he felt his existence buzz, the part of him still standing in the frozen forest where the Train had been split, and information came flooding in from that body all at once.","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR smells something unique left behind in this place.|","|THE SLEEPLESS FIEND is surprised. He says that whatever has been found here is his.|","...!","Noah’s newborn Root drank the information from that body in a single breath, and he sensed it the malicious weavings of Immensity surging back toward the frozen forest, two of the beings whose war he could not perceive turning their terrible attention toward the fresh scent of a Root that should not exist!","He moved decisively.","He hurled his existence toward his Existential Root Domain, toward the sealed space that answered to no one but him, the one place in all of existence that not even an Immense One could enter!","HUUM!","His existence had already begun to fade, in the span of an instant, dissolving out of the frozen forest toward safety, and he could feel the tug of his impenetrable space reaching to receive him, pulling him home.","But.","An undeniable force closed around him and pulled him back!","It was not a thing he could fight. It seized his fading existence the way a hand seizes a fleaf in the wind, absolute and effortless, and it dragged him back out of his retreat, back toward the frozen forest, back into the open where the scent of his Root hung bright and exposed.","| THE SLEEPLESS FIEND says: friend. Do not go quite yet. Come back out here.|","...!","An undeniable force pulled him, and Noah’s eyes went cold.","He set his newborn will against the impossible grip, and in the same instant he made his decision!","Because he would not be caught, would not be held, would not be dragged before an Immense One to be studied and cracked open.","If he could not escape, then he would simply cease. He would dissipate his existence here completely, this body, this presence, all of it, scatter himself to nothing before any Immense One could close a hand around what he had become!"]},{"number":5764,"title":"Chapter 5764: Chapter 5763: A Delectable Treat! II","paragraphs":["The undeniable force held Noah’s fading existence in the open, and would not let it go!","He hung there, half-dissolved, dragged back from the threshold of his own sealed Domain, and above him in the churning obsidian snowy foam loomed the two of them.","They were vast and indistinct, present one moment as enourmous eyes and gone the next, THE SLEEPLESS FIEND and THE UNPAID COLLECTOR turning their terrible attention upon the small bright thing that should not exist.","| What a scent ,| the Fiend said.","|A fresh Root of Immensity, reaching its little weavings out into the open. I have not smelled one of these in an age. And a unique one, at that. How fortunate for us that you did not have the sense to stay hidden.|","Noah did not struggle against the grip. Struggling would have told them how weak he was, and they did not need to know that yet!","\" You have me confused with something worth your time,\" he said, and his voice came level with no fear in it at all. \"I am a watcher who wandered in. There is nothing here for you.\"","|A watcher who ceased and reformed at the rim of my Narrative, many times over, and now wears the scent of a newborn Root. No.| The Fiend’s threads gathered, almost amused. | You are something rarer than a watcher. Come here, little friend. Come out into the open where I can look at you properly. I only want... to look.|","The grip tightened. Noah felt himself dragged another fraction back from safety, felt the tug of his sealed Domain reaching for him and losing him, and he made his decision then.","Dissipation it was!","HUUM!","And that...was when something unique bloomed!","Existence buzzed and turned upside down.","He recieved and overabundance of new information!","Shockingly, a slime arrived!","It dropped into the frozen forest out of nowhere, a shapeless blob of pure golden light, and the moment it appeared, both of the vast indistinct figures above went still. Not surprised, quite. Cautious!","The Fiend’s writhing threads slowed. The Collector’s looming shape drew back a fraction. The golden slime landed upon the air between Noah and the two Immense Ones, small and bright against their enormity, and it announced itself!","| THE DIMENSIONAL DEVOURER, Poona, has arrived. She says that this time, she will not fail!|","...!","The golden blob rose, and it flowed upward, and it changed. The gold took a shape and refined itself, and where a slime had been there stood a young woman, delicate and slight, with a fall of golden hair and a face of quiet loveliness and no aura at all, nothing, less presence than a candle.","She was tiny before the two indistinct titans hanging in the foam ahead of her, a slip of a thing against beings vaster than Dimensions!","She did not look tiny when she spoke.","\" Do the two of you really want to fight just as the cold has come? \" Poona said, \" Look at yourselves. As grand and immense as you have grown, as high as you have climbed, and here you are, the both of you, ganging up to snatch at a little junior who has barely opened his eyes. How despicable are you, truly? Will your greed have no end at all?\"","|Move aside, Slime ,| the Collector said, and the way he said the word slime....frankly, it was very off putting as if he wss using it as a derogatory word!","|This one was found in our Narrative. That makes his disposition a matter for those who found him. Not for a scavenger who arrives late.|","|The Root is unclaimed ,| the Fiend agreed, mild as ever. | What is found belongs to the finder. Step back, little Devourer, and I may let you keep the parts we do not want.|","Poona smiled.","It was a dangerous smile, and it did not touch the ease in her voice at all. \" Well. I have laid a claim to the protection of this junior. As of this moment, he stands under... a certain umbrella. You understand what that means, I think, both of you. You offend me here, and you do not merely offend me. You offend a great many as you should know where I stem from. So... \"","She tilted her golden head. \" What will it be?\"","Silence actually came down!","The two Immense Ones did not move, and Noah, hanging held in the cold, watched two of the most terrifying beings in existence weigh a slip of a golden woman with no aura and choose, against every instinct their greed was screaming at them, to do nothing.","The grip on his existence did not release, but it did not tighten either. They watched. They watched threateningly, their vast indistinct shapes hanging in the snow, and they did not act.","That inaction... told Noah more about who Poona was than anything she had said. Shd had said they would offend a great deal of many where she came from so...where the hell did she come from?","She turned from them, and she came to him, drifting close through the falling snow, and her voice dropped.","\" Little guy, \" she said. \"I really cannot afford to fail to bring another one of you back this time. So listen to me, and sense to the trueness of my existence as your newly formed Root should be very sensitive. I do not mean you any harm. Not the way these two fuckers did.\"","She glanced back at the titans, unbothered. \"Let us go, before either of them talks themselves into something stupid, okay?\"","...!","This unknown and terrifying being, who had made two Immense Ones stand still with a smile, was speaking to him as though she were coaxing a frightened animal down off a ledge.","And Noah, still gathered and ready to scatter himself to nothing, held that readiness, and reached out with his newborn sight into the boundless flowing information all around him, and read her.","He read the Trueness pouring off her, the deep weave of what she was, and in all of it, in every thread, there was no malice. None. Whatever else she was, whatever she wanted, she did not want to harm him, and his newborn existence could not find a single lie in her.","He did not lower his guard. But he did not scatter himself either.","\" Just who are you ,\" he said, \" really?\"","Poona’s smile turned almost fond.","\"I am merely Poona. THE Dimensional Devourer.\" She drifted a little closer. \" You do not understand yet what you are, so let me tell you, since it is the reason two Immense Ones just tried to snatch you out of the sky. A newly formed Root of Immensity is one of the rarest thing in existence, little guy. It is an entire path, an entire future of Immensity, sitting exposed at its very beginning. Untouched. Unspent. Full of everything it could ever become. To an Immense One greedy enough, a fresh Root is a Panacea. A cure, a fortune, a treasure beyond price, because to devour it is to swallow a whole path of potentail before it has walked a single step.\"","Noah went very still at that!","\" So ,\" Poona said brightly. \"I am going to tug on your existence now, and pull you somewhere safe. Do not kill yourself off, and do not run away, all right? It would waste a great deal of my effort, and I have had a very long day!\"","Noah thought about it. He weighed the two watching titans and their held greed, the golden woman with no lie in her, the impossible situation he had walked into simply by becoming what he was!","And he trusted his intuition more than anything else!","He let his readiness to cease uncoil, just slightly.","Then he turned his cold gaze one last time upon THE SLEEPLESS FIEND and THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, the two vast indistinct greeds hanging in the frozen foam.","And in the next instant, he and Poona were gone as gold light flashed!"]},{"number":5765,"title":"Chapter 5765: Chapter 5764: Legacy! I","paragraphs":["Poona pulled him through existence, and Noah felt every layer of it pass!","He did not resist the tug. They sank down through layers of reality and up through tiers of Dimensionality, past depths he had never known were stacked beneath existence, with existence peeling open around them and folding shut behind, and he catologed every one of them as they went. It was a great deal to take in!","And then they arrived, and the place they arrived in was grand.","The Existential Conduits were here, the great pillars of flowing authority he had first seen threading the void above the sundered Train. But here they did not merely rise and stretch. Here they had been bent and shaped.","Woven into structure and form, the veins of existence itself coaxed into architecture, and out of them stood grand buildings and soaring towers, whole halls and towers raised from living rivers of Infinity and Source and Loom-light, coursing bright through walls that were somehow both solid and made of pure flowing authority.","And through those Conduit-buildings, moving freely, drifting between the towers and perching on the towers, went the Conduit Lifeforms, thousands of them, the incandescent critters of the deep, at home here in a way they had not been in the wild veins of the void.","It was an ancient place, and its Dimensionality was terrifying to stand within.","Above the towers, Dimensions and Observable Existences hung in the air like stars, whole domains turning gently in the dark as though they were nothing more than lanterns strung over a courtyard.","And beyond the towers rose mountains, vast ones, and they were not mountains at all, Noah saw, but Elsedimensions grown into the shape of mountains, great masses of sealed reality climbing into the heights with Existential Conduits running through them like rivers of light threading a range of peaks.","A civilization raised in the veins of existence, older than most things Noah had ever encountered, grand beyond the grandest empires!","And over all of it, heavy and constant, fell the snow.","The cold had reached even here. Even this ancient place of terrifying Dimensionality, this domain grown from the bones of existence, lay under the falling white, the Long Night’s chill permeating the Conduit-towers and the star-hung domains and the Elsedimension mountains all alike. It fell thick as beside him Noah saw Poona shiver.","She grimaced, and waved a small hand, and a coat wove itself around her out of nothing, thick and warm, and Noah’s new eyes saw that it was filled with boundless invisible authority, layer upon layer of it.","\" Ugh ,\" Poona said, pulling the coat close. \" It reaches everywhere now. Even home. \"","Then she brightened, and turned to him, and there was real satisfaction in her face. \" But look at this. Look at you, standing here safe! I did it. I actually did it this time!\"","She said it with the pleasure of someone who had needed a win and finally gotten one.","\" You should understand... \" she went on, walking now, leading him in among the Conduit-towers under the snow. \" Some Immense Ones, the greedy ones, the hungry ones, they would rather just eat the young. A fresh Root, swallowed whole, no thought given to it. That is what those two were. That is most of them, if I am honest.\"","She glanced at him. \" But not all. Some of them care about legacy. About what comes after. About whether the path continues once they are gone. And you have arrived at a place built by one who cared about exactly that. \" A small, proud smile. \" This place. This whole Domain. It was founded here by her.\"","She led him on, through the towers and beneath the hanging Domains, until they came to the foot of one of the great Elsedimension mountains, and there, at its entrance, stood a statue.","Noah looked up at it, and his new sight resolved what it was made of. Existential Conduits. The veins of existence themselves, bent and woven and set into the shape of a figure, rivers of flowing authority coursing through the carved form so that the whole statue glowed from within, blue and obsidian and white and a dozen colors he had no names for, an entire being sculpted from the living power of the deep.","And the figure it made was one he knew.","It was small, and rough, and hunched. A caveman shape of thick limbs and unadorned skin, calloused hands cupped as though pouring something out. And beautiful, terribly and anciently beautiful, even rendered in flowing Conduits a mile high.","It was Lucy!","Poona stopped before the statue, and she bowed her head, and when she spoke her voice had lost all its lightness and gone quiet and reverent.","\" This is the one responsible for all of it, \" she said. \" For this place. For me. For every one of us who ever awoke a Root and lived long enough to grow it. Before she left existence, she built this. An Immense Legacy, raised here in the deep, to give the young a place. Somewhere those who had awakened their Existential Roots of Immensity could thrive, and grow, and become what they were meant to become, without being hunted down and devoured for the treasure they carried before they ever had the chance to walk their path.\" Poona looked up at the glowing figure.","\" This is her Legacy. She is THE Acharya of Immensity. Lucy!\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes shone.","He thought of Lucy in the record, walking through her Primordial forest, telling him to go and experience existence for the first time now that his Root had emerged. She had not warned him how dangerous that would be. She had not told him that stepping out into the open with a fresh Root was to hang a jewel before every greedy Immense One nearby!","She had simply smiled and sent him out.","But now he stood before her Legacy, where someone belonging to it had found him at the exact moment two titans closed their hands around him, and pulled him free.","Had she expected that? Had she known, when she sent him out unwarned, that her Legacy would reach him before the hungry ones could? That a thing she had built at the beginning of existence would still be standing at the end of an Age?","He could not know. She was a record, and records did not answer follow-up questions. But standing here, looking up at her made of the veins of existence, he thought it was not impossible. It was not impossible at all!","Poona was already moving on.","\" Come ,\" she said, turning from the statue and leading him deeper toward the mountain’s entrance. \" There is a great deal here, and you will need time to grasp all of it. In these Empyros Immense Legacy Mountains, you will find others like you, some who have awoken a Root of Immensity and not yet formed their Immensity, still growing, still becoming. And in some places, yes, you will see true Immense Ones, the ones who care about what comes after as they won’t try to eat you...for the most part.\"","She glanced back at him, and the lightness returned to her. \" There is much for you to understand. But first things first. Let me take you to Sir Moriarty.\"","...!"]},{"number":5766,"title":"Chapter 5766: Chapter 5765: Legacy! II","paragraphs":["<Those Who Remain>","Seconds after Poona and the anomaly vanished, the sky changed.","An aura descended over the frozen forest and the sundered halves of the Train, and it was Immensity of a weight that even THE SLEEPLESS FIEND and THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, who were no small things, felt in their own existences.","The two hazy titans, who had loomed so terribly only moments ago, went somber beneath it.","Then it took a shape.","A figure formed in the churning snow, hazy and purple, humanoid in its outline but wrong in its crown, because from its head rose a pair of horns that did not stop. They twisted upward and outward endlessly, spiraling into the dark above without ever reaching an end, coiling on and on past where sight could follow.","The purple haze of it pressed down on the ruined region, and the two Immense Ones who had been the mightiest things present a breath ago now stood in the presence of something mightier still.","The horned figure spoke, and his voice boomed out across the frozen dark as it came edged with the flatness of a being who was used to being obeyed.","\" Where is the Anomaly that was just here?\"","It was almost a command. Almost. And THE SLEEPLESS FIEND, who did not care to be commanded by anyone, let a cold light pass behind his luminous eyes at the tone of it.","But he did not act imposingly. He weighed the horned figure’s Immensity against his own, and he simply answered!","\" One of those from the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity came,\" the Fiend said, \" and took him.\"","...!","Existence seethed!","The purple haze roiled, the snow whipping violently around the horned figure, and he looked at the Fiend and the Collector like a colleague looks at others who have broken something priceless through sheer stupidity.","\" You did not think ,\" the horned one said slowly, \" that an emerging Root, forming in the very first hours after the Long Night began, might be a thing worth holding on to?\"","Neither answered.","\" One of the few things we were able to scry, across the whole of existence, through all the fog the winter has thrown over the future ,\" he went on, and each word landed heavier than the last, \" was this. That one of the three named in THE AUGURY OF THE LONG NIGHT, one of the three at the turning, would be the first to form a Root after the Night descended. The first. And you had that thing in your hands, both of you, hands closed around it, a piece of the single most important puzzle we face in this dreadful cold...\"","The horns coiled endlessly above him. \" And you let anothrr walk up and take it out of your grip? Really? Truly?You fucked it that badly?\"","...!","The Fiend’s threads buzzed, and the Collector’s mass seethed, their own Immensity flaring at the humiliation of the words! And the Fiend looked over, and his voice came cold and imperious.","\" None of that information was shared with us,\" he said. \" We were told nothing of a scrying, nothing of an Augury. We caught a scent, we found a Root, we moved to take it. Perhaps if belonging to a Legacy actually granted us the benefits it is supposed to grant, rather than leaving us to guess in the dark like common hunters, we would have known to hold it more carefully.\"","The horned figure waved a dismissive hand, and the snow settled.","\" The Long Night has only just begun, \" he said, the anger cooling into something colder and more organized. \" There are things the ones who are not core to this still do not know. That is a failure of ours, not of yours, and it will be corrected. Let us go back, so that everything is made clear to everyone, and so that nothing like this ever happens again.\"","He turned his endless horns toward the deep. \" We have known for a long time that one of the three is little Riven. He has been groomed and contained this whole time. If we could have gotten our hands on a second of the three as well, then surviving the Long Night would have been all but guaranteed.\"","\" But we know where they took him now. So it may be that we simply do everything in our power to take him back. Come. There is a great deal to prepare.\"","...!","He turned and dissolved into the deep of existence, his endless horns the last of him to fade, and a breath later the Fiend and the Collector followed, gone into the dark after him, and the frozen forest was left empty under the falling snow with no one to see it grow.","—","Far away, in a Domain lost in existence and time, Sir Moriarty worked at his corpse and watched a screen.","The illusory screen hung in the drifting snow of his hall, and upon it moved two small figures, Poona in her lovely borrowed shape and the anomaly at her side, walking the road of Conduit-light toward him.","Moriarty drew a thread of pale authority from the dead Immense One splayed before him, held it to his small neat spectacles, and set it aside, and did not look away from the screen as he worked.","Behind him, silent, a verdant eye opened in the air.","It was vast, and it was filled with an Immensity Moriarty did not turn to measure, and it wached the screen over his shoulder.","\" The first Root formed after the Long Night, \" it said. \"Is it confirmed that he is one of the three? We cannot build what we are building on guesswork.\"","Moriarty did not stop his work.","\" We will know for certain in due time ,\" he said, calm as still water. \" Even Poona does not know what he might be. None of the others do either. So I will take charge of it myself, and confirm it quietly, as we go. Do not worry.\"","The verdant eye did not answer at once. It gazed at the figure of Noah on the screen intently.","\"I never much cared for the future ,\" it said at last. \" Why would I? I can always change my present. And I never much cared for this Augury of the Long Night, all its cryptic little verses about turnings and threes.\"","A pause, and the eye narrowed. \" But THE Acharya of Immensity took it seriously. Lucy took it seriously and she told us that when the Night came, it would be our chance. Our one chance to stop being what we are. To no longer be Those Who Remain.\"","The verdant light deepened. \" So we make sure. We gather every piece the Augury names, and we hold them, and we do not let a single one slip away because someone was careless. With the Long Night, the path is open again. The door that closed on us all those ages ago has cracked. And we cannot, we will not, merely Remain.\"","The eye held on Noah’s small figure a moment longer.","Then it closed, and was gone, and Moriarty was alone with his corpse and his screen and the falling snow.","He drew another thread of dead authority from the splayed Immense One, and he simply murmured to himself again!","\" And at the turning, count three,\" Moriarty said. \" One shall look upon all that is, and grieve. One shall take up every weight, and not set it down. One shall no longer remain, and yet remain.\"","He set the thread aside, and reached into the corpse for another, and on the screen the two small figures drew closer to his hall.","\" One shall no longer remain, and yet remain,\" he said again, softer, and watched the anomaly come!"]},{"number":5767,"title":"Chapter 5767: Chapter 5766: Legacy! III","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Poona led him up through the mountain as they crossed many intricate Existential Conduits.","Now, even as they moved, he continued to collect information as he didn’t take Poona’s words as law. He knew very well how in existence, nobody did anything without reason. Everybody was selfish! Even Atlas had his aims.","So he simply had to grasp what the aims of Poona and this Legacy were, even if they didn’t mean him harm.","After going deeper into the Elsedimension Mountain filled with Existential Conduits leading the way...","Noah felt a whole sealed reality shaped into the form of a peak open up, Existential Conduits running through it like veins of light through stone, and at its heart, in a great open hall, waited the thing that ruled it.","It was...an octopus.","Noah stopped where he floated and simply looked.","A vast titan of dark coiling flesh sat at the center of the hall, tentacles moving through the drifting air with unhurried precision, and around it wound slow rivers of white and gold, currents of pure authority threading between islands of nothing.","Whole Dimensions floated in the space above it like lanterns. Snow drifted down through all of it, impossible and constant. And upon what passed for the creature’s face perched a pair of small, neat spectacles, absurd against its enormity, catching the gold of the rivers.","This would be the one Poona said was...Sir Moriarty?","Before it lay the corpse of an Immense One!","It was splayed and pinned in the drifting air, opened and parted and studied, and Moriarty’s tentacles worked through it calmly.","\" Sir Moriarty ,\" Poona said. \" This time I reached in time and brought back another Root for the Legacy. This earns me some points, yes? The Fiend and another were ready to sniff him up...\"","The octopus set down the thread of authority he was holding.","He turned, and the small spectacles turned with him as his eyes settled upon Noah with undisguised interest.","\" So you did. Come in. Gaze upon everything as I am sure it must seem odd and interesting...\" Moriarty said!","Noah stood in the drifting snow of the hall and looked at the octopus. There was power, first, an ancient and terrible depth of it that Noah could not find the bottom of. Question marks upon question marks!","\" You are wary ,\" Moriarty said, watching him. \"","This is good. Wary is how the young survive long enough to become old.\"","He waved a tentacle, and a thread of the white-gold river coiled up and offered itself as a seat, which Noah declined.","\" Let me guess. You do not trust where you are, you do not know what I or others want, and you are even suspicious we dragged you here to eat you as well. Am I close?\"","\" You are... close.\" Noah said.","\" Hmm.\"","Moriarty adjusted his spectacles with a delicate curl of one tentacle. \" So let me spare you the suspense. This is THE Acharya of Immensity, Lucy’s Legacy. These are the Empyros Immense Legacy Mountains. Yes, this is a real sanctuary. No, there is no catch you have not already guessed. Yes, some of the beings here are Immense Ones, and no, they will not eat you, because Lucy built this place with laws in its very structure and even the greediest thing here honors them, partly out of respect and partly because breaking them is a great deal more painful than they would like.\"","Noah listened intently!","\" This is where the ones who care about legacy bring the young to grow. It has been here for a long time.\"","He turned one bright eye fully upon Noah then.","\" So. Since we are getting to know one another. What kind of Root did you form?\"","It was asked lightly, but it was heavy!","And Noah did not have an answer. His own weavings could not sort him into either box.","He deflected.","\"I have only just formed it,\" Noah said . \"I am still learning what it is.\"","It was somewhat true.","\" Fair enough ,\" he said mildly. \" A Root is a private thing when it is new, and you would be a fool to unwrap yours in front of a stranger. Poona, head back for now. I will finish the introductions with The Stranger.\"","...!","\" Okay! \" Poona didn’t delay as she waved her hands and disappeared!","Sir Moriarty set his tools down and fully looked at Noah as with just the two of them here and a corpse of an Immense One behind, the air became heavy!","\" There are two kinds of Root in all of existence,\" Moriarty said. \" Only two. Every awakened Lifeform you will ever meet is one or the other.\"","He drifted on. \" The first is the Conceptual Root. A Root of idea. Of law, of narrative, of dream, of pure concept. It grows into what we call an Empyros Immense Lifeform, and an Empyros does not fight Existence as much as rewrite it. The Conceptual path is grand, subtle, and terrifying in the way a well-written sentence is terrifying, if you understand what a well-written sentence can do.\"","\" The other. \" Moriarty’s spectacles caught the light. \" The Physical Root. A Root of body, of flesh, of appetite, of raw dimensional mass and force. It grows into a Fiend Immense Lifeform. And a Fiend does not rewrite Existence A Fiend simply is larger than Existence’s ability to argue with it. THE SLEEPLESS FIEND you just came across is exactly what his name says he is. A Fiend of the Physical path, grown vast. He is a decently powerful one that is nigh unkillable...\"","Noah’s eyes shone brightly!","\" This is why the paths matter,\" the octopus went on. \" It is not a category. It is life and death.\"","Noah could not say for certain which he was!","Everything about him said Conceptual. He was a Dreamer. An author. A thing that had spent its existence imposing narratives, dreaming realities true, bending stories to his will, all of it concept, concept, concept.","But his Root had refused to say so!","He thought of his Infinity, the thing at the root of his Root. Dialetheic. A truth that is also its opposite. Finite and infinite at once, holding two contradictory things and being true in both without choosing.","What would a Root born of that principle be? Conceptual, or Physical?","Both. Neither?"]},{"number":5768,"title":"Chapter 5768: Chapter 5767: Legacy! IV","paragraphs":["He shook his head as he fished for more information.","\" And an Immense One, \" Noah said. \" In all of this...what is an Immense One, really?\"","Moriarty looked at the drifting snow with luminous, terrifying eyes of power!","\"A Root ,\" he said, \"is a seed. That is all any of you are, all of you young ones here. A seed cracked open, full of everything it could ever be, and nothing it is yet. And an Immense One is what happens when a seed is given enough time, and enough safety, and enough adversity in the right measure, to grow. From seed to sprout. From sprout to tree. From potential, all the way to bloom.\"","He turned his small spectacled eyes on Noah. \" You are a seed. A strange one, an interesting one, a seed I cannot classify, but a seed. The tree is the goal. Immensity is only a Root that has finished growing. Out there across existence, many like you are devoured before you can bloom, unless you remain in your Existential Root Domain. But Immensity is hard to fully grasp by being idle as many try different things to survive.\"","The snow fell over the Domain relentlessly.","\" And the winter, \" Moriarty added, \"is very, very hard on seeds. This place...tries to make it a bit easier for seeds to grow. This place does not want your loyalty.\"","Noah looked at him.","\" We are not some sect. We do not care whether you develop a fierce sense of belonging to us, or a deep sense of duty toward us, or whether you weep tears of gratitude every morning at the thought of our kindness.\"","Moriarty drifted along.","\" You owe us nothing. Not belief, not service, not affection. Grow strong, leave when you like, forget my face entirely. It is genuinely all the same to us.\"","\" That is a strange thing for a sanctuary to say,\" Noah said.","\"It is a strange sanctuary .\" Moriarty’s tone stayed dry. \" We are not run for our own glory. Everything here, every law, every kindness, every seed we save from the winter, is done for one reason, and one reason only. Because she wished it.\"","He did not have to say who!","\" Lucy did not build this place to gather followers. She had no interest in being worshipped. She built it because she wanted the young to have a chance she did not have. And so we honor her wishes, all of us, the greedy ones and the kind ones alike. Out of respect for her. She is the only thing any of us truly bow to here, and she is not even present to see it.\"","WAA!","Noah found that on this particular ideal... he believed it. Their reverence towards that being!","\" So no ,\" Moriarty went on, \" you will not be asked to swear anything, or join anything, or become one of us. But you will be given something, because she wished that too. A gift she handed down before she left, for every budding Root that finds its way here.\"","He slowed. \" And it is the reason most of the young survive long enough to bloom at all. A Root grows on its own, you have felt that already, I imagine. It secretes its own Dimensionality, raises its own weight, climbs a little every day whether you lift a finger or not. That is the nature of a Root. But growing on its own is slow. Achingly slow. It is a seed pushing up through hard groud one grain at a time, and a seed that grows only at that pace will not become a tree before the winter finds it. Not in an Age like this one.\"","He turned his small eyes on Noah.","\" So Lucy left us a way to grow faster. A Narrative Immense Inscription Art . And it does one thing, one beautiful and terrible thing! It lets a budding Root reach out, across the whole of existence, across Time, Parallel Time, Apocryphal Existences, Multidimensions, Elsedimensions...everything really, and pull in what it needs to grow!\"","\" Pull in...what, exactly?\" Noah asked.","\" Immensity .\" Moriarty said the word with weight. \" Existence is not empty, you have seen that now. It is full. Full of authority, full of flow, full of the whole churning chaos of everything that ever was and is and will be, all of it moving through the Conduits and the deep at once. And scattered through that chaos, rare and fine, are slivers. Molecular units, if you like, of pure chaotic Immensity. Loose fragments of the very thing your Root is trying to become. They drift through existence unclaimed, across every distance and every age, and the Art lets you reach out and gather them, and feed them to your Root, so that it grows toward the tree not one grain at a time but by the mouthful. It is how a seed becomes truly Immense before the winter can kill it. It is how any of us ever did.\"","Noah’s existence sharpened with the interest!","\" It is the hardest thing you will ever attempt. When you reach out across existence, you do not reach into a tidy shelf of Immensity waiting to be taken. You reach into everything. All of it, at once, the entire boundless flow of chaos, every current and every stream, information beyond counting, most of it useless, most of it wrong, most of it nothing to do with what you need. And you must reject all of it. Every flow but the one. You must reach into the roar of the whole of existence and refuse every single thing pouring toward you except the rare, fine slivers of Immensity, and then, across a distance and a time you cannot even imagine, you must pull those slivers, and only those, toward yourself, without dragging in a single scrap of anything else.\"","He let that sink!","\" It is a sieve,\" Moriarty said. \"A sieve held up against an ocean, and you are trying to catch a specific grain of a specific sand while the whole sea pours through your hands. Most of the time you will fail. Most of the time you will reach for a sliver of Immensity and pull in a great slop of chaos you did not want, useless information, foreign flows, things that fight your Root instead of feeding it. That is the ordinary danger, and it is bad enough.\"","His voice dropped. \" But it is no longer the ordinary danger, because The Long Night has come. And the winter has changed what is out there in the flow.\"","The snow fell heavier around them, as if the words had summoned it!"]},{"number":5769,"title":"Chapter 5769: Chapter 5768: Legacy! V","paragraphs":["\" There is cold in the chaos now,\" Moriarty said.","\" The descending cold has soaked into the flows of existence themselves, and some of the information drifting out there is no longer merely useless. It is frozen. It is destructive. Reach into the flow carelessly now, cast your sieve without the discipline, and you may pull in a sliver of The Long Night itself, a shard of that killing cold, and draw it straight into the heart of your budding Root. And a Root is a fragile thing. It is a seed, cracked open, soft and new. The cold that the mightiest Immense Ones can barely hold at bay would freeze a young Root solid in an instant, and there is no coming back from that. So the Art was always hard. Now it is hard, and it will kill you if your discipline slips.\"","He looked at Noah steadily. \"I would not blame you for waiting. Many do. They grow the slow way and hope to outlast the winter. Some of them even manage it.\"","\" Show me the Art,\" Noah said.","Moriarty regarded him a moment silently.","\" Very well. Watch closely. And do not flinch.\"","The octopus rose.","And the Immensity came off him!","Noah’s existence pulsed as grand Immensity bloomed!","It was no lesser than THE SLEEPLESS FIEND! Well, likely greater as this mosntrous being was likely a fiend too.","The hall trembled with it! The rivers of authority bent! The floating Domains shuddered on their strings, and Noah understood, all at once and with perfect clarity, that the affable creature who had told him he owed nothing and offered him a seat of light was one of the most terrifying existences he had ever stood beside, and had simply chosen, out of respect, to be gentle about it!","From that unfurled Immensity, Moriarty conjured the Art.","It bloomed in the air between them, an Inscription, intricate beyond intricate, a vast and terrible methodology of interlocking weavings that turned slowly in the snow, and Noah looked at it and saw the whole shape of it at once, the reaching, the rejecting, the sieve held against the ocean, the discipline that pulled a single sliver of Immensity across all of existence and time and let nothng else through.","It was the hardest thing he had ever been shown. It was also, he saw in the same breath, beautiful. Why was it so beautiful?","Moriarty extended it toward him, and Noah reached out, and accepted it.","| You are viewing the weavings and understanding of THE NARRATIVE IMMENSE INSCRIPTION ART: IMMEGAGENESIS.|","...!","Understanding the thing before him was not easy. But Noah was a dreamer, and dreaming was how he understood anything.","Profundity and reverie moved through his mind as he turned over everything the octopus had said, the idea of reaching out across every kind of existence to gather slivers of a thing he could not even have perceived an hour ago. He was a Provenance Lifeform. He generated everything he held, made it himself, and now his Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin generated his Provenance and his growth from within without asking anything of anyone!","But if a being wanted that growth faster, it seemed, it could reach outside itself and pull.","And when he came to the methodology of the Art, he found the shape of it familiar, and almost smiled.","It was an inscription.","It felt like the engineering Atlas had been drilling into him this whole time, and yes, it was intricate, layered with countless seams of Dimensionality turning inside it, a structure grander than anything Atlas had shown him. So what?!","He had carved inscriptions before. His body flickered, and infinite illusory pages flowed off him and into the floating Inscription of IMMEGAGENESIS, reading it, tracing it, learning it, and then his existence did what his existence did best.","It copied.","Beside the Art Moriarty had conjured, a second one began to form. Noah recreated its entire structure from nothing, layer by layer, every seam and layer and turning of Dimensionality, an identical Inscription blooming in the drifting snow beside the original. Then he waved his hand, and the new one flowed to him, and he closed his fingers around it, and his existence shone with resplendence as he took it.","He could feel Moriarty watching him.","The octopus looked at him intently, the small neat spectacles catching the light.","But Noah revealed nothing of himself. He simply sat down in the snow, and turned his attention inward, because his mind was full now, full of the way to spread himself across existence, which was all this Art really was.","IMMEGAGENESIS took the state he had reached in his transformation and sharpened it into a technique. He had learned, becoming what he now was, that existence was a set of boxes he could occupy at once, in different places, in different times, all together.","The Art took that raw ability and made it a craft. It let an existence stretch itself across those boxes on purpose, into layer after layer of reality, and perceive all the boundless information flowing through each one, the slivers of Immensity hidden in the roar of everything, and then reach out and pull them home.","It was, he thought, like a man learning to read a whole library at once. Not one book at a time, page by page, but every book in every room, open and legible in the same instant, and the trick of it was to find the single true sentence you needed in all those millions of pages and lift it out without carrying away the rest.","And to implement it, he was simply writing another inscription into his existence. But this one needed no Gu, no elements, none of the materials Atlas had taught.","This inscription asked only that its methodology be paired with a Root of Immensity, and then it would begin to cycle through the whole of an existence, reaching out for the boundless weavings of information across the deep.","So Noah reached out.","And.","HUUM!","His head rose, and from his eyes there erupted beams of golden-blue light, because the density of it nearly overwhelmed him. The information came flooding in the instant he opened, a booming roar of everything at once, more than any mind was built to hold, crashing into him from every layer and box of existence he had streched himself across!","His existence buzzed with the pressure of it, and he spoke to himself!","\" My weavings are grand ,\" he said. \" No amount of information can overwhelm me. This is the first time I have met this Art. But I have always met this Art. I have always cast my weavings across the bounds of information and existence. I am proficient in this, because I have always been proficient in this. I am. I am. I AM!\"","BOOM!","His existence stabilized.","And as it steadied, invisible threads erupted all around him and became visible, endless fine strings of light unspooling out of his seated figure and stretching away in every direction, across layer after layer of Dimensionality, out into box after box of existence.","Every thread was information. Every string a line cast into a different room of the boundless library, drinking what flowed there.","And at the very core of his existence, at his Root, he felt what all that information carried.","Cold.","It carried a tremendous, terrible cold. Frost crawled across his existence as the threads drew their harvest home, and beside him Moriarty stirred.","\" Take it slow ,\" the octopus said, and there was caution in it now. \" Many have to be careful, and The Long Night has made this far worse than it ever was. You could do irreparable harm to your existence. You could freeze your very Root. Take it slow.\"","He was told to take it slow.","Noah did not take it slow .","As his senses spread through the boundless weavings, he cut apart and ignored the lifeforms that pressed on him like a storm, the churning weight of it filling this Domain and every Domain around it. It might have been information about others who had just formed their Roots in the Legacy. It might have been the weavings of full Immense Ones.","He did not care about any of it. He wanted the slivers of Immensity, the hidden ones, the fine loose fragments of the thing his Root was trying to become.","He was demanding with his own stretched existence, which felt now as though it spread out without end. Show yourself to me. Expose yourself. Open wide!","His existence buzzed as he screamed it inwardly, bellowed it into the roar of all that information.","And yet.","He could not sense a single thing that named itself Immensity. Not one sliver. Not one loose fragment of the thing he had reached across all of existence to find.","He frowned, and outwardly his seated figure fluttered with the endless light of illusory pages and the narratives of an infinite dream, and he said it aloud.","\"I cannot sense any slivers of Immensity.\"","...!","The words snapped Moriarty’s eyes wide, and a sudden somberness moved into them.","\" Nothing? \" the octopus said. \" Some small ones should be drifting even through this Domain. Your existence should have stretched itself far already, farther than most ever manage on a first attempt. And you... sense nothing at all?\"","...!","Noah spread his senses out again, further, harder, into every box and layer he could reach.","And he felt only the endless blue-white wave of the cold.","Frost gathered thicker on his body as he reached, and he found The Long Night and nothing else. He visualized his endless strings of information, every one of them, all those fine lines cast across existence, and every single one carried the same thing back to him. Layers of snow. Layers of cold.","He looked down the length of all those countless threads, and where there should have been the whole churning wealth of existence, there was only winter, drifting down every line at once.","Nothing else.","\" Was I...mistaken?\" Moriarty said quietly beside him, in a deep and troubled voice.","Was he mistaken. Mistaken on what?","Noah did not ask. He did not care what the octopus meant. He reframed his focus and looked instead at the only thing he could sense at all.","The Long Night. The flakes of snow.","The cold.","It was so pervasive that it buried everything else, drowned out every other current of information, made it almost impossible to gaze at anything but itself. And Noah, sitting frozen in the falling snow with the whole of existence stretched out through him and nothing but winter coming back, turned the strangeness of that over, and asked himself the question underneath it.","What was this thing, that even Immense Ones felt it? That even Poona, who made two titans stand still with a smile, had to weave herself a coat of Immensity against it? What could reach past all of that?","And the thought came to him.","When it came to a thing that was truly immense, truly grand, then this cold, these endless particles of snow, were more immense than anything else in existence, right?","His existence went still.","What?","The cold that affected even Immense Ones was something more immense than them?","It was only a thought. He had only thought it. But the instant he thought it, he could not stop thinking it, could not unthink it, as he sensed the weavings of THE Long Night pouring down every thread and through every layer around him.","THUMP!","He felt the beat of his own heart, and a ridiculous, terrifying idea bloomed in him.","And a flicker of fear bloomed with it, because for all he had become, he was still human, and the idea was ridiculous!","But he felt possessed by his own intuition, the same intuiton that had never once led him wrong, and it did not care about the fear, and it opened his mouth for him.","\" Come ...\" Noah said. \" Come...COME!\"","BOOM!","His existence opened itself.","His Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin opened wide, the infinite Root of him unfolding, and instead of reaching for the slivers of Immensity that would not show themselves, Noah reached for the only thing that would.","He pulled on the terrible cold. He pulled on the snow. He pulled on the Long Night itself, and dragged it toward his existence!","...!","And Moriarty, beside him, saw a thing that stopped even his ancient mind.","The snow moved.","All of it, at once, across the whole of the Domain, every falling flake and every drift of the descending cold turned as though a tide had been called, and it surged toward Noah’s small seated figure like an endless sea rushing to a single point, countless waves of white pouring in from every direction toward the one being in all of existence mad enough, or lost enough, or grand enough, to open his arms and call the winter home!"]},{"number":5770,"title":"Chapter 5770: Chapter 5769: Pain! I","paragraphs":["Pain was one of the most important things an existence could feel.","Most of the time, pain was a message. It was the plain, screaming report that something harmful to your existence was happening right now, and that you needed to act, to pull away, to run, to make it stop.","When a person put their hand over a fire and it burned, the pain was not nonsense. The pain was information. It was existence saying urgently, get your hand away from the fire, you dumb fuck.","And most of the time, people listened to their pain!","Most of the time, they should. A great deal of survival is nothng more than the wisdom to obey the thing that hurts.","But not always.","—","Noah was in a tremendous amount of pain.","The cold of THE Long Night was inside him now, and the freezing of it was not like heat’s burn. It was slow. It was a stilling. He felt every quark of his existence beginning to drag, to thicken, to lose the quick bright motion that made it alive, as though the whole churning engine of him were being packed in slower and slower ice!","His Provenance slowed. His Infinity slowed. The endless illusory pages that flickered off him came slower, and then slower, and his existence, the whole vast grand thing he had just become, was being brought grinding toward a halt.","Every existence, when The Long Night descended, had turned its authority and power to one task, which was to hold the cold OUT. To wall it off. To spend everything it had keeping the winter from reaching the core of it.","Noah had done the opposite. Noah had reached out and pulled the winter INTO the very Root of his Immensity!","And the pain of that was beyond bearing. He felt his Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin, the always-turning heart of what he was, go translucent, whitening, taking on the pale blue of deep ice. And from the Root the change spread outward, up through his weavings, out along his frozen threads, into his body, until Noah sat in the drifting snow of the Domain and became, in every visible way, a statue of ice.","...!","Moriarty stared at him with utter incredulity.","And in the next moment a verdant eye bloomed into the air, its own Immensity roiling off it, and it looked at the rivers of snow still pouring endlessly into the frozen figure, and it blinked.","\" Are you fucking serious? \" it said. \" This was our piece. This was one of the three, maybe, and you let him turn himself into a block of-\"","\" Wait .\" Moriarty’s deep voice rolled out across the hall.","\" Wait? Wait for WHAT? \" The verdant eye flared. \" How did you let a potentially key figure turn himself into a popsicle in front of you? Why would such an idiotic chain of events be permitted to happen? I cannot fathom what possessed you to sit there and watch while he-\"","\" Wait ,\" Moriarty said again, and he did not look away from Noah’s frozen figure, not for an instant!","His small neat spectacles were fixed on the statue of ice as though he could read something in it the eye could not. \" Wait.\"","But wait for what?","The rivers of the Long Night went on pouring into the frozen thing, into a body that held no life now, no aura, no breath, no sense of anything living at all. By every measure the eye and the octopus both possessed, Noah Osmont had ceased. He had frozen solid at the core, and a Root frozen solid did not thaw!","They watched. And the winter poured in. And the ice held still.","—","Inside the pain, inside the profound stilling cold, Noah felt one thing that would not stop.","It pulsed. At the very Root of his existence, beneath the freezing and the slowing and the grinding halt of everything else, his Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin kept beating, and each beat carried a small terrible warmth. It was full of him!","Full of his boundless Infinity, his self-made Provenance, everything he had built himself into from nothing. And where the cold pressed in on his thoughts and his weavings and whispered to all of it to cease, to stop, to end, the pulse at his Root answered.","No.","The cold said cease. The pulse said no!","The cold said stop. The pulse said no!","Again, and again, and again, a heart that had generated itself from nothing refusing, with each beat, to be told it could not go on.","Until.","\" AHH!\"","Noah’s existence drew breath, as though it had a breath to draw, as though it had ever needed to breathe at all. Blue and white poured off him and through him, and slowly, gradually, his existence began to acclimate to the thing it had swallowed, and a prompt bloomed before his frozen eyes.","| By standard convention, your existence has ceased to function.|","|Your existence has arrived at ??????|","His existence had ceased. Hah!","He would never agree to such words. Cease was a thing that happened to lesser existences. He had died and returned already, more than once, and he was not about to accept the verdict of a convention that had never met a being like him. His existence had not ceased.","But the other line was true. His existence had arrived somewhere. And exactly where, the prompt would not say.","The thought had barely formed when everything around him became clear, and what he saw was enough to make even Noah go still.","He was somewhere no living gaze had ever fallen!","It was....","Oh!","It was a place of cold beyond cold, a frozen domain stretching out further than sight, and everything in it was ice, or frost, or the deep blue stillness of things frozen forever.","The ground was rimed. The air itself hung heavy with drifting crystals.","And across the whole of that endless frozen expanse ran rivers and seas of white and blue, slow shining currents of pure cold winding away to horizons Noah could not find the end of, a whole existence built out of the substanse of the Long Night.","And seated upon those rivers were...the dead!","Not dead, quite. Worse than dead. Countless lifeforms, of every race and shape and size Noah had ever seen and a great many he had not, sat cross-legged upon the frozen currents, meditating, still as the ice around them.","Thousands of them. Tens of thousands, and more beyond that, seated in silent ranks across the frozen seas as far as he could perceive. And every one of them had eyes that were blank. No cognizance. No life. No spark of any awareness behind them at all, just open blank eyes staring at nothing while a swirling pillar of pure cold rose around each seated figure, wrapping them, feeding them, holding them in whatever frozen trance had taken them.","They sat. All of them sat.","Only Noah had risen!","He stood among the endless seated ranks, the one figure in all that frozen underworld who was upright, who had opened his eyes to cognizance instead of losing it, who looked around at the drifting crystals and the shining rivers of cold with alarm sharp in his gaze.","He turned, searching, taking in the impossible scale of the place.","And in the far distance, he saw a figure he knew.","It stood raised above the seated ranks, illusory and vast, and around it rose the single largest pillar of light in all that frozen expanse, a column of cold so immense it dwarfed every other. Its hands were lifted high. Its eyes, like all the rest, were blank, empty of any life or knowing. And from its raised palms poured endless rivers of the cold, feeding out into the frozen seas, feeding the whole terrible place.","Noah knew that figure. He had watched it die. It was The Overseeing One, the Immense One Vakochev had torn apart on the sundered Train, sitting here in this frozen underworld with blank eyes and lifted hands, pouring out the winter itself!","...!","Noah felt the chill sink deeper and deeper into his existence, and alongside it, threaded all through the horror of it, came understanding, and wonder.","Because even now, even standing in this frozen place of blank-eyed meditators and a dead Immense One pouring out the cold, his existence had not stopped doing the thing it had begun. It went on drinking!","The winter kept flowing toward his Root, and around his own risen figure a pillar of cold swirled and rose, exactly like the thousands around the seated dead, and he absorbed it.","A pillar of cold for every seated thing.","Thousands of them, blank and lifeless and still.","And only Noah had risen."]},{"number":5771,"title":"Chapter 5771: Chapter 5770: Pain! II","paragraphs":["The more his existence drank the particles he could not yet name, the more he understood.","He had no better word for them than the weavings of The Long Night, and so that was what he called them, and he drew them in, and with every one that sank into his Root a little more of the shape of the thing came clear to him!","He raised his hands, palms turned up, the same posture as the dead Immense One pouring the winter in the distance. But where light flowed out of that blank-eyed titan, something else flowed into Noah. Rivers of freezing white-blue brilliance ran down into his open palms, gathering there, pouring inward toward the Root that would not stop drinking.","Around him, the frozen underworld had become a storm.","He sat at the center of a swirling blue galaxy of snow, a slow turning vortex of white and blue drawn from every directon, pillars and rivers of the cold bending away from the seated dead and toward the one figure who had risen. It spiraled into him, all of it!","And Noah, half-frozen, his lips barely able to part, began to whisper, and as he whispered the storm answered, more and more of the freezing brilliance turning to feed him.","\" When heat leaves a room ,\" Noah said, \" nothing has been added. You have only removed the agitation. The air slows. The dust settles.\"","A pillar of white-blue bent toward him and poured in.","\" Many call this cold a catastrophe. An unprovoked curse. A sudden horror falling out of a broken sky. It is none of those things.\" His whisper carried, low and certain, through the frozen dark.","\" It is... the withdrawal of an unearned indulgence. It is the arrival of pain.\"","More rivers turned. More of the winter came to him!","\" Existence looked upon the work of entire ages, and it saw nothing worth preserving. It saw billions of lineages rotting inside the same borrowed frameworks. It saw the same scripted wars fought over and over, and not a single authentic new thing produced across ten thousand cycles. So it adjusted the temperature. It introduced a cold. A new...Cycle.\"","The storm tightened around him, and the brilliance poured down into his palms!","\" The cold is not malice. It is a boundary condition. It is existence dropping its floor to zero and asking every lifeform one non-negotiable question .\"","His frozen lips shaped the words slowly. \" Can you generate your own fire? Or were you only ever warming your hands over someone else’s funeral pyre? The high with no foundation turn to glass, because they were always made of glass. The weak endure, because they never had a blanket to lose in the first place.\"","He drew one long breath of the freezing air.","\" This... is not the end of things. It is the beginning of an existence filled with Immensity.\"","BOOM!","His words landed heavy and clear in the frozen dark, and the instant he finished them, something moved!","Off to the side, among the endless seated ranks of blank-eyed things, one of them turned its head.","Its gaze came around to Noah, and it was hollow, empty of any life or knowing, and yet it had turned, and it had turned toward him!","It had the body of a great lion, heavy and powerful, muscle wrapped in pale frost-rimed hide. And where a lion’s head should have sat, there was another head entirely, a thing that was not quite a lion and not quite a man and not quite any beast Noah could name, wrong in a way the eye slid off of.","Terrible coldness wreathed the whole of it, pouring off its frame in visible waves, and it rose from its seat on the frozen river and fixed its hollow gaze upon the one figure in all that underworld who had dared to rise.","Then it moved!","Noah barely saw it. One instant it was seated across the frozen expanse, the next its paw was smashing down toward his head, and he threw up a hand on pure instinct.","BOOM!","The impact was terrible!","It caught him and flung him up and back, tearing him off the frozen river, hurling him across the underworld until he smashed into a massive floating meteorite of glacial stone, a stellar mountain of ice hanging in the frozen dark, and the crash of him against it cracked the ice for miles.","And his eyes cleared!","The pain and the impact tore him out of his reverie, out of the half-frozen trance of drinking the winter, and Noah’s whole existence buzzed suddenly with frost and Provenance both.","He pushed himself up off the shattered glacial stone and looked across the dark at the thing that had struck him.","It spoke. Its voice was heavy, and it carried no cognizance at all!","\" What could you possibly know about beginnings ?\" it said. \" About the cold? What do you know of pain? In existence, there is only pain. There has only ever been pain. You understand nothing of this cold, and nothing of that pain. Disappear.\"","...!","The thing rose to its full height, and then it came at him, and it came terrifyingly fast!","It did not strike the way a beast strikes, or the way a human strikes. As it moved, the air in front of it changed. A figure took shape there, a solid three-dimensional thing hanging in the frozen dark, edges hard and bright, a simple pointed solid of only a few faces, and it glowed a deep yellow.","The instant it finished forming, everything inside its bounds pulled, wrenched toward its center with a violence that would have bent his whole existence like a crumpled piece of paper!","His Provenance surged as an endless sea of Dreams erupted around him!","He dodged, and frost sheeted off him with the motion, and another figure was already taking shape.","This one was larger and more complex, a many-faced solid glowing violet, and where the yellow one had pulled, this one shoved. The space inside it detonated outward in a wave of repelling force, and Noah felt like it could throw him countless Gigaparsecs away and even push his Quarks apart!","The push caught his shoulder and flung him spinning through the frozen dark, and he caught himself on nothing but the sheer weight of his own Provenance, immense frost pouring off his existence as he did.","The yellow and the violet shapes formed in front of this lifeform carried invisible waves of authority and frost as they came at him again, pull and push, one after another, faster now, and Noah set his own existence against them!","Rivers of dream poured off him, and rivers of Infinity, all of it laced through with the frost he had drunk into his Root, surging up around his figure in a churning storm of white-blue brilliance. And into that storm he spoke, dragging the words up out of his frozen chest, the oldest and truest thing he had, the Letters of his own Tongue.","\"I AM .\"","WAA!","The pulling shape closed on him, and his Provenance met it, and the frost-laced rivers of his dream held the pull at bay.","\"I AM !\"","The pushing shape detonated against him, and he did not fly this time. He stood, existence buzzing, frost and dream and Infinity roaring around him, and he bellowed it again into the teeth of the thing that had come to unmake him.","\"I AM! I AM! I AM!\"","Each repetition landed like a hammer on an anvil, his own existence asserting itself against a reality that the beast was trying to reshape, refusing the pull, refusing the push, refusing to be moved or unmade or told what he was!","The frozen underworld shook with it. Glacial waves erupted where his rivers met the beast’s figures, whole sheets of ice thrown up from the frozen ground and detonating in the dark!","And all around them the seated ranks sat blank and undisturbed through the violence, thousands of hollow eyes staring at nothing while the one risen thing and the one that had come to put it down tore the frozen dark apart between them!"]},{"number":5772,"title":"Chapter 5772: Chapter 5771: Pain! III","paragraphs":["Noah had let it go on long enough.","His eyes opened wide, and from them poured beams of incandescent light, cutting through the frozen dark as he spoke a single word!","\" Enough!\"","WAA!","And he imposed THE MORTAL COIL.","The Word settled over the two shapes the lifeform had just rendered, the yellow that pulled and the violet that pushed, and it did to them what it did to all borrowed things. It named their authority as a mortal, ending thing, and the authority answered. The shapes dimmed. Their edges softened!","The terrible force bound inside them dropped by half in an instant, the pull weakening, the push guttering, and Noah reached out and closed his hand and crushed both of them as they burst into nothing.","Then he brought his hand down!","It fell like a hammer! The whole weight of his Provenance came down with it, more than five hundred, an existence that had generated itself from nothing and refused to be told what it was, and it smashed into the frost-wreathed beast with a force the frozen thing could not hold.","BOOM!","The lifeform exploded!","It came apart all at once, its lion’s body and its wrong unnameable head and the terrible cold that had wreathed it shattering outward into countless drifting pieces. And then the pieces turned.","They did not scatter and fade. Every shard of the shattered beast, every wisp of its frost and every fragment of its weavings, turned in the frozen air and streamed toward Noah, drawn to him like the winter itself was drawn to him, pouring into his existence and his Root.","And with them came the pain!","Noah’s whole existence seized as the fragments sank into him. They came full of a suffering so vast and so old that it rolled through him in waves and nearly took him to his knees. It was not his pain!","It was the Yali’s, and it was worse than any wound, a deep and grinding agony threaded through with every dark thing an existence could feel, terror and despair and a bottomless, exhausted hopelessness, the emotional sediment of a thing that had been made to hurt for so long it had forgoten there was anything else.","It poured into him with the frost and the knowledge, and for a moment Noah, who did not show pain had to fight simply to keep standing under the weight of a stranger’s misery.","And prompts bloomed across his sight.","| You have collapsed the weavings of a YALI NIGHT LIFEFORM.|","|You have absorbed wisps of its knowledge of THE LONG NIGHT.|","|You have experienced the pain of a lifeform that was among thousands experimented upon for millions of years by an unknown existence, across a small region of existence.|","|What you feel is merely a sliver of that pain.|","A sliver.","Everything crashing through him now, the terror and the despair...all of it was a fraction, a single drop wrung from an ocean.","| You are perceiving a system of existence: THE RENDERING.|","|A wielder conjures a closed figure, a Shape, and everything inside its bounds is manipulated. The COLOR of the Shape decides what it does. The COMPLEXITY of the Shape decides how strong it is. A simple figure of few faces is weak. An intricate figure of many faces is devastating.|","|The YALI wields the Rendering through NEGATIVE PROVENANCE PSEUDO-IMMENSITY. It generates nothing of its own. It renders using the borrowed, hollowed authority of the Long Night that pours through it, an imitaton of true Immensity, a power that mimics the real thing without the living Root beneath it.|","|THE YELLOW SHAPE: a figure of Pull. Everything within its bounds is drawn toward its center. At the strength this Yali rendered it, it could crush an existence inward with a force a trillion collapsing Dimensions could only dream of.|","|THE VIOLET SHAPE: a figure of Push. Everything within its bounds is thrust outward. At the strength this Yali rendered it, it could push an existence apart until its very quarks split and disintegrated.|","...!","Noah stood among the falling snow with the last of the Yali flowing into him, the pain slowly ebbing as his existence swallowed it.","He understood now what had nearly killed him. Not a beast as much as...a victim. A hollowed, tortured thing rendering shapes of pull and push out of borrowed cold, wielding a power that pulled hard enough to crush trillions of dimensions and pushed hard enough to scatter his atoms!","And then, above him at this time, the wasteland stirred.","Noah lifted his incandescent gaze, and from the endless ranks of blank-eyed seated things, ten of them rose at once!","Every one of them emanated waves of light grander than the thing he had just dissipated, deeper, stronger, further along whatever terrible road had made them.","Ten hollow figures, rising from the frozen rivers, ten pillars of cold swelling around them, and all ten turned their empty gazes up toward the one risen thing in all that frozen dark.","They spoke, at the same instant, in one flat cognizance-less voice that carried no anger and no life at all.","\" You do not understand anything about pain.\"","...!","Then they turned into streaks of light and surged toward him!","And Noah continued to drink the rivers of the Long Night as he watched on coldly!","The ten came at him as streaks of light, and Noah met them the way he had learned to meet everything.","He took what had tried to kill him and made it his!","He had watched the Yali render its shapes of pull and push, and then learned all about it when he devoured its weavings.","The methodology seemed...lethal!","So!","As the first streak resolved into a hollow-eyed thing lunging for his throat, Noah raised a hand and his Provenance answered, and a shape bloomed in the frozen air before him. His own. A figure of pull, yellow-bright, rendered not out of borrowed cold but out of his own boundless self-made authority.","He caught the lunging thing inside it!","The shape pulled, and it did not pull cleanly. Noah made it worse than that. He tightened the figure as it drew the hollow lifeform in, wrenching the body toward a center that kept shrinking, and the thing came apart inside the pull the way meat comes apart in a grinder, crushed and wrung and torn all at once!","Its existence shattered, and streamed toward him, and poured in!","And the pain came with it!","He saw it die. Not this death, the true one, the old one. He saw a creature of scaled hide and too many eyes, a thing that had once been proud, held down while an Immense One peeled the authorty out of it strip by strip, made it into a hollow engine for the cold, and left it seated in the dark for an age with just enough awareness to know what it had lost. The memory sank into Noah with the frost!","The second came, and the third.","He rendered a shape of push for them, violet and hard, and when they surged toward him he detonated it and smashed them away, hurling the hollow things back across the frozen underworld, buying the half-second he needed!","When a hollow lifeform came close, too close, thinking to grapple him, Noah conjured a shape of push directly against its body, an inch from its frame, and let it fire. The thing did not fly away. It could not!","The push had nowhere to send it but apart, and its whole existence was pulled in every direction at once, torn into streams of light that flowed, all of them, into him.","They fought him, and they wept as they fought.","Every one of the hollow things looked at him with the same accusatory gaze, empty of cognizance and full of something worse than cognizance, and from the blank eyes of several of them ran tears, bloody tears sliding down frost-rimed faces while they threw their borrowed shapes at him and died on his own.","They did not know why they hated him. There was not enough left in them to know anything. But something below knowing had turned its grief on him, and it said, over and over, in the flat chorus of the dying, the same thing.","You do not understand pain.","The fourth died, and the fifth, and Noah absorbed each one, and each one gave him a death. A city of them, frozen. A lineage, harvested. A mother-thing that had been made to watch. He took it all in, every unjust ending, every strip of authority torn from a living thing by an Immense One’s patient hands, and his existence buzzed and swelled and grieved with the inflow of it, and still he did not stop!","He was ruthless. He had to be. He rendered pull and crush, push and scatter, moving through the ten hollow things with cold efficency.","The sixth he crushed into a pulling shape until it was a point. The seventh he pushed apart at the seams. The eighth and the ninth came together, and he caught them both in a single yellow figure and drew them into each other until there was nothing left to draw!","And then there was one.","The tenth rose before him, and it was a woman.","She had white hair, long and drifting in the frozen air, and her existence was already crumpling, already coming apart under the weight of everything Noah had done to her kind and the weight of whatever had been done to her long before.","Bloody tears ran from her hollow eyes. She did not render a shape. She did not lunge. She only looked at him as her existence failed, and she spoke, and unlike the others, her voice was not entirely flat.","Something had surfaced in her at the very end, some last drowned ember of the self she had been before an Immense One hollowed her out.","\" Do you,\" she said, \" understand our pain?\"","Noah stood still.","\" Why did you never do anything about our pain?\" Her existence guttered, streaming apart into motes of white light that drifted toward him even as she spoke. \" Will you do anything now, now that you take all that we have left?\"","...!","And then she was gone, dissolving into light, and her existence flowed into Noah like all the others, and her pain flowed with it.","Hers was clear. The others had been hollowed past memory, their agony a formless roar. But something in the woman had held onto herself to the very end, and so what poured into Noah was not just pain but a life.","He felt her taken. He felt the Immense One’s hands.","His existence buzzed and shook with the memory of it, and the prompts bloomed through the grief.","| You have collapsed the weavings of ten YALI NIGHT LIFEFORMS.|","|You have absorbed their pain, their memories, and the manner of their unjust deaths. Each was hollowed by an unknown Immense One and made an engine of THE LONG NIGHT eventually. |","|What you carry now is no longer a sliver.|","And with the last of the white-haired woman came understanding of a shape he had not seen before.","| THE RENDERING: a third Shape analyzed and absorbed.|","|THE GREEN SHAPE: a figure of Grow. Everything within its bounds is made to expand. At the strength these lifeforms render it, it can force an existence to grow beyond what it can hold, swelling its weavings past their own bounds until the existence bursts apart from the inside.|","|You now perceive three of multiple Shapes: Pull, Push, Grow.|","Noah stood alone in the frozen dark, ten deaths heavier, an entire chorus of stolen lives buzzing and grieving inside a Root that would not stop drinking the winter, and the woman’s last words would not leave him.","Will you do anything now, now that you take all that we have left?"]},{"number":5773,"title":"Chapter 5773: Chapter 5772: Condition!","paragraphs":["Noah breathed heavily, and his existence drank on!","More and more of the rivers poured into him, and he had a word for them now, or nearly one. Negative Immensity.","That was what these endless currents of snow carried, slivers of it, the power the hollow Night Lifeforms had wielded against him, the thing that let them render their shapes and bend reality so terribly inside their bounds.","It was Immensity turned inside out, hollowed and cold, and it was flowing into his Root without pause.","His existence buzzed with the possibilities of it. One had risen first. He had taken it, and ten had risen. He had taken them, and now the question remained. How many more were about to rise?","His Root did not feel finished drinking. Not yet. He could feel it, still reaching, still swallowing the winter, still not done becoming whatever it was becoming. He looked down, past his own feet, across the endless frozen underworld to the seated ranks below.","\" Motherfucker.. .\"","He could not help the curse.","Because down below, the largest pillar of all had begun to move. The hollow figure of the dead Immense One, the one who had sat with his palms raised and the rivers of the winter pouring endlessly out of them, was rising from his seat! His blank eyes, empty of all life, lifted from the frozen river and came around, up, across the whole vast dark, and settled directly on Noah.","Noah looked back at it. He had only wanted to keep drinking. That was all. But nothing was ever made simple, and it never would be!","He shook his head, and his voice boomed out across the frozen dark.","\" Now this is just ridiculously unfair. I could face the other ones. But you, getting up right now? There is not even a need to fight.\"","Yes.","He could feel the pressure of the thing, and it was not a pressure he could stand against. This was the Immense One whose corpse, out in external existence, had given rise to a record of Lucy herself. Whatever stood here in the frozen dark was beyond him. There was no version of this fight that Noah won!","The massive figure of the Overseeing One rose into the air, blank-eyed and vast, and it spoke..","\" Existence... is rarely fair, \" it said.","\" Immense Ones have stood before lesser lifeforms who had no power, who could do nothing to defend themselves, and they have done to them whatever they wished. Others across existence have done whatever they wished and ended countless lives. That was unfair. It happened anyway. Across existence, countless unfair things occur every single minute. \" The hollow gaze held him. \" So why can existence not be unfair to you?\"","HUUM!","Why could existence not be unfair to him.","The words were heavy and suffocating!","The massive figure rose higher, and seas of coldness surged up around it and began to turn, rotating slowly around the risen titan like stellar galaxies of pure winter, vast wheels of white and blue circling a dead thing that could unmake him with a thought.","Noah looked on coldly, and he thought.","He turned over every possibility he had, every move, every art, every scrap of what he had become, and the honest answer was that there was not much. Not against this. But the dead thing had not struck him. It had risen, and it had spoken, and it had not struck, and that meant something.","A thing that meant to kill him would have killed him. This one wanted something else, and where there was a want, there was a door.","So Noah thought about everything he had learned, every sliver of knowledge he had drunk from the endless cold, and he found the shape of a question, and he asked it grandly.","\" Existence can always be unfair to me ,\" Noah said. \"I will take it as it comes. But this is not simply unfairness, is it? I have understood something, drinking all of this. This endless cold of the Long Night is a natural selection, laid across everything in existence. It is the arrival of pain and accountability. \"","His incandescent eyes did not waver. \" So why. Why do you try to stop me from taking it?\"","...!","He had to ask, because he could feel his Root transforming, feel it nearly there, nearly done with whatever it was making of him. Nearly. But not quite!","The hollow Night Lifeform drifted until it came level with him, blank eyes to incandescent ones, and it answered.","\" This power is intended to apply pressure across a slovenly and corpulent existence, \" it said, \" and to rectify many wrongs. You cannot take it unless you agree to do what it intends. Kill the viruses plaguing existence, and allow existence to thrive. That is the condition of THE LONG NIGHT.\"","...!","A condition.","To take this power, he had to agree to a condition!","To kill what plagued existence, and let existence thrive. Noah held that, and a piece of a much larger puzzle turned over in his mind, because now he understood, or thought he did, why Lucy had risen from the Overseeing One’s corpse out in external existence and planted a dense forest of frozen worlds across the ruin. The cold did not only kill. It cleared ground. It killed the rot and made room for new things to grow.","Noah thought about it for only a moment.","\" Existence is vast, and it is full of terrors ,\" he said. \" I can accept a condition to cleanse existence.\"","WAA!","And the moment the words left him, the underworld answered.","All across the endless frozen expanse, every seated figure that stretched away past the limits of sight, countless blank-eyed hollow things, raised their heads at once. Every hollow gaze turned upward and found Noah, all of them, in the same instant, and every one of them spoke together, in a single flat voice that rolled across the frozen dark like a tide.","| So it shall be.|","...!","HUUM!","The hollow Immense One clenched its fist.","And in the next moment, the frozen wasteland rose to answer the pact!","Existential Conduits erupted from all around, from the frozen rivers and the glacial stone and the drifting dark, great pillars of them filled with white-blue frost, and they came swirlng up around Noah’s figure, encircling him, wheeling slowly like the galaxies of cold that turned around the dead titan!","And from those Conduits, tendrils lashed out. Potent, pure, brilliant white-blue, they whipped through the frozen air and fastened onto him, one driving into his chest, others onto his arms, his legs, his limbs, fixing him in the center of the swirling pillars.","And through those tendrils, the purest slivers of Negative Immensity he had yet touched began to pour into his existence.","The pain was ten times worse!","It was beyond the Yali’s, beyond the ten, beyond anything he had swallowed so far, a flood of pure hollowed cold driven straight into the core of him, and Noah’s whole existence seized under it.","But his Root did not falter!","For the first time since he had reached out and pulled the winter into himself, his Root stopped feeling as though it might cease. It stabilized. In the middle of the worst pain he had ever known, the always-turning heart of him steadied, took hold, and began, once again, to pulse. And with each pulse it transformed his existence, the way it had transformed him once before in the dark.","Gradually, the excruciating agony began to plateau. And then, past the plateau, it changed. The burning of the cold cooled into something else, a deep and steady coolness that was not pain at all, spreading through him from the Root outward.","His Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin grew heavy, and vast, and grand!","And it accepted The Long Night, fully, wholeheartedly, drawing the endless winter into itself and making it, at last, a part of what he was!"]},{"number":5774,"title":"Chapter 5774: Chapter 5773: Target!","paragraphs":["<Existential Interlude- Commitment>","In one of the earliest ages, when existence was still deciding what it would remember, there was an Immense One who made a promise.","She was called the Lamplighter, because in the dark of that age she had lit the first lights, and beings had gathered to them, and from those who gathered she had made a Provenance Lineage, a line of existences born of her own origin and carrying a spark of what she was. She loved them.","And when the first winter of that age came, and the hunting things came with it, she stood before her Lineage and she said: I will hold the dark back from you, all of it, for as long as one of you still breathes.","And existence heard her say it.","The winter was long. The Lamplighter held. She held for an age, and it cost a little of herself every night, spent against the dark so her Lineage could sleep. And then a night came when a greater thing than the winter stood before her and offered her a bargain: step aside for one night, only one, and be made whole, be given back everything the holding had taken.","One night. Her Lineage would never know.","The Lamplighter was tired past the reach of words. And she stepped aside.","For one night.","In the morning she stood again, whole and restored, and held the dark back as she always had, and she told herself no promise had been broken, because she had only rested, and the dark had only taken a little.","But existence had heard her say it. All of it, for as long as one of you still breathes .","And existence does not hear the words a being means. It hears the words a being says. She had said all of it. She had given one night. And a commitment, once made, is not a thing that bends to how tired you are.","Her Lineage began to fail. A spark went out here, a line of descent went dark there, and she could not find the cause, and she burned herself down to nothing searching for it, and never once understood that the cause was a night she had already forgotten. The last of her Lineage died with her name on its lips, and she died holding it, and existence, which had heard her promise, kept its own side to the very end.","A commitment is not a wish. It is a sentence you write into existence, and existence finishes the sentence whether or not you are still there to read it.","—","<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah did not know how long he had been gone.","He opened his eyes, and the light around him was dim, the Existential Conduits that had swirled up to bind him now hanging quiet and low, their white-blue frost dimmed to a soft glow. The tendrils had withdrawn. The pact was made. And his body, when he looked down at it, was glistening.","He was not the same shape!","A suit of Provenance wrapped him, a second skin of living light that clung to every line of his frame, pale white-blue and faintly luminous, fitted so close it moved as he moved, more a state of his existence than a garment.","Beneath it his body had changed. The muscle of him looked as though it had been cut from crystalline ice, clear and faceted and cold, and he understood without testing it that it was harder than any material he had come across in all of existence, a body that had drunk the winter and set!","His hair had gone white-blue, drifting in the still air. From his eyes rose a pillar of light, magisterial, cold, a column of radiance that lit the dim Conduits arond him. And on his chest, where his heart would have been, a mobius strip turned. It spun endlessly, a twisting band of light looping back into itself without beginning or end, turning like an engine, and Noah knew what it was! It was the reflection, worn on the outside now, of the Root that turned inside him without cease.","Prompts bloomed across his pillar-lit sight.","| Your Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin has devoured dense concentrations of Slivers of Negative Immensity.|","|It has transformed. It is now a DUAL CONCEPTUAL AND PHYSICAL EXISTENTIAL ROOT OF IMMENSITY.|","|It has grown. Its transformation is still ongoing.|","Dual!","Noah read the word twice. Every Root in existence chose a side, Conceptual or Physical, Empyros or Fiend, and Moriarty had walked him through the whole absolute divide of it, and his own Root had refused to answer. Now it had answered. Both!","It had drunk the winter and come out the other side as a thing the octopus had no box for, a Root born of an Infinity that was true in two directions at once, and now true in both!","| Elevated capabilities, current:|","|Your Root now adds 40 to 80 to all attributes daily, scaling as it grows.|","|You have grasped the initial weavings of the inherent Ruling of Existence of THE RENDERING, as it was preset within the Night Lifeforms.|","|You have developed immunity to the basal cold effect of THE LONG NIGHT. Only that effect, for now.|","|Your Provenance, and all weavings of your existence, now carry the undeniable chill of Negative Immensity. It can penetrate any form of authority.|","...!","The chill that had nearly ended him was his now, threaded through everything he was, and it did not respect authority, any authority, the way the Long Night itself did not respect the mighty. Whatever he touched with his Provenance from this moment carried the winter in it!","He looked at himself!","| THE True Human Emperor / THE Human Dreamer|","|VERITAS: 611|","|PROVENANCE: 624|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 606|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 618|","|Provenances: THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer (native, generated), THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign (claimed).|","|Infinity: DIALETHEIC INFINITY.|","|Existential Root: THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin. A Dual Conceptual and Physical Existential Root of Immensity. Transformation ongoing.|","Six hundred! He took all of it in calmly.","Then the snow came around him, drifting close, and he felt something he had not felt since the Long Night began.","A breeze!","The snow moved past his crystalline skin and it was only snow. Cool, soft, a breeze off a winter field. The cold that had crawled into his Root and frozen him solid touched him now and found nothing to freeze, and he stood in the falling white of the frozen underworld and felt, for the first time in a while...comfortable.","Then he blinked.","Because he sensed pages fluttering.","He looked ahead, and there was a woman.","She stood in the air before him where no one had stood a moment ago, and she wore a dress of frost, white and flowing, that moved around her as though it were made of falling snow that never landed.","She was tall, and she was still, and had dark hair drawn back from a pale sharp face, a mouth that had never needed to smile, eyes that held a coldness and an imperiousness beyond any measure Noah had for either. She looked like a thing that had been obeyed since before obedience had a name.","And her eyes held cognizance!","Every other thing in this underworld had stared at nothing out of blank hollow eyes. This one saw. She looked out over the frozen expanse with a mind behind her gaze, and down below her, all across the endless ranks, the hollow Night Lifeforms had gone back to sitting, settling onto the frozen rivers once more, storms of snow gathering and turning around each of them as the underworld resumed its long cold work.","She did not address him. She did not greet him, or name him, or acknowledge in any way that he had risen where thousands had not, or that he had made a pact with the Long Night that not one other thing in this place had ever made. She simply reached out, unhurried, and plucked one of the pages fluttering around her out of the air.","It looked like a sheet of ice. Thin, clear, faintly glowing.","She threw it toward him, and she spoke.","\" Your first target to cleanse ,\" she said. \" You have twenty-four hours.\"","...!","Noah caught the page.","It was cold in his hand, though the cold no longer meant anything to him, and on its surface an image had formed, an image set into the ice the way a face is set into a frozen pond.","A young man. He had the bearing of a young king, the poise of one born to a throne, handsome and compsed. But his eyes were wrong for his face. They were aged. Ancient. The eyes of a thing that had lived far longer than the young face that held them, looking out of that youth with a weight no youth should carry.","And Noah knew him!","He had met this being before. He had read and understood the unfortunate thing that had been done to him, a Vessel that had been targeted by THE Sealed One as what stood in that young king’s body was neither wholly itself nor wholly the thing that had tried to take it.","It was Adrastia!","The one who had the rather unfortunate case of being mixed with THE Sealed One!"]},{"number":5775,"title":"Chapter 5775: Chapter 5774: Nature Is Self Sustaining!","paragraphs":["Noah turned the page of ice over in his hand, and the image of the young king turned with it, and beneath the face, script formed in the frost.","It gave him a place. It was nowhere near the Cluster where he had last seen the young king. Adrastia had gone far. He had crossed out of the split train entirely and sealed himself inside an Elsedimension, a pocket of reality set apart from the ordinary flow of existence.","The script named it only by its shape, a small sealed Elsedimension hung off the edge of a dying Dimension, quiet and hidden and hard to find. Adrastia was there!","Noah read it twice, and then he looked up at the woman in the frost dress.","\" He did nothing wrong.\"","She did not answer. She stood in the air above the seated dead with her pages fluttering around her, and she waited like a person waits for a child to finish a sentence they have already decided is foolish.","\" I have met him ,\" Noah said . \"I have read him. Something came to swallow him whole and he did the one thing none of the others managed. He fought. He swallowed half of it back. What is standing in that broken Dimension is not THE Sealed One wearing a body. It is a being who was attacked, and refused to go quietly, and got left holding half of his attacker inside his own skin for his trouble.\"","He held the page up. \" That is not a virus. That is a wound.\"","\"A wound does not stop bleeding, \" the woman said, \" because it was unfairly given.\"","Her voice was calm!","\" The condition does not ask whether a thing chose to become what it is ,\" she went on. \"It asks only what the thing is. And what sits inside that Elsedimension is a piece of THE Sealed One, alive, connected, and growing. A half is still a half. Do you imagine the plague cares which of its carriers meant no harm?\"","\"I imagine the plague does not get to write its own justification, \" Noah said.","\" No. Existence writes it. You agreed to that a while ago. You have always agreed.\"","She plucked another page from the air, looked at it, let it go. \" You said the words. The dead below you heard them. Existence heard them. That was a commitment, and I would counsel you, as one who has kept a great many of them, to understand what you have promised before you begin arguing about which of the promised things you would prefer not to do.\"","Noah was quiet for a moment.","\" Can you be...a bit clearer on this target?\"","\"The target is not his death,\" she said.","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","\" You were told to cleanse. You assumed cleansing meant killing. What plagues existence inside that Elsedimension is the Assimilation Factor. The connection. The living thread that runs from the being called Adrastia back to THE Sealed One, and through which THE Sealed One still reaches, still grows, still uses him whether he knows it or not. That thread is the virus. The man is only the host.\"","\" So the goal ,\" Noah said slowly, \" is the thread.\"","\"The goal is to eliminate the Assimilation Factor’s connection to THE Sealed One. Entirely. There are two ways to do that.\"","She raised one pale finger. \" You may sever his life completely. A dead host carries no thread.\"","A second finger arose.","\" Or you may split him from THE Sealed One completely. Cut the thread and leave the host standing, whole, and his own. The condition does not care which. Existence does not care which. Both cleanse.\"","Her eyes held his. \" Only you care which. So choose, and be quick.\"","...!","Noah looked down at the page, at the young king with the ancient eyes. There was always a door!","The door opening now...he felt like he could do it. After all, he held the Provenance for it!","He looked back up at her.","\" Who...are you?\"","She regarded him for a long moment, and when she answered, her voice had changed!","\"I am a caretaker ,\" she said. \"I am a remnant of the cold. That is all of what I am, and it is enough.\"","The pages turned slowly around her.","\" When a Night comes, it gathers everything that sat down under it. Every existence that went hollow. Every pain that was inflicted and never answered for. Every wrong that was done in the warm ages and left to rot because no one was cold enough to correct it. The Night keeps all of it. It does not forget. And from all of that, from the boundless pain and the boundless retribution the ages leave behind, something is left over. A residue. A thing that stays when the winter passes, to tend what the winter made.\"","Her cold eyes did not blink. \" That is me. I am what is left of every Night that came before this one. I am a collection of pain that was never answered, and a collection of retribution that was never paid. I am not a lifeform. I was, once, the way you are now. I have set that down. I am the cold’s caretaker, and I hand out its pages, and that is all.\"","\"I am handing you this page. I have handed you the next page, and the one after. I am standing in the next Night, handing pages to whatever rises then. It is all the same act. Some experience it as a sequence because they are still young enough to stand inside time. I am not. I see the whole of the count at once, the way you see the whole of a page.\"","The faintest tilt of her head. \" You will finish with this target. And when you do, you will have your reward, before the next page. That also is already so.\"","Noah held the sheet of ice, and the ancient eyes of the young king looked up at him out of it.","\" Why not target THE Sealed One himself?\" Noah’s voice was level. \" If the thread runs back to him, cut the root. You hand me a page for the smallest vessel and leave the thing that made the vessel untouched.\"","For the first time, she looked at him the way a thing looks at something it finds faintly interesting.","\" You do not have the capability to fully destroy THE Sealed One ,\" she said.","\" No one standing where you stand does. He is protected by many dredges of existence. He is protected by unsavory legacies and things.\"","The snow fell between them.","\" So why would he be your target? Existence does not hand a Dreamer a page he cannot finish. It hands him the page he can. The smallest thread. That... is why the one with The Assimilation Factor is the target. Not because he matters most. Because he is where the knot has a loose end. Pull it. The rest unravels, in time, or it does not.\"","...!","Noah floated calmly.","She drifted upward into the falling snow, and the pages went with her, and Noah stood alone above the seated dead with a face made of ice in his hand and a clock he could not see already running.","He looked at the young king’s ancient eyes one last time as before him, snow gathered while The Caretaker looked around serenely and said lastly...","\" Nature inevitably restores balance. Nature is self-sustaining. What will be...will always be.\"","...!","---","<Epigraph- The Legend of The One Who Shone>","In the age before the age, when existence was crowded with the mighty and no one had yet learned to be afraid of being seen, there was a young thing who shone.","He was not entirely the strongest. In that age there were True Infinite Lifeforms whose Infinity had crossed all thresholds, and there were True Source Lifeforms rooted so deep in THE Primordial Source that nothing could unravel them, and there were Primeval Ones who had been old when the frameworks were laid, and there were Descendants of Those Who Remain who carried a sentence in their blood that no lesser thing could speak. The young thing was none of these. He was only bright.","But he was very bright.","He burned so brilliantly that when he stood among the True Infinite and the True Source and the Primeval and the Descendants, all of them ancient, all of them terrible, every eye slid off of them and setled on him.","The very Provenance of Quiet came to him first.","The Provenance of Quiet was old, older than the mighty, and Quiet had watched a great many bright things come and go. Quiet said to him, You are shining. Do you know what shining does? It does not make you strong. It makes you found. Let me sit on you a while, the way I sit on the deep places, and you may live a very long time and no one will ever come to see why.","The young thing laughed at Quiet. He said, I did not join the two fires so that I could hide in the dark like a thing that never joined them. What is the use of being the only lamp if no one sees it lit?","And Quiet, who did not argue, went away.","The Provenance of Brilliance came to him next, and Brilliance did not have to say anything, because Brilliance was already blooming in him, and he loved it, and he let it out.","He shone across Dimensions. He shone across the whole of the age. He shone so brightly that the light of him reached places that were not meant to be reached by anything that small.","And in one of those places, something that had not slept in a very long time opened its eyes.","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND sat in a height that the mighty of that age could not perceive. It had watched True Infinite Lifeforms rise and fall without stirring. It had watched Primeval Ones graze whole Dimensions without stirring. Nothing in that crowded age had ever been strange enough to make it move.","The lamp made it move.","It came down. It came down out of its height and it stood before the young thing who shone, and everything went very still and very quiet, the way Quiet had wanted the young thing to be, and had been refused.","And the Fiend looked at him and wondered...what makes this one different?","What the Fiend found in the young thing who shone was an anomaly, a thing that had never been in existence before and should not have been there then, and that whatever it was, the Fiend did not leave once it had seen it. That had been the starting point for many, many things.","Everything that came after came from that.","Everything .","Every lineage that was burned for standing near his road, and every road that was bent so that it would lead to him. The countless lives that were changed, and the far more countless lives that were ended, across ages the young thing had not yet lived when the Fiend first looked down at him. All of it, they say, hung on one thing.","Someone had shone too brilliantly. And something had come to see why.","The Provenance of Quiet still sits on the deep places as it knows a critical, undeniable lesson.","Sometimes, it is more than all right to be low key."]},{"number":5776,"title":"Chapter 5776: Chapter 5775: Assimilation! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Drifting back from the cold place was surprisingly easy.","Noah felt the visage of The Caretaker fade, her pages and her frost dress and her cognizant eyes dissolving out of his awareness the way a dream dissolves in the first breath of waking, and then there was only the pull of his own body, far away and frozen, calling him home.","CRACK!","He opened his eyes in the Domain where an Immense One in the shape of an octopus was looking at him.","BOOM!","The frost shattered around his figure. It burst outward in a ring, the ice that had sealed him shearing off in sheets and spining away into the drifting snow, and the rivers of cold that had been pouring into him without pause for however long he had been gone simply stopped.","They hung in the air, arrested, as though the winter had reached the end of what it had to give him and found the vessel already full. And yet he still looked like a block of ice. His body glistened crystalline and white-blue where the frost had fallen away, and when he lifted his hands, they were the hands of a thing carved out of dreaming ice, clear and cold and faintly luminous, and they moved.","Moriarty’s eyes went unfathomably bright behind the small neat spectacles.","\" You ,\" the octopus said, \" are not dead.\"","...!","He was not dead!","The words were ridiculous ones, and Noah felt exactly how ridiculous as he sat there in the falling snow and took stock of what had come back with him. His Provenance of THE Human Dreamer had passed six hundred, and it no longer sat quietly inside him the way it had at two hundred, or even at five.","Paired with its seat in his Unique Existential Root of Immensity, it felt like a blinding sun! The very idea of his Provenance swirled around him, a slow gravitational pull that he could feel affecting everything in reach, the snow, the light, the dim Conduits, the attention of the ancient thing watching him.","And he understood, sitting there, why.","Existence leaned toward what was self-made.","That was not a rule he had been taught. It was a thing he could feel now.","Everything borrowed in existence had to be held up by something else, propped and fueled and fed, and the moment the fuel ran out it fell. But a thing that had generated itself from nothing needed no prop, and so existence, which was tired of holding things up, leaned toward it the way water leans toward the lowest ground.","The grander he became, the harder existence leaned. He was no longer a thing that stood in existence. He was a thing existence had started to lean toward!","And now that he had harnessed The Long Night itself, all of it, his Provenance Essence and his Osmontian Tongue and every instrument he had ever used to reach his aims, had been sharpened with an extremely cold edge.","\" No ,\" Noah said, and his voice came out steady and a little strange, carrying frost in it. \"I am not dead. How could I be, when my Dream is only just getting started?\"","He let that sit a moment, and then he asked the thing he actually wanted to know, before anything else.","\" But I am curious about something. If I am to be outside, wandering across existence, not in here and not in my Existential Root Domain, just how long would it take before an Immense One could sense me and come for me?\"","The question was clearly not the one the octopus had expected. Moriarty had the look of a being with a great many questions of his own stacked up and waiting, and this one had cut in ahead of all of them.","But he answered anyway as his shining eyes rested on Noah.","\"A newly born Root is like a signal, \" Moriarty said. \" It broadcasts. Some of the greedy ones search for that signal automatically, the way a predator’s ear turns toward a sound before the predator has decided to listen. Once a fresh Root is out in external existence, it might take only a few minutes before something senses it and locks it down. If one of them is already in proximity, seconds. \"","\" You do not need to take that risk. So long as you remain here. And you really should remain here, because...\"","His tentacles stilled.","\" How is it that you survived taking in rivers of the cold of the Long Night?\"","...!","How?","Noah rose from where he had sat.","Ice fell from him as he stood, the last of the frost sloughing off his shoulders and his arms and scattering across the snow, and he clenched his hands, and the crystalline makeup of his body moved with it, slowly gaining more life, more warmth of motion.","\" My Dream would not allow me to die. My Root...it simply decided to dream bigger than the death the cold offered.\"","He rolled his shoulders once, and ice cracked and fell.","\" Ah. Anyway. Thank you for the Inscription. I need to acclimate to what has changed in me. Is there a mountain here, or an abode of some kind, that I can call my own while I do?\"","He asked it casually. He knew the Immense One before him wanted to ask a great many more questions than that. He was not feeling especially sharing.","Because even this one had secrets.","Noah had not been entirely gone, in his state of freezing death. Some part of him had still been here, and it had caught a few words of a conversation, spoken over his frozen body between Sir Moriarty and something else, something with a voice like a verdant weight.","The conversation had been about him. About what he was. And a being that discussed a frozen guest with an unseen third party, in words the guest was not meant to hear, was a being that was not revealing everything, however warm its spectacles.","So Noah looked at him calmly, and gave him nothing, and Moriarty looked back.","And then the terrifying lifeform smiled, brilliantly and he clapped his tentacles together.","HUUM.","A figure stepped into being beside the octopus.","It was humanoid, tall and lean. Its skin held the deep blue-green of a sea seen from beneath, and faint ridges ran along its temples and down the sides of its throat, closed now, like the memory of gills.","Its eyes were large and dark and wet-bright, and a fine webbing showed between the fingers of its hands. It was dressed, incongruously, in a black butler’s suit, immaculate and severe, and over the suit, Noah noticed, it wore a heavy fur-lined cloak pulled close, and beneath the cloak it was shivering. It bowed to Sir Moriarty with the ease of long practise.","\" This is a Legacy Keeper, \" Moriarty said. \" Someone who may be considered a servant of this Legacy. There are many like him. Verys.\" The Keeper straightened.","\" Take our young friend here to THE Glacial Elsedimension Mountain and get him settled. The cold does not seem to bother him. After you are settled, Poona or I may call for you soon enough.\"","...!","Noah looked at the being called Verys, who turned and bowed to him as well, and then waved one webbed hand. A rift tore open in the air before them, a clean seam of light, and the Keeper stepped aside and gestured toward it, politely, the way a good servant gestures a guest through a door.","Noah looked at him, and his sight opened the Keeper up without asking.","| VERYS, LEGACY KEEPER|","|VERITAS: 250. POTENTIA: 250. PONDUS: 250. PROVENANCE: 0.|","Two hundred and fifty across the board, and not a single point of Provenance!","Two hundred and fifty of strength, and it could not keep him warm.","Noah felt no contempt for the Keeper, who had bowed to him correctly and would open a door for him without complaint.","It was only the ground sloping, the way it sloped for everything. Existence leaned toward what was made. It did not lean toward what was given, however much was given.","He nodded once to Sir Moriarty.","Then he stepped through the rift.","And at the same time, as his crystalline body passed into the seam of light, he did another thing.","He began extending his existence outward.","It was slightly dangerous. He knew exactly how dangerous, because the octopus had just told him, minutes, seconds if something was close. But his Provenance was a grand one, grand enough that it had very nearly hidden from the eyes of Immense Ones even before he formed his Root, and he sent it out now, carefully, quietly, out of the Legacy and across external existence, toward a small sealed Elsedimension hung off the edge of a dying Dimension.","Toward the place where Adrastia was!","He would dream his Infinite Dream again. He would never let himself be in any one place for more than a few minutes. He would move, and move again, so that even if some greedy thing out in the dark caught the signal of his Root, there would be nothing left where it looked for anything to lock onto.","The rift closed behind him, and the Glacial Mountain rose ahead, and he began to dream an endless dream!"]},{"number":5777,"title":"Chapter 5777: Chapter 5776: Assimilation! II","paragraphs":["<Achilles Adrastia>","Existence was a unique thing.","It held everything, and it held it strangely, and no two pieces of it were quite alike. But there was a thing more unique than existence itself, and Achilles had built his whole life on it. The capability to assimilate it. To take a piece of existence into yourself, whatever it was, whoever it had belonged to, and make it a part of what you were.","He had assimilated a great many things across his life. Powers, weavings, authorities, the cores of enemies and the gifts of friends, whole systems of existence swallowed and woven into his own. Most of it had settled. Some of it had fought. None of it had ever been as problematic as the monstrous weavings he had assimilated weeks ago, and none of it had ever kept him awake the way those did now.","The trees nearby did not care about any of that.","They grew out of meteorites, here, in this sealed pocket of existence that held no life but his and hers. Tens of thousands of them, stellar trees rooted in drifting stone, their trunks pale and their leaves a vivid pink, streching away through the dark in every direction like an orchard planted across a night sky.","And through all of them whipped the snow. A heavy storm of it, white and endless, driving between the pink-leaved boughs and across the meteorites and through the empty space where no wind should have been, because The Long Night did not need wind to fall.","Achilles leaned against the nearest tree and watched it come down.","He looked young. He always had, a young king’s face, handsome and composed. But his eyes had long since stopped matching it. They were old eyes, aged past the youth that held them, and lately they had gotten older still.","He wore a multicolored coat pulled close against the cold, layers of shifting hue woven from a dozen assimilated authorities, and he was not alone. Rose leaned against his shoulder with her arms wrapped around it, her green hair blowing in the storm, her own coat as many-colored as his, and the two of them watched the pink leaves and the falling snow together in a place where nothing else lived.","\" What exactly will you do, Little Fatty?\"","Rose asked quietly, without looking away from the storm.","\" We have not come across any problem we could not overcome. Not one, in all this time. But this one... \" She tightened her arms around his shoulder. \" This one feels neverending.\"","...!","Neverending!","That was the word for it, if there was a word. That was what it was to assimilate a portion of THE Sealed One.","Every time Achilles thought he was peeling back the layers of possibility, getting closer to autonomy, closer to a self that was fully and finally his own, he found only more layers underneath. The weavings of THE Sealed One were not a thing you assimilated. They were a thing you fell into, and the further you fell the more you understood how vast and how disastrous the fall was. Even now, weeks in, he had not found a bottom.","\" He has so many weavings stretched across existence and time ,\" Achilles said, \" that even now, he considers me nothing more than a part of him that is not fully aligned yet.\"","The snow drove between the pink boughs.","\" He has not moved against me. Because I cannot lose you, and the others. And he can sense that. He can sense the commitment I made, that the moment he reaches for everything I have, I collapse all of it. Every weaving of my Assimilation, gone, the whole of what I am, so that he takes nothing. He knows I will do it. So...he waits like a venomous fucking thing...\"","Achilles let out a slow breath that turned to frost. \" But I can feel him reaching a new precipice. Somewhere out there, he is about to gain enough that he can overwhelm me even with the threat. And when that time comes, I will have no choice but to take the gamble. I will assimilate all of him that I can reach, all at once, and the whole of it will come down to whether I succeed, or whether he takes everything I have instead. It is...\"","He did not finish. He sighed, and raised his hands toward the falling snow and the pink leaves, as though he might catch some answer in them.","And at exactly that moment...","HUUM!","His existence pulsed.","It was the deep hard pulse of an assimilator’s whole being registering a presence, and his expression went heavy at once, and he pushed off the tree and rose to his full height, because ahead of them, across the orchard of pink and stone, existence was tearing.","It tore like a page!","The dark between the trees split along a clean seam, and out of the tear flooded light. Golden blue. It poured into the sealed Elsedimension in a tide, and out of the light, stepping through the torn page of existence as easily as a man steps through a door, came a lifeform!","Achilles had seen a great many lifeforms. He had assimilated a great many. He had never seen one whose mere arrival did what this one’s did!","The moment it stood in the orchard, the orchard changed. The nearest pink trees shivered, and their leaves began to turn, the vivid pink draining out of them and a deep blue gold flooding in, spreading from tree to tree in a wave that ran outward from the lifeform’s feet.","And the snow stopped. Not slowed. Stopped! Ten thousand flakes hung motionless in the air around the torn page of light, arrested mid-fall, as though the Long Night itself had paused to look!","Achilles felt his existence churn. A profound oppression settled over the orchard, a pressure that was not aimed at him and did not need to be. His instinct, which measured everything as a thing to be taken, looked at this lifeform and found nothing it could take. That had never happened before. Not once!","Then he looked closer, and closer, and past the boundless Infinity and Immensity that seemed to fill the lifeform’s eyes, he recognized the face.","Was this not...THE Osmontian? Noah Osmont?!","He knew that face. He had crossed paths with this anomaly a few times and each time, Achilles had reached out with the sense that measured all things and found that he could not find the bottom of this one!","So why had he appeared here? Now?","Achilles kept his expression heavy and his voice calm.","\" Hello ,\" he said. \" To what do we owe the pleasure of your appearance here today?\"","The lifeform looked at him.","The pressure did not lift. If anything it settled deeper and when the lifeform spoke, its voice boomed out across the orchard.","\" Adrastia ,\" it said. \" THE Ninth Adrastia Emperor King, is it?\"","The hanging snow did not move!","\"I have come for your Existence.\"","...!","Achilles’s expression went heavy and defiant in the same instant, and beside him Rose flared.","Verdant flames spilled out of her, green and bright against the blue gold of the changed trees, and her body began to drink the authority around it, assimilating the surrounding weavings!","She did not step back and she did not flinch from the pressure that had stopped the snow. She looked at the monster across the orchard with the same defiance in her face that was in his, undaunted by his authority, and her flames climbed higher!"]},{"number":5778,"title":"Chapter 5778: Chapter 5777: Assimilation! III","paragraphs":["<Achilles Adrastia>","Achilles had spent a long life learning when not to move, and this was one of those times.","Of course, standing still was easier said than done. Rose’s flames were climbing beside him, and the pressure of the thing in the torn light had settled over the orchard and every instinct he owned was telling him that a man who did not act was a man who got acted upon!","But he held his ground.","\" You and I have had no negative dealings ,\" he said. \" One of the last times I was near you, you came down with THE Creature to attack another Vessel of THE Sealed One. Not me. \"","He kept his voice level. \" So before I do everything I can for my survival, can you at least tell me why?\"","Why, indeed.","Why now, and why here, in a sealed pocket of existence that no one should have been able to find? Why him, of all the scattered pieces of THE Sealed One drifting through existence like seeds? Had he done something, some careless thing weeks ago, that had marked him as the first to be gathered? Or had he simply been the easiest to reach? Achilles did not know!","In fact, the lifeform did not answer him at all. Not the question he had asked, at any rate. It drifted closer across the changed orchard, the blue gold spreading through the trees ahead of it, and when it finally spoke it seemed to be picking up a different conversation entirely, one that had begun without him.","\" Was that the time you assimilated the weavings of THE Sealed One? \" Osmont said, almost idly. \" Perhaps I should have been more thorough back then, and none of this would have happened. Oh well .\"","\" When I say I am here for your Existence, I mean it. I am here to ensure your Assimilation Factor is never grasped by THE Sealed One. Consider me... your savior.\"","WAA!","Achilles had barely finished hearing the word when the anomaly’s hand rose and came down toward them.","He did not think about it! The light of dozens of assimilated Prime Causes and First Causes poured out of him at once, and assimilated Primordial Source surged up dark beneath it, and assimilated Infinity rose over all of it, and around himself and Rose he threw up a bubble of every color he had ever swallowed, seething and bright, a wall made of a lifetime of taking.","And yet nothing struck it!","The bubble held and seethed and waited, and no blow came against it. Instead, the orchard simply went away. The blue gold trees and the hanging snow washed out like paint under water, and in their place there were seas, golden and dreaming and slow, rolling out to every horizon under heavy golden clouds. Compared to the hand that had come down, it was almost gentle. Compared to anything Achilles had ever seen an enemy do, it was far more frightening.","Savior, the anomaly had said. Was that actually what this was? Had a being that stopped snow with its arrival truly come all this way to help a man it barely knew? Achilles wanted to believe it, but..","What he could not dismiss, though, was the authority.","It wrapped around everything now, this golden dreaming light, and it was unlike any weaving he had ever taken into himself or ever failed to. His existence seethed at the nearness of it!","The oldest instinct he owned, the one that had built him from a hungry man into a king, whispered the way it always whispered, that he should take it, assimilate it, now, before it was gone!","And in the very same breath he understood that he could not.","But even that was not the truly unsettling part.","The truly unsettling part was that, just by standing near this authority, he had begun to think about his goals. His dreams. He had not asked to. He had not wanted to, not here, not in the middle of a standoff with something that could end him.","And yet the thoughts came anyway. What kind of authority did that to a person? What kind of power made a being remember what it wanted, simply by being close?","Since he could not measure the thing itself, he did what he had always done. He measured the one who trusted it.","\" Taylor of the Light always carried the highest belief and confidence in you ,\" Achilles said. \" I will use her character as the basis of trust, since I have nothing else to use.\"","He lowered the bubble by a fraction, and only a fraction. \" So. If you truly came to help, what is it you think you will be able to do? I am irreversibly bonded to THE Sealed One. I assimilated a portion of his weavings of existence, and my Assimilation is absolute. It does not take a thing partway. I am that part of THE Sealed One now, and at the same time I am not him, and there is no line between those two facts that I have ever managed to find.\"","He held the anomaly’s gaze. \"It is not a matter of separating two existences. It is a matter of cutting apart a single one. If you can help with that, then by all means, go ahead. I am only unsure that it can be done.\"","In truth, he had turned the problem over ten thousand ways. Every angle of Assimilation he knew, every trick a lifetime of taking had taught him, and not one of them ended with him still standing.","So perhaps it was not so strange that he would take the help of a monstrous lifeform as readily as any other, if the help was real. He had a family to think about, after all. He had Rose.","And he had made himself a promise, in the long nights since the weavings settled into him, that on every morning still to come, however cold and however cruel, she would wake beside his face. His own face. Not the face of an ancient monster wearing whatever was left of him.","So he raised a hand and pushed her gently back.","\" Stay behind me.\"","\"Fatty...\" She caught his sleeve befofe she let go, though her flames did not lower, and Achilles stepped forward out of the bubble to stand before the titanic figure alone.","Up close, he could feel what it emanated, and he found that he knew it. Provenance Essence. He knew the shape of that authority from the memories of THE Sealed One that lived inside him now.","Achilles had not thought Osmont had come this far. So maybe, he told himself. Maybe there was a chance.","The anomaly looked him over, up and down. Then he nodded, once.","\" Are you human? \" Osmont said. \" Do you dream?\"","Achilles blinked.","Of all the things he had braced himself to hear, that had not been among them. Was it a test? A riddle?","\"I was very much born human,\" he said slowly. \" And of course I have dreams. Everyone has dreams.\"","The anomaly’s reply came grand and quiet.","\" Then I will simply be making a dream come true ,\" he said. \" Open your existence to me. Let me see.\"","His dream.","Behind him, Rose’s expression had gone heavy. He thought about his Dream, since he had been asked to, and found that he did not have to look far.","His Dream was Rose. His Dream was his children. His Dream, if he was honest, had always been existence itself. He had wanted, from the very beginning, to assimilate every aspect of existence there was, to take all of it into himself until nothing anywhere could shake him, until he stood on a foundation made of everything. He had wanted to assimilate everything!","And was that not still true? Had the weavings of THE Sealed One changed what he wanted, or only what he feared? When he looked at it plainly, the wanting was exactly where he had left it. He could assimilate everything.","That was his Dream, and of course he wanted to reach it. And if this anomaly, this being that stopped snow and turned trees to gold and made him remember what he wanted simply by standing near him, could actually put him back on the road toward it, then perhaps the price of finding out was one he could afford.","Achilles was decisive, as he had always been.","He sat down where he stood, on the golden dreaming sea, in a meditative position, and as he settled his body changed. The young king’s flesh gave way to what lay beneath it, a crystalline figure shifting through every color at once, every authority he had ever swallowed visible now in the facets of him. A man made, quite literally, of everything he had taken.","He opened his eyes and looked up at the titan before him.","Neither of them said a word. The one standing reached out, and a frosty crystalline hand came down and rested, lightly, on the crown of his head.","| You have opened the weavings of your existence to THE HUMAN DREAMER.|","|A terrifying Provenance has begun to permeate across your existence.|","|Your existential genome is being studied.|","|Your Dream is being studied.|","A heavy Immensity spread through the whole of him, and Achilles steeled himself against it, and held!","Then the cold authority began to move. It moved through his existence and it found, in a matter of moments, the seam he had spent ten thousand attempts failing to find.","Achilles felt his existence stop. Had it truly been there all along, that close, that simple, and he had never once been able to see it? Or was it only there now, because a hand grander than his own had come looking?","He did not have time to decide. The authority had found what it was looking for, and it began, without any ceremony at all, to cleave!","It cleaved!"]},{"number":5779,"title":"Chapter 5779: Chapter 5778: I Am Me!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah’s hand rested on the crown of the crystalline king’s head, and beneath it, he marveled.","He had expected the lifeform to be unique. The Caretaker had said as much. But expecting a thing and holding it under your palm were not the same, and what he held now was stranger than anything he had braced for.","Achilles Adrastia had not devoured the facets of existence he carried. This existence was a chameleon. It did not eat what it assimilated. It became it, seamlessly, so that the Prime Causes and the First Causes and the Primordial Source and the Infinity inside him were not swallowed things siting in a stomach. They were him. Every one of them, as native to his weavings as his own name!","And that, Noah understood, was exactly why he should have died weeks ago.","Because a chameleon that becomes what it touches has no defense against touching something too large to become. He had assimilated the weavings of THE Sealed One, and by every law of his own nature he should simply have become THE Sealed One, the way water poured into a larger vessel takes that vessel’s shape.","THE Sealed One was far too complex, far too vast, far too old for a single existence to become and remain itself. And yet Achilles had held on!","He had become a piece of the ancient monster and, by some stubbornness Noah could feel humming in the crystal under his hand, refused to finish becoming it. He had stopped halfway, and lived there, in a place no assimilator should have been able to survive.","So the task was not to pull two things apart. It was to find, inside a single existence, the line between what was the king and what was the monster, and cut along it without cutting the king.","Fortunately, Noah had been made for exactly this kind of work.","He had two Provenances, and they had never before been asked to do one thing together. THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer had become terrifying in the manipulation of dreams since his Root formed, terrifying in a way he was still learning the edges of.","And THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign, could reach into the genome of existence itself and alter it, excise it, edit what a thing was at the level of its deepest weaving. One of them could see. The other could cut. So he set them to their tasks!","The Dreamer’s Provenance went in first, and it did not go looking for THE Sealed One. A being’s existential genome was a tangle beyond reading, and the monster’s weavings were threaded through every strand of it.","But a being’s Dream was not a tangle. A Dream was the simplest true thing in any existence, the thing under all the other things, and Achilles had just shown him his! Rose! His children! Existence itself, assimilated whole!","So Noah followed the Dream! He let his Provenance sink down along the shape of what Achilles wanted, and every strand of the genome that answered to that wanting, that pulled toward Rose and the children and the hunger to become everything, lit up gold in his sight. And every strand that did not, every thread that pulled instead toward sealing and collecting and finishing and owning, stayed dark.","There was the line! Not a seam Achilles had failed to find, but a seam that could only be seen by a thing that read Dreams, because the Dream was the one part of a man an ancient monster could not counterfeit!","Then the Immense Sovereign’s Provenance came down like a knife along the line.","It was cold work, and it was fine work, the cutting of a single existence into what it was and what it had been made to carry!","The dark strands parted. The gold ones held. The Assimilation Factor, the living thread that ran from this crystalline king back through the deep to THE Sealed One, came free under the edge of his Provenance and was severed, cleanly, completely!","The golden storm of Provenance Essence roared around the two of them, and Achilles Adrastia opened his eyes.","He did not move at first. He sat in his crystalline form in the middle of the storm and simply listened.","\" It’s... quiet ,\" Achilles said.","His voice was hoarse with astonishment.","\"I don’t hear the buzzing. There was always a buzzing. An old horror, incessant, at the back of everything, every moment since I took him in.\" He turned his head slowly, as though the silence might be hiding somewhere. \" It’s gone. I can’t hear it at all...\"","Noah nodded, and reached to withdraw his hand, and was about to finish the work when something caught his sight.","Oh?","The excision had cut the thread. It had not cut the memories. Those had been assimilated, made native, become Achilles the way everything he took became Achilles, and so they had stayed on the king’s side of the line, and now they lay open under Noah’s palm like pages in a book he had not meant to read.","They were hazy. Rough. Half-ruined by the cutting, almost unrecoverable. But he could see enough of them to know what they were about, and what they were about made him look at the crystalline figure under his hand a second time.","Immense Ones. And a Legacy!","Memories THE Sealed One himself had carried, of dealings with Immense Ones, and of a Legacy, a structure of the kind Lucy had built, though whether it was hers or another’s the ruin of the memory would not say!","Noah had not thought THE Sealed One was so deeply connected to the Immense Ones. He remembered the words of The Caretaker about how THE Sealed One was protected by dredges and legacies as he couldn’t help but sigh!","\" Existence is infinitely vast ,\" Noah said, looking down at the king, \" and it has so many weavings of power that no one has ever counted them. I recently made grand advancements. Advancements that let me see existence, and even time, differently than I did. I have already begun outlining how I might share that advancement, and that way of seeing, with those closest to me.\"","He let the hand on Achilles’s head rest a moment longer. \" And I could always use an experimental subject.\"","Achilles’s crystalline eyes rose to his.","\" As you elevate your Dimensionality, I learn. You will eventually need to reach the point of forming a Root of Immensity of your own. It is not easy. It does not begin where you might think. It begins with your own Chorionic Gonadotropin, the signal of your own becoming, and you have a unique Factor of Assimilation, which means you could very possibly form a unique kind of Assimilation Chorionic Gonadotropin, with my help. \"","He glanced, briefly, at nothing, at a clock only he could feel running. \" But I am out of time here, and I will have to change scenery to experiment with you further. Do you want to try?\"","...!","He asked it calmly. But the man beneath his hand was smiling now, brilliantly, the smile of someone who has just been handed back his own existence and offered a road on top of it, and Achilles reached out with his senses.","\" Thank you ,\" Achilles said. \" And yes. Just give me one second...\"","The golden storm faded!","The dreaming seas rolled away, and the heavy clouds thinned, and the two of them stood once more in the sealed Elsedimension among the blue gold trees and the hanging snow, exactly where they had left it. And Achilles Adrastia stood up.","He was flesh again, the young king’s face and the ancient eyes, though the eyes seemed younger now by a great deal. He turned. He looked at the beautiful green-haired woman standing behind him with her flames burned down to embers and her face heavy, and he crossed the distance to her in three strides and pulled her against him and held her so tightly that Noah, watching, thought he might crack her.","Then he kissed her. Then he laughed, out loud, the laugh of a man who has been holding his breath for weeks.","\"I am me ,\" Achilles said into her hair. \" All me!\"","...!","\" Really? \" Rose pulled back to look at his face, her hands on either side of it, searching. \" Really?!\"","\"All me.\"","She made a sound that was half a laugh and half something else, and then she was kissing him, and he was kissing her, and the embrace between them went from relief to something a good deal warmer with a speed that suggested the two of them had forgotten, entirely, that they were not alone.","Noah, being human, allowed them a moment. He had a family too. He knew what it was to hold someone and find them still themselves.","Prompts bloomed across his sight while he waited.","| You have interfered in, and steered, a grand unfolding Dream.|","|Your Provenance increases by 25.|","|The gaze of an unfathomable existence is seeking to understand how one of its grandest tools was just separated from it.|","...!","Noah looked at that last line, and raised his brows.","Then he looked at the two embracing lifeforms before him, who showed no sign at all of stopping.","\" Time’s up,\" he said. \" Let’s go.\"","His Provenance blared!","It flooded out of him and took the orchard, the king, the woman, the whole of the small sealed space, and drew it into his Dream, and he took Achilles Adrastia and Rose out of the Elsedimension where they had hidden and carried them, in a single beat of his Root, toward another.","One with far heavier security. One where a part of him already stood among broken clocks and numbered meteorites, in a Dimension that had come apart from time itself. Atlas’s Elsedimension of shattered hours!","HUUM!","They were gone.","---","The orchard stood empty. And slowly, the way a held breath lets go, the blue gold drained back out of the trees, and the leaves returned to their vivid pink, and the snow that had hung motionless in the air remembered that it was falling, and fell.","For a few moments the Elsedimension was only an orchard on drifting stone again, with no one in it.","Then, moments later...","BOOM!","The sky tore open!","Not a page this time. Eyes! Multiple massive eyes forced their way open across the heights of the sealed Elsedimension, one after another, gazes the size of Dimensions blinking into being where no gaze should have been able to reach, and the pink trees bent under the weight of being looked at.","|THE SLEEPLESS FIEND casts his gaze across the orchard, and is displeased.|","|\"A Root was just here. The scent of it is still on the trees.\"|","|THE UNPAID COLLECTOR’s gaze narrows.|","|\"The same one. The one that slipped us in the frozen forest.\"|","|THE GLOATING JAILER is puzzled.|","|\"How did it sense our coming so quickly? We had not even finished arriving.\"|","|THE SLEEPLESS FIEND does not answer the Jailer. His gaze turns downward, toward the orchard floor.|","|\"And you. You were the one who alerted us to this place. You said a project of yours was taken away here.\"|","...!","The words fell into the orchard from the sky, and below, existence opened.","Infinity spilled out of the air between the pink trees, and THE Primordial Source spilled with it, the two of them pouring open together the way no two authorities in existence were supposed to be able to pour, and out of the joined flood stepped a humanoid figure.","He was young, and he was ancient, and the two facts sat on him without quarreling. Tall, and lean, and pale as a thing that had never once needed the sun.","Long hair fell past his shoulders, pale gold shading toward white, and his face was cut fine and cold and aristocratic, every line of it composed.","His eyes were gold. Not warm gold. The gold of a thing found at the bottom of a very deep place. He wore a long dark coat that hung to his boots, severe and old-fashioned and immaculate, and he stood among the pink trees as though he had stood in a thousand such places and found them all equally beneath him.","It was THE Sealed One!","And it was not a vessel.","This was not a puppet. This was the genuine article, the hand behind every vessel! and his existence pulsed, slow and heavy and unfathomable, with a Root!","A Root of Immensity, seated in him, growing, and so dense that the snow could not get near him. It fell all around him and stopped, a hand’s breadth from his coat, and drifted away, as though the winter itself had decided he was not a thing it cared to touch!","He looked around the orchard coldly, at the pink trees, at the drifting stone.","\" A Unique Existential Factor of Assimilation,\" THE Sealed One said, \" that would have made for a unique Aspect of my growing Root. Taken. It is a great shame.\"","He turned one pale hand over, as though weighing the loss in his palm. \" Though I believe I may know who is responsible.\"","He raised both hands then, pale and long-fingered, into the air around him, and breathed in.","\"I can smell his arrogance, tyranny, ans brilliance ,\" he said. \" And his Infinity. I know that Infinity. It is my greatest loss across the whole of existence, so far .\"","His gold eyes lifted to the massive gazes hanging in the sky. \" The culprit should be a lifeform known as Noah Osmont.\"","...!"]},{"number":5780,"title":"Chapter 5780: Chapter 5779: Time! I","paragraphs":["In the age before ages were counted, there was a Lineage that did not know what an hour was.","They were a Provenance Lineage. The First one among them had generated her own origin out of the dark.","They lived in a valley at the bottom of existence where nothing had yet been measured. They did not count their days, because no one had told them days could be counted. They only lived them, one after another.","And through that valley, though none of them could see it, there ran a river.","Time ran through the valley. It ran through everything, in that age as in every age, and it was the one thing in all of existence that every being received in exactly equal measure and no being ever kept.","The Lineage stood in it up to their necks and did not know it was there. They aged in it. They loved in it. They died in it, and were carried off downstream, and the ones left standing wept and did not know what had carried their dead away.","Of that Lineage there was a daughter who noticed the river.","She was not the strongest of them, nor the wisest. But she was the one who stood at the bank one evening and watched her mother be carried off, and asked the question none of the others had thought to ask.","What is this thing that takes us? And where does it go?","So she went looking for it!","She walked out of the valley, which no one of her Lineage had done, and she walked a very long way, and at the end of the walking she found The Provenance of Time.","The Provenance of Time was sitting on a stone. Time was not old, and Time was not young. Time had the face of everything that had ever happened and the eyes of everything that had not happened yet, and it was not doing anything at all, because Time does not do things. Time only...passes.","The daughter said to it, You take my people. I have watched you carry them off. I have come to ask you to stop.","The Provenance of Time said, I do not take. I do not give. I am the only thing in existence that every one of you receives equally and none of you keeps. Your people are not carried off by me. They are carried off in me.","The daughter did not accept this. She was of a Lineage that came from nothing, and such beings do not accept.","She said, My First mother generated her own origin. She owed nothing to any framework. Why then must I stand in your river like a fish? Why must I receive you as everyone receives you? I will make my own. I will generate a Time that is mine, the way she generated an origin that was hers, and then you will not carry me anywhere I do not choose to go.","And Time, who had heard this before, and would hear it again, said only, You may. It has been done. But understand what it costs, for I will not tell you twice.","The daughter did not ask what it cost. She did not ask!","She went back to her valley, and she sat down at the bank of the river she could now see, and she began to generate. It took her an age, though she did not count it, because she still did not count. She reached into the self-made fire her Lineage carried and she made, out of nothing, a Time that was hers.","Her own Provenance of Time. Not the common river that ran through everything, but a private current, originatng in her and answering to no one, which she could slow, and hasten, and stand outside of, and which would never carry her anywhere she did not choose to be carried.","And the day it was finished, she became Immense!","She stepped out of the river. That is all it took, in the end, once the current of her own was made. She stepped up onto the bank, out of the common Time that ran through everything, and stood in her own, and looked back down at the valley of her Lineage from a place where no hour could reach her.","She saw her people aging. She had not aged. She saw her sisters grow old and be carried off downstream, and she stood on the bank and could not reach them, because her hand was in one Time and theirs were in another, and a hand cannot cross that.","She saw her children, and her children’s children, live whole lives between one of her breaths and the next. She called to them, and her voice arrived in the valley a generation late, or a generation early, so that they heard a stranger shouting from a bank they could not see.","And in time, which was still running for them though it had stopped for her, her Lineage forgot her. Just like how a river forgets a stone it no longer touches.","They told stories about a daughter who had gone looking for the thing that took their dead and had never come back, and the stories were true, and she stood twenty paces from the storytellers and could not make them hear her.","That is the Provenance of Time. It is one of the grandest Provenances there is, because it is the only one that lets a being stand outside the river every other being drowns in. And it is the grimmest, because the river is where everyone you love is standing, and to leave it is to leave them, and a being with its own Time is the loneliest thing in all of existence!","Time had told her. It had said, understand what it costs. She had not asked.","Some say she still stands on the bank above a valley that no longer exists, watching a river with no one in it. Some say she learned to step back down into the common current for a moment at a time, to hold a hand that would slip from hers a heartbeat later, and that this was worse.","And some say that every Immense One who has ever stood outside an hour is that same daughter, learning the same lesson, in a different valley, and that Those Who Remain are only the ones who never once stepped back down!","Time was always a dangerous thing to play with.","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah stood in three places at once, and none of them was safe.","The first was the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity, where his body sat under Verys’s care on the Glacial Mountain. The second was THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering, where a part of him hunted Rare Gu and never stopped moving. The third was here, at the peak of a violet tree that stretched away for light years, in a Dimension that had come apart from time.","The gazes of the Immense Ones did not reach well into these last two. Their Ruling of Existence still let them watch a great many things. But it did not let them watch everything.","At this time.","The air tore beside him!","Achilles and Rose stepped out of it onto a branch.","The ring on Noah’s finger buzzed.","Atlas rose out of it, an old man made of light, and the billowing snow of the Long Night passed straight through his illusory chest without slowing. He looked at the two newcomers, and then at Noah.","\" We were close ,\" Atlas said. \" We were this close to sniffing out where my old Workshop is. Why bring newcomers now?\"","He nodded at them. \" Who are they?\"","\"Somewhat unique lifeforms,\" Noah said. \" They were connected to THE Sealed One. I severed that connection seconds ago. And that old one, it turns out, is connected to a great many Immense Ones. Some of them are likely among those who killed you all those years ago.\"","...!","Atlas blinked.","He looked Achilles up and down, slowly, like a craftsman looking at a tool he did not make and cannot yet place.","\" Connected how? \" he said.","\"I don’t know yet. The memories are half-ruined. But there were Immense Ones in them. And a Legacy.\"","Achilles rose from where he had crouched. His eyes were shining!","\"I am Adrastia ,\" he said. \"I am thankful for what Osmont did to help me. And it seems he is not done doing so.\"","He looked at the old man of light as he asked Noah. \" You mentioned... a Root of Immensity?\"","...!","Atlas glanced at Noah. Noah inclined his head as he nodded.","\"I want to try inducing the formation of a Root of Immensity in others. I am doing it now. Here, with him, and at my home. Different subjects, the same work, at the same time.\"","Atlas tilted his illusory head.","\"A Root is generated ,\" he said. \" It is not given. That is the whole meaning of the word. So how would you induce anything?\"","Noah looked out over the light years of violet branches, and when he answered, his voice had the flat calm of a man describing something he could see from a great height.","\"I am a space the house of existence was built in ,\" he said. \" When I stand near an existence, that existence begins to remember what it dreams. I do not hand anything my Root. I show their existence the shape of beginning, and whether it begins is their own weaving. Well, in theory. I could act to induce something made from his own signal of becoming. His own Chorionic Gonadotropin.\"","Atlas was silent for a while. The snow went through him. Noah turned to Achilles.","\" Your Assimilation Factor. The thing THE Sealed One wanted from you. He wanted it because it is the only one of its kind. You do not devour what you take. You become it. And a Root grows from the signal of a being’s own becoming. So I intend to build something out of that. A signal that tells existence to keep growing you into everything you assimilate, without end.\"","Achilles’s crystalline eyes did not leave him as he grasped all these possibilities!","\"That has no precedent, I believe. \" Atlas said.","\" Nothing I have done these past days has precedent, \" Noah said.","...!","He looked at the three of them, the old man of light and the chameleon of a king and the silent woman, and he spoke more of his existence.","\" Existence is not static for me anymore. It is dynamic. I can see the equation of it turning, and I can see that most of the walls in it are only places no one has pushed. A great many things are possible now that were not possible a week ago. Just because a thing seems impossible does not mean it will remain so.\"","He looked at Atlas. \" My Provenance is that of a Dreamer. I dream a thing, and existence adjusts to agree. So I will ask you the only question that matters. Why can I not dream impossibilities into existence?\"","...!","Atlas did not answer at once.","He looked at Noah for a long moment! He crossed his illusory arms.","\" You want to dream impossibilities. Then dream this fairly simple one. Dream that we have already found my Workshop. Here. Now. We’ve been looking for some time now while avoiding the gazes of others.\"","WAA!","Noah was already looking at the sky as his Provenance came off him in a flood of blue gold! The violet tree bent away from it! The snow turned to gold in the air! He did not search for the Workshop. He did not reach for it. He simply dreamed, plainly and completely, that the four of them were standing before the hidden Workshop of Atlas, in this Elsedimension, now.","| 25 Provenance Essence expended.|","|You have dreamed an arrival. Existence is adjusting to agree.|","Existence shuddered!","The branch was gone! The tree was gone! For one instant there was nothing under them at all, and Rose’s grip closed hard on Achilles’s arm, and neither of them made a sound.","Then there was ground!","They stood on stone, and around them raged storms of time!","Hours blew past like weather! Whole seasons went by in a gust and came back the other way! The sky was a sheet of purple turning in slow spirals, and through it fell the snow of the Long Night, which alone in that place seemed to fall at the ordinary speed, one flake after another, indifferent to what the hours were doing.","And ahead of them rose a massive statue!","It was a serpent. It stretched away for Gigaparsecs, a coil of stone so vast that its far end was lost in the purple, and its head had come round to meet its tail, and its jaws were closed on it. It was eating itself! It had been eating itself, by the look of the stone, for a very long time, and it was no nearer to finishing.","\" Time ,\" Atlas said quietly. \" Eating its own tail. I was young when I carved it. But it seems your Provenance is truly grand...\"","Then he stopped, because they all felt it now.","Auras! Many of them, and every one of them the aura of a Provenance Lifeform, a being that had generated its own origin, dense and self-made and unmistakable as they circled the vastness of this statue.","And near the base of the statue, where a purple barrier of time hung shimmering across the way like a curtain of years, a dozen figures stood pressed against it, working at it, trying to get through.","The dozen turned around!","Twelve pairs of eyes found the four of them at once!","They were foreign Provenance Lifeforms, all twelve.","Rose’s flames lit green at her fingertips and stayed there, low. Achilles moved half a step in front of her without seeming to decide to.","The old man of light was not looking at the twelve. He was looking past them, past the purple curtain, at what lay behind it, and his voice, when it came, came only inside Noah’s mind, so quiet the storms of time could not have heard it.","\" Well ,\" Atlas said. \" This is my Workshop. We can finally get going on the matter of time. \"","...!"]},{"number":5781,"title":"Chapter 5781: Chapter 5780: Time! II","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","The twelve Provenance Lifeforms did not run!","Twelve foreign Provenance Lifeforms, standing at the base of a statue of time, had felt four beings appear out of nothing at their backs, and not one of them flinched toward flight. Instead they turned and spread, and came unhurried across the storming ground.","At their front walked a woman with hair the color of old bronze, bound back hard against her skull. Her eyes had held one expression for so long that Noah doubted they remembered any other.","She wore a coat of layered grey that the storms of time slid off without touching, and she moved like a magistrate carrying a sentence already written.","\" You newcomers will be smart to leave ,\" she said.","\" This Elsedimension, and every Relic in it, has been claimed by THE Vheldrani Provenance Lineage. Claimed across ages. We have paid the toll on this place a hundred times over, in blood and in years, and it is ours by every weaving that binds a thing to a claim.\"","Her bronze eyes moved across the four of them and dismissed them in the moving. \" You are trespassers on a hunt that was old before your Lineages had names. I do not know what you are. I frankly do not give a damn. Get out, and take your pathetic selves with you before we decide the trespass is worth the trouble of correcting.\"","Behind her, the eleven spread wider, and the storms of time bent around them as their Provenance buzzed and distored the surrounding Existence!","Noah looked at the twelve, and their measures opened to him.","| VHELDRANI PROVENANCE LIFEFORM| |VERITAS: 211. POTENTIA: 208. PONDUS: 214. PROVENANCE: 219.|","The woman was the strongest of them. The low two hundreds. The eleven behind her were less, all of them dense and self-made and genuinely grand by the measure of everything he had spent his whole climb fighting, and all of them beneath his own current standing by a distance where the number of it stopped meaning anything.","He had crossed six hundred not long ago! He grew forty to eighty more with every turn of Existence whether he lifted a finger or not. And twelve beings in the low two hundreds had come to shoo him away?","He looked at that and found it faintly, coldly amusing.","\" You have made a mistake,\" Noah said.","The bronze-haired woman’s eyes narrowed.","\" Hey, I really dont want to have a back and forth as it has gotten very cold recently. The mistake is yours as the best you can do is leave.\"","\" Not that mistake .\" Noah lifted a hand, unhurried. \" You looked at me, and you decided what I was, and you did it quickly, because your people decide things quickly. That is the mistake. You should have looked just a bit longer.\"","\"I have looked long enough to know you are one and we are twelve.\"","\"You have looked long enough to count us. You have not looked long enough to understand that the count does not matter. Even if there were a million of you, the count still would not matter.\"","WAA!","And he dreamed!","WAA!","His Provenance came off him, blue and gold, and it did not fall on them as an attack falls. It rose around them slowly, and the twelve moved to shed it as they would shed any hostile weaving, and found nothing to shed, because there was nothing hostile in it! It was only a dream, settling over them, asking their existences to agree.","\" What is this?! \" the woman said, and for the first time her voice held a sense of alarm!","\"I dreamed of you ,\" Noah said, \" as statues.\"","The rivers of his Provenance closed!","There was no tearing, no burning, no unmaking. Noah simply dreamed that these twelve foreign Provenance Lifeforms were frozen figures, drifting statues, silent and still and carried forever on the currents of existence, and existence agreed!","The bronze-haired woman had time to open her mouth.","Then the grey of her coat turned to stone, and the bronze of her hair with it! The expression her eyes had worn for an age set hard and stayed, and the certainty in them was the last thing to freeze, still there and cold when the rest of her had already gone still. She did not fall, because there was no down to fall in.","She hung where she had stood, turning very slowly in the storms of time, a magistrate of stone holding a sentence she would never finish reading!","Eleven more went the same, one after another, mid-step, mid-spread, mid-thought!","Twelve statues where twelve claims had stood, drifting apart on the currents, growing smaller toward the far purple, not one of them having landed a single word of protest that existence had bothered to hear.","It was very quiet afterwards!","\"Hmm,\" Atlas said.","Noah was already moving ahead!","He crossed the storming ground toward the base of the serpent, toward the purple barrier of time that hung across the way like a curtain of years, the barrier the twelve had spent who knew how long failing to cross.","He stopped before it, and did not touch it. His gaze went instead to the ring on his own finger, and he waited.","The ring shone!","Atlas’s light poured out along Noah’s hand and into the curtain, and the curtain knew it. The same hand had made both, keyed to the same maker, and the barrier parted before that key. The years drew back. A path opened into the coil of the serpent, dim and cold and older than the storms outside it!","They went in!","—","Inside the serpent, time waited.","The walls of the coil were stone that was not quite stone, dark and smooth, threaded through with faint lines of light that pulsed slow, like something very large breathing in its sleep! The path curved away ahead of them, spiraling down toward a core they could not yet see, and the deeper they went the quieter it became, until the only sounds were their own passage and that slow pulse in the walls.","Noah walked at the front, and he spoke as they walked, quiet, to the old man of light beside him.","\" The Vheldrani were open to me when their Dreams ceased ,\" he said. \" Their memories, at least what they were thinking of when they died.\"","\"And? \" Atlas said.","\" They did not come here on their own. They were sent to this place, to strip it of your Relics at the behest of another.\"","Atlas was quiet for a moment. \" Whose behest?\"","\"THE SLEEPLESS FIEND.\"","The light in the walls pulsed once, twice, in the silence, and when the old man started forward again the warmth had gone out of his voice.","\" Okay. Anything else?\" Atlas said. \" Tell me the rest.\"","\"This is not their first hunt in your Elsedimensions. They have taken things from you across the ages in different Elsedimensions. Small things. Tools. Fragments. The Fiend has been picking your bones a very long time, one Relic at a time, and paying Lineages of Provenance Lifeforms to do so.\"","Atlas nodded for a moment.","\" The small things they can take. I expected that. Let him have every workbench and every failed prototype and every clever little toy I left lying around, and much good may they do him.\"","The light in the walls steadied and hardened.","\" But the truly critical things, Dreamer. The things I hid in the deep places, behind curtains of years, in the coils of serpents that eat their own tails. Those were never supposed to be grasped. Not by him. Not by anyone. One of them is here. THE Quill of Chronos.\"","Noah listened intently.","\"I made a great many things in my life ,\" Atlas said. \" Most of them were cleverness for its own sake. Cleverness is worth having for its own sake. But a few of them were more. A few of them were what I built once I understood, finally, what I was up against, and how badly I was losing.\"","The light pulsed beside him. \" THE Quill of Chronos is one of those. With it, I wrote an inscription. A single inscription, into the weaving of an Elsedimension, and that inscription twisted time itself to my favor. Do you understand what a being could do who could write time?\"","\"I am beginning to,\" Noah said. He thought of a serpent eating its own tail, and a place where hours blew past like seconds.","\"You built this whole Dimension around the Quill, yes?\"","\"I built this whole Dimension to hide the Quill, and to hide the inscription I wrote with it, and to keep both out of the hands of beings who would use them to do to existence what I only ever did to a single Elsedimension.\"","Atlas’s voice dropped. \" And now a Lineage sent by THE SLEEPLESS FIEND has found the door to it. Because they were here, THE Sleepless Fiend should sense something. I built these Elsedimensions to keep his kind out, specifically his kind, and he has never once set foot in one, which means he cannot simply follow us in. But nothing is guaranteed. Nothing has ever been guaranteed in existence. You saw that with the Vasiliou Provenance Lineage\"","...!","\" Then we move quickly ,\" Noah said.","\" Yes. We get the Quill. We get out.\"","The old man of light almost smiled. \" And then, Dreamer, and only then, you can play at inducing Roots and dreaming impossibilities to your heart’s content. But first, my Quill. Before the winter and Immense Ones and everything else in existence remembers this place is here.\"","Noah looked down the spiraling path, into the deep of the serpent, and the slow light pulsed in the walls, and somewhere far below, at the core they could not yet see, something old and precise waited for the first hand in an age that had a right to it.","He did not intend to walk the whole of that path as he had a faster way now.","\"I dream ,\" Noah said, quiet, \" that we do not have to search for long. That the Relic is close. That we are coming up on it now.\"","WAA!","|25 Provenance Essence expended.|","|You have dreamed a shortening of the way as you bypass many traps of time. Existence is adjusting to agree.|","|The distance between you and THE Quill of Chronos has begun to collapse toward zero...|","The spiraling path blurred! The slow light in the walls streamed past, faster and faster, the coil unwinding around them, the core rushing up to meet them, and the four of them dissolved forward into the deep of the serpent of time!","...!"]},{"number":5782,"title":"Chapter 5782: Chapter 5781: Impossibilities! I","paragraphs":["The core of the serpent was a storm that did not move.","Or rather, it moved in a way that had nothing to do with going anywhere. The four of them stood at the mouth of a chamber vaster than the coil that had brought them to it, and across the whole of that chamber ran rivers.","Rivers of time. They wheeled in slow circles around the center, ring inside ring, dozens of them, each one a current of raw Dimensionality of Time given a shape and a course, and where a river passed near the wall the stone aged a thousand years in an instant and un-aged a thousand more as the current curved away.","One ring ran forward. The next ran back. The next ran forward again, faster, and the air between them shimmered where the two speeds met, so that a mote of dust caught in the seam might be young on one side of itself and ancient on the other.","At the very center, held in the still eye where all the rings turned around nothing, a quill spun!","It was purple shading toward gold, no larger than a feather from a large bird, and it turned end over end in the emptiness at the heart of the storm, and it was the most patient thing Noah had ever looked at.","Everything in that chamber raged. The quill only turned, slow and even, as though it had all the time there had ever been, which, Noah understood, was very nearly the case.","\" There ,\" Atlas said. An old man made of light, standing at the mouth of a storm he had built. \" THE Quill of Chronos. Exactly where I left it.\"","Rose looked at the wheeling rings watched intently. Achilles stood very still, watching the currents with an attention Noah had not seen on him before.","\"I did not hide it behind a lock,\" Atlas said. \" Locks are for things you expect a clever being to reach. I hid it behind time itself.\"","He gestured at the rings, and the light of him flickered where a current passed. \" Every one of those rivers is Dimensionality of Time. Walk into them, and they will spend you and revert you for millions and billions of years with the degradation of Time itself. They will pour age into you until there is nothing of you left that has not already happened, and then they will keep pouring, and you will be a thing that was, and never quite is.\"","\" It works on nearly anything. When I set it turning, I judged it strong enough to drain a being approaching the level of an Immense One.\"","The old man’s light dimmed. \" But time did not sit still while I was gone. The rivers have been turning for ages, and a river of time that turns for ages grows deeper. Whatever I set them to drain when I built this place, they would drain something grander now. I do not know how much grander.\"","He looked at the rings for a long moment.","\" My weavings here cannot carry us through that,\" Atlas said as he turned toward Noah.","\"So, you may have to put in some work again.\"","Noah looked at the rings, and began to gather himself for the crossing!","But at this time...","\" Can I be of use,\" Achilles said, \" and not just stand at the back?\"","Noah turned.","The Emperor King had stepped forward a pace, his crystalline eyes fixed on the wheeling rivers, and there was a hunger in his stillness that had nothing to do with battle.","\"I wanted the first thing I assimilated after THE Sealed One to be grand, \" Achilles said.","\"I have not taken anything into myself since you cut the old monster loose. \"","He nodded at the storm. \" This... seems grand. Heavy Dimensionality of Time, grown stronger across the ages, strong enough to spend something nearing an Immense One. I would like to try.\"","...!","Noah considered him.","He was curious, in truth. THE Sealed One had wanted this Factor of Assimilation badly enough, and Noah had cut it free without yet seeing it used on anything worth using it on. A river of time that could drain a near-Immense being was worth using it on!","\" Try ,\" Noah said.","Achilles walked toward the storm.","He did not rush it. He crossed the floor of the chamber toward the outermost ring at an even pace, a young king in a coat of shifting color, and Rose took a half-step after him and then made herself stop with eyes filled with worry.","The first river caught him before he touched it!","Its influence reached out ahead of the current itself, and where it fell on Achilles his existence began to age! It happened without violence, without a sound. The young king’s face lined.","The color went out of his shifting coat, greying at the edges. His shoulders drew down, and his stride shortened, and by the time he stood a single pace from the raging river he was not a young king anymore!","He was an old man, bent and thin and worn, with a thousand extra years hanging off him that had arrived in the space of ten steps, and Rose clenched her fists!","Achilles reached the river. He lifted one aged, trembling hand toward it.","\" Assimilate.\"","The word came out of him slow and cracked, an old man’s whisper, and the vibrant river of time buzzed at the sound of it.","Then it went out, not aside and not around, but into him! The whole raging ring of Dimensionality of Time buzzed once, a rising note, and poured into the old man’s outstretched hand and up his arm and down into the deep of him, the current unwinding from its course and vanishing into his existence entirely, until where a river had turned there was only empty air, and the ring inside it wheeled on as though nothing had been taken from beside it.","Noah watched, and read the body of the thing that had been an old man!","The age was already reversing. The moment the river entered him, the years it had poured into him found somewhere else to go, absorbed and reweighted and made a part of the whole, and Achilles’s bent frame straightened, the lines smoothing out of his face, the color returning to his coat, the young king coming back up out of the old one like how a drowned man comes up out of a river.","The snow in the surroundings whipped down heavily!","By the time he lowered his hand he was himself again, young-faced and ancient-eyed, and he did not stop.","On to the next river. He would Age, he would whisper, he would assimilate and come back young, and move again. Then the next!","One after another, Achilles Adrastia crossed the storm of time, and it was the strangest crossing Noah had ever watched. Every river spent him, and every river he took, and with each one the taking came easier, because his existence was becoming the thing it swallowed. By the sixth river he barely aged at all approaching it. By the ninth, the influence that had bent him double at the first ring passed over him like a draft through an open door.","Noah’s own eyes had grown heavy with time. Standing near so much raw Dimensionality of Time, even from the outside, even untouched, pressed a weight of ages against his existence, and he held it off with his Root seamlessly.","By the last river, there was nothing left to spend.","Noah looked at Achilles as he approached the final raging ring, and his sight told him a thing he had not expected. The signature of Achilles’s existence and the signature of the river had become the same. Not similar. The same .","The Emperor King had assimilated so much Dimensionality of Time that he no longer read as a being standing near a river of time. He read as a river of time that had learned to walk!","The last current did not age him at all!","Achilles stood before it, whole and young, and lifted his hand, and did not whisper. He did not need to. He waved his fingers, once, an easy motion, and the last river of Dimensionality of Time uncoiled from its ancient course and came to him, flowing and dancing around his hand like water poured over stone, curling between his fingers, before it too sank into him and was gone!","The storm was over, the chamber gone still.","Where dozens of rivers had wheeled around a spinning quill, there was only air, and a young king standing at the center of where they had been, shining.","His whole body held a stellar purple luster now, deep and slow and terrible! A light that pulsed the way the walls of the coil had pulsed, like something very large breathing in its sleep. He looked at his own hands, and then he looked up, past the empty air, at nothing Noah could see.","\"It is not a river ,\" Achilles said quietly . \"I always thought it was a river. Everyone does. You stand in it, and it carries you, and one day it carries you off.\"","He turned his shining hands over. \"It is not a river. It is a room. I have been standing in one room my whole existence, thinking the walls were moving, and they were not moving. And now I have taken the room into myself, and I can feel the shape of it, and it has doors I never knew were there. \"","His ancient eyes came down to Noah’s. \" I... did not know time had so many doors.\"","HUUM!","Noah floated forward.","His eyes lingered on Achilles for a moment!","\" The Dimensionality you just assimilated,\" Noah said, \" may be enough to serve as the basis of your own Chorionic Gonadotropin. Get ready to use it soon.\"","He then crossed the still air to the center of the chamber, to the empty eye where the storm had turned, and there the quill still spun, patient, purple and gold, waiting. He reached the place where it turned and looked at it, and the weaving of it opened to him.","| THE QUILL OF CHRONOS|","|A Relic of the engineer known as ATLAS. Function: The inscription of Time.|","|With it, an inscription may be written into the weaving of a place that bends the flow of Time to the writer’s favor.|","|Grade: ??????|","|Origin: ??????|","|Remaining capacity: ??????|","|Further functions: ??????|","Half of what it was would not resolve! Question marks sat where the deeper truth of the thing hid behind a wall Noah could not yet read. It did not matter. Atlas would know, and Noah had not come to read the thing. He had come to take it.","A bubble of the Provenance of THE Human Dreamer closed around the quill, and it stopped spinning, held in a dream of stilness, and the whole chamber went quiet in a new way, as though the last turning thing in it had finally been allowed to rest!","He did not intend to linger in a place a dead man had warned him Immense Ones might sense.","\" Let’s go.\"","He imposed his Provenance around all four of them, and the core of the serpent of time was gone!","—","The Glacial Elsedimension Mountain rose white and endless out of the deep of Lucy’s Legacy, and the snow never stopped falling on it.","It was a mountain that was also a sealed reality, and it climbed higher than a mountain had any right to, its slopes pale and clean and softened under a blanket of snow.","Near its shoulder, where the slope leveled into a wide white shelf, stood a monastery. It had been built out of golden Existential Conduits, the veins of existence coaxed into walls and a low roof and a single arched door, and the gold of it glowed warm and steady through the falling white, the one warm thing in a world of cold and quiet.","Snow gathered on its roof and did not melt.","Snow filled the air around it, drifting slow and soundless, each flake catching the gold of the walls as it fell, so that the monastery sat inside a slow golden storm of its own light!","Nothing moved on that mountain but the snow.","Nothing sounded but the snow, which made no sound at all. It was the most peaceful place in all of existence!","And Noah sat outside the monastery in the middle of it, on the white shelf, and let the snow fall on his crystalline shoulders and did not brush it off.","A golden bubble of light bloomed in the air before him soon after.","It held a spinning quill, held still. And a breath after it appeared, two more shapes came into being on the snow beside it. A green-haired woman and the king who shone with the luster of a hundred assimilated rivers of time. Noah nodded to them.","\" Welcome to the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity ,\" Noah said. \" It is...somewhat safe here. As safe as anywhere is, now.\"","Rose looked at the falling snow, at the golden monastery, at the endless white slope, and for the first time since the orchard, her shoulders came down from around her ears!","Achilles did not look at any of it. He was looking at his own hands, which still pulsed with that slow stellar purple, his whole existence buzzing with Dimensionality it had not finished settling, a transformation still turning over inside him.","Noah watched him for a moment.","\" Your existence is transforming ,\" Noah said. \"It will keep transforming for a while yet as that makes now as good a time as any.\"","He rose from the snow. \" Why don’t we see whether the impossible is possible?\"","He had done it once already. Inducing a unique Chorionic Gonadotropin in a being already turning with fresh Dimensionality of Time could not be so much harder than that, right?","And there was more in it than kindness. A Dream of Assimilation, spun out across existence through a being who became everything he touched, was a Dream Noah would be steering. The further it spun, the more Provenance it would return to the hand that dreamed it!","He looked at the shining king in the falling snow as his eyes burned with grand ambitions!","\" Sit ,\" Noah said. \" And dream with me.\""]},{"number":5783,"title":"Chapter 5783: Chapter 5782: Impossibilities! II","paragraphs":["On the Glacial Mountain, the snow continued to fall.","It lay a hand deep on the golden eaves of the monastery and drifted against the arched door, and it filled the air so completely that the far slopes had gone grey and then simply vanished.","A few Conduit Lifeforms sheltered under the roof, their light dimmed to embers.","Out on the open shelf, two figures sat facing each other, and only one of them was comfortable.","Noah wore nothing heavier than thin garments of his own Provenance, and the snow slid off his crystalline shoulders as if it had been a feather all along.","Across from him, Achilles sat buried in a coat of many-colored authorty so thick it looked like armor, and still, every little while, a shiver ran through him.","Noah closed his eyes.","His Provenance moved around him in slow blue-gold rivers, and he let himself feel all of it, the turning of his Root, the weight of his existence settling deeper into itself. What he felt was simple.","It felt good!","A human felt good after a meal, or among good company, or at the end of a day’s work that had turned out well. Understanding existence felt exactly like that to Noah. Every time he stood a little higher than the day before, the same warmth rose in him that a farmer might feel looking over a field he had planted himself.","For some, that height wore that feeling out of a climber. That past a certain point the view stopped being beautiful and became merely tiresome, and whoever stood there grew bored, and cold, and looked down on everything smaller.","And yet here he was, higher than he had ever stood, and he loved it more than ever!","He put that down to the human at the center of him.","Humanity, as far as he could tell, was the part of a being that kept being glad. Without it the climb became a hunger, and at the end of that road waited an emotionless thing. He would much rather stay the kind of being who could sit in the snow and enjoy a hard day’s work.","And this was a hard day’s work. A Root of Immensity was a thing a being had to grow for itself, by every account in existence. He meant to start one inside someone else. At home, in his Existential Root Domain, the same work had already begun with THE Infiniverse and Ruination, but they were bound to him and would come easier. Achilles was a stranger’s existence, built in a stranger’s grammar.","That was what made it worth doing!","Nothing complicated was needed. His own template, built from studying an Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin, would not be copied into the king. Instead his two Provenances would take what made Achilles himself, his genome, his Assimilation Factor above all, and press those into the shape of a signal that was Achilles’s alone.","It would only work on an existence tall enough to carry it. Below a hundred in any measure, the forming alone would tear a being apart. A Root formed on its own only somewhere near four or five hundred, in Trueness or Pondus or Provenance.","Achilles should have enough to survive the attempt!","Noah opened his eyes.","\" This will strain you, \" he said. \" It may collapse you. Whatever happens, hold on to what you are.\"","A smile moved at the corner of the king’s mouth, the first Noah had seen from him on the mountain. \"I have been holding on to what I am for weeks now, let’s go!\"","Two rivers of Provenance left Noah and went into the king!","The first moved through Achilles like lamplight through a dark house, room by room, and in every room it found something that had once belonged to someone else and now belonged entirely to him. A First Cause from a fallen Observable Existences. An Infinity drunk from a dying sea. A thousand authorities, and not one of them sat in him like a stone. They had all become Achilles, as rain that falls into a river becomes the river, and at the heart of it all turned the thing THE Sealed One had wanted: the Assimilation Factor.","Noah’s second river closed around it and began to press.","He did not wrench it. He coaxed it inward, steadily, toward the turning, self-feeding form of a becoming-signal, and after a long moment of resistance, the Factor began to follow.","Light gathered at the center of the king!","A knot of many colors drew in on itself beneath the heavy coat and brightened as it drew. A quarter formed. A third. Half. For one held breath it turned bright and nearly whole, and Noah let himself think it might simply finish.","But...","It broke!","BOOM!","Dark lines split across Achilles’s existence like fractures through ice under too much weight! The signal was grander than the vessel that held it, and the vessel was coming apart, and Noah began to draw his Provenance back before the cracks could reach the edges of the man.","He never finished.","Achilles turned on the failing signal and did what he had done his whole life to everything that threatened him. He took it. He assimilated the collapsing Chorionic Gonadotropin whole, and the cracks slowed, and sealed shut.","The king lifted his head, old eyes burning as blood spurted from his nose and mouth!","\" Again!\" he roared into the snow. \" Do it again!\"","Noah pressed the Factor a second time!","It came together faster, because a piece of the first was already woven into Achilles, and it climbed past half before the dark lines came as it fell apart. The king did not wait for them to spread. He swallowed the second failure himself and bared his teeth for a third.","The third broke at two thirds, and he took it.","The fourth broke brighter, throwing the shadows of the eaves across the snow in long gold bars, and the Conduit Lifeforms woke under the roof and turned toward him.","By the fifth, the snow around the two of them had melted in a ring from sheer pressure of existence!","By the sixth, Noah’s Provenance was running hot, and Achilles’s coat had split along one shoulder, and beneath the tear his skin shone with a light that was not quite any color.","Everytime a blank Chorionic Gonadotropin tried to form, it failed!","He caught the seventh at the very edge of collapse, with a sound like a man lifting something far too heavy and refusing to set it down.","The eighth failed closer still, and he took that too!","He was heaving at this point as a distant Rose stood imperiously trying not to show any emotion!","On the ninth, the signal reached the point where every other had cracked, and...it did not crack.","There was nothing left in Achilles for it to strain against. Eight failed becoming-signals were woven into him now, and the shape was no longer a stranger to his existence. The ninth did not have to force its way in. It only had to finish.","It finished!","The Assimilation Chorionic Gonadotropin held!","A pillar of light tore out of Achilles Adrastia and struck straight up into the falling snow, every color he had ever assimilated turning through it at once! The snow above the shelf blew outward in a vast ring! The monastery’s golden walls hummed!","| An Assimilation Chorionic Gonadotropin has formed within the lifeform, Achilles Adrastia.|","|Stability: LOW. The foundation is uneven. It was built from nine attempts, and eight of them remain visible in it.|","Noah could see them now: eight ragged seams running through the turning signal, eight places where the whole of it might one day split.","So he spent more.","He ran his Provenance along the seams one by one, smoothing each into the next until they lay flat in a single foundation, and the pillar brightened as he worked! Its ragged edges drew in! Its hum deepened into something clear and certain, and the drifting flakes caught fire in a hundred colors as they fel!","His own Root had been built around a true piece of an Immense One’s becoming, pressed into his hands by Vakochev.","Achilles had no such piece, only his own Dimensionality and Noah’s help, so his Root would begin lower. But lower was not small.","Starting from a king who had swallowed the powers of a dozen lineages and a hundred rivers of time, lower was still very high indeed.","And Achilles, alongside many others, could be seen as lifeforms with their own grand dreams and stories, but it did not bother Noah for being able to help such beings.","One did not grow grander alone. Nor was it shameful for one to receive the help of another to get to where they were.","Did he not receive help from Vakochev with the Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin? Did he not help Vakochev himself to have one of his bodies freed?","He did not doubt that in time, Achilles would be able to form a Root by himself. After all, the fucker could Assimilate anything. What he was doing was giving a guiding hand and accelerating the entire process.","Nobody was alone in existence as connections made many things possible and allowed for progress to be much faster, and Dreams...connected a great deal of beings as Noah would freely do whatever he wanted to do to expand his Dream, and any dreams of those around him.","|A Root has been induced and formed in another lifeform.|","|The Assimilation Chorionic Gonadotropin has formed in the lifeform, Achilles Adrastia. It is a Unique Conceptual Root of Immensity.|","|For guiding the dream of another and allowing it to bloom to fruition, your Provenance has increased by +50.|","|THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer will continue to gain Provenance depending on how far the Dream of the lifeform, Achilles Adrastia, extends across existence.|","...!","Yes. There was also his own selfishness as he would benefit from this!","Achilles sat inside his pillar of light with his coat torn from one shoulder, breathing hard, staring at nothing Noah could see. Something inside him had just begun to grow, and he did not yet know how large it meant to become.","Noah’s eyes shone!","He looked at the king and the pillar and the shining result of an afternoon’s work in the snow, and he saw it for what it was. A piece of glorious engineering, finished well.","Impossibilities would only remain impossibilities for others.","Not for him. Never for him!"]},{"number":5784,"title":"Chapter 5784: Chapter 5783: Targets and Roots I","paragraphs":["The achievement of one was the achievement of another.","Noah looked at Achilles sitting inside the fading pillar of his own light, and he could see it on the man’s face. The king’s eyes had gone wide and far away, full of something that had no easy name, a mix of awe and grief and a strange new hunger, as if he had just stepped outside a house he had lived in all his life and found the sky was bigger than he had ever been told.","Noah knew that look! He had worn it himself, not so long ago, sitting in a dark he had just reforged himself out of.","Achilles would be seeing existence differently now. The Existential Conduits rising through the snow, pillars of flowing authority stretching away into the grey. The small incandescent Conduit Lifeforms drifting under the monastery eaves, which a moment ago he would not have been able to perceive at all.","How beautiful all of it was, and how complicated, and how much of it had always been right there in front of him. And beyond that, maybe something more!","A man who had just swallowed a storm of raw Dimensionality of Time was probably not going to feel an hour pass the same way ever again.","Time...","Noah turned his head. Behind him, still wrapped in its bubble of dreaming Provenance, THE Quill of Chronos hung in the falling snow, purple and gold and perfectly still.","Then it was gone!","The bubble shrank to a point of light and vanished, and the voice of an old man rose out of the ring on Noah’s finger, dry as ever.","\" You shine too brightly sometimes with what you can do, \" Atlas said. \" Pulling a Root out of a stranger in the middle of a snowstorm. Honestly. I’ll take the Quill, unlock it, and confirm everything inside it still works after all this time. As for the Inscription I have in mind, a Rare Gu is still a requirement, sadly. No way around it. We can only forge it after you obtain one. When you do, we start. For now, you have attracted something with all that brilliance.\"","...!","Noah lifted his head.","High above the white shelf, where the snow thinned into the grey of the upper air, an eye was opening. It was enormous, gold-flecked and bright, and it bloomed across the sky like a lamp being uncovered, and Noah recognized it at once.","Poona!","| THE Dimensional Devourer, Poona, looks down on the Glacial Mountain with great interest.|","|She says she did not expect another Root to rise on the mountain you only just began residing in.|","|She is astonished. She is excited. She says she cannot wait to see what else might arise in the Legacy, now that you are here.|","The golden eye lingered a moment longer, bright with something that looked very much like delight, and then it closed and was gone, and the grey sky was only sky again.","The snow fluttered!","A figure stepped out of it onto the shelf.","Verys, the Legacy Keeper, in his immaculate black suit and his heavy fur-lined cloak, the ridges along his throat pressed closed against the cold. He crossed the snow and bowed to Noah, deep and correct, and as he straightened his large dark eyes slid, just for a moment, to the multicolored figure of Achilles, and stayed there a beat longer than courtesy strictly required.","\" Sir ,\" Verys said. \" I have been tasked with passing on a message.\"","Noah waited.","\"The Legacy wishes to ascertain the talent and power of its new entrants. Those who stand to become Immense Ones in the wake of the Long Night.\"","The Keeper clasped his webbed hands before him. \" It is an opportunity to exchange information and Dimensionality in a controlled setting, without the risk of death. In one day, all Lifeforms with a Root of Immensity will have the chance to spar with others within this Legacy.\"","He paused, and his eyes went once more to Achilles.","\"It appears the Legacy was waiting for one additional being before it began. That quota has now been met.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone, and he gave a slight nod.","A chance to see others on the path to becoming Immense Ones? Other Roots, other ways of climbing, other Dreams? That was worth seeing! And it was a day away, which meant he still had a day to get things done first. Very convenient!","He looked over at Achilles, and past him, at the green-haired woman standing a short way off in the snow, watching her king with eyes that were, frankly, a little hungry.","Noah rose to his feet.","\" Take some time to settle into your new existence,\" he said to Achilles. \" Then decide what you want to do. You could stay in this Legacy until you become an Immense One. If you leave for external existence as you are now, you may simply be eaten.\"","He brushed a little snow from his sleeve. \" Your memories of THE Sealed One, and anything else that comes back clearer now, let me know once your existence has settled.\"","Achilles opened his multicolored eyes.","\"I will not forget these favors easily ,\" he said, and his voice was heavy. \"I will be sure to repay you.\"","Noah only nodded.","Favors. Well...they were, in a sense. He had not done any of it purely for Achilles’s sake, though. Every step further the king’s Dream spun across existence would come back to him as Provenance, and he had just planted a very large Dream indeed. It was a good investment! He saw no reason to spoil a moment of gratitude by pointing that out.","He turned to the Keeper.","\" He can get his own abode, yes? His own Elsedimension Mountain?\"","\"Yes, Sir. \" Verys bowed. \" My colleague will take him there.\"","There was a flash, and another Legacy Keeper stood beside Verys in the snow!","She was a Provenance Lifeform, and she was gorgeous in a manner that seemed almost deliberate, as if someone had set out to design a servant nobody could look away from. Red hair fell past her shoulders in heavy waves, bright as a banked fire against all that white.","She wore the same black uniform as Verys, cut to a figure that was generously curved and made no effort to hide it, and a fur stole draped across her shoulders. Her face was fine-boned and warm, her smile easy, and when she bowed toward Achilles her eyes were shining.","\"I am Tatiana ,\" she said. \" I will be serving Sir...Achilles, is it? I am here to lead you to your Elsedimension Mountain.\" Her smile widened by a degree. \" And to serve any of your needs.\"","...!","Before Achilles could answer, Rose was beside him!","She had been a short way off in the snow. Now she simply was not, and was instead at his side. She reached up, took hold of the back of Achilles’s neck, pinched, and lifted, and the Emperor King of a thousand assimilated authorities rose to his feet exactly like a cat picked up by the scruff!","Rose did not look at him. She looked at Tatiana, and her voice was very cold.","\" He won’t need anyone to serve him ,\" she said. \" Just show us to this mountain.\"","...!","Even Noah blinked!","Tatiana held Rose’s gaze for a long moment! Then she bowed, smoothly, with a smile that had gone just slightly cold at the edges, and a golden rift opened in the air beside her. Achilles, still held by the neck, managed to turn his head far enough to meet Noah’s eyes, and nodded to him one last time, a little ruefully.","Then Rose let go, and he stepped forward after Tatiana into the rift, and Rose followed right behind him, close enough to step on his heels.","The rift closed. The snow filled in where it had been.","Noah looked at the empty place a moment longer. A Keeper of Lucy’s Legacy had bowed first. Having watched Achilles get lifted by the scruff of his own neck, he could understand why!","Then he turned his attention inward.","Verys had not moved. The Keeper stood a respectful distance away on the shelf, hands clasped, waiting in the storm, and the snow came down heavier around both of them, thick enough now that the monastery’s golden walls were only a warm blurr. Noah sat back down in the middle of it and closed his eyes.","He had finished it. The first page!","A target handed to him by the Caretaker, in the frozen underworld, on behalf of whatever the Long Night truly was. The Assimilation Factor was severed from THE Sealed One, cleanly, and the man who had carried it was walking into his own new Root with a woman holding his collar. The Caretaker had told him that he would have his reward before the next page.","So what would the next page be?","He reached for the cold. Everything else in existence reached away from it. He reached toward it, down into the long quiet chill of the Long Night that lay under the snow and under the mountain and under everything. He let it fill his senses.","And he felt it take hold of him, and pull!","The Glacial Mountain fell away, and the golden monastery, and the patient Keeper in the storm, and Noah felt himself drawn down, and down, toward the Cold Place once more!","---","The Cold Place had not changed much at all.","The seas of white and blue still ran to every horizon, slow and shining and endless. The drifting crystals still hung in the air like dust in a sunbeam that had frozen solid. And on the rivers, rank beyond rank, the Hollow Night Lifeforms still sat in their silence, blank-eyed and cross-legged, each one wrapped in its own turning pillar of cold. Beasts and giants and things with too many limbs, lions with the wrong heads, shapes Noah had no names for, thousands upon thousands of them, and not one had moved since he left!","Before them the cold surged!","It came up out of the frozen seas in great rolling rivers and poured over the seated ranks and away into the dark, and the pillars around each of the dead drank from it, and the whole vast underworld breathed in and out with it, slow as a sleeper!","Noah stood among them, the only one standing, and felt the cold wash past his crystalline skin as a breeze.","It was strange, honestly! The last time he stood in this place he had been half-frozen, drinking a winter that was trying to kill him, and ten hollow things had come at him with shapes that could crush Dimensions. Now it felt almost like visiting a house he had once been sick in.","Familiar, a little grim, and nowhere near as frightening as the first time. Was that what it meant to grow? Places stayed the same size, and you did not?","\" You finished the page.\"","She was there! The pages turned around her in the air, slow sheets of ice catching the pale light, and her frost dress moved like snow that never finished falling. The Caretaker looked at him with those cognizant eyes, the only eyes in all that frozen dark that actually saw anything, and her face held nothing at all.","\"I did ,\" Noah said. \" The thread between two lifeforms is cut. The host is his own again.\"","\"I know .\" She did not sound pleased, or displeased. \" You chose to cut the thread and leave the man standing. It is already so, and it was already so before you chose it. Here is what I said you would have.\"","She lifted one pale hand, and something rose out of the frozen river at her feet.","It was small. That surprised him! A sliver of crystal no longer than a finger, pale blue at its edges and white at its heart, and its inside was not smooth but branched, fine and intricate, a snowflake grown down into itself layer apon layer until the pattern was too small to follow. It pulsed! Slowly, once every few breaths, a faint light moved through it from the heart outward, and every time it did, Noah felt his own Root answr.","He knew that pulse!","It was the same slow signal Vakochev had pressed into his hands in the snow above the frozen forest. Keep growing this. Do not stop. Fainter, much fainter, and cold all the way through, but the same!","The crystal drifted across the space between them and settled into his open palm, and his sight opened it.","| LESSER KRYOS EXISTENTIAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN|","|A natural treasure of THE Long Night. It forms only in the deepest cold, where the frozen remains of past Nights settle for an Age around what an Immense One left behind, and condense.|","|Potency: roughly one fourth of a genuine Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin.|","|Nature: a signal of becoming, frozen. It carries the chill of THE Long Night in every layer and will not warm.|","|Use: may be absorbed to feed the growth of an existing Root, or used as a seed around which a Root may be induced in another existence.|","|It will not disperse. Cold things keep.|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone!","A fourth of the real thing! That did not sound like much, until one remembered what the real thing had done! A single whole unit, pressed into his hands with a warning and a shrug, had become the seed of everything he was now. And this one would not run out in a day. It would simply sit in his palm, pulsing, and wait for him to decide what to do with it.","He already had a few ideas.","He closed his hand over the crystal. It was cold, and it stayed cold, and he did not mind at all!","\" That is the reward ,\" the Caretaker said. \" Now the next page.\"","She plucked a sheet of ice from the air. It turned once in her fingers, and then she let it go, and it drifted to him and hung before his face, and in the ice an image was already forming!","A face. Or something wearing a face, as a hall wears a door. Vast, cold, and heavy with the weight of a trillion extinguished Dimensions. A gaze Noah had last felt closing around him over a frozen forest, greedy and patient, reaching for a newborn Root as if it had every right to.","THE UNPAID COLLECTOR!","...!","Noah looked at the page, then at the Caretaker, then back at the page again!","\" Are you... serious?\" he said.","The Caretaker did not answer, because she had already answered, and they both knew it.","\" The first page was a man with half a monster in him, sitting alone in an orchard ,\" Noah said. \"I could do that. This one is an Immense One. \"","He tapped the ice. \" The difficulty seems to have risen somewhat. From doable, to impossible.\"","Doable to impossible. Not even impossible for him to fucking boast about how his Dream could make impossibilities into reality. He had to be somewhat realistic!","Noah was not afraid. He did not do afraid. But he was honest with himself, and honesty said a being in the low six hundreds did not simply go hunting an Immense One on a whim!","The Caretaker’s pages turned around her, slow.","\" The Cold believes you may be uniquely capable of drawing THE UNPAID COLLECTOR out,\" she said. \" It does not ask you to kill him, or even to wound him. Bring him into whatever domain you are standing in, and hold him there. A few seconds. \"","Her flat eyes held his. \" That is the whole of your part. After that, your part will be done.\"","...!"]},{"number":5785,"title":"Chapter 5785: Chapter 5784: Targets and Roots II","paragraphs":["Leaving the Cold Place was easy. It was the page that came back with him.","Noah drew his attention up out of the frozen underworld and settled it into the body that waited for him in his Existential Root Domain, and the sheet of ice came too, hanging at the edge of his thoughts with a vast, greedy face set into it. THE UNPAID COLLECTOR!","An Immense One. Bring him into a domain and hold him there a few seconds!","Impossible, he had told the Caretaker.","Well...maybe not entirely impossible!","The Collector was a being who wanted things. That was the whole of his nature, written into his very name. And not so long ago, in the Vasiliou Elsedimension, that same Immense One had looked at Thalia and promised, very calmly, that at any moment he chose he would rip them in half.","Noah did not need to find the Collector. He needed the Collector to come looking for something he wanted, in a place Noah had chosen. And for that, he needed Thalia.","The plan was only budding yet. But it was budding nicely!","He set it aside for now, because there was something closer in front of him, and he had been meaning to get to it.","The Existential Root Domain stretched out around him in every direction, soft and boundless and entirely his. Blue-gold clouds drifted through it without any wind to move them at al, and far below, THE Infiniverse turned slowly in its singularity, a whole empire held the size of a breath, its Realms glittering like frost on glass.","Threads of light ran out from it into the dark, strung to every Dimension it had ever touched. It was quiet here in a way nowhere else in existence was quiet. Nothing entered unless Noah wished it. Nothing could.","And floating before him, waiting, were the two who had been with him longest!","THE Infiniverse hung in the clouds with her starlit eyes half-lidded, her long hair drifting around her like a slow tide of night sky. Beside her, Ruination floated straight-backed and composed, her crimson gaze steady on him, the Circlet of the Quintessential Ruin catching the blue-gold light across her brow.","\" Enough experimenting ,\" Noah said. \" Enough theories. What needed to be proven has been proven. The two of you can forge your own Roots now.\"","\"And there should be an overabundance of boons sitting in THE Tide That Owes Nothing by now. Everything I have given lately. Cutting a man loose from THE Sealed One. Handing a Root to someone who never had one. Use all of it. Every return. Take everything the Tide has been holding and spend it on two Roots of Immensity for the two of you.\"","...!","THE Infiniverse’s eyes opened fully.","Then prompts began to bloom, Ruination’s prompts, crisp and orderly as ever!","|All nine Foundations, including THE Tide, have exceeded their previous ranking. All nine have been granted a ranking of THE INEFFABLE VERSE.|","|THE Unkneeling Crown: INEFFABLE.|","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing: INEFFABLE.|","|THE Mirror That Keeps: INEFFABLE.|","|THE Hunger That Refines: INEFFABLE.|","|THE Unmoved Verdict: INEFFABLE.|","|THE Pure Trajectory: INEFFABLE.|","|THE All-Drawing Stillness: INEFFABLE.|","|THE Remembered Truth: INEFFABLE.|","|THE Sovereign Existence: INEFFABLE.|","|Of note: THE Tide That Owes Nothing no longer returns a number. Its return upon giving has transformed. It now returns what can be dreamed.|","...!","What can be dreamed!","Noah read that line twice. For as long as he had carried the Tide, it had paid him in multiples. Twenty thousand times. A hundred thousand times. Big numbers, but numbers, with a ceiling somewhere even if he had never reached it.","Now there was no number at all. The return on a gift was whatever he could dream it into being, and he was THE Human Dreamer.","He nodded once.","Then he sat down in the air, cross-legged, as if the clouds were a floor, and closed his eyes. Across from him, THE Infiniverse and Ruination did the same, three figures seated in a loose ring in the middle of a boundless blue-gold sky.","He already knew what he wanted for each of them.","Ruination had always been information to him, from the very first. The voice in his head that counted his enemies, predicted their blows, kept his records, told him when he was about to do something grand and foolish. So her Root would lean toward information. Toward knowing, and keeping what she knew.","THE Infiniverse had always been existence to him. His whole empire lived inside her. Realms, oceans, the sleepers in their chrysalis, all of it held in her as a world holds its seas. So her Root would lean toward existence itself, and toward Dimensionality, toward growing more of both.","He would only guide the lean. What each of them became would be theirs.","He raised his head.","Above the three of them, existence tore!","It split open like a seam in cloth, and out of the tear poured light, liquid and heavy, blue and gold, flooding down into the Domain in slow rivers that shone as they fell!","| THE Tide That Owes Nothing has released its returns.|","|Recent acts of giving recognized: the severing of the Assimilation Factor from THE Sealed One; the forging of a Root of Immensity in another lifeform; the steering of a grand Dream; and all that has accumulated since the last release.|","|Return: PURE NATAL BUILDING BLOCKS OF CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN.|","|The raw material of becoming, unshaped and unowned, as it exists before any being claims it.|","...!","Noah looked up at the pouring light!","Nine attempts. He had needed nine attempts in the snow to force a single Root into Achilles, out of nothing but the king’s own failures. And here was the thing itself, the stuff that becoming-signals were made of, pouring out of the sky by the river.","He reached up and took hold of the rivers!","There was no grabbing in it, only guiding, as a farmer guides water into a field where the channels are already dug. Half the flood he drew down toward Ruination, and it poured into her, and she stiffened where she sat as the light filled her.","The other half he drew toward THE Infiniverse, and she tipped her head back and received it with her eyes closed and her lips parted, like dry earth taking in the first rain of a long season.","And inside both of them, two signals began to form!","He kept his hands on the work, steady, turning Ruination’s toward information and THE Infiniverse’s toward existence. He watched for the first crack, the first wobble, the first dark line spreading out from a half-built signal, and it never came!","It was nothing like Achilles!","Both signals rose clean and whole, turning without a tremor, each one brighter than the last moment, drinking the pure material of becoming from the Tide and settling it into themselves as if they had always known where it went. There was no strain. No fracture. No roaring for another try.","Noah had come prepared to spend everything, and he had not even needed to reach for the Lesser Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin sitting cold in his keeping. The Tide’s gift was simply enough!","And while he worked, he looked at the two of them.","They had always been there. From the beginning! Ruination was connected to his budding infinity, and THE Infiniverse was a floating island in the Beast World!","Through the wars and the casting out and the long dark under the stone, through every mad, greedy, reckless thing he had ever done, they had stayed, and they had never once asked what it would cost them. His most loyal companions. And he wanted more for them than worrying about him. He wanted them to be happy. Fulfilled. Something more than the two voices that kept him alive.","But he also knew them, and he knew what they were. They had been made from him and alongside him, and they were so tangled up with him that their fulfillment would always come back to him somehow, whether he wanted it to or not.","Very well, then. If their happiness was bound to him, he could at least make sure that what they were bound to was grand.","He smiled, and finished it.","The two signals closed, and held, and brightened, and in one breath THE Infiniverse and Ruination blazed!","THE Infiniverse changed first. Light ran down her arms and out through her fingers and did not stop there, spreading outward into the clouds in branching lines, and along those branches, small bright things began to bud.","Observable Existences. Tiny Dimensions, swelling like fruit on a bough, each one turning with its own light. Her drifting hair lifted and spread above her into a canopy of stars, and when she opened her eyes, a whole slow sky of new Dimensions was turning in them. She looked like a tree that had learned to grow Domains!","Ruination changed differently. Script rose across her skin, fine lines of it, climbing her arms and throat and brow beneath the Circlet, a tongue Noah did not know written in charcters that looked very old. But unlike the marks on a Hieroglyph Runestone, which crawled away from any eye that tried to read them, these held still. They let themselves be seen.","They simply refused to be changed. Her crimson eyes filled with text, line after line of it scrolling past too fast to follow, and every line stayed exactly where she had put it!","| THE COSMOGONIC CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN has formed within THE Infiniverse.|","|Root of Genesis. Type: PHYSICAL.|","|Signal: \"Grow more of existence.\" She generates new Observable Existences and Dimensions from her own authority as this elevates her towards her Immensity.|","|Grows into: a Dimension-producing being. THE Infiniverse becomes a tree that grows boundless Dimensionality.|","|THE ARCHIVAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN has formed within Ruination.|","|Root of the Record. Type: CONCEPTUAL.|","|Signal: \"Keep what you have seen, and obtain endless information.\" She grows by information and its use. Everything she observes is kept, perfectly, and her Root thickens with every record she holds. She may reach across existence to obtain more.|","|Grows into: a being whose memory cannot be edited. Those Who Remain rewrite the Records of existence. The only un-editable memory known is a Hieroglyph Runestone. Ruination may become the first living existence to approach a Runestone’s nature: a self-made record no Immense One can overwrite.|","...!","Two Roots! One Physical, one Conceptual.","Noah sat in the clouds and looked at them, the tree of domains and the living record, both of them still blazing with the first light of their own becoming, and he felt something move in his chest that was not grand or cosmic at all.","He was human, after all!","And there was a fear he had carried for a long time without saying it to anyone. That one day he would climb so high that no one he loved could follow. That he would stand at the top of everything and look around and find the view was his alone, because every face he cared about had been left somewhere far below, too small to see.","He looked at THE Infiniverse, budding domains at her fingertips. He looked at Ruination, the unchangeable record written across her skin. Both of them looking back at him.","Whatever height he reached, it seemed, these two at least would be standing beside him when he got there.","Noah did not interrupt them.","THE Infiniverse sat with her eyes closed and her hands open on her knees, and small new Dimensions kept budding along the branches of light that ran from her fingers, swelling, turning, settling into place like fruit ripening on a bough in fast time.","Every so often one of them flickered and went out, and she frowned very slightly and grew another in its place, a little better than the last. Beside her, Ruination had not moved at all. Only her eyes moved, the text in them scrolling past line after line, and every so often her lips parted as if she had just read something she had not expected to find written anywhere.","They were both somewhere far away, inside the first hours of their own becoming! He knew that place. He had sat in it himself, in the dark, reforged and alone, with nobody to tell him what any of it meant. Nobody had interrupted him either. He would give them the same courtesy.","So he let his thoughts go elsewhere.","There were hours before the Legacy’s sparring gathering. A whole place of beings with Roots of Immensity, all of them on the same road he was on, all of them curious about each other. He was curious too. And then there was the Collector, whenever Noah decided the time was right, which meant whenever Thalia was ready to play her part. Two big things ahead of him, and neither of them urgent yet.","Another was him finding a Rare Gu, but that should be the easiest.","Which meant that, right now, he had time.","And right now, if he was honest with himself, he missed his family.","They were all dreaming. Amelia, Henry, Seo-yeon, Adelaide, Eon, Barbatos, the Queens, all of them, living their long lives inside the Dream Engine while their bodies floated in pools of Sanguine Mana on the golden shore.","He had put them there himself. It had been the right thing. Growth in a sheltered dream, centuries for every day outside, a place to become grander without being eaten while they did it.","But he missed them anyway!","He could do something about that, couldn’t he? They were in a Dream. He was THE Human Dreamer. And his existence did not much care about time anymore, or distance, or which room of existence he happened to be standing in. So why exactly was he sitting here missing them?","He smiled, stood, and stepped down into THE Infiniverse!","The Domain fell away behind him and he came out onto the Early Veiled Shore, onto golden sand under a sky of drifting blue and gold, with the endless sea whispering in on his left and the island farmland stretching away on his right. Warm. Always warm here, even now, with the whole of existence freezing!","The great chrysalis of the Dream Engine hummed on the shore ahead of him, pale and shining, and all around it, in their pools of crimson-gold Mana, floated the dreamers.","He walked among them, slowly.","Henry, with his old face at twenty and his brow creased in some dream-argument. Seo-yeon, curled small and smiling. His mother, very still, very peaceful. Eon’s jaw set hard even asleep. And there, in a pool a little apart from the others, the Mana lapping softly at her shoulders, lay Adelaide.","Her blue hair floated out around her in the pool like ink in water. Her face was calm, but not quite peaceful. There was something in the set of her mouth that looked like concentration, as if even asleep she was in the middle of working on something difficult.","Noah smiled at her.","Then he took one step forward, and chose, simply, to step into her dream!","| You have entered the Dream of ADELAIDE.|","|Time within this Dream runs far faster than time without. Estimated time lived within since the Dream began: many years.|","...!","He was standing on a balcony!","It was wide and made of pale stone, with a carved railing cold under his hand, and it looked out from the height of a great castle over a city that went on for miles. Towers and halls and bridges climbed the slopes belo him, roofs of dark slate and red tile, banners snapping in a hard wind. And everything was white!","Snow fell thick out of a grey sky and lay deep on every roof and every street and every ledge, blanketing the whole city so completely that the towers looked carved from sugar.","And the streets were alive!","People moved everywhere down there, small at this height and busy. Humans in heavy cloaks, carrying loads across a market square. Beastmen among them, broad-shouldered and fur-maned, a wolf-headed guard leaning on a spear at a gate, a pair of horned children chasing each other through a drift, a bear-shouldered merchant shouting prices across the snow.","Smoke rose from a thousand chimneys. Somewhere a smith’s hammer rang, steady and patient.","Noah stood very still.","He knew this place! Or rather, he knew the place it was built from. The Beast World. It was not a copy, quite. It was grander than the real thing had ever been, tidier, more beautiful, as if someone had taken the memory of it and spent years building it back up with love and very careful hands.","\"I wondered when my husband would come see me in my dream.\"","The voice came from behind him.","\"Years have passed, you know!\"","... !","Noah turned.","Adelaide stood in the doorway of the balcony, and she looked like an empress!","Her blue hair was bound up in a high crown of braids, a few loose strands falling past her cheek. She wore a gown of deep sea-blue trimmed with white fur, heavy and imperial, the kind of dress meant to be seen from the far end of a throne rooom.","And around her, on every side, moved Mana. Not a trickle. Waves of it, boundless and slow, rolling off her in visible currents and swirling back, so thick that the snow falling near her melted before it could reach her shoulders!","She looked at him for one long moment.","Then she crossed the balcony in three strides and threw her arms around him, and held on hard!","Noah held her back.","And as he held her, he felt her existence against his, and he blinked. She had grown. A great deal! Her Dimensionality had climbed past everything she had been when he laid her down on the shore, past the whole of the Finite Verse, and was just beginning to press into the first stages of the Transfinite. Years of dreaming, all of them spent growing. In a dream he had given her, she had simply refused to sit still.","He smiled into her hair.","\" Sorry it took so long, \" he said. \" What have you been up to?\"","Adelaide pulled back just far enough to look up at him. Her eyes were pulsing, light moving in them in slow waves, blue and bright.","\" Just trying to continue what you cast out ,\" she said. \" Your First Infinite Scale, THE Genesis Scale. Your Second, THE Source Scale. I’ve been rebuilding them. And I’ve started designing a Third. THE Dimensional Scale!\" Her mouth tightened.","\" But forget all that. Time is unforgiving in this place, do you know that? It’s been so long I almost dreamed another version of you, just to have someone to... talk to!\"","She did not wait for an answer.","Her hand closed on the front of his garment, and her pulsing eyes flashed, and there was something in them now that was not scholarly at all.","\" Get over here, \" Adelaide said. \"I have missed you!\"","...!","And Noah, THE True Human Emperor, who could step through time and dream impossibilities into existence, was yanked bodily off the balcony and into the room behind her before he had the chance to say a single word!"]},{"number":5786,"title":"Chapter 5786: Chapter 5785: Targets and Roots III","paragraphs":["Time, Noah was learning, had stopped being a thing that happened to him.","Inside Adelaide’s dream, months went by. Snow came and went over her imagined Beast World, festivals were held and forgotten, and she built whole new Chapters of the Third Scale on paper covered in tight blue script. Outside, on the golden shore, barely an hour passed over her floating body.","And Noah, who stood in both places at once, felt neither of those clocks. His existence was anchored to itself. However fast or slow the room around him ran, his own perception ticked by at its own steady pace, and to him, the whole of those months felt like a few pleasant minutes.","He could not interfere with her dream too much. It was hers, and a dream steered too hard by someone else stopped being a dream and became a cage. But he could guide it. He could sit with her over her papers and point at a line and ask why it had to end there. He could tell her what he had learned about Infinity, the Absolute and Transcendent and Dialetheic kind, and watch her eyes widen and her pen start moving again. So he did.","Then he went visiting others.","Barbatos was fighting a war of necromancy in her dream, a glorious and completely unnecessary one, and winning it with great style.","Henry was running a farm as he looked happier than Noah had seen him before. Seo-yeon was forging one Observable Existence after another while designing new causes.","His mother sat in a garden and grew things, and when Noah sat down beside her she took his hand without saying anything, and they stayed there a long time.","Kazuhiko...well, the swordsman had pivotted entirely and had writen forty novels. All of them trash smut!","But at least they were his!","And then there was THE Emperor Penguin.","Noah stepped into that particular dream and stopped, because he was standing in a throne room of polished black ice, and it was full of soldiers. Tall, gleaming, robotic Dimensional Lifeforms, rank upon rank of them, standing at perfect attention. Every single one of them had... Noah’s face.","At the far end of the hall, on a throne carved from a glacier, sat a small, round, flightless bird with its flippers crossed importantly over its belly.","\" Soldiers !\" the penguin cried. \" Polish my throne! Fetch new fish! Bow, Osmonts, bow!\"","A thousand Noah-faced soldiers bowed.","The real Noah looked at this for a long, quiet moment.","Then he walked down the length of the hall, between the bowing copies of himself, and the penguin saw him coming and went pale under its feathers!","\" RAA! Master! \" THE Emperor Penguin flapped off the throne and hit the ice. \" Master, this is just a dream! I would never dare think of you as a servant! Never! Ah! AH!\"","THE Emperor Penguin received a correctional beating. A thorough one! It was, Noah felt, important that such a dream never be repeated.","Hours of his existence passed like that, and they were good. Almost relaxing!","—","HUUM!","Some hours later, a body of his stood in the Vasiliou Elsedimension, and the Vasiliou Elsedimension was empty.","The great halls were silent, and the gardens lay under snow. Every family of the Lineage had been relocated, one family after another, and all that remained of them here were their houses, standing quiet with their shutters closed, and the long white avenues between them.","Snow was falling even here. The Long Night had reached this sealed pocket like it had reached everywhere else.","It was beautiful, though.","The snow came down slow and silent, catching the pale gold light of the Elsedimension’s sky, and lay on the roofs in soft round drifts and along the garden walls in neat white lines. The bare trees were iced to the tips of their twigs, and the air smelled clean and sharp. It was the kind of snowfall that makes a person want to stand still and breath, the kind children remember for the rest of their lives.","In the middle of the main avenue stood three figures.","Thalia, and on either side of her, her parents. Aurelius and Rosalia Vasiliou. Thalia had used THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign on both of them, reaching into their existential genomes and remaking them, and now they were Elselifeforms. Their existences shone differently, rewritten from the root, their Provenance forever altered. They stood straighter. They glowed faintly in the falling snow.","Thalia looked at them both.","\"I will take revenge on THE UNPAID COLLECTOR,\" she said. \" For our Lineage. For everything he took from us.\"","\"But none of you can stay to witness it. Go, for now.\"","...!","Aurelius looked at his daughter with nothing but love in his face, and nodded.","Rosalia did not look at her daughter. Rosalia looked at Noah, and glared, with the full weight of a mother who believed her daughter’s troubles had all started the day this man walked into her life. Which, to be fair, was not entirely wrong.","His mother-in-law was troublesome. Noah paid it no heed.","He lifted a hand, and the two of them vanished, carried away into THE Infiniverse where nothing that hunted the Vasilious could follow.","Then it was only him and Thalia, alone in the snow!","He crossed the white avenue to her. She wore a great heavy coat of Provenance authority, deep gold and crimson, turned up at the collar against the cold, and her red-gold hair had come loose and blown across her face. He brushed it aside. Snow was catching on her lashes. Her freckles stood out bright against her cheeks in the cold.","\" So ,\" Thalia said, looking up at him. \" How do you plan to draw out an Immense One?\"","\" Simple .\" Noah did not lower his voice. \" That fucker promised he would appear the next time I held you. To split us both in half. So that we would be afraid of so much as touching each other.\"","He slid his hand to the back of her neck. \" So I am going to hold you. Loudly. And we will see whether THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, one of Those Who Remain, will do anything at all while the prize he promised himself is taken by someone else.\"","There was that, and there was also the fact that by having their records read, Immense Ones could know or sense something. If he directly adressed an Immense One and an obsession of theirs? He would definitely come!","And so he kissed her.","He kissed her there in the falling snow, slow and unhurried, and while he did, he let his voice go out with all his authority behind it, booming across every white avenue and silent house of the Vasiliou Elsedimension.","\" THE UNPAID COLLECTOR,\" Noah said, \" must be a cluster of trash and worthlessness. The kind that sits on s couch and watches while what was his gets taken. What a bum of one of Those Who Remain!\"","Thalia smiled against his mouth!","\" An Unpaid Collector, \" Noah went on, still kissing her, his voice rolling off the snowbound roofs. \" He cannot even collect. Some debt he is. He made a promise and then went back to sleep. I am holding her right now, you senile little shit. I am holding her and I will keep holding her. Where are you? Did you forget which Dimension you left your remnant balls in?!\"","...!","Not even a second passed.","HUUM!","The Vasiliou Elsedimension shook!","It shook to its foundations, the houses rattling on their stones, the iced trees shedding their snow all at once, the whole sealed pocket of existence groaning like a ship in a storm! And above Noah and Thalia, in the pale gold sky, two eyes opened.","They were utterly cold. Vast, and flat, and filled with a hatred so complete it had gone past anger into something quiet.","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR looks down upon the two of you.|","|He says he has never once, in all his existence, been so insulted by an insect and a whore.|","|He says your deaths will not be light ones. Even if THE REMINISCING WIDOW comes here herself again, nothing will change.|","...!","Noah looked up at the eyes, and went quiet.","There was nothing he could do about this. Not yet. Not right now! The weight of the thing above him currently was so grand that it made the Fiend’s grip over the frozen forest feel gentle. Even with his Root, even at six hundred and growing, he was nowhere near an Immense One, and he knew it.","At that very moment it was taking everything he had just to keep himself and Thalia from trembling under the pressure bearing down on them from above.","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR notes your silence.|","|\"No more words from you?\"|","Noah held Thalia a little tighter.","\" Well ,\" he said. \"I am only buying as much time as possible.\"","...!","The eyes above them blinked, once, in the middle of their rage.","And in the next instant, the snow thickened.","All at once it was everywhere, pouring out of the gold sky so densely the houses vanished behind it, heavy and white and driving, and a sound erupted out of the heart of it, a booming sound that did not come from anywhere Noah could point to. The cold eyes of THE UNPAID COLLECTOR were forced downward, dragged out of their height, and as they came, a body came with them!","A massive hazy form now stood in the skies above the Vasiliou Elsedimension. Noah could barely perceive it, a shape too vast and too grand for his sight to hold. But he could see one thing clearly on it now, and that thing was grimness.","The Collector raised both hands to the sky and pushed.","Above him, a thin film of white had appeared across the heavens, pale and smooth as frost on a windowpane. He pushed against it, and it did not break. He pushed harder, and the whole Elsedimension shuddered, and still it held. It was a barrier, and a terrible one, and it had not been put there to keep anything out. It had been put there to keep him in!","Then, directly above Noah, the snow began to gather.","It converged, spiraling in from every direction, thickening, taking shape. A figure formed out of it. Blue-white and jagged and never quite resolving, with two pale points of ice where its eyes should be, and a face Noah had seen twice now. Once in a Runestone’s memory, smiling at him across an age. Once rising out of a dead Immense One’s corpse above a frozen forest.","The frost-visage of Lucy!","It looked up, calmly, at the vast hazy form of THE UNPAID COLLECTOR held beneath the white.","| THE UNPAID COLLECTOR stares down at what has formed below him.|","|\"What...the fuck is this?\"|","...!","Noah’s Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin beat faster in his chest!","His job was done. Draw the Collector out, hold him a few seconds. He had done exactly that. But he had not known what would come to finish it! This Hollow Night Lifeform wearing the image of Lucy herself, standing calm beneath an Immense One who was pushing at the sky and failing to get out.","He was curious!","Why did the Long Night want THE UNPAID COLLECTOR dead? What was this thing, really? And just what was he about to be allowed to witness?!","The snow began to wrap around him at this time.","It came in close around him and Thalia, thick and deliberate, and Noah frowned. From somewhere inside it, flat and quiet, came a voice he knew.","\" Your task is complete ,\" said the Caretaker. \" Your presence here is not conducive to what needs to occur.\"","...!","Motherfucker!","Before he could see a single thing more, the snow took hold of his existence and moved it. Just moved it, bodily, out of the Vasiliou Elsedimension and across existence and down, layering this body of his onto the one already sitting in the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity.","He was on the Glacial Mountain, in the snow outside the golden monastery.","And beside him, blinking and still flushed, stood Thalia!"]},{"number":5787,"title":"Chapter 5787: Chapter 5786: Death and Progeny I","paragraphs":["The snow on the Glacial Mountain came down as quietly as ever, as if nothing at all had happened anywhere.","Noah stood in it, solemn, with the Vasiliou Elsedimension still burning behind his eyes!","Somewhere across existence, an Immense One was being held under a white film of sky by a thing wearing Lucy’s face, and he had been moved out of the room before the first blow landed.","Thalia stood beside him, breathing hard. Her furry coat was still dusted with the snow of another Dimension.","\" What happened?\" She looked up at him, and there was frustration in her gaze. \" We won’t be able to know his fate?\"","He had told her the shape of the plan before they went. Not all of it, because he had not known all of it, but enough. That he meant to bait THE UNPAID COLLECTOR into showing himself. That when the Collector came, something else would come after him, something grand enough to handle an Immense One, and that their part ended the moment the trap closed. She had agreed at once, before he even finished the sentence.","Of course she had!","That being had hunted her Lineage. Thalia had not agreed because she wanted to watch him fall!","And instead, they had been swept out of the room like dust.","Noah did not like it either! He had stood there with his Root beating faster in his chest, staring up at a frost-visage and an Immense One and the beginning of something few had ever seen, and the Caretaker had simply decided he did not need to see it.","\" I’ll try to keep track of exactly what happens,\" he said. \" For now, go and get your parents settled into THE Infiniverse...\"","Thalia looked at him a moment longer. Then she nodded.","Noah waved his hand, and she was gone.","He stood alone in the snow outside the golden monastery for a little while after that. Then he sat down, closed his eyes, and reached for the cold!","—","The Cold Place received him without ceremony!","The frozen seas ran to every horizon, blue and white and shining. The Hollow Night Lifeforms sat in their thousands on the rivers, blank-eyed in their turning pillars, breathing the winter in and out.","Nothing here knew or cared that an Immense One was being brought down somewhere across existence. Nothing here had ever cared about anything.","And The Caretaker was already waiting, her pages turning slow around her in the air!","\"I want to see it, \" Noah said in a very straightforward manner!","\" You cannot.\"","\"I still want to.\"","\" Wanting has never once been a kind of sight.\" The Caretaker regarded him with those flat, cognizant eyes, and the pages turned.","\" Your Dimensionality could not hold that battle if I laid the whole of it before your face. Two Immensities are touching. Where they touch, existence does not record the event so much as look away from it. You would perceive a pale smear and a sound with no source. You would learn nothing, and some part of you would tear in the effort of learning it anyway.\"","Her voice did not change at all.","\"I will give you glimpses later. When it has ended, I will give you what remains. That is the measure your sight can hold, and so that is the measure you are given.\"","Noah’s eyes pulsed!","Well. She was not wrong! He had watched Vakochev and the Immense Ones clash over the sundered Train, and with an Infinite gaze turned on it he had caught an arm through a curtain and the sound of a breaking jaw and nothing else. Glimpses were all he had ever gotten. At least this time someone was offering a bit more.","\" The page is finished, \" The Caretaker said. \" What was owed for it is owed.\"","She lifted one pale hand!","Two slivers of crystal rose out of the frozen river at her feet, pale blue at the edges and white at the heart, their insides branched into snowflake paterns too fine to follow. They pulsed together, slow and cold, and Noah’s Root answered them before he had even reached out!","| LESSER KRYOS EXISTENTIAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN x2.|","|The reward for a page completed. It wasn’t that much work, anyways.|","Two more! He now had three sitting cold in his keeping, each one a quarter of a genuine unit of true Immensity, and none of them would ever disperse.","Then a third thing rose from the river!","A page. A sheet of ice, thin and clear and faintly glowing, and it drifted across the air toward him and turned once as it came.","\" Here is the next ,\" The Caretaker said. \" Look at it for as long as you need.\"","Noah took it out of the air!","On its surface, letters formed! Not the crawling script of a Runestone but plain obsidian characters, black and sharp against the ice, and they spelled a name he knew.","THE REMINISCING WIDOW!","And beneath the name, an image. Eyes. He recognized them at once.","Noah stood in the frozen dark and said nothing for a long moment.","He thought about Atlas. Of course he did! She was Atlas’s widow, in every sense that counted.","And here she was on a frozen page in a dead place, handed to him by the winter.","\"Is she marked for death?\" Noah said. \" Am I meant to lure her to her end, as I lured the Collector?\"","\"No.\"","The word came without weight and without reassurance.","\" This page asks for a messenger, not a hunter.\" The Caretaker’s pages turned. \" Carry what I give you to her, and bring her to a place. She holds a power that was made for exactly one lock, and there is exactly one thing behind that lock, and no other hand in existence can turn it. Deliver the message. Have her agree to go. Then the page is finished, and nothing further is asked of you. Of her, a great deal. Of you, nothing.\"","Beside her, the air thickened, frost gathered out of nothing, and a scroll formed. Ice and rime, bound closed, cold as the botom of the sea, and it floated across the space between them.","Noah took it, and his gaze was heavy!","\" What does all of this mean?\" Noah said. \" What is the purpose here? I severed a thing from THE Sealed One. I held an Immense One in place so something could fall on him. Now I am to move another Immense One across existence to a place of your choosing.\"","He lifted the scroll slightly. \" Three pages, and not one of them resembles the others. So what is the end goal?\"","The Caretaker was quiet!","Around her the pages turned, and beneath her the thousands of Hollow Night Lifeforms sat in their cold, and somewhere far above, an Age went on freezing.","\" You are basically asking what the winter is for, \" she said at last.","Her flat eyes did not leave him.","\"A winter is not a tool. It does not lift, or carry, or strike. It comes, and it takes whatever cannot hold itself, and what remains, remains. No hand forged it to drive a nail.\"","The pages stilled around her, all at once, as if they were listening.","\" And yet. Threads are being cut that were tied before the first of Those Who Remain ever drew breath. What was scattered is being gathered. What was gathered is being scattered. And a door that was shut a very long time ago has begun, in places, to be unshut. In these epochs and boundless others...the cold has always remained supreme.\""]},{"number":5788,"title":"Chapter 5788: Chapter 5787: Death and Progeny II","paragraphs":["The Caretaker told him nothing more!","Whatever was happening in the Vasiliou Elsedimension was still happening, and the frozen underworld had nothing else to give him until it finished. So Noah opened his eyes on the Glacial Mountain and stood.","The snow that had gathered on him while he was away slid off his shoulders in soft white sheets.","He looked around.","Behind him the golden monastery glowed, and the slope fell away below the shelf into grey. Snow kept coming, as it always did now, and he stood in it and turned the new page over in his thoughts.","THE REMINISCING WIDOW.","A message to carry, an unread scroll of ice, and a woman who wore Atlas’s ring. He would have to decide when to begin, and how, and how much of it to tell the old man in his other ring.","None of those were small questions.","Then he blinked, because someone was standing behind him!","Verys had not moved! The whole time, the Legacy Keeper had stood a few paces behind him on the shelf, hands clasped, cloak pulled close, as still as a statue left out in the storm. There was snow piled on his shoulders an inch deep, and he had not brushed it off!","Noah looked at him, and remembered, belatedly, that there was a sparring session in a few hours.","A sparring session he had agreed to and then not bothered to learn a single thing about.","Who exactly would he be facing? Beings on the road to Immensity, fine, but how far along that road? Were they down under five hundred in their attributes? Or did having a Root push them higher?","\" What can you tell me,\" Noah said, \" about those in this Legacy who have Roots?\"","Verys smiled, and bowed, and the snow fell off his shoulders at last.","\"It would be my pleasure, Sir.\" He straightened. \" Would you walk with me?\"","He rose off the shelf, lifting into the air as easily as a man stepping off a stair, and Noah rose alongside him.","From above the Glacial Mountain, the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity went on forever!","Noah had seen it once already, arriving at Poona’s side. Now he looked. Mountains rose in every direction as far as sight could go, each one a sealed Elsedimension grown into the shape of a peak, some white with snow like his own, some black and glasy, some green, one burning a slow sullen red from summit to root. Well, snow pervaded all of them regardless.","Between them, far below, the ground was rivers! Broad, winding rivers of purple and gold, braiding and parting and braiding again across the whole floor of the Legacy, shining up through the falling snow.","Existential Conduits climbed out of that shining floor like the trunks of impossible trees, pillars of flowing authority rising past the mountains and away into the heights.","Conduit Lifeforms drifted everywhere between them, small incandescent things in their thousands, riding the currents, perching on the pillars, sipping from the authority that ran through them. A flock of them swept past Noah close enough to touch, bright and chiming, and vanished into the snow!","And above it all hung domains.","Dimensions and Observable Existences floated in the sky of the Legacy by the thousands, each one turning slowly on its own axis, glittering through the snowfall like lanterns hung over a festival that had been going on since before memory. Some were close enough that Noah could make out oceans on them! Others were only sparks.","Verys led him out over the purple and gold rivers, unhurried, as if he had walked this road ten thousand times, which he probably had.","\" Sir asked about the Roots, \" the Keeper said. \" To understand them, it helps to understand where most of them come from.\"","\" When Those Who Remain write sentences into lesser things, or lie with Provenance Lifeforms, they produce Descendants. Some of those Descendants are fairly powerful. \" Verys glanced down at a mountain passing beneath them, black and glassy.","\" But when Immense Ones lie with each other, what arises is something far more terrifying and very rare. Among those rarities, some of those children are born with a Root already in them. An Inherent Root of Immensity.\"","Noah looked at him. \" Born with it?\"","\" Born with it, Sir. Imagine the genetic material of two Immense Ones making up the whole of your weavings.\" Verys smiled faintly.","\" What a child like that can inherit has no ceiling. Some inherit more than others, of course. Two parents of the same greatness do not always make two children of the same greatness.\"","\" And the ones who inherit less?\"","\"If they are grand enough, and if they are born with an Inherent Root, they stay within their parents’ Legacy, where they can grow in safety. If they are not...\"","Verys spread one webbed hand. \" They go out into existence. Across Dimensions and Observable Existences. They are encouraged to found Lineages of their own, and breed Descendants, and wait, and see whether something grand might arise from their blood in some later generation.\"","Noah thought about that. About the Vheldrani, twelve self-made beings in the low two hundreds, sent to pick a dead man’s bones on an Immense One’s errand.","About the Vasiliou, hunted for generations, and all the other Provenance Lineages that had drifted through his road like leaves.","\" So that is what a Provenance Lineage is ,\" he said.","\" Some of them, Sir. A few Descendants who found each other and built their Provenance up across the ages, and never quite made it into a Root.\"","The Keeper’s large dark eyes were thoughtful. \" Some of them are lucky. Existence has accidents in it, and sometimes an accident happens in the blood, and a genius rises out of a Lineage that had no business producing one. When that happens, and the genius forms a Root, the whole Lineage earns the right to live in a Legacy again.\"","Noah thought of the people he had carried here.","\" You, Sir, have brought in a few beings who do not have Roots,\" Verys went on, as if he had heard the thought. \" But it is within your allowable limit.\"","\"What is the allowable limit?\"","\"A few hundred should be fine, Sir. Whatever family and servants you choose to keep.\"","A few hundred!","\" But the ones you will spar with in a few hours,\" Verys said, \" are mostly Progeny. Children of Immense Ones, born with their Roots. Very few are like you, or like Sir Achilles, who formed a Root themselves.\"","He slowed, and his voice dropped, as a storyteller’s voice drops before the part of a story that matters. \" Among them, there are three you should watch for.\"","\" Who?\"","\" The first is Sir Dravos. Progeny of THE Ashen Cantor.\"","A glance at a mountain burning sullen red in the distance. \" His Root is Physical. The second is Sir Batiatus. Progeny of THE Hollow Choir, and he should hold a Conceptual Root.\"","Noah almost smiled!","\" And the third?\"","Verys did not answer at once! They were passing between two Existential Conduits, the pillars rising on either side of them like the doorposts of some enormous hall, and the Keeper waited until they had come out the other side.","\" Ma’am Minerva...\" he said. \" Her mother is an Immense One with a gaze as green as early spring. Her Root is Conceptual. Everyone in this Legacy expects that when this Age ends, she is one of the few who is meant to be standing as an Immense One in the next.\"","He paused. \" Others at her stage of power will not be at the sparring at all. They have earned the right to stay away. Minerva has earned it too. She is coming anyway as she seems very...enthusiastic for battles.\"","A gaze as green as early spring!","Noah kept his face exactly as it was. But he remembered, very clearly, a voice with a verdant weight to it, spoken over his frozen body in Moriarty’s hall. A voice that had talked about him, and about what he might be.","\" And you know all of this how? \" he said.","Verys bowed slightly as they flew, and something that was very nearly mischief crept into his calm face.","\" Legacy Keepers like me have our own network, Sir. We love to gossip about the goings-on of the Legacy. It is one of the few pleasures of the position.\"","He looked up at the falling snow. \" And since the snow began to fall, a great many things have begun to happen! You, Sir, are one of the more recent pieces of gossip.\"","...!","Noah raised his brows!","\" You gossiped about me?\"","\"Of course not, Sir. \" Verys bowed again, deeper, the very picture of respect. \" But Tatiana did. And of course Ma’am Poona is very talkative. The other Immense Ones of her standing tend to stay away from her for exactly that reason among others, so she has a great deal of time to talk to those of us who cannot leave.\"","He straightened, and his wet-bright eyes were perfectly innocent!","\" She...may have mentioned a few things regarding you.\""]},{"number":5789,"title":"Chapter 5789: Chapter 5788: Death and Progeny III","paragraphs":["Verys was showing him a garden when the cold pulled at him.","It was a strange garden, grown on the shoulder of a green Elsedimension mountain, and every plant in it was a small sealed Dimension!","The Keeper had been explaining, in his mild, pleased voice everything here.","Then the cold reached up out of the deep of existence and took hold of Noah’s Root, and tugged!","He knew that tug by now. He sent a sliver of his existence down after it, and kept the rest walking beside Verys among the sealed afternoons.","—","The Cold Place was the same, and the Caretaker was already waiting!","She did not greet him. She raised one pale hand, and the frozen air in front of him thickened into a sheet of pale light, flat and bright as ice on a still lake.","\" You wished to see,\" she said. \" Your sight can hold three glimpses. Here they are.\"","The first glimpse opened!","It was the Vasiliou Elsedimension, or what was left of it. The houses were gone. The white avenues were gone. There was only a churning grey light where a sealed reality had been, and in the middle of it hung the hazy vastness of THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, and below him, small and still, stood the frost-visage of Lucy.","The Collector spoke!","Noah could not hear the words, but he could see what they did. Wherever the Collector’s voice fell, existence rewrote itself. A whole region of the churning grey turned to gold, then to coins, then to an account written in letters of light, and every line of that account said the same thing: mine.","He spoke again, and the air around Lucy was declared his. He spoke again, and her very existence was entered as a debt, owed to him, payable now, and existence agreed to it! That was what an Immense One of his kind did. He did not throw his power at a thing. He said what was true, and existence rearranged itself to make it so.","It was the grandest act of authorship Noah had ever witnessed!","And the frost-visage of Lucy looked at him.","That was all. She stood in the middle of an existence that had just been rewritten into a debt with her name on it, and she looked up at the Collector with her pale ice eyes, and nothing happened to her.","His words landed on her and slid off. Her name sat in the account as owed, and she did not become owed. The Collector had written a perfect sentence, and he had written it on a mountain, and a mountain does not care what is written on it!","Then that glimpse went dark.","A second opened!","Lucy moved!","She did not speak. She did not answer his sentences with sentences of her own. There was no art in what she did at all. She took a single step up into the sky, and the whole Elsedimension sank under the weight of that step, and she drew back one hand and struck the Collector.","That was it. She hit him!","Noah saw the blow land, and saw everything the Collector had written shatter around it like glass under a hammer!","Every rewritten region, every account, every line that said mine burst apart at once, because none of it had anything to hold onto. The Collector’s power was a story told to existence, and Lucy was not a story.","She was simply heavier than the story, and so the story broke. The hazy vastness of the Immense One caved around her fist, and the white film of sky above him cracked from end to end, and he did not fall because there was nowhere left to fall to.","Darkness again.","A third opened!","It was over!","The churning grey had gone still. The white film of sky had faded. And in the middle of the stillness drifted a corpse, vast and ruined and no longer hazy at all, only dead, the body of THE UNPAID COLLECTOR lying open to the cold with nothing left in it to argue for its own existence.","The snow was already pouring in!","Great rivers of white drained into the dead Immense One from every side, the same way they had drained into the Overseeing One above the frozen forest. And out of the corpse, something began to rise!","It came up slow and enormous, heavy beyond measure, a titan of frost with a body like a mountan range and four legs like the pillars of a cold cathedral. Its back was covered in long shaggy fur, white and rimed and hanging in frozen ropes. Two great tusks curved out and up from its head, pale blue ice as long as rivers, and its eyes were blank.","A mammoth, or the shape a mammoth would take if winter itself decided to walk. It lifted its trunk to the dead sky and opened its mouth, and no sound came out, and the snow around it doubled!","The screen went dark and did not open again.","...!","Noah stood in the frozen dark and said nothing at all.","He understood it now, in a way no lecture had ever taught him. Moriarty had told him once that an Empyros rewrites the rules of a fight, and a Fiend is simply stronger than the rules.","He had nodded and thought he understood. He had not. The Collector had rewritten existence itself with a sentence, and Lucy had broken the sentence with her hand. That was the difference! One of them was the grandest writer Noah had ever seen. The other was the page.","And there was something else, something colder.","Two Immense Ones had died in the span of a few days. Two! Beings that had stood at the top of existence since long before Noah was born. And both of them had died, one way or another, because of something he had done.","The Overseeing One had fallen to a Vestige he had helped write back into existence. The Collector had fallen because he had held his wife in the snow and called an Immense One a bum until it came down to kill him.","Around the Caretaker, the snow was growing heavier!","He saw it thicken as she stood there, her pages turning, the flakes coming down denser and denser, as if the winter itself were answering a death.","\"A tiny bug starves in a puddle of mud, \" the Caretaker said.","\" Somewhere else, very far away, a giant who ruled a thousand Dimensions has his throat opened and dies. To everything that bowed to the giant, it feels like the end of existence. But existence does not pause for either. The snow goes on falling. No one weeps for the bug. The giant, in the end, receives the same.\"","The snow thickened.","\" Neither of them asked to arrive. They came, they took up a little space for a while, and when their time ran out, existence took that space back. Between the arriving and the leaving, they walked about. They ate, and slept, and fought over patches of ground, and told themselves they mattered. Because they could feel fear, they assumed existence could feel their pain. They shouted their names into the dark, certain that something out there was keeping count.\"","A pause, very slight.","\" Nothing is keeping count.\"","The flakes fell so thick now that her frost dress was vanishing into them.","\" Look back at everything that lived before you. Beyond counting. And for nearly all of it, nothing it did mattered at all. It was noise. It thought the thoughts its elders handed it, lived by rules it did not write, labored until it broke, and went into the cold without moving a single grain of sand. The moment it was gone, it was as if it had never been.\"","Her flat eyes held him through the snow. \" And now this winter has come. It hates nothing, and it does not hear how loudly anyone screams. It walks through the room and clears it.\"","The underworld had gone very quiet around her. Even the rivers seemed to slow.","\" Many will live through it, and many will not. You cannot stop that. The only thing that was ever truly yours is the span between arriving and leaving. That is the one place anything gets to choose. \"","The Caretaker’s voice dropped lower still. \" And nearly everything wastes it. They spend it afraid. Borrowing warmth from someone else. Begging the roof to hold. They live copied lives, die common deaths, and go back into the dark without leaving a mark.\"","The snow was a wall now! Only her eyes showed through it.","\" Being alive is nothing. A stone is alive enough to sit where it was put. So is a corpse. If the time you have is to mean anything, surviving the cold will not be enough. Asking existence for permission to breathe will not be enough. You must stand on your own feet and make something so true, so stubbornly and entirely your own, that when the dark swallows everything, existence is forced to remember you were here.\"","She let the silence stand for a long moment.","\" Arriving is common. Leaving comes for everyone. The span between is an empty page, and nearly everyone who ever held one wrote down someone else’s name, closed their eyes, and was forgotten. \"","Her gaze did not waver. \" So I ask you. What will you etch across existence? What will you dream, you who call yourself THE Human Dreamer, that will be grand enough to one day not be like the Collector who now lies dead? He became an Immense One. It did not save him.\"","The snow stopped thickening. It simply hung there, heavy, waiting.","\" What will you do differently?\"","...!","Noah opened his mouth.","Nothing came!","He, who had an answer for Immense Ones and Runestones and prophecies, who had talked his way past titans and dreamed his way through impossibilities, stood in the frozen dark before a caretaker of the cold and found, for the first time in a very long time, that he did not have one."]},{"number":5790,"title":"Chapter 5790: Chapter 5789: The Death of Time! I","paragraphs":["Noah did not have an answer good enough to give, so he did not give one.","What would he do differently? He meant to climb. To gather power, all of it he could reach, and become an Immense One.","But the Collector had done exactly that, and it had not given him a grand life. It had given him a long one, and then a cold end in a Dimension of snow at the hand of a thing that did not even speak. Bug or one of Those Who Remain, a being lived, and then it died. Becoming Immense only made the second part take longer.","So he looked at the Caretaker a moment longer, standing in snow so thick now it was nearly a wall, and he left.","The hours after that passed slower than any hours had passed for him in a long time.","But they passed.","—","THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering was never still, and this corner of it least of all!","In this place, Noah floated in a region where time itself had gone murky, as if the weavings here had been left out in the rain for a few billion years and started to rot.","Old currents of it hung in the air like smoke that had forgotten how to rise, grey-violet and heavy, and through them drifted things he could only half-perceive: the outline of an ocean that had dried long ago, the echo of a Dimension that had not been born yet, stretches where a single moment had been worn so thin by repetition that he could see straight through it.","It felt ancient in a way nothing else in the Chrysalis did.","On either side of him floated the two who had been with him longest, and they had come out of their acclimation changed!","Ruination’s crimson eyes no longer simply glowed. Beams of crimson light shot from them in steady lines, reading everything they touched, and she wore a long coat of crimson and gold, cut clean and severe, with the unchangeable script of her new Root showing faintly at her collar and wrists.","THE Infiniverse wore a thick fur coat of many colors, heavy and trailing, and her face held an expression Noah had rarely seen on it before. Imperious. Unbound","The look of a being who had just discovered exactly how much reality she could hold in one hand.","He had brought them here to test those new Roots, and for a second reason as well. He needed a Rare Gu for the Time Inscription. More than that, if he could manage it, he wanted a Rare Time Gu.","He had been ranging across the endless stretches of the Chrysalis for hours with this body, until at last he found this domain, soaked through with the old weavings of time.","\" Master, if you can bear with me a little bit, I will explain my vision at this moment in time... \" Ruination said.","Her crimson beams swept slowly across the murky currents as she spoke.","\"A lifeform looks at the dirt beneath its feet and believes that is all there is to see. Ask it what happened a moment ago, and it must remember. Ask it what happens next, and it must guess. It spends its whole existence peering through a crack in a wall, watching existence slide past one second at a time.\"","The beams paused . \"I...no longer look through the crack.\"","Noah waited. She was clearly not finished!","\" When I open my senses now, distance stops being a road that must be walked. In THE Infiniverse, a million Dimensions from here, a woman drops a clay pot. I do not simply see it fall. I see her fingers letting go. I see the pot hanging in the air. I see the five different ways it may break against the floor, all in the same breath. The past is not a memory. Tomorrow is not a mystery. They are only... different corners of the same table.\"","She turned her head, and the beams turned with it, into the deeper murk.","\" Across this domain, I have already located the information of two Rare Time Gu. Where they are, where they have been, and where probability says they will be one minute from now. I can take you to where they will be, Master, and we can simply wait for them to arrive.\"","...!","Noah smiled.","She was showing off a little. He did not mind in the least!","\" Lead ,\" he said.","They followed her. Each step they took crossed gigaparsecs, the murky currents blurring past, and at the place Ruination chose they stopped, and waited, and the Chrysalis came to them.","It was a place of purple clouds, slow and towering, and between them spun disks of raw time! Great flat wheels of it, violet-edged and whirling, and anything they touched was severed from billions of years in an instant, cut clean out of its own history. One sliced through a drifting rock ahead of them and the rock simply was not there anymore, had never been there, left no trace!","None of the disks came near the three of them. Around Noah and his companions, rivers of dream flowed slow and serene, blue and gold, and the disks of time curved away from them like wind parting around a standing stone.","And far ahead, through the clouds, they saw the Gu!","There were two of them, and they were titanic!","Each one looked something like a butterfly, if a butterfly had been dragged up from the deepest trench of a lightless sea. Their bodies were long and transluscent, lit from within by cold bioluminescent lures that dangled from their heads on thin stalks.","Their mouths were rimmed with glassy needle teeth, and trailing tendrils drifted beneath them for miles. But their wings were glorious. Vast and violet, burning with time, every scale a small flame of shifting hours!","And the two of them were holding a chain!","It ran between them, purple and gold, each end clasped in a set of long pale claws, and along its length flowed a current Noah recognized at once, because he had drunk its like from a river of time only days ago. Provenance. The Provenance of Time itself, coursing back and forth between the two great Gu without pause.","| RARE GU: THE ANCHORED HOUR (bound to the Past).|","|VERITAS: 471. POTENTIA: 468. PONDUS: 476. PROVENANCE: 489.|","|RARE GU: THE UNARRIVED HOUR (bound to the Future).|","|VERITAS: 474. POTENTIA: 470. PONDUS: 472. PROVENANCE: 491.|","|A mated pair, joined by a chain of their own Provenance of Time. One lives entirely in the Past. The other lives entirely in the Future. Neither exists in the present at all.|","|A blow struck at one may be undone by the other before it lands, or will already have been avoided in a moment that has not yet come.|","|Their attributes are not extreme. Their paradox is.|","...!","Noah’s eyes narrowed. High four hundreds. Beneath him, on paper, by a fair margin. And none of that mattered in the least, because how exactly did you hit something that was not here? One of them lived before the blow and the other lived after it, and between them they held the only moment where a blow could land.","The two Gu turned their great heads toward the three intruders.","|THE ANCHORED HOUR and THE UNARRIVED HOUR speak as one.|","|\"You are strong. We see it. We have always seen it, and we will see it again.\"|","|\"But strength is a thing of the present, and we do not live there. Many greater than you have come. None of them could pass the paradox of what was and what will be. We have mastered it. Leave, or be left behind.\"|","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly!","He was already moving to answer when THE Infiniverse stepped forward.","There was no asking, and no glance back at him. She simply took one step past his shoulder into the purple clouds, and her multicolored coat swung heavy behind her, and the whole domain felt her arrive!","The disks of time turned toward her at once, a dozen of them, a hundred, whirling in to cut her away from her own history. They struck her, and they broke! Instead of cutting, they shattered against her like thrown plates against a cliff, because there was too much of her.","A disk like that could sever a rock from billions of years. It could not sever her, because she was not a thing that had happened. She was simply there, heavier than anything in the domain, too vast to be cut out of anything!","The Gu reacted. THE Unarrived Hour wrenched its burning wings, and in the future THE Infiniverse had not yet reached, it had already moved. THE Anchored Hour pulled on the chain, and the moment she had just stepped through began, quietly, to unhappen behind her.","In answer, THE Infiniverse raised one hand.","Domains grew from it!","Dimensions and Observable Existences budded off her fingers, as they had budded along her branches in his Root Domain, but these did not stay small. They swelled as they fell, heavy, whole, each one crowded with seas and continents and weight, and she let them drop into the domain of purple clouds one after another after another. Ten. A hundred. Thousands! More!","The Gu’s paradox needed a gap. A narrow space between what was and what would be, where the two of them could live apart and pass a blow back and forth between them. THE Infiniverse did not argue with that paradox, or try to reason her way past it, or rewrite its rules.","She filled the gap with existence, pouring new Dimensions into the space between past and future until there was no space left, until the Past and the Future were packed so tight with sheer grown reality that they had nowhere to hide from each other, and nowhere to hide from her!","The chain between the two Gu went taut!","THE Infiniverse walked forward through her own falling domains, and took hold of it.","Noah watched her do it, and he saw a snowbound Elsedimension, and a frost-visage taking a single step, and a hand closing on an Immense One who had written existence into a debt.","The Collector had been a writer, and Lucy had been the page. These Gu had written a paradox, and THE Infiniverse was the page too. She did not out-think them. She simply had more existence than their idea could hold. That was what a Physical Root meant!","That was what it would grow into, one day: a Fiend. A thing that was stronger than the rules!","She pulled!","The Anchored Hour came out of the Past, dragged by its own chain. The Unarrived Hour came out of the Future. Both of them, wrenched screaming into the one moment they had never stood in, the present, and there, at last, they could be touched!","Chains bloomed from THE Infiniverse’s hands, bright and many-colored, the same brilliance as her coat, and wound around both Gu, wings and tendrils and lures, binding the burning violet down. The great creatures thrashed, and the chains did not care!","She turned, and walked back through the purple clouds toward Noah, dragging the two bound titans behind her like a hunter bringing home the season’s catch. The falling domains settled around her into slow orbits, and the disks of time kept their distance now, and the Provenance of Time still ran up and down the golden chain between her prisoners, though neither of them could escape into it anymore.","She stopped before her Master, and let them drop at his feet!","\" Master ,\" THE Infiniverse said. Her voice was calm. Her face was imperious and utterly unbothered. \" Your Rare Gu.\""]},{"number":5791,"title":"Chapter 5791: Chapter 5790: The Death of Time! II","paragraphs":["The two Rare Time Gu lay bound at Noah’s feet in THE Infiniverse’s many-colored chains, their violet wings dimmed, their long lures trembling, and he reached down to take them.","And yet...","He never touched them!","A moment before anything happened, Ruination went rigid!","Her crimson beams had been drifting lazily across the purple clouds, reading the spin of the time-disks and the slow currents between them, and all at once they locked in place. The script at her collar and wrists flared bright. The endless text scrolling through her eyes stopped scrolling, and held on a single thin line that had just appeared at the far edge of everything she could see.","\" Master ,\" she said.","Her voice was as level as ever, but it came quickly, and Ruination never spoke quickly.","\" There is a branch. Point zero zero zero three percent. It should not be possible for it to...\"","It should not be possible, but...it happened anyway.","The Provenance of Time came down on them like a falling sea!","It poured out of the purple sky in heavy, turbulent sheets of violet and gold, and every current of it was thick with more ages than the whole murky domain had held a breath before. The time-disks spinning through the clouds stopped dead mid-turn, frozen in place like coins dropped into ice!","The towering clouds stopped drifting. Even the light changed. It began arriving late, reaching Noah’s eyes a long, strange instant after it should have, so that everything he looked at seemed to be happening a little in the past.","At his feet, very quietly, the two bound Rare Gu began to weep.","Noah moved on instinct. He reached for his Provenance, for his Root, for the rivers of dream that had kept every danger in this domain curving harmlessly around him and his companions like wind around a standing stone.","Nothing came!","That was the first strange thing. His Provenance had not gone anywhere. He could feel all of it, vast and blue and gold, filling him exactly as it always did. It simply would not move.","His Root was there too, turning at the center of him, except that it was not turning. It had been caught mid-beat, like a heart that had been told its next beat was not permitted.","Beside him, THE Infiniverse had frozen with one hand half-raised! The domains she had grown hanging motionless in their orbits around her. Ruination’s beams were still lit and still fixed on that impossible branch, and she could not turn them away from it.","So Noah reached for the one thing on him that had never needed his permission.","THE Enduring Gu Elsedimension Ring sat on his finger, and at its heart was an Existential Narrative Displacement, woven there for exactly this. The moment any authority grander than his own closed around him, it would tear him out of that place and throw him somewhere safer, whether he willed it or not.","And yet...","It did not fire!","He understood why a heartbeat later.","The ring’s displacement worked by carrying him into the next moment, somewhere else. To do anything at all, a being needed a next moment to do it in.","And there was no next moment anymore!","Something had reached across time and taken it away. The clock had not been stopped. The next moment had simply been removed from existence around them, so that every authority and every Root the three of them owned stood pinned inside one single instant, whole and grand and completely useless, with nowhere at all to go.","It was a very simple thing. That was what made it so terrifying.","Far above, something began to show itself!","At first there was only an absence. A place in the purple sky where the light did not arrive at all, a shape made out of lateness. Then the lateness gained edges, and the edges gained weight, and Noah began to see, or almost see, or see in pieces his sight could not quite hold together.","A limb came first, jointed and impossibly long, reaching down through the clouds like the hand of a clock that counted Ages instead of hours. Then another. Then a body, segmented and vast, each segment a great slab of something like amber, deep gold and translucent, and inside each slab, perfectly preserved, lay an entire Age!","He could see them! Oceans and cities and burning stars, and the tiny frozen figures of beings who had lived and died long befor anything he knew had begun, all of it sealed segment upon segment down the length of a body that ran on past the edge of his sight.","Wings spread above it! They were not made of any substance at all. They were made of stopped moments, thousands upon thousands of frozen instants gathered from every corner of existence and laid edge to edge like scales.","Then the head came down through the clouds!","It had no face. Where a face should have been there was only a smooth dark hollow, and around that hollow, set like a crown, were eyes. A great many eyes, and in each one a different Age was still happening. Noah looked into one and saw a Dimension being born. In the one beside it, the same Dimension dying. In the next, a war, and in the one after, the same war won by the other side.","| THE FIRST GU OF TIME.|","The prompt gave him nothing else. Beneath the name lay only a smear of question marks that his sight slid off of, as though the rest of what she was had quietly declined to be read.","\" You have come a very long way to take something that was never yours,\" THE First Gu of Time said.","Her voice did not come from the hollow where her face should have been. It came from the stopped moments in her wings, all of them at once, cool and clear and perfectly composed.","\"I have watched your kind come. Across more Ages than you could count if I gave you every moment I hold to count them in.\" The crown of eyes turned, unhurried, toward the two bound Rare Gu, and the Ages burning in them softened very slightly. \" Tell me. What did these small ones do to you, that you should hunt them?\"","The Rare Gu whimpered in their chains.","\"I have seen lifeforms like you move through my children as reapers move through a field. You take them. You grind them down. You bind them into rings, render them into engines, and pour their small lives into vessels to keep yourselves warm, and then you call it craft, as though the word makes it clean. What gave you the right?\"","Noah could not answer. The instant held his mouth as firmly as it held everything else.","\" Consider it turned around,\" THE First Gu of Time went on, quietly. \" Consider my children moving through your Dimensions and your Observable Existences. Through your proud Lineages. Taking your Descendants from their cradles and your Provenance Lifeforms from their halls, and grinding their bodies into material for our own warmth.\"","Every eye in her crown held him. \" How would it feel, to be the harvest? I have asked this of a great many of your kind. Not one has ever answered me well. Why is there such cruelty in all of you?\"","WAA!","And Noah thought...of the Common Dream Gu sealed at the heart of the ring on his finger. It had dreamed only of warmth, and of being left alone. He thought of the Common Gu that had died screaming in his first failed inscription, cracked apart by a Letter too heavy for it to carry, and of how he had come to this domain today to take a Rare Gu and forge it into a tool, and had never once, not for a single breath, cared.","It was kill or be killed right? Natural selection?","He had looked at them as material!","And the Collector, not so very long ago, had looked at the Vasilious in a similar manner.","He did not like how close those two thoughts sat to each other. He did not like it at all.","\" You are silent? Nobody truly ever has a devent answer as at least...you are silent.\" THE First Gu of Time said.","Her crown of eyes turned away from him, slowly, and came to rest on THE Infiniverse and Ruination.","\" These two are dear to you ,\" she said. It was not a question. \" I have seen every moment you have ever spent looking at them. They are very dear.\"","...!","Something in Noah’s pinned existence strained against the instant so hard that the frozen moment around him creaked.","But...","It did not break!","\" Then they will learn what my children learn,\" THE First Gu of Time said. \"I take no pleasure in it. But you have made it clear that you learn nothing from words. Perhaps you will learn from this.\"","She never touched them. There was no need!","THE Infiniverse’s domains began to age and die!","The small new Dimensions orbiting her, the ones she had grown only moments ago from her Root of Genesis and been so quietly proud of, went grey. Their seas dried to craked beds. Their continents crumbled. Whole spans of time were forced through each of them at once, and one after another they withered to dust and drifted away from her like ash from a dead fire.","THE Infiniverse could neither move nor cry out, but her starlit eyes were open, and Noah saw in them exactly what she felt: every one of those domains dying as she was made to feel their death amplified by many times!","And Ruination kept recording as her Root was the Root of the Record. Everything she observed, she kept, perfectly and forever, beyond the reach of any hand that might try to edit it. Pinned in place, unable to look away, she could not stop THE First Gu of Time from pouring the grinding deaths into her. The sinilar long, slow experience of a Gu being taken apart for material, again and again and again, and every instant of it written into her unchangeable record.","Noah watched the two of them forced to experience and record boundless deaths in amplified time, pinned and powerless, his Root frozen mid-beat and his Provenance sitting vast and useless inside him, and he knew what defeat was!","He had tasted it before, and it always sucked. But he had never tasted it like this.","Then, very slightly, the instant loosened around his mouth.","The First Gu of Time wanted him to speak!","Noah did not beg as he did not know how, and he would not have done it here even if he had. But he did not lie either. He had been honest with himself when a caretaker of the cold asked him what he would do differently and he found he had no answer. He could at least be honest now.","\"I am human ,\" Noah said.","His voice came out low and steady.","\" And humans make mistakes. I will take this as one of mine. I came here to take your children the way I have taken others, and I never once asked what that meant to them. That is on me.\"","He held the crown of burning eyes with his own. \" But you and I are not enemies past forgiving. We have a disagreement. So...what price needs to be paid for you to stop here?\"","The eyes did not blink. The Ages inside them went on happening.","\"I do not have the power right now to steer this where I want it to go. I know that. You have made very certain I know it. But I will have that power, in the future. Above everything else I am, I am determined. So determined that if I had to, I could make it the one absolute aim of my existence to ruin Time itself.\"","The frozen disks hung in the air around them. The dust of THE Infiniverse’s domains drifted slowly past. Ruination’s eyes kept writing.","\"I would rather not, \" Noah said. \" So. What price needs to be paid for us to go our separate ways?\"","...!"]},{"number":5792,"title":"Chapter 5792: Chapter 5791: The Death of Time! III","paragraphs":["THE First Gu of Time considered his question for a long moment.","Snow fell heavily all around them!","The Ages kept burning in her crown of eyes while she did. A Dimension was born in one and died in the next. A war was won, then lost. Somewhere in the frozen amber of her body, a whole civilization went on standing exactly where it had stood when she sealed it, and never noticed that it had stopped.","\" They acted at your behest ,\" she said at last.","Her gaze moved, unhurried, across THE Infiniverse with the dust of her domains still drifting around her, and across Ruination with her eyes still writing.","\" They took my children because you wished my children taken. So I will not ask them to pay for it any longer. Let us see instead what you are made of.\"","Her voice stayed as cool and even as still water. \" You may take their pain for them. In exchange for letting them go, and for letting you go, you will experience the Death of Time itself.\"","...!","Experience the death of time itself?","Noah did not know what that meant. A being that could take the next moment out of existence did not offer a price that could be understood before it was paid.","It was a heavy thing!","He nodded anyway, without a word.","At once, the instant loosened! Not around him, but around the two beside him. He felt the anchoring locks on THE Infiniverse and Ruination come undone, felt their Roots catch their next beat and their authorities start to move again, and he saw THE Infiniverse’s starlit eyes turn to him, and Ruination open her mouth.","He waved his hand before either of them could speak!","They were gone, sent back through the Chrysalis and down into the safety of his Existential Root Domain. Better that way. He did not want to argue with them, and he did not want them to watch.","Then he stood alone in the frozen purple sky, before THE First Gu of Time.","The two Rare Time Gu had slipped free of their many-colored chains the instant THE Infiniverse left. They drifted now near their ancient mother, their violet wings burning bright again, their long lures swaying, and the Past-bound one turned its eyeless head toward him with a slow, satisfied tilt that was nothing but gloating. The Future-bound one looked at him as if it already knew how this ended.","Perhaps it did.","\" Hold still ,\" said THE First Gu of Time. \" There is nothing you can do to make this easier.\"","Her wings opened wide!","Every stopped moment laid along them came loose at once, thousands upon thousands of frozen instants, and they turned into rivers!","Boundless rivers of time, violet and gold and roaring, poured off her wings in a flood that filled the whole sky, and every one of them came down on Noah.","Instead of striking him, they entered him!","Through his chest, through his eyes, through the spinning mobius at the center of his crystalline body, the rivers of time surged in, and Noah felt himself come apart into every direction at once!","—","He felt like he was dreaming, but it was not a dream.","He...was very small!","He was so small that he had no eyes, no mind, nothing at all except a wall of thin skin and a hunger. He drifted in a warm dark sea he could not perceive and divided, and divided again, and ate, and divided, and never once knew he was alive. Then the warm sea grew cold, and he stopped. That was the whole of it. A microbe, born in a drop of water somewhere, and dead when the water dried.","He was an insect.","Six legs, a hard green shell, and one summer spent climbing the same tall stalk of grass, again and again, toward a light at the top he could never quite reach. Eating. Singing with his wings in the evening. On the last warm day of the year a bird took him from the stalk, and he felt its beak close, and that was that.","Then a virus, never knowing what it was. A mouse, afraid for its entire short life, and right to be. A great grey wolf that ran for eleven years across a winter forest and died old and alone in a den it had dug itself.","Time started, and time died!","He was an orc!","His name was Gashr, and he was born on a battlefield in a Dimension that did not remember him, in the mud behind a war camp, to a mother who died that same night. He grew up hard. He grew up fast. He learned to swing an axe before he could read a single runne, and he learned to read runes anyway, secretly, by firelight, from a stolen book he hid under his bedroll for twenty years.","He fought in nine wars and won six. He married a one-armed smith who made him laugh. They had four children, and he buried two of them. He was eighty-one when a young warlord with a borrowed Intent burned his village for the ore beneath it, and he died in the doorway of his own house with the axe still in his hands, and the last thing he thought was that he had never finished the stolen book.","Time moved.","He was now a fae, glass-winged and bright, and lived nine hundred years in a moonlit forest singing songs to the trees. The forest was cleared for a road. She followed it for a while, then stopped following, and faded away into the morning light.","He was a goblin named Nib, who stole shiny things and was proud of every one of them and was, all things considered, very happy. He was hanged for a stolen spoon at the age of forty. It had been a very nice spoon!","He was a Gu!","Small and pale and new, a Common Gu, born out of loose existence in the drifting light of a Chrysalis, a hundred of one thing and nothing of anything else. It did not want much: to drift, to be warm, to be left alone.","For a while, it was. Then a hand closed around it. A great, patient, greedy hand, and he felt himself taken, and bound, and set on a workbench, and slowly, carefully, ground down into material for someone else’s ring. It hurt the entire time. It took a very long time. Nobody asked him anything, and when it was over, there was nothing left of him but a faint glow in a stranger’s craft.","Noah felt that one more than any of the others!","Time moved on.","He was a Provenance Lifeform, self-made, proud, who spent three million years building a Lineage out of nothing and watched another Provenance Lineage collect it in an afternoon.","He was a Descendant, born with a sentence in his blood, who lived four hundred years in a gilded court knowing every day of it exactly when he would die, and died exactly then, cursed.","And at the very last, he was an Immense One!","An Immense One!","No one could have held all of it. He stood at the top of existence for longer than there had been anything to measure it by, and existence agreed with every word he spoke, and he grew bored, and then cold, and then far beyond cold.","He watched Ages rise and fall like breath on a window. Whatever he wanted, he took, because nothing had ever told him no. And then one day something did, something he had never seen coming, and his vastness caved around it, and he learned, for the first and only time, what the smallest bug in the mud had always known.","That everything ends!","Microbe, insect, orc, goblin, Gu, Immense One. Killed or faded or simply finished.","Each life he lived, he lived through to its very last moment, and he felt each last moment arrive. And when the last life ended, he was not released.","He was held there, at the end of all of them at once, and made to feel every death he had just lived, not one after another but together, all of them, the whole weight of time running out for everything at the same instant.","That was the death of time.","It was the worst thing he had ever felt!","Even the cold of the Long Night felt mild!","It went on and on, past anything that had a name, past the frozen underworld, past any lives he lived!","He had no body to scream with and no mind left to break, and he did not break anyway, because some small stubborn thing at the very center of him refused.","It was human, that thing. It was the part of him that had lived every one of those lives and remembered, even in the worst of it, that every one of them had been worth living.","He held on to that.","He held on to it through the end of everything!","—","Around Noah, in the frozen purple sky, his body changed!","The rivers of time were still pouring into him, but they were no longer flooding him. They were being taken in. Drawn down into his Root, which had begun, very slowly, to beat again, and every beat it took pulled more of the lived and ended time inside it and pressed it close.","His Provenance did not grow. That was the strangest part of all. It did not swell or surge or climb. Instead it compressed!","Every life he had lived pressed down into it like snow packing into ice, layer on layer on layer, countless years of living and ending crushed into something smaller and denser and harder with every beat of his Root, refined past anything a mere number could hold.","His Root drank it and was reinforced, deepened, hardened, until it turned inside him with a weight it had never had, the weight of having been every kind of thing there was.","His body followed!","The crystalline frame thickened, broadened at the shoulders and chest, the long lean lines of him filling out with the dense, heavy muscle of a man who had lived more lives than there were stars.","The youth drained out of his face. Not old, not bent, but older. Fine lines settled at the corners of his eyes. His jaw set harder. He looked like someone who had worked a very long time and endured a great deal and come out the other side stronger for every day of it.","And around him, clouds began to bloom!","Clouds of dream. Soft, pale, shining faintly blue and gold, they rose off his skin and spread out through the frozen sky, slow and silent, and where they drifted near the weavings of time, the weavings flickered!","The stopped disks of time, frozen mid-turn, trembled in their places. Currents of old violet smoke wavered and blurred at their edges.","Even the time-scales laid along THE First Gu of Time’s own wings shivered as the dream-clouds brushed past them, and for one long, astonishing moment, something in all that frozen time stirred, and softened, and began, faintly and against every law that had ever governed it, to dream.","Time itself was dreaming!","THE First Gu of Time pulsed!","Her crown of eyes, which had watched countless Ages without once looking away, turned toward the clouds drifting through her wings. The Ages burning in them flickered. For the first time since she had appeared, she did not look like a being who already knew how everything ended.","The two Rare Time Gu had stopped gloating. They shrank back against their mother, lures trembeling.","In the middle of the dreaming sky, Noah opened his eyes.","They were not young eyes anymore. They held an age that had nothing to do with years, the age of a microbe and an orc and a goblin and a Gu and an Immense One, the age of every life he had just lived and every death he had just felt, and they were so ancient that for a moment that one could mistake them for the eyes of an Immense One.","He looked at her for a long while before he spoke.","\" Thank you ,\" Noah said.","His voice was quiet, and deeper than it had been.","\" Thank you for showing me that .\" He glanced at the two Rare Gu pressed close against her amber body, and then back up at her crown of burning eyes. \" And I apologize for what I did. Wholeheartedly. I will not use Gu as materials for anything I do. Not again.\"","The dream-clouds drifted around him, and the frozen time went on dreaming.","\" My dreams. My time. My humanity ,\" Noah said. \" That will be enough.\"","...!"]},{"number":5793,"title":"Chapter 5793: Chapter 5792: A Boundless Dream of Time!","paragraphs":["For a long while after he spoke, nothing in the purple sky moved except the clouds of dream drifting off Noah’s shoulders.","He let them drift. He was still sorting through what had just been poured into him, the microbe and the orc and the goblin with his very nice spoon, the Gu on the workbench, the Immense One who learned at the very end what every bug in the mud had always known. It was a great deal to carry. He found, a little to his suprise, that he did not want to put any of it down.","THE First Gu of Time watched him with her crown of burning eyes!","\"Gu are a passive kind ,\" she said at last. \" We do not hunt. We do not hoard. For the most part, we do not even want. And a great many beings have taken that as permission. \"","The Ages in her eyes turned slowly. \" The worst of them, and the one who took more of my children than any other, was an engineer. His name was Atlas.\"","...!","Noah kept perfectly still!","On his finger, the faint illusory ring that only he could see gave no sign of anything at all.","\" He is gone now ,\" THE First Gu of Time went on, \" but his way of thinking has outlived him. Others study what he left and try to walk where he walked. They collect my children as ingredients, as though a living thing were a measure of salt.\"","Her voice stayed soft and even. \"I will not ask you to make it your life’s work. But if you continue to travel this place, and you see any being grinding down a Gu, I would have you stop them. And save whichever of my children you can.\"","She let her gaze drift out over the frozen time-disks, the violet smoke, the vast drowning dark of the Chrysalis beyond them.","\"I am a Gu myself, you understand. I am passive as well, most of the time. I would have remained so today . But the cold is spreading everywhere now, and a great many of my children will die in it no matter what anyone does. I could not simply watch while two more were taken on top of that.\"","Noah inclined his head. He had nothing to say to that which would have been worth saying.","\"Existence is vast ,\" she said, more quietly. \" It does not have to be cruel.\"","The frozen disks trembled faintly in the dream-clouds around them!","\" You should also know that with the coming of the cold, doors that were shut for a very long time are beginning to open again. Those who are already Immense will not find those doors easily. Most of them will never find them at all. Those who grasp Immensity in this cold, on the other hand, may have a chance. \"","Her many eyes settled on him. \" I have a few children in whom I see that chance. There is a brilliance in them. I saw a similar brilliance in you when I passed this way, and in the two you brought with you. That is why I found it such a shame to see what the three of you were doing.\"","She was quiet for a moment.","\" You have a chance. All of you do. But in existence, that is all it will ever be. A chance. Nothing at all is guaranteed.\"","Then her wings, which had gone still, began to stir again!","The two Rare Time Gu drew in close against her amber body. The stopped moments along her wings rippled like scales settling on a great animal about to rise. And as the vast shape of her began to withdraw into the purple sky, THE First Gu of Time turned her crown of eyes back to him one last time.","\"I meant to tell you that you have been touched by time, \" she said. \" But that is not quite right, is it. Your dreams are unusual. They have taken the time into themselves rather than the other way around.\"","The Ages in her eyes flickered, curious. \"I doubt you will ever reach where I stand, where time is concerned. But should you grasp something profound, and wish to challenge time itself, you will find me at the very end of it.\"","BOOM!","The sky shook, once, and THE First Gu of Time was gone!","The two Rare Gu went with her, violet wings shrinking into nothing, and in the space where her vast amber body had hung there was only purple cloud and slow violet smoke. Around Noah, the frozen time-disks lurched, caught their spin again, and went on turning. The light started arriving on time!","The next moment came back into existence as quietly as it had left, and everything that had been pinned in place simply continued, as though it had never been stopped at all.","Noah stood alone in the dreaming sky!","He was quiet for a long time. Then he raised his hand and looked at the faint illusory ring on his finger.","Atlas had not said a word since the purple sky came down. Not one! The old engineer, who had an opinion on everything and could not bear to let a clever thing pass without comment, had been utterly silent while a First Gu named him the worst hunter of her children in all existence.","\" Atlas ,\" Noah said calmly. \" The Time Inscription you meant to write with your Quill. What was it going to do?\"","He asked without accusation. But he asked it knowing now, as he had not known that morning, that even the grandest inscription was not absolute. That behind every clever piece of engineering there might be a great many small lives that had never been asked.","The ring stayed silent a moment longer.","\" It...was an inscription for advantage, \" Atlas said at last. His voice was quieter than Noah had ever heard it. \"Time, turned to your favor. As the seconds passed, you would charge it, and when it was charged you would activate it, and your Provenance and your foundations would gain the progression of days. Or weeks, or months, depending on the rarity of the Gu at its heart and the depth of your Provenance. That was the plan, anyway. But now...\"","He did not finish.","There was no need. Noah had promised, in this same purple sky, not to hunt Gu or use them as material for anything he did. And an inscription with a Rare Gu at its heart was exactly that.","\" Then I will make things simpler for myself,\" Noah said.","He lowered his hand.","\" Gu are external. At the end of the day, that is all they are, to someone like me. Something outside of me, taken and made use of. Your engineering needed them because it was your engineering, built your way, on your terms. That is not a flaw in it. It is simply what it was.\"","He looked out across the turning time-disks. \" But I can have my own existential engineering, and it can need different things. For me, my dreams are enough. My dreams are sufficient. And right now, my dreams have more perception of time, and more weavings of time, than anything I could have caught and put in a ring.\"","HUUM!","Noah closed his eyes, and raised his hands!","The dream-clouds around him surged! They rose off his skin thicker and brighter than before, rolling out through the purple sky in great slow banks of blue and gold, and through them, from somewhere deep inside him, rivers of Infinity began to pour. Dialetheic Infinity, the finite and the infinite at once, a truth that was also its own opposite. It had always run through him. But now it was different.","Now every river of it carried time in it, violet threads of lived and ended moments woven all through the blue and gold, running beside every current.","\"An impossibility ,\" Noah said quietly, with his eyes still closed, \" is only a moment that has not been dreamed yet.\"","The rivers rolled out around him!","\" People think Infinity means more. More and more and more, forever, a line that never stops. It is not that. Infinity is every moment at once. The beginning and the end of a thing, and everything between them, all held in the same hand. I have been every kind of life there is, from the first breath to the last. So I know.\" He opened his hands wider.","\" Nothing is impossible that has a beginning. And everything has a beginning. Even the end of time began somewhere.\"","In that deep, strange stillness, he lifted one hand and laid it against his own chest.","Time poured out of it!","Boundless and violet and gold, spiling out of the spinning mobius at the center of him and away into the dreaming sky, and as it poured he remembered. Gashr in the doorway with her axe. Nib and his spoon. The small pale Gu on the workbench. The wolf in its den. The Immense One who had never once been told no. Every life he had lived, from its first moment to its last, and every stretch of time that had begun and ended inside each one.","\"A dream, from its beginning to its end, is a measure of time,\" Noah said. \"A dream can start. A dream can end. And that alone is enough to mark where time begins, and where it stops.\"","His hand stayed flat against his chest. \" Between my dreams and existence, there is a gap. I can only ever try to close it. I can only ever live my dreams, across time.\"","...!","His Provenance raged around him!","It came off him in a great storm, as it had in the frozen underworld, but it was not blue and gold alone anymore. Purple ran through it now. Deep violet hues, the color of the Rare Gu’s burning wings and the amber of THE First Gu of Time and every stopped moment in her scales, threaded through every current of his Provenance, and the whole storm of it turned and turned and would not settle.","| THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer has acquired a Quality of Time.|","|Having lived and ended countless lives in the Death of Time, your Dreams now measure time from within.|","|The first Osmontian Inscription has been forged: THE OSMONTIAN INSCRIPTION OF THE DREAMING HOUR.|","|Ingredients: your Root. Your Provenance. Time. Nothing external.|","|Passive, THE Lived Hour: while you live, your Dreams live longer. Every second that passes in existence, your Provenance and foundations are refined as though far more time had passed within your Dreams. At present, days for each second. As your Provenance deepens, weeks. Then months. No charging is required. It does not stop.|","|Active, THE Dreamt Epoch: by entering a deep Dream, you may compress a far greater span of refinement into a single held moment. The span scales with the depth of the Dream and the density of your Provenance.|","|Passive, THE Hour That Dreams: weavings of time that act upon you are drawn into your Dreams. Near you, time does not simply pass. It dreams, and a dreaming hour moves as you would have it move.|","...!","It was everything Atlas had meant to build!","More, in places! And there was no Gu at the heart of it. There was nothing at the heart of it at all except Noah himself, his Root and his Provenance and the time he had lived through in the dark. It was his, entirely and truly, in a way no ring on his finger had ever been.","The illusory ring was silent for a long moment!","\"I promised to teach you a great many things,\" Atlas said. There was something in his voice Noah could not quite place. Not bitterness. Something older and more tired than bitterness. \" Why do I get the feeling that you are about to tell me you don’t really need my engineering?\"","Noah opened his eyes.","\" Everyone’s path is different, \" he said. \" You were a grand engineer. You can still build things as you always built them. I am not an engineer. I am a dreamer, who can choose to engineer things when he wishes. And I dream of infinite possibilities, so what I do and what you do are going to part ways sometimes.\"","He looked at the ring. \" You helped me. I can still help you. But I will follow my own path the way I choose to. I will learn every wonder existence has to show me, and then I will take them into myself however I see fit.\"","He lifted his gaze from the ring, out past the turning time-disks and the violet smoke, into the vast and boundless dark of the Chrysalis.","\" Existence breathes. Epochs pass. Civilizations rise and become monuments, and the monuments crumble into memory, and by the time that breath comes again, even the memory is gone. All of them. Boundless civilizations, boundless dreams, every one of them lost somewhere in time. \"","His Provenance roared around him, blue and gold and purple. \" And in all those epochs, in all of that lost time, I...want to reign supreme.\"","HUUM!","The dream-clouds rolled outward across the whole of the sky!","\" I want to experience boundless existence,\" Noah said, \" and reign supreme!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5794,"title":"Chapter 5794: Chapter 5793: There Will Only Be Me!","paragraphs":["<THE Sealed One>","The feast had been going on for three days, and THE Sealed One had enjoyed almost none of it.","It was held in the great hall of the Aurum Crest, the highest palace of an Observable Existence that the Superbius Gilded had ruled for eleven thousand years. The hall was gold. Everything in it was gold, the floor and the pillars and the long tables and the vaulted ceiling far overhead, where a painted sun made of real, burning light hung eternally at noon.","The Superbius liked it that way. Pride was the root of their power, and nothing fed pride quite like a room that shone back at you from every surface.","There were hundreds of them at the tables. Tall and beautiful and gilded to the fingertips, their skins shining faintly with the Ego that made them what they were, their voices loud and warm and very pleased with themselfs. They told stories of old conquests and laughed at the stories they had heard a thousand times, and toasted each other’s victories, and argued, fiercely and happily, about whose great-great-grandfather had been the grander tyrant, and then they toasted that too.","And every few minutes, one of them would rise, and lift a golden cup, and turn toward the head of the table.","\" To our great honor!\"","\"To THE Sealed One!\"","The whole hall would roar it back, cups raised, faces bright, and THE Sealed One would incline his head and lift his own cup, and smile.","He was very good at smiling!","He sat at the head of the long table in a high-backed chair of gold that the Superbius had made for him specially, tall and pale and composed, his long hair pale gold shading into white, his long dark coat immaculate against all that shining metal.","On either side of him lounged a Luxuria. One was dark-haired and laughing, draped half across the arm of his chair, feeding him grapes she had dipped in honey. The other sat curled at his feet with her head resting against his knee, humming some old song of her people, content in the simple, uncomplicated way of a being whose whole existence was built around wanting and being wanted.","They were happy. All of them!","He watched them being happy, and he tried.","He had always tried. Across more Ages than he could count, THE Sealed One had sought out connection as other beings sought out food.","Thats why he mixed in with useless Gilded Ones like he was today. He had mixed with Descendants and Provenance Lifeforms at certain points. Just to...feel.","He had sat at feasts like this one in a thousand Observable Existences. He had lived for centuries among the Gilded in particular, because the Gilded felt so loudly. The Superbius and their bottomless pride. The Luxuria and their hungers. The Ira and their glorious, burning rage. They lived so openly and simply inside their own emotions, and he had always thought that if he stood close enough to feelings that strong, some of it might catch in him, as a spark catches in dry grass.","It never had.","He had tried Descendants. Walked among the sons and daughters of Those Who Remain, with their borrowed grandeur and their sentences in their blood. He had tried Provenance Lifeforms, proud self-made things who should, of anyone, have understood what it was to stand alone at the top of something. And every time, in every hall, at every table, it was the same.","He felt like an outsider!","No guest still learning the customs, either. An outsider as a man is an outsider at an anthill.","He could sit among them, and talk with them, and let them feed him grapes and toast his name, fuck them and make love to them, and underneath all of it he could feel, as clearly as he felt his own heartbeat, that he was above them.","All of them. Every being in every hall he had ever sat in. And a being who stands above everything cannot touch anything. He can only look down.","The Luxuria at his side pressed another honeyed grape to his lips, laughing.","The hall roared his name again.","THE Sealed One set down his cup.","\" This... isn’t it,\" he said quietly.","The dark-haired Luxuria paused, a grape halfway to his mouth. \" My lord?\"","\" This isn’t it .\" He looked out across the golden hall, at the hundreds of shining, laughing faces. \"I don’t feel a thing.\"","HUUM!","He snapped his fingers!","The sound was very small. It was the only sound in the hall for a moment, because every voice in it had stopped at once. Then every Gilded Lifeform in the Aurum Crest burst!","Hundreds of them, all at the same instant. The Superbius at the long tables, mid-toast, cups still raised. The Luxuria at his side with the grape in her fingers, and the one at his feet with her song half-sung.","Every one of them came apart into a puddle of crimson gold blood that splashed across the golden floor and the golden tables and the golden walls, until the whole shining hall was painted red and gold and dripping!","There was no scream. There had been no time for one!","THE Sealed One sat very still in his gold chair in the middle of it as for ever a brief moment...he almost felt something . Almost!","Then he opened his mouth!","The blood came to him. It rose off the floor and the tables and the walls in long slow ribbons, crimson gold and shining with the last of all that pride and hunger, and flowed across the air and into his mouth, and he drank it. All of it!","Every drop of Ego and every scrap of feeling that had lived in hundreds of Gilded Lifeforms a moment ago, and he took it into himself without hurry, like a man finishing a cup of water he is not particularly thirsty for.","When it was done, the hall was only gold again, and very empty, and quiet.","His expression had not changed at all through any of it. There was no pleasure on his face. No triumph. Only a tired, faraway apathy, and under the apathy, if anyone had been left alive to see it, something very much like sadness.","He sighed.","\" You’ve been watching from up there this whole time ,\" THE Sealed One said to the painted sun. \" What is it?\"","...!","The painted sun opened!","It split down the middle like an eyelid, and behind it there was no sun at all, only an eye. Vast and dark and old, burning with a sleepless, patient attention that did not blink, and never had, and never would!","| THE SLEEPLESS FIEND regards you from above.|","|\"You are truly a hateful thing.\"|","|\"And yet all of them believe you hold the best chance of opening the door. So they support you.\"|","THE Sealed One laughed softly, and leaned back in his golden chair.","\" But you were always the one who found me,\" he said. \" Ages ago, when I was only bright and very young and very stupid about it. You came down to look, and you never quite left .\" He spread his pale hands. \" So. Any news?\"","| THE SLEEPLESS FIEND answers coldly.|","|\"You will be given what you want.\"|","|\"You missed the one called the Assimilation Factor. That was careless of you.\"|","|\"But every other identified Anomaly, every Undefined Lifeform we have found, will be given to you to devour. Your list is long.\"|","...!","And in the empty golden air of the hall, names began to rise!","They wrote themselves in lines of pale fire, one after another, drifting up toward the vaulted ceiling like sparks from a bonfire that would not stop burning.","THE REMNANT SEER.","THE LAST OF HOUSE VESPER.","THE ORCHARD THAT WALKS.","THE INFINITY EATER.","THE CONTINUUM PARADOX.","THE WRITER OF MYTHOS.","ANAXIMANDER.","THE CREATURE...","On and on they climbed, dozens of them, a long burning column of every strange and singular existence that had drawn the notice of Those Who Remain in this cold Age. And at the very top of the list, larger than the rest, brighter than the rest, burning above them all:","NOAH OSMONT.","...!","THE Sealed One rose from his chair and walked out into the empty hall! He lay down in the middle of it, on his back, among the bones.","There were a great many bones. The Gilded had left them behind when their blood came to him, white and scattered across the golden floor, and he lay in them as another being might lie in a field of grass, and looked up at the burning names.","\" Do you know ,\" he said, \" how unlikely it is that any of them will ever become anything?\"","His voice drifted up toward the painted eye, calm and conversational and completely without mercy.","\"I have watched anomalies for a very long time. Existence throws them up by the thousand, these strange little one-of-a-kind things, and everyone gets very excited, and then they die. They die in wars. They die in winters. They die of their own cleverness. The chance that any single one of them becomes something that matters is so small it barely deserves the word.\"","He lifted one pale hand toward the column of fire and let his fingers trail across the names. \" So why leave it to chance? Why let them squander it? I can take every one of them into myself. Their lives. Their existences. Everything strange and singular about them, all of it put to use as fuel for something far greater than any of them would ever have become on their own.\"","He smiled up at the name at the very top.","\" They should be grateful, really. It is the only way most of them will ever mean anything at all.\"","The names burned on above him. THE Sealed One lay in the bones and the gold and looked at them for a long, long time.","\" They keep saying three ,\" he said softly. \" THE Augury of the Long Night. Three at the turning. It is the one scrap of it any of them could scry through the fog, and they will not stop repeating it. I am tired of the number.\"","His gold eyes narrowed.","\" There will not be three. There will only be one. There will only...be me.\"","BOOM!","The empty hall shook! The golden pillars trembled on their bases, and the bones across the floor rattled and jumped, and the burning names above flared so bright that for a moment the whole Aurum Crest was lit with pale fire from end to end!","Above him, the vast dark eye of THE SLEEPLESS FIEND watched without blinking.","|THE SLEEPLESS FIEND recites words he has only recently come to hold.|","|\"And at the turning, count three.|","|One shall look upon all that is, and grieve.|","|One shall take up every weight, and not set it down.|","|One shall no longer remain, and yet remain.|","|By their three hands the cloth is torn, or the cloth is woven anew,|","|and no living soul may say which\"|","THE Sealed One went very still among the bones!","Three is a number, and one is a number. For all their scrying, the Immense Ones had only ever held a scrap of THE Augury of the Long Night, a count of three glimpsed through the winter’s fog.","| THE SLEEPLESS FIEND observes.|","|\"You say there will only be one. The Augury does not disagree with you. It simply declines to promise.\"|","The eye pulsed, once, slow.","|\" Come to the Legacy. A great variety of Gu have been captured for your consumption.\"|","|\"They are all feeding you. Fattening you up. Pouring everything they have into the hope that you are the one who opens the door.\"|","|\"If you do not deliver what they want, boy, oh boy.\"|","...!","THE Sealed One laughed!","He rose from the floor among the bones, slowly, unhurried, and the last scattered droplets of crimson gold blood on the golden floor lifted and flowed into him as he stood. He straightened his dark coat, and looked up at the eye of THE SLEEPLESS FIEND, and at the burning list of everything he meant to eat, and at the one name that shone above all the others.","\" Epochs have passed ,\" THE Sealed One said.","\" The same things will rise, and the same things will fall, and the same small bright things will think they are special right up until someone takes them.\"","His gold eyes shone in the empty hall.","\"In every epoch that has passed, and in every epoch still to come, only one will remain supreme. And it...will be me.\"","...!"]},{"number":5795,"title":"Chapter 5795: Chapter 5794: Myths and Legends!","paragraphs":["<THE Writer of Mythos>","The page was white before her, and then it was not as words appeared.","I will die.","She tore it away. Beneath it lay another page, just as white, and she set her pen to it with great care, meaning to write something else entirely. A river, perhaps. A mountain. A girl walking home in the rain. Anything at all.","And yet...","I will die.","She tore that one away too!","The floor around her desk was deep in pages. Hundreds of them, thousands, drifting in soft white banks against the legs of her chair, and every one of them said the same three words in the same neat hand. Her hand. She had not meant to write a single one of them!","She sat at the heart of an Existential Immense Domain, and it was not hers. It was far too grand to be hers. It was a library that had no walls, only shelves, shelves that climbed up past the reach of any sight and went on climbing, carved from a dark and polished wood that had never grown on any tree.","Every shelf was packed with books, and every book was a life, and every life was written in ink. Rivers of that ink ran slow and black through the air between the shelves, curling and settling, never spilling a drop. The whole place smelled of old paper and of rain on stone. There was no ceiling. Far above, where a ceiling should have been, there was only a vast pale sky of blank parchment, and across it, even here, fell the snow.","This was the personal domain of an Immense One. THE MATRIARCH OF INK!","Her mother.","The Writer of Mythos dipped her pen again. The ink came up black and shining. She held it over a fresh page for a long time, and she thought, very hard, of a river in a green valley in spring.","And yet..","I will die.","...!","She set the pen down. Her hand was shaking!","\" Since the snow began to fall ,\" she said quietly, to the shelves, to the ink, to the endless pale sky, \" this has been the only Mythos of my existence. The only one. Before, I could write anything. A war and its ending. A kingdom and its fall. My own next breath, if I wished, and my Narrative would agree to it. Now my Narrative has only one thing left to say to me, and it will not stop saying it.\"","She looked down at the banks of white pages drifting around her ankles.","\"It tells me I will die. Not in some far Age, not someday. Soon. And no matter what I write, however I try to write around it, this one line is always what comes out of the pen.\"","Her voice caught, just slightly. \" And it tells me who. It will be existence itself that kills me. Not an enemy, not a curse. Existence. \"","She laughed, and there was no humor in it. \" Isn’t that cruel, Mother? That the Mythos I am most certain of is the one I most want to be wrong?\"","The ink in the air went very still!","Then the whole domain seemed to lean toward her, as a room leans toward the one who owns it, and the pale sky above rippled like a page being turned.","| THE MATRIARCH OF INK speaks.|","|\"Nothing will collapse you. Nothing will take you from me.\"|","|\"If existence itself comes calling, my ink will write it a different ending. I have written endings for things far older than existence’s patience.\"|","The rivers of ink curled close around the desk, slow and protective.","|\" And you are THE Writer of Mythos, are you not? Then write a different ending. Write a Mythos in which, whatever comes, you do not die.\"|","|\"Your next Mythos is your Root of Immensity. Finish it. Once you have, I will take you to THE Legacy of THE Fraternity. I have a few friends there, at least.\"|","The Writer of Mythos wiped her eyes with the back of her ink-stained hand.","\" Why not THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity?\" she asked. \" The few weavings of Mythos I have ever caught about Legacies all say it is one of the grandest there is. Lucy founded it. THE Acharya.\"","|\"THE Acharya is not the only grand Lifeform ever to rise in existence and found a Legacy,\"| said THE MATRIARCH OF INK. |\"She was one of the most powerful, certainly. But the grandest Legacy is not always the most fitting one. There are things in THE Legacy of THE Fraternity you can obtain that will suit you far better than anything in hers.\"|","The ink settled.","|\" But put all of that aside for now. Write your Mythos. Write your Root. I will share my Immensity with you freely.\"|","|\"You were born with a Root of Immensity already in you, and you refused it, because you wanted to earn one of your own. You have earned it. You have labored long enough. Now you need only claim what was always yours.\"|","|\"It is time for you to ascend.\"|","...!","The Writer of Mythos was quiet for a moment.","Then she smiled. It was a glorious smile, bright and sure and a little fierce, the smile of a girl who has been told by the only voice in existence she has never once doubted that she is allowed to win.","She nodded!","There was no fresh page this time. Instead she pinned up her long dark hair with the pen, then drew it free again, turned it in her fingers, and set its nib against her own wrist, against her own skin, against her own existence!","And she began to write!","The ink flowed out of the pen and into her, bright and black and glittering, and the rivers of her mother’s ink rose up all around her in answer, pouring down through the endless shelves toward the little desk at the heart of the Immense Domain. The pale sky rippled from end to end, and the white pages on the floor lifted in a slow spiral around her chair.","Her pen moved, and a Mythos of her own Root began to take shape across her skin.","But somewhere at the very back of her mind, where the pen could not reach, a single line was still waiting. It had not gone anywhere. It simply sat there, patient and certain, in her own neat hand.","I will die.","—","<THE Creature>","There was nothing where their Observable Existence used to be.","It was not even emptiness, since emptiness was at least a kind of shape. This was undefinition, a vast murky foam of obsidian that went on in every direction, bubbling slowly, with no floor and no sky and no edge, as though existence had been scraped out of this place and nobody had ever bothered to fill it back in.","Once, there had been a home here. A small Observable Existence, the one where he had first opened his eyes, and Osmont was also born here, and Anaximander, and a great many others, all of them sprung from the same unremarkable corner of everything. THE Sealed One had taken it. Now there was only the foam!","THE Creature sat in the middle of it.","The snow fell here too. It fell everywhere now. But here it did something it did nowhere else. It did not settle on him or slide off him. It flowed into him, drifted in through his vast dark shoulders and out through his back, and around him in slow eddies, moving through his body exactly as it moved through the foam, as if there were no difference between the two. As if he were not sitting in this empty place at all, but were simply part of it.","As if he were one with existence!","He was titanic now, even for him as an invisible statue seemed to be fully layered unto him. His figure rose out of the obsidian foam like a mountain range with a man’s shape, wreathed in flames, white and obsidian, burning together and never mixng, the white in the black and the black in the white. And beneath the flames, simmering close against his skin, lay a Provenance that had no color at all. Neither clear nor blank, it was simply the color of existence before anyone had decided what color existence should be.","He raised one enormous hand and looked at it.","\" What was established in the future, \" THE Creature said, \" is bleeding into the present.\"","His voice was flat, unhurried, heavy as always.","\" My Provenance of existence in the future is my Provenance of existence now. I brought it here.\" He turned the hand over, slowly. \" But to do so, I crossed many bounds. Did things existence does not do. That...bore a cost.\"","He lowered his hand to his chest.","There was a crack there! It ran from his collarbone down toward his heart, jagged and faintly glowing, and through it, if anyone had been close enough to look, they would have seen something forming inside him. A Root. A Root of Immensity, and not of any one thing in particular, but of existence itself!","It was beautiful and it was vast and it was fractured, split through along a line that did not close, and every so often it flickered, unsteady, and when it did, the flames around THE Creature flared too high, and something moved across his flat, heavy face that was very nearly anger, or very nearly grief, before it settled again.","He sat with that for a while, in the foam and the snow.","Then, for the sake of stability, he opened his mouth.","\" Anaximander ,\" THE Creature said. \" Come .\"","...!","One second later, his oldest friend was standing beside him in the undefinition, with his hands in his sleeves.","He looked exactly as he always had. White scholar’s robes, a little rumpled. Tousled hair. No authority on him at all, none whatsoever, and still the obsidian foam drew back from his feet as though it had remembered a rule it had forgotten. Only his eyes had changed.","They were older than they had been, far older, the eyes of a man who had spent a great deal of time in places where time behaved strangely and come back carrying some of it.","Anaximander smiled at THE Creature.","He did not say anything. He simply stepped closer and laid one hand on the titan’s vast shoulder.","The flames eased! The crack across THE Creature’s chest steadied its flickering glow, and the thing that had been moving across his face grew still.","\" Big guy ,\" Anaximander said gently. \" Why does it seem that you did something so hasty?\"","THE Creature was quiet a moment.","\" Existence moves whether the rest of us move or not ,\" he said. \" It moved faster than I expected. So I had to catch up. \"","The white and obsidian flames turned slowly around him. \" A Great Ruler cannot hang back while everything moves past him. I did what had to be done. Like existence, I bear what I must.\"","He looked down at the scholar beside him. \" As do you, my friend.\"","...!","Anaximander said nothing to that. He only kept his hand where it was.","THE Creature regarded him for a long moment, through the drifting snow.","\" Existence now, or existence years from now,\" he said. \" It is still existence. Let me help an old friend. Let me bring your weavings from the future into the present.\"","Anaximander shook his head, still smiling a little.","\"I don’t need anything right now, \" he said. \" I’m good with where I’m at.\"","THE Creature looked at him.","He looked at his oldest friend in the whole of existence, the one who had come every time he was called, the one who had put a hand on his shoulder in a place where nothing else remained, and something in the vast, flat, heavy face shifted in a way it almost never did.","\"I do not wish to be alone, Anaximander,\" THE Creature said.","The snow drifted through him.","\" Existence is boundlessly lonely. Far too many things exist in it, and still one can feel desolate among all of them.\" The flames burned low and steady.","\" There is much to be done. It would be grand if we could move as we used to. Together.\"","...!","Anaximander was quiet for a while.","Then he smiled, lightly and he sighed.","\" Okay ,\" he said . \"I was thinking of relaxing for a bit, but...\"","He tipped his head back and looked up at the snow falling out of the endless obsidian dark. \" Those with power and the means to use it have a responsibility not to only relax. Alright. Alright.\"","HUUM!","With that, existence began to swirl!","The obsidian foam churned. The undefinition around them heaved and rolled, and out of the dark overhead, boundless storms of snow came cascading down, thicker than they had fallen anywhere, pouring over the two figures in the place where their home had been.","Anaximander raised a hand to shield his eyes.","THE Creature did not!","The snow poured down on him, and for the first time since he had sat in this place, it did not flow through him. It settled! It gathered on his vast shoulders, heavier and heavier, the weight of a whole Age’s winter piling up on him in the dark.","Anaximander glanced at it, and reached up as if to brush it off.","\" Leave it ,\" THE Creature said.","He rose to his feet, slow and titanic, with the whole weight of the falling winter on his shoulders.","And he did not set it down."]},{"number":5796,"title":"Chapter 5796: Chapter 5795: Sparks and Fear!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","THE First Gu of Time was gone.","The purple sky of the Chrysalis had gone back to being only a sky.","The time-disks spun on through the clouds as though nothing had hapened. The violet smoke drifted. Far off, something enormous and slow turned over in the murk and went back to sleep. And Noah stayed exactly where he was, floating in the middle of it all, because he had just been given a new piece of himself and he wanted to understand it before he took it anywhere else.","THE Osmontian Inscription of THE Dreaming Hour.","He had forged it out of nothing but his own Root, his own Provenance, and the time he had lived through. No Gu at its heart. No borrowed material. It was his in a way nothing he had ever carried had been his, and yet he needed to fully understand what it actually did. The prompts had told him, of course. But prompts were only words. He wanted to feel it.","So he started with THE Lived Hour!","He closed his eyes and turned his attention inward, and waited for a single second to pass.","It passed!","And inside him, far more than a second went by. He felt it happen. His Provenance turned over and settled, turned over and settled, again and again, as though it had been left to work at itself through a long quiet day with nothing to disturb it. His foundations did the same. An entire day’s worth of refinement, worked through in the space of one breath, and then the next second came, and it happened again.","That was all it did. It simply kept happening, every second, without being asked!","Noah opened his eyes and looked at his hands.","He had half expected his attributes to start climbing. That was what progress had always looked like, for most of his rise. More. Bigger numbers, bigger reserves, a bigger shadow thrown across existence. But that was not what THE Lived Hour was doing to him at all.","It was pressing him down!","Every second, every hidden day of refinement packed inside that second, pressed his Provenance a little closer together. Tighter. Denser. The same amount of him, fitted into a smaller and smaller space, as a blacksmith hammers the same iron over and over until the metal that comes out the other side weighs the same and is nothing like what went in.","He looked deeper, down past his foundations, past the Root, down to the very smallest pieces of what he was made of.","His quarks!","Not long ago, in a very different stage of his existence, he had remade every quark of his body one by one into something that carried his own aims. They were still there, all of them, countless as sand. But now, looking at them, he found each one packed. Crammed full!","Dense with his Provenance, blue and gold, pressed into every one of them past anything he would have believed a single quark could hold. And threaded all through that Provenance, cold and clean, was something else.","The Long Night!","The cold was in him. It had been in him since the frozen underworld. But he had always felt it as something he carried. Something he survived. Now, looking down at his own quarks, he saw that the cold had been compressed in alongside his Provenance, layer on layer, until the two had become one substance. Warm and cold. Dream and winter. Neither fighting the other.","As he watched, snow began to surge around him!","The Long Night’s snow reached deeper into this murky corner of the Chrysalis, and it came drifting down through the purple clouds toward him, and sank in! Rivers of it, drawn out of the sky, flowing into his crystalline body and down into the packed quarks, and every flake that sank in was pressed down with everything else, and every flake left him cleaner.","As the snow poured in and the Lived Hour pressed and pressed, he felt more and mofe sublime. One by one, any rough specks were ground out and pushed away, until his whole existence, from the surface of his crystalline skin down to the smallest packed quark, was unblemished!","Then he looked at his Root.","THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin turned at the center of him as it always did, the endless mobius spinning in his chest. But it turned heavier now. Slower, with more behind it. And when he looked at it closely, with everything he had, he could see its two natures more clearly than he had ever seen them.","He had known now that his Root was Dual. Conceptual and Physical at once.","On one side of it, the Conceptual side, he could feel the Dreamer. The part of him that dreamed a thing and watched existence adjust to agree. That was the Collector’s kind of power, the Empyros kind, the power of a being who could write something true and make existence live inside the sentence.","One day, if he lived long enough, that part of his Root would make him an Empyros Immense Lifeform, able to rewrite whatever he looked at.","And on the other side, the Physical side, he could feel the weight of his Dreams and infinity and everything else. The packed quarks. The cold compressed into his body until his body had become harder than any material in existence. That was Lucy’s kind of power. THE Infiniverse’s kind. The Fiend kind, a being simply heavier than the rules!","One day, that part of his Root would make him a Fiend Immense Lifeform, so dense and so real that no sentence anyone wrote could hold him.","Both at once!","He had watched the Collector write a perfect sentence on a mountain and break against it. He had watched THE Infiniverse fill a paradox with so much existence it had nowhere left to hide. One of them had been the writer. The other had been the page.","He was going to be both!","Noah smiled quietly, alone in the purple sky. What a ridiculous thing to be. A writer who was also the page, a dreamer who was also the weight. Was there anything in existence that could argue with that?","He did not know.","Then he looked up, and stopped smiling!","He had been floating in this same place for a long while now, testing and feeling and turning his power over, without moving at all. No attack, no dream sent outward, no reaching for anything around him. Only himself, sitting still, letting the Lived Hour work.","And everything around him had begun to dream!","The time-disks nearest him had slowed. Their violet edges had gone soft and blurred, like a thing half remembered. The purple clouds had drifted into strange shapes, towers and faces and wide calm seas that had never been clouds before, shapes that came from nowhere any cloud could have learned them. The violet smoke of old time curled into slow spirals, turning over and over like a sleeper shifting in a warm bed. Even the Dimensions far off in the murk twinkled in a new rhythm, slow and even, like breath.","And drifting close by, not ten paces from him, was a Gu!","A small one. Common, pale and new, the sort he would once have reached out and taken without a second thought. It floated in the purple air with its thin wings drawn in, perfectly still, and it was not afraid of him. It was asleep! Curled up in the dream that was spreading out of him through this whole region of the Chrysalis, and whatever it was dreaming about, it looked content.","Noah looked at it for a long moment.","He did not reach for it!","The whole murky domain around him, the clouds and the time and the smoke and the stars and the small sleeping Gu, had been dreaming quietly while he sat in the middle of it. Simply because he was there. Simply because of what he was.","His Dreamer’s sight opened, and showed him!","| NOAH OSMONT: THE TRUE HUMAN EMPEROR/ THE HUMAN DREAMER|","|VERITAS: 668. PROVENANCE: 761. POTENTIA: INFINITE. PONDUS: 659. OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 674.|","|DENSITY: REFINED. Each point of every attribute now holds far more than it once did. The numbers have not kept pace with what they measure.|","|ROOT: THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin. DUAL CONCEPTUAL AND PHYSICAL EXISTENTIAL ROOT OF IMMENSITY. Future path: EMPYROS and FIEND, at once.|","|PROVENANCES: THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer (Quality of Time). THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign.|","|INFINITY: DIALETHEIC.|","|NINE FOUNDATIONS: INEFFABLE.|","|INSCRIPTIONS: THE Osmontian Inscription of THE Dreaming Hour. THE Existential Foundational Narrative Inscription.|","|STATE: Unblemished. Quarks compressed with Infinity, Provenance, and THE Long Night.|","|PASSIVE EFFECT: Existence near you begins to dream.|","...!","The numbers had barely moved, and he was stronger than he had ever been. Well, barely may have been the wrong word as he HAD been at 500 attribute a day ago.","Noah looked at the panel for a long while, and then at the sleeping Gu, and then out across the whole dreaming domain.","\" With all of this ,\" he said quietly, to no one, \"it should be possible.\"","The clouds drifted in their strange new shapes. The Gu slept on.","\" To dream, and to live freely .\" He let out a slow breath. \" Nothing in existence can be guaranteed. The First Gu was right about that. The Caretaker was right about that .\"","He looked down at his own unblemished hands. \" But I can guarantee my own Dream. That much, at least, I can do.\"","He closed his eyes.","—","Far away across existence, in the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity, another part of him opened its eyes on the Glacial Mountain.","The snow was still falling on the golden monastery. Verys still stood a few paces off, patient in his fur-lined cloak. But the light had changed, and Noah could feel, in the particular stillness of the mountain and the faint new hum running through the Conduits beneath it, that an entire day had truly passed now. Somewhere in the Legacy, things were about to begin.","And in the Existential Root Domain, a third part of him sat in the blue-gold clouds, watching two women.","THE Infiniverse and Ruination had not said much since he sent them home. They had stood beside him before THE First Gu of Time and been able to do nothing, not one thing, and it sat on both of them heavily.","THE Infiniverse had already begun growing new domains to replace the ones that had crumbled, faster than before, harder than before. Ruination sat very still with her eyes scrolling, reading back over everything her Root now kept. It looked very much like they were both about to throw themselves into their own progression grander than they ever had before!","Good!","But one thing at a time.","Existence was vast, and they were young. For all three of them, things were only just beginning to unfold.","And Noah found that what he felt, looking ahead at the Legacy’s gathering, was curiosity. What kind of beings would he meet? What dreams did they carry, what power, what strange and singular ways of looking at existence?","He wanted to know. Not so he could take any of it. So he could learn from it, and dream grander for having seen it.","That was how it had always gone for him, when he thought about it honestly.","THE Creature. Anaximander, who needed no authority at all to be exactly what he was. Ul’moreth. Eon. Atlas and his brilliant, restless engineering. Poona. Moriarty and his spectacles. The Caretaker. And now THE First Gu of Time, who had shown him what everything felt like from the inside, right to its end.","Every one of them had looked at existence differently, and every one of them had given him a spark he could never have struck on his own. Who he was now, he was because of all of them.","That was why he could not simply hide. He could not seal himself away in his Existential Root Domain and grow in the dark, safe and alone, where nothing grand could find him. A being who hid could not dream anything but the inside of its own hiding place!","He had to go out. He had to experience existence, all of it, the frightening parts and the wondrous ones, to be able to dream truly grand dreams.","That was how, across every epoch, he would truly be supreme.","Not by being afraid!"]},{"number":5797,"title":"Chapter 5797: Chapter 5796: The Convocation of Roots! I","paragraphs":["In THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity.","The Existential Conduit beneath Noah’s feet was warm, and it was moving rapidly.","It did not look like a road. It looked like what it was, a vast pillar of flowing authority bent over on its side, pale gold and faintly humming, a river of existence’s own veins laid out through the snowy air of the Legacy.","But it was as firm underfoot as any paved street, and it carried whoever stood on it along its length like a current carrying a leaf, smooth and quiet and sure. Those who knew the Legacy called them the Keepers’ Roads.","Every mountain was joined to every other by them, a web of glowing pathways running through the falling snow between the peaks, and all of them, today, seemed to be running in the same direction.","Verys stood a pace ahead of him on the Conduit, hands clasped behind his back, cloak pulled close against the cold.","Noah looked around.","He was not the only one being carried. Far off across the snowy gulfs, on other Conduits, other small figures stood in pairs. A Legacy Keeper at the front of each, dressed in black and fur the same as Verys, and behind each Keeper, a being.","Some of them were small at this distance. Some of them were not small at all. A great winged shape rode one Conduit in the far east, its wings drawn tight against the snow. A figure made of what looked like slow-burning coal stood on another. Every one of them was fairly powerful, and every one of them was heading the same way.","Ahead of them all rose a mountain!","It was larger than any Elsedimension Mountain Noah had seen in the Legacy, by a long way. It dwarfed the peaks around it as a grown man dwarfs children, broad at its base and climbing, climbing, into the grey of the snowing sky until its summit was lost in cloud.","Snow blanketed it from root to peak, the same as everything else. But even beneath the snow, it seemed to glow faintly, as though something inside it had never quite finished being bright.","\" The Elsedimension Mountain everyone is gathering on ,\" Verys said without turning, \" is called THE Firmament Mountain.\"","\" Mmm ,\" Noah nodddd.","\" It is the oldest mountain in the Legacy, Sir. The first one THE Acharya ever raised .\" The Keeper’s voice took on the careful tone of a man reciting something he had been taught young.","\" Legend says that on this mountain, THE Acharya of Immensity was ambushed by ten other Immense Ones at once. And legend says that she pressed down a single finger, only one, and crushed the whole of their collective Immensity beneath it, and painted the mountain in their blood.\"","HUUM!","Noah looked at the distant snowy peak.","\" Legend says,\" Verys went on, mildly. \" But who knows what really happened, Sir.\"","...!","Ten Immense Ones. One finger!","Noah had watched a single frost-visage of Lucy break THE UNPAID COLLECTOR with one blow. He was not inclined to call the legend an exaggeration.","The Conduit carried them on through the snow, and as the Firmament drew nearer, Noah began to count. A few more pairs converging from the north. A cluster from the west, three Keepers leading three beings in a line.","Others from below, rising up out of the purple-gold rivers on Conduits that climbed like stairways. Ten. Twenty. Thirty. Dozens of them, all beings with Roots of Immensity, all converging on the one great mountain from every direction at once!","He kept himself very reserved.","That had been decided before they left the Glacial Mountain. His Provenance he drew in tight, close against his crystalline skin, and held it there. His Infinity he pulled down into the packed depths of himself where nothing outside could feel it. And he stilled his dreams, so that the snow around him fell only as snow and the Conduit beneath him stayed only a Conduit, and nothing near him, not one flake, began to dream.","He wanted to look first. To see how deep this Legacy really ran before anyone looked back at him.","—","THE Firmament Mountain did had a plain flat surface for a peak.","The Conduits carried everyone up its sides in long glowing spirals, past slopes of blue-white snow and old carved stone half buried beneath it, past great weathered statues of figures Noah did not recognise, standing with their hands raised as though they were holding up the sky.","And at the very top, the mountain simply stopped climbing and opened out, flat and broad and perfectly level, a vast white plain as wide as a small country, open to the snowing sky on every side.","Verys called it THE Plain of Accord.","Everyone who arrived stepped off their Conduits onto the edge of it, and Noah stepped off with them, and looked around.","He did it carefully, the thinnest touch of his Dreamer’s sight, reading only what was offered on the surface. It was enough.","A woman made of what looked like deep water stood a little way off, her whole body clear and blue and faintly rippling, small fish of light swimming slowly through her chest. She read at around six hundred in most attributes.","A tall thin man beside her wore a robe that was not cloth but written text, lines of shifting script running down from his shoulders to his feet, and he read nearer seven hundred.","Further along, a being with the head of a stag and a crown of antlers hung with small bells stood very still, and every bell rang softly whenever he breathed, and Noah read him at nearly eight hundred in attributes!","Five hundred. Six hundred. Seven. The very strongest near eight hundred!","And almost every one of them had their own Provenance! Most of them were self-made, or Progeny with Provenance of their own grown on top of what they had inherited. Ethereal things. Otherworldly things, every one of them looking as though they had stepped out of some older and stranger Chapter of existence to stand here in the snow.","And yet...","Noah looked at the stag-headed one again, the one at nearly eight hundred Provenance Essence, and waited to feel it. The pressure. The weight a being that far above him on paper should have pushed against his existence just by standing nearby.","It did not come!","His existence felt nothing. No oppression at all. The stag-headed being stood there shining with eight hundred Provenance Essence, and Noah, at a number lower than that, simply looked at him and felt entirely at ease.","Was that the compression? Was his foundation really so dense now, every point of him packed so tight by the Lived Hour and the death of time, that a being with more on paper simply could not press on him? He did not know. Nothing could be assumed yet!","Everyone flowed toward the center of the plain, and Noah flowed with them.","Above the center, the thrones hunng.","They floated in the snowing sky in a great ring, dozens of them, high above the plain, each one carved from something different. There was one of black glass, and one that was a single colossal bone, and one made of living wood still in leaf, and one that seemed to be a hollowed star. Every one of them was empty.","Except one!","Poona sat on hers grandly, a throne of pale gold like the curve of a great eye, her legs crossed, her chin on her hand. Her eyes were bright. And when Noah looked up, those bright eyes found him at once and lit up, and she waved at him, openly and cheerfully, from her throne above the gathering of Roots.","Noah waved back.","Several of the beings around him looked from Poona to Noah with open curiosity. He paid them no mind.","Verys led him on across the snow, to where a ring of golden clouds hung a little above the plain, drifting slow and soft and bright. There were dozens of them, arranged in a wide circle beneath the thrones, and each one had a name written across its side in flowing golden script. Verys stopped before one.","It said Osmont!","\"If Sir will take your position ,\" the Keeper said, \" things will begin soon.\"","He bowed.","\"I wish you luck, Sir.\"","Noah rose and sat on the golden cloud. It was softer than it looked and warmer than the snow, and it held him easily. He looked to either side.","Dozens of other golden clouds stretched away around the ring, each with its own name, most still empty. And nearest to him, close enough to speak without raising his voice, was one that read Adrastia.","It was empty!","Noah looked at the name for a moment. He wondered how far that monster of assimilation had come in a single day, with his brand-new Root and his river of time and the woman who lifted him by the scruff of his neck.","He waited.","And while he waited, something locked onto him!","It came from far across the plain, a stifling pressure that closed around his existence and held, heavy, focused, aimed entirely at him.","For one moment he thought an Immense One had turned its eyes his way. But it was not that. It was not quite that heavy. Close, very close, closer than anything he had felt from a being that was not Immense. But not quite.","Noah turned his head to the right.","A figure had just arrived at the edge of the plain, stepping off the last Conduit, and her eyes were already on him. Piercing eyes, green and burning, and around her, existence itself seemed to be suffocating, the ground shimmering at her feet as though it were not sure it wanted to stay solid under her.","She wore a long green robe, heavy and fine, trailing through the snow behind her. On her head sat a crown of verdant leaves and thorns, and it hung there lazily, tipped a little to one side, as if she had put it on in a hurry and never bothered to straighten it.","Noah’s sight opened her.","|MINERVA.|","|VERITAS: 999. PROVENANCE: 999. POTENTIA: 999. PONDUS: 999.|","|ROOT OF IMMENSITY: ??????|","...!","The snow falling all around the plain whipped suddenly heavier!","Noah raised his brows.","Nine hundred and ninety-nine in everything. And a Root he could not read at all. He had not done anything yet. So why did it feel as though he had already been marked as a target?","Minerva looked at him a moment longer, her green eyes steady and unreadable.","Then she turned away, as though he were no longer interesting, and walked to her own golden cloud on the far side of the ring, and sat.","—","The golden clouds filled!","One after another, Legacy Keepers led their charges across the snow and bowed them onto their places, and the ring of clouds under the empty thrones began to fill with terrifying figures. The water-woman. The man robed in text. The stag with the ringing bells. A towering figure in forge-dark armor who sat heavily on a cloud marked Dravos.","A pale smiling youth with a restless mouth on one marked Batiatus, already talking to his neighbor. Dozens more, each stranger than the last, each with a Keeper standing a pace behind their cloud.","And as they filled, Noah sensed that Minerva was not alone at her height.","There were others. A few of them, scattered around the ring. One sat so still in a cloak of grey mist that the mist did not move even in the wind.","Another hummed a low tune that made the snow around her fall in slow spirals. They were close to Minerva’s level, some of them. Perhaps one or two were at it.","Existence was vast, truly. Every single being on this plain carried a Root of Immensity, and every one of them had a Keeper of their own, and there were still more of them arriving!","Many of them talked freely, clearly old acquaintances, laughing and arguing across the gaps between their clouds. Others, like Noah, sat silently and watched.","Then, on the cloud beside him, someone sat down.","Noah turned his head. Achilles Adrastia had arrived, his young king’s face calm, his ancient eyes solemn and new at the same time. He sat on the cloud marked Adrastia and looked over at Noah, and nodded once, gravely.","Behind his cloud, two women stood side by side. Tatiana, red-haired and gorgeous in her Keeper’s black, smiling very grandly at nothing in particular. And Rose, standing exactly one pace closer to Achilles than Tatiana was, with her arms crossed and her face perfectly pleasant.","Achilles looked away from Noah and around at the whole gathering, at the thrones and the clouds and the terrifying figures and the Keepers, and his eyes widened slightly.","There was a great deal to see. The entire plain seemed packed with power, with existences, with Roots.","The last golden cloud filled at this time.","And the sky cried out!","It happened seconds later. Above the ring of thrones, the grey snowing sky split open, not in one place but in many, one after another all around the great circle, and through every opening an aura bloomed!","Auras of Immense Ones!","They came down onto the floating thrones one by one, and their very existence announced each of them as they came!","| THE DIMENSIONAL DEVOURER, POONA, already seated, raises a hand in greeting to the others.|","|THE ASHEN CANTOR descends upon the throne of black glass. Embers drift from its shoulders and sing as they fall.|","|THE HOLLOW CHOIR takes the throne of bone.|","|THE DISSECTING SCHOLAR settles onto a throne of polished instruments, adjusts his spectacles, and looks over the Roots below with open academic delight.|","|THE VERDANT REGARD takes the living throne in leaf. A green gaze, soft as early spring, settles upon one golden cloud below and stays there.|","|THE SALT-CROWNED MATRON takes the hollowed star. The snow around her throne turns to brine and falls as rain.|","|THE LANTERN OF THE LAST SHORE descends. Its light is warm. Its throne is empty of anything but that light.|","|THE KEEPER OF THE UNBROKEN VOW arrives, and says nothing, and has never needed to.|","And more still, throne after throne filling, until dozens of the floating seats were occupied!","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly!","Some of the Immense Ones he could see clearly, vast and terrible and perfectly visible on their thrones. A titan of ember and ash!","A great soft shape of green light. Moriarty with his tentacles and his spectacles, beaming!","But others were only haze. Their Dimensionality was simply too deep, and they let it express itself freely, so that when Noah looked at their thrones he saw only a blur of light and weight and presence, a shape his sight could not hold together no matter how hard it tried.","Power!","This was power! His whole existence buzzed with it. A few dozen Immense Ones, gathered in one ring above one mountain, each one of them a blinding sun. Was this all of them? Or was this only a glimpse of how deep the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity truly ran?","Below the thrones, all around the ring, the beings on the golden clouds began to rise.","They did it together, without anyone telling them to. The stag stood with his bells ringing softly. The water-woman rose. Minerva stood, unhurried, crown still tilted. Even Achilles rose from his cloud, straight-backed, eyes lifted to the ring of suns above.","Noah was the last!","He stood, slowly, and looked up at the thrones. Every one of them seemed to blaze like a sun in the snowing sky.","Standing was no issue. He could respect their power! They had come very, very far to sit where they sat, further than he had come yet.","But he looked up at those floating thrones, at the beings on them shining through the snow, and he could not help wondering.","How long would he stand down here on a cloud, instead of sitting up there on a throne?","Only time would tell!"]},{"number":5798,"title":"Chapter 5798: Chapter 5797: The Convocation of Roots! II","paragraphs":["They all stood grandly and the thrones settled, and for a long moment nothing on THE Firmament Mountain moved but the snow.","It fell over the Plain of Accord, over the ring of golden clouds and the strange figures standing on them, over the Keepers waiting a pace behind each cloud. It drifted up toward the floating thrones of black glass and colossal bone and living leaf, and on the Immense Ones seated there it simply vanished, like flakes landing on hot stone.","Then Sir Moriarty rose!","He rose from his throne of polished instruments without any ceremony at all, eight tentacles uncurling, small neat spectacles glinting, and yet the whole plain turned toward him at once, every Root Bearer and every Keeper, as though he had rung a bell.","\"Welcome ,\" Moriarty said. It carried to every corner of the plain without seeming to try. \" Welcome to THE Convocation of Roots. A Root that never meets another Root grows crooked, and one that never tests itself grows soft. So we gather you here, on the oldest mountain in the Legacy, and let you find out what you are. The rules are few.\"","A tentacle lifted. \" First, no one dies. A bout ends when one of you yields, is carried from the Plain, or a Keeper steps between you. Do not argue with your Keepers when they do. Several are considerably older than they look.\"","Behind Noah’s cloud, Verys did not blink!","\" Second, there is no order of bouts. There is only the Challenge. Step into the center and name who you wish to face. The one named may refuse, once , in the whole of the Convocation. A refusal is remembered. The Legacy has a very long memory.\"","One refusal. Spend it, and everyone watching would know exactly who had made you flinch! Noah thought of this and set it aside. He did not intend to flinch from anyone here.","\" Third, and the one most of you came for. Favors. Any Immense One seated here may grant a Favor to whoever impresses them. A sliver of their Immensity. A lesson. A Relic from their keeping. A door opened that you could not open yourself.\" His spectacles glinted.","Above him, the thrones stirred!","| THE ASHEN CANTOR shifts on its throne of black glass. Embers fall from its shoulders. It appears bored.|","|THE HOLLOW CHOIR murmurs in a thousand low voices. It is taking bets. It will not say on what.|","|THE SALT-CROWNED MATRON has already chosen three favorites and intends to be proven right.|","|THE DIMENSIONAL DEVOURER, POONA, is very excited, and would like everyone to know it.|","Noah almost laughed. He sat very still on his golden cloud instead, and turned the rules over one by one.","A tournament, then, where the audience were the titans of the Legacy and the prize was their attention. Winning was worth pride and standing. But a Favor was worth more than every win on this plain put together.","Okay!","He kept his Provenance drawn tight and his dreams still. First he wanted to see how the others fought. Information first.","\" Then let us begin, \" Moriarty said. \" Who steps first onto the Plain?\"","The cloud marked Dravos sagged as the figure on it stood.","He was huge! Dark armor covered him from throat to heel, scorched and dented and glowing dull red along evry seam, as though the fire inside had never gone out. He stepped down onto the plain, and the ground beneath the snow dented into a shallow crater under a single step.","A Physical Root, Progeny of THE Ashen Cantor, built to be heavier than anything in his way!","On the throne of black glass, the embers stopped falling for a moment.","Dravos walked toward the center, each step a slow crater, and the whole ring of clouds watched him go. He clearly meant to go first, and felt no need to wait for anyone’s opinion on it.","Yet at this time...","\" Wait, wait, wait!\"","Every head on the plain turned!","Someone was running up the last Conduit, actually running, feet flying along the glowing path with no Keeper in front of her! She came over the edge in a spray of snow, skidded to a stop with a hand on her knee, and grinned around at everyone.","She wore a silk dress of deep blue embroidered all over with gold, high collar closed at the throat, slits cut high up both sides so nothing would ever get in the way of her moving.","Her black hair was wound into two tight spiraled buns tied with white ribbons, half loose from the run.","And her legs!","They were the first thing anyone noticed and the last thing anyone would forget.","Thick, powerful thighs heavy with muscle, the thighs of someone who had spent her whole existence kicking things that did not want to be kicked, and calves drawn tight as strung bows beneath them, bare but for white wrap-bands at the ankles and soft cloth shoes!","Every shift of her weight moved them with a coiled, springing ease that promised a great deal of violence.","She was thick!","Her face was round and cheerful, eyes crinkling at the corners with a smile Noah suspected never left.","She bowed to the thrones, too fast and almost slipped on the snow.","Noah’s sight opened her.","| SHEN HUALING(LING).|","|VERITAS: 1. PROVENANCE: 1. POTENTIA: 1. PONDUS: 1.|","|ROOT OF IMMENSITY: ??????|","...!","Noah’s smile faded.","One in everything!","And every hair on Noah’s body lifted at once!","It was not pressure. Minerva pressed on him like a weight from afar. This girl pressed on nothing at all, and standing near that absence felt like standing beside a mountain that had decided to look like a pebble.","His packed, compressed existence, unbothered by beings at eight hundred, went quietly still.","Across the ring, Minerva had gone very still too.","The girl brushed snow off her knee and waved at everyone.","\" Sorry for being late! But I was promised to go first!\"","Moriarty was quiet a moment. \" Promised by whom, young lady?\"","She tipped her head back and smiled, not at Moriarty but at one of the hazy thrones, where an Immense One sat so deep in its own Dimensionality that no one could see it at all.","\" Oh ,\" she said cheerfully. \" You know.\"","The hazy throne did not answer!","In the center of the plain, Dravos turned his helmeted head slowly toward her, and the red at his seams brightened.","\" The Plain,\" he said, like a furnace door grinding open, \"is mine first.\"","She looked him over, the armor, the craters, the glow, and her whole face lit up!","\" Big fucker, you need an opponent anyways. Loosen the fuck up! Come on!\"","She hopped down off the Conduit and walked out onto the Plain of Accord, soft shoes leaving small neat prints beside his craters. She stopped a few paces in front of him and bounced on her toes, once, twice, rolling her shoulders, the great muscles of her thighs flexing and settling.","\" Ready? I am Ling, big fucker, and I...love to fight!\"","Dravos did not answer her as he was actually a but angry!","He planted his feet, and his Provenance came out of him!","It poured off his body in a red-black flood that did not stay a flood for long. Hardening, it set in plates and ridges and interlocking scales, layer on layer, like molten iron setting on an anvil, until he stood inside a second suit of armor built over the first, taller than before, broader, every seam of it running with a dull forge-glow.","His Provenance had a name, and it announced itself in the heat rolling off him: THE Provenance of THE Unquenched Forge. Whatever touched it would be hammered. Whatever struck it would be struck back.","He took one step toward her, and the Plain of Accord shook!","The crater under his foot was deeper this time. On the golden clouds ringing the plain, Root Bearers who had been lounging a moment ago sat up straight, and more than one of them gripped the edge of their cloud as it rocked!","This was a Progeny of THE Ashen Cantor, a Fiend-path Root, and he was genuinely grand.","\" Yield ,\" Dravos said. \" I do not hold back well as it would be a shame for there to be an accidental death. You feel...ridiculously weak. Do you even have any Provenance?\"","Ling bounced on her toes, ribbons swaying, and looked him up and down with open admiration as if she had never seen someone so fucking stupid.","\"I came here to test myself against the truly grand,\" Dravos went on, his voice grinding out of the helm. \" Not to break a girl who ran up the stairs late. Step off the Plain.\"","\"Aw,\" Ling said. \" That’s sweet!\"","And she stepped in.","WUU!","She did not use a single authority. Noah watched for one, a weaving, a flicker of Provenance, anything at all, and there was nothing. She simply took one step forward, turned her hips, and kicked.","Her shin met his breastplate.","BOOM!","It rang like a bell the size of a Dimension being struck! The sound rolled out across the whole Plain of Accord and up into the thrones and away over the snowing mountains of the Legacy, and in the middle of it, THE Provenance of THE Unquenched Forge caved in around the shape of a single girl’s leg!","Dravos went backward!","He slid, feet still planted, carving a trench through the snow and the stone of the oldest mountain in the Legacy, a hundred paces of it, before he stopped.","\"...!\"","The plain went dead silent!","Then Ling was on him again!","It was not a fight. It was a performance, and she was having the time of her life! She kicked from the knee and from the hip, snapping strikes that cracked the forged plates wherever they landed. Her open hands swung out like hammers and the armor buckled under her palms. Then up his chest she ran, launched off his shoulders, came down heel-first on his helm, and landed laughing.","Then she threw a flurry of kicks so fast they stopped looking like kicks at all, only a blur of thick powerful legs and flying white ribbons, and every strike sprayed blood and red-hot flakes of shattered Provenance across the snow!","She laughed the whole time. Bright, delighted, cheeks flushed, and getting less sane by the second.","Dravos roared, and his Root answered.","Noah felt it happen! Across the ring, the forge-glow of THE Ashen Cantor’s throne flared in answer to its son. The Physical Root inside the armor bore down on itself, and Dravos grew heavier. Denser. The plain groaned beneath him as his weight doubled, doubled again, until he was a being simply stronger than the rules of the fight, the Fiend-path made flesh, too heavy for any blow to move!","And yet..","Oh, and yet!","Ling kicked him, and he moved!","It did not matter. None of it mattered! However heavy he made himself, she was heavier still, a girl with 1 in every measure, and his weight meant nothing at all to hers.","Noah let his Provenance unfurl, just a little. Just enough to look properly.","And he saw it!","Her existence had abandoned everything else. There was nothing in her but one thing. No layers, no borrowed weavings, no Causes or Intents or grown foundations stacked on top of a Root, as everyone else carried theirs. Her Root did not sit inside her. It was her, from her skin to her core, all of her. The Root and the girl existed as one.","She was a Root of Immensity!","...!","Above the plain, the thrones broke their composure.","| THE ASHEN CANTOR rises half out of its throne of black glass. Its embers have stopped singing.|","|THE HOLLOW CHOIR falls silent, all thousand voices at once.|","|THE SALT-CROWNED MATRON leans forward. \"...What is that child? Whose child is it? Is she one of the new entrants?\"|","|THE DISSECTING SCHOLAR is writing very quickly. His spectacles nearly slipped.|","|A hazy throne ripples. It appears pleased.|","Ling ducked a haymaker that would have flattened a mountain range and came up grinning, blood on her smile.","\" More !\" she shouted. \" More, more, give me more! Are those big muscles for show? Is all that Provenance for show?! Lots are watching- dodge this at least!\"","HUUM!","She swept his legs out from under him. His guard dropped. She stamped once, hard.","The Plain of Accord cratered!","The ground caved inward around her foot in a bowl wider than a city, and Dravos went down into the bottom of it in a crash of shattered armor, and the whole mountain shuddered from peak to root!","On its throne, THE Keeper of the Unbroken Vow pulsed once.","It was over!","A Keeper was already at the bottom of the crater, an old grey-bearded figure in black and fur who had not been there a heartbeat before, standing over Dravos with both hands raised and his face perfectly calm. Dravos lay in the ruin of his own forge-armor, alive, barely, plates scattered across the snow in smoking pieces. His Root flickered weakly inside him like a banked coal that someone had stepped on.","Ling stood at the rim of the crater, breathing hard, ribbons hanging loose, blood speckled across the gold embroidery of her dress, and beamed.","Noah sat back on his cloud, and let his Provenance settle tight against his skin again.","A Physical Root, crushed. Not by a greater Physical Root, not by an Empyros rewriting the fight, but by something that had thrown away everything that was not its Root, until there was nothing left of her to be anything else. Dravos had carried his Root. She simply was hers. And a being that is entirely one thing cannot be split, or weighed against itself, or found wanting in any part, because there are no parts!","So that was what the 1s meant. Not weakness. There was only one of her, and it was all Root!","How did a being even get like that? And what had she given up to do it?","He did not know. He wanted to!","|THE ASHEN CANTOR speaks, and its voice is a forge.|","|\"The child lost. I grant him a Favor regardless. Let him remember why he needed it.\"|","Down in the crater, Dravos went very still. Somewhere under the ruin of his helm, Noah suspected, a young giant was trying very hard not to weep.","Because that was a fucking humiliation.","A Favor to its own defeated son. A mercy, and a humiliation, and the whole Legacy had just watched it land.","| A hazy throne speaks. No one can see what speaks.|","|\"A Favor to the girl.\"|","Ling looked up at the haze and bowed, too fast again, bouncing on the snow. Then she turned and walked back along the ring of golden clouds, humming.","She passed right in front of Noah’s cloud, and looked up at him.","She winked.","\" Big boy ,\" she said cheerfully, \"I want to see how you would do between my thighs! I’ve heard a little about you! I’ll let others take the ring for now but afterwards...you and I need to have a go...\"","...!","She skipped off before he could answer and sat down on the very edge of the Plain, with no cloud of her own at all, swinging her legs over the drop and humming to herself.","Noah watched her go, and for once he genuinely did not know what to say!"]},{"number":5799,"title":"Chapter 5799: Chapter 5798: The Convocation of Roots! III","paragraphs":["After Ling, the Convocation found its rhythm, and the bouts came fast.","The water-woman stepped onto the Plain against a Progeny wreathed in white fire, and for a moment the fire seemed to have the better of it, roaring over her in sheets.","Then she simply went deeper. Her Dimensionality sank beneath the fire’s, a whole ocean opening under the Plain where no ocean should fit, and a tide rose out of it lit from within by swimming fish of light. It closed over the flames from below, where they could not reach, and drowned them!","Batiatus went next, and talked the entire time.","\" Your left foot is slipping ,\" he said, and it slipped. \" You are tired ,\" he said, and his opponent staggered. \" That blow will miss ,\" and it missed, by an inch, every sentence true for three breaths within a few paces of him, his Dimensionality pressing each word into the ground around him like a stamp.","He was gloriously, unbearably annoying. He was also winning, right up until he challenged the stag-headed one!","The stag lowered its antlers, and every small bell hung on them rang once.","The sound did not travel outward. It sank inward, down into the Dimensionality of the space around it, and where it reached, speech stopped existing. Batiatus opened his mouth, and nothing true came out.","Nothing at all came out! He mimed a very rude sentence in silence, and the stag struck him off the Plain.","Then the figure in the grey cloak of mist stood, and its opponent attacked, and every blow passed straight through where it seemed to be. It sat at a depth of existence its opponent could not reach, so every strike landed on a shadow a layer above it. It did not move once. The opponent exhausted itself on nothing and yielded!","And Favors fell from the thrones like coins tossed onto a stage. A glint of light from the Salt-Crowned Matron. A murmur from the Hollow Choir. A slip of green from the throne in leaf.","Noah watched all of it, and learned.","Not by copying. He had no interest in carrying someone else’s water or wearing someone else’s silence. But every bout was a different answer to the same question: what is existence, and how does one stand in it? What were their dreams?","The water-woman believed depth was power. Batiatus believed words were. The mist believed it was enough simply to be where no one else could reach. Each of them was a way of looking, and each one struck a small spark somewhere in his own Dream. He let the sparks land, and kept them.","Then Achilles stood.","The king stepped off his cloud onto the snow!","Achilles walked to the center and looked across the plain.","\" You ,\" he said to the stag.","...!","It was a strange choice. Noah read Achilles’s panel as he walked and found his attributes barely reaching four hundred. The stag stood near eight. Half the Plain seemed to think the same thing at once as they could also measure relative Dimensionality, and a murmur ran around the golden clouds!","The stag’s bells rang as it stepped onto the arena as if it had been offended!","The silence came down on Achilles like a falling wall, and the stag came with it, antlers lowered, and he took the first blow full on. He flew. He hit the snow and rolled and came up bleeding, and the stag was already on him agian.","The first exchanges were ugly. The stag was twice his weight in every measure, and every time its antlers came down, the silence came with them, pressing into the Dimensionality around Achilles until even his breath seemed to stop existing. He was losing, badly.","But he was very, very hard to catch.","Noah saw it before anyone else. Achilles was not dodging through space. He was dodging through time, stepping a fraction of a moment out of where the antlers came down, sliding half a heartbeat sideways so a blow meant for him landed on the place he had been.","He was slippery as an eel in a river of hours. And while he slipped, he was reaching.","The bell-silence closed on him again.","And this time he did not dodge it. He let it in.","\" Assimilate ,\" he said, and nothing came out of his mouth, because the silence took the word. It did not matter. The silence went into him anyway, and became him, as everything he touched became him!","The next time the stag’s bells rang, Achilles rang with them, and the silence broke against a king who was now made partly of silence himself!","A gasp went up from the whole plain!","On his throne of instruments, Moriarty set down his quill and leaned forward.","Then the time came out even more!","Achilles’s body flickered. Young. Old, suddenly, lined and white-haired and thin. Young again. His fist met the stag’s shoulder before his arm had moved, and his foot was already planted where the stag was going to step. All of him shone faintly purple with the signature of the rivers of time Noah had watched him swallow, and for a long moment, the smaller king held the larger stag to a standstill!","And then the cold came!","Frost spread from his feet. It ran out across the plain in fine white lines, spidering over the snow, and the falling snow above him bent in its fall, all of it curving toward him as though he were drawing it in. His breath went pale in the air. It was not a man’s breath. It was a winter’s breath, long and slow and old.","Noah went utterly still!","He knew that cold. He had knelt in it in a frozen underworld, and drunk rivers of it. It was packed into his quarks, compressed alongside his Provenance, and he would know it anywhere in existence.","Had this monster... begun assimilating THE Long Night itself?","The stag slowed. Its bells rang, muffled. Its hooves dragged in the frost. The cold was on it now, in it, pulling every movement down toward stillness, and Achilles slipped around it through the edges of time, striking, striking!","HUUUM!","But not wounding.","Achilles could slow the stag and evade it forever, stepping between moments and dragging winter behind him. He simply did not have the power to break it. Every blow he landed skated off a being twice his weight and left nothing but frost.","A Keeper stepped between them as nobody wanted to watch an endlessly boring fight, so it was called!","A draw.","The stag stood utterly furious at having a draw by something so weak, rimed to the tips of its antlers. Achilles stood across from it, breathing slow, and around him the snow was still falling. It neither melted on him nor froze him. It simply settled into him and was gone, as it settled into Noah.","Above the plain, several thrones stirred, and not warmly.","| THE SALT-CROWNED MATRON watches in silence. The rain around her throne has turned to sleet.|","|A hazy throne dims.|","|THE ASHEN CANTOR’s embers fall very slowly.|","None of them said a word. They did not need to. The Plain of Accord felt the chill all the same!","Achilles walked back to his cloud and sat. He looked across at Noah with solemn eyes, frost still clinging to his lashes, and gave a slight nod.","What was this monster thinking? And...had he been brought into the folds of The Caretaker as well?","Noah tapped his knee thoughtfully!","Behind him, Rose finally moved. She reached out and brushed the frost off his shoulder.","It did not come off.","And at this moment, across the ring, Minerva rose!","She leaped!","She came down in the middle of it, and as she landed, seeds spilled from the hem of her green robe. Small, green, glowing, dozens of them scattering across the snow, and wherever one fell, a Dimension bloomed. Tiny ones, pocket realities opening like flowers, each one green and full of leaves and gone again in a breath.","She lifted a hand and pointed.","\" Osmont.\"","...!","The plain went silent. Every Provenance Lifeform and every Progeny on the golden clouds turned to look at him at once!","Above, THE Verdant Regard’s green gaze sharpened until it was almost painful to be under. Poona leaned forward on her throne, eyes shining. Moriarty set down his quill again, laced his tentacles in his lap, and arranged his face into something very carefully neutral.","Was it finally his time to make a move?","Noah stretched and stepped down off his cloud, and walked out onto the snow to face her as he wasn’t fearful even though she was grand!","Her voice came into his mind.","\" There’s been a lot of talk, in case you didn’t know. Some of the Immense Ones think you’re one of them. The three. There’s a prophecy of the Long Night, and I don’t even know if you know it, but Mother and some of the others have been whispering it since the hour you were brought here.\"","Her green eyes held his.","\"I don’t believe it. I reject it. Why should existence listen to a rhyme? Why should everything that is be bound to three supposed beings?\"","\". ..I’m sorry. For the animosity it seems I have. It isn’t you, really. I just want to prove them wrong. Existence is too grand to be steered by three beings. It has to be. Or what are the rest of us for? Just background? Just nothing?\"","Her crooked crown caught the snowlight.","\" The moment anything is born, it has a role to play. Some love to think the man in the gilded chair matters more than the farmer pulling weeds in the dirt. They convince themselves existence is a grand play, where a few loud names run the stage while everyone else is scenery filling up the dark. It doesn’t work like that. Not one role is grander than the next. No one is a background character, made just to watch someone else live. The king, the beggar, and the stray dog. Every single life carries its own weight.\"","...!","Noah almost smiled.","Him? One of the three, in some random prophecy? He could say with a fair amount of certainty that that was not the case. For a long while now, he had been reining in the weavings of THE PROTAGONIST, precisely so that they would not drag him into the center of anything grand and ridiculous without his say!","He could be mistaken for some grand figure, certainly. But he was not going to fit neatly into any role that others had designed for him in advance!","\"I don’t know whether I’m one of three ,\" he answered, calm, in his mind to hers. \" I don’t much care. I don’t live by prophecy either. I live by my Dream. We agree on more than you think so...let’s find out who’s right anyway.\"","They had just been eye fucking each other intently this whole time as from above, a booming command came!","\" Begin ,\" said Moriarty.","Minerva looked at him.","That was all she did at first, and it was enough. Where her gaze landed, existence was judged, and what was judged began to grow. The snow at Noah’s feet sprouted. Green shoots burst up through it, budded, bloomed into pale flowers, rotted, and returned as fresh shoots, all in the span of a single glance!","Roots of green authority tore up out of the Plain and out of the empty air itself, thick as tree trunks, wrapping around him, growing into whatever they held and through it, meaning to take root in him and grow him into something else.","They found nothing to grow into.","Noah stood still and let them try. The roots wrapped his crystalline body and pressed, searching for a seam, a borrowed thread, anything at all that was not his own, and his compressed existence gave them nothing. There was no soil in him that was not already him. The roots slid, and scraped, and could not sprout.","But the pressure behind them was immense. Nine hundred and ninety-nine in everything, all of it bearing down at once, and for the first time since the frozen underworld, his crystalline skin buzzed!","A thin line of light opened along his forarm, and another across his ribs!","Minerva’s voice rang out loud this time, for the whole plain to hear.","\" You’re holding back? Everyone here is watching you! Why won’t you confirm or deny what they think? Let’s make everything clear right here! Let them all know there are no chosen ones!\"","Noah looked at the green roots wrapped around his arms, at the flowers blooming and dying at his feet, and then up at her.","\"I’m... learning at this moment ,\" he said. \" Your weavings. Your Provenance. Your Dreams. I am trying to understand, before anything else.\"","Minerva’s eyes flared, green, then white with anger.","\" Then understand this!\"","The whole Plain of Accord erupted into a forest of Dimensions!"]},{"number":5800,"title":"Chapter 5800: Chapter 5799: No Immensity! I","paragraphs":["The Plain of Accord was gone!","In its place, in a single heartbeat, stood a forest older than any forest had a right to be. Trees the size of mountains tore up out of the snow, trunks thick as rivers, canopies lost somewhere up among the floating thrones, and they did not stand still.","They grew, and died, and grew again. Every leaf that budded on them held the weight of a Dimension blooming into being, and every leaf that fell was that Dimension collapsing, thousands upon thousands of them erupting and dying and erupting again in every branch, so that the whole forest roared with the sound of realities being judged!","On the edge of the Plain, Ling clapped, eyes shining.","On the golden clouds, Progeny and Provenance Lifeforms leaned forward as one, and no one said a word.","And in the middle of it all, Noah stood and took the forest on his body.","It came down on him from every side. Roots thicker than towers wrapped his legs and crushed. Branches swung like the arms of titens. Leaves fell on him like a rain of breaking Dimensions!","His body glistened through it. His crystalline skin had taken on the sheen of ancient jade, dense and deep and faintly luminous, and beneath it infinite dreams and Provenance moved in slow blue-gold currents. It held. Even so, Minerva’s Provenance was so heavy that fine cracks kept spreading across it, one after another, light leaking out of each thin line!","But he held on.","Against a being at nine hundred and ninety-nine in everything, crashing down on him with the weight of an entire Dimensional forest, he held on!","Every second had been a day of compression for him, and every one of those days was packed into him now, and it was grand. His foundation did not so much as tremble.","Oh!","But what more could he do?!","He let the lid come off.","Not all at once. One layer at a time, carefully, as a man opens a door into a room he has never entered. Stellar golden clouds billowed out of him first, soft and bright, rolling out through the roots and the trunks into the forest around him.","The dreams went first.","Wherever the golden clouds drifted, the forest slowed. Its frantic growing and dying turned lazy and strange. Trees that had been erupting toward the sky began instead to bloom into shapes no tree could ever have learned, towers and faces and curling stairways of bark that led nowhere.","Leaves drifted down slowly, turning over and over as they fell. Time itself, near him, began to dream, and Minerva’s growth-speed stumbled in it!","Noah then let the Physical side of his Root press outward, all the dense weight of those packed quarks, the cold of the Long Night crushed down into every one of them. His body simply became heavier than her forest could move. The great roots around his legs wrapped tighter, and heaved, and lifted nothing. He was not holding them back. They simply could not find the strength to move him!","Then the Conceptual side.","He looked at the forest around him and dreamed, plainly and completely, that it was a forest in a dream.","And existence half-agreed!","Around him, the trunks went hazy at their edges. The roaring of breaking Dimensions softened into something far away and muffled, the sound of a storm heard from inside a warm house. Half the forest was still real. Half of it was a dream Noah was having about a forest, and that half began, very gently, to sleep.","This was it. This was what he had seen from the inside, in the purple sky of the Chrysalis!","Minerva wrote growth onto existence. That was her Root, an Empyros’s power, judging and growing and rewriting whatever her eyes fell on. And Noah was heavier than the writing, the Fiend’s answer, a thing so dense that no sentence could lift it. But he also wrote back, dreaming his own sentence over hers.","He was both. The writer and the page!","Her judgment landed on him, and he stood.","His dream landed on her forest, and it slept!","He took a step forward.","Then another!","He walked through her forest toward her, step by step, across the dreaming Plain, and everything she threw at him either broke on his weight or fell asleep in his dream. Across from him, Minerva’s eyes flickered coldly in his sight.","Above the Plain, the thrones broke.","|THE DIMENSIONAL DEVOURER, POONA, is standing on her throne and cheering.|","|THE DISSECTING SCHOLAR’s spectacles have fogged. His quill is racing.|","|THE ASHEN CANTOR’s embers have stopped.|","|THE VERDANT REGARD’s gaze has gone cold and fierce. It is fixed on her daughter.|","|A voice from a hazy throne: \"...His power is lower. So why is she not dominating?\"|","|Another answers: \"One of them walks the path of a Fiend, but still...\"|","...!","Minerva felt it.","Noah watched her realize it. She had come onto this plain to dominate, to show the whole Legacy that no chosen one existed, that existence was not bound to three beings whispered about in the snow. And she was not dominating!","In front of every throne and every cloud, she was being pushed back across the Plain of Accord by the very being she had meant to disprove.","Her pride was cracking, and her argument with it.","She stopped. She drew one long, calm breath, and lifted her head toward the sky. Toward the ring of floating thrones, and every Immense One seated on them.","Then she looked back down at Noah, and spoke to him alone.","\"To live true to yourself ,\" Minerva said into his mind, \" means you keep walking even when the ground gives out beneath your feet. It means you believe in what you are doing even when the whole of existence looks at you, spits in the dirt, and calls you a fool. Even when existence itself stops believing in you.\"","Her green eyes held his, steady.","\" But where is the line? How far can someone push before stubbornness just becomes madness? How true can anyone actually live? When the sky says no, and the cold says no, and every turning of the road says no, and no, and no again, how much can you believe before your own ribs crack under the weight?\"","She did not look away.","\"I don’t know where that edge is. Maybe you only find out when you fall off it. But I know what sits inside my own chest. I believe in my own skin. I believe in what I can build with my own hands. And right now, I don’t believe in this existence. I don’t believe its rules, and I don’t believe its winter.\"","The dreaming forest drifted around them, slow.","\" So if existence wants to tell me no, let it. I will pit my belief against existence itself. And we will see which one breaks first.\"","...!","Minerva stopped attacking.","Her forest died all at once. Every mountain-trunk, every root, every leaf of breaking Dimension, gone in an instant, crumbling into green dust that the snow buried in moments. The Plain of Accord lay bare and white again, and silent.","In the silence, she whispered aloud.","\" Then I’ll become Immense right here, and prove it with that.\"","...!","What?","Motherfucker, what?!","HUUM!","She called everything.","Every sliver of Immensity she had ever been given, she drew into herself at once. Everything she had inherited from her mother. Everything she had grown on her own. Every Favor ever granted to her by any throne. It all came pouring in from wherever it had been kept, green-gold light streaming across the snow toward her, and her Root blazed!","The Plain of Accord shook to its foundations!","On the golden clouds, Progeny and Provenance Lifeforms cried out and gripped the edges as they rocked. Above them, the thrones leaned in, all of them at once.","| THE VERDANT REGARD half rises from her throne of living leaf.|","|\"Minerva. Stop.\"|","\"Not here, child!\" Moriarty’s voice cracked across the plain, sharp for the first time since Noah had known him. \" Not in this cold!\"","Noah went still.","THE First Gu of Time had said it, in the purple sky of the Chrysalis. Those who grasp Immensity in this cold may have a chance. Only a chance, and nothing guaranteed. And Minerva was actually trying it, here and now, in front of everyone?!","At this time.","The snow answered her.","It thickened. It spiraled. Out of the grey sky above the thrones, it began to pour toward her from every direction at once, a vast white vortex drawing down onto a single figure in a green robe at the center of the Plain. The Long Night had turned its attention onto a Root trying to become Immense beneath it.","And for one heartbeat, she almost did it!","A crown of green-gold light rose over her hed, far grander than the crooked one of leaves she wore. Her figure grew, climbing upward, vast and radiant, until she stood taller than the floating clouds. Behind her, a shape formed in the air, tall and narrow and edged in light!","And on her chest, the Root of Immensity that had always been hidden from Noah’s sight blazed into view, and it was changing. Its fibers were thickening, branching, reaching upward into a trunk. It was becoming a tree!","An Immensity was blooming, right there on the Plain of Accord!","Awe lit every face on every cloud. Even the thrones went still.","But...","The light of an opening door shut.","Her eyes filled with belief and immensity became ashen!","No door opened and let her through. It simply closed, soundlessly, in her face.","Her Root cracked.","Then it severed!","BOOM!","The sound of it carried across the whole Legacy, from the Firmament Mountain to the farthest peak, the sound of a great tree breaking in half. Green light poured out of her like blood, spilling down her robe and into the snow, and Minerva screamed!","\" OOOOOH!\"","Her eyes rolled back, showing white.","Then they turned pale!","And she spoke, but it was not her voice.","It was layered. Ancient. Calm, and terrible, a great many voices speaking together through a single throat, and every word fell on the silent Plain like a stone.","|No door shall open, because no new Immensity shall rise to open it. In the endless winter, no new Immensity shall arise!|",".. .!","Absolute silence.","Every Immense One on every throne went still. Several of the hazy thrones flickered violently, their shapes jolting in and out of sight!","On his throne of instruments, Moriarty’s quill snapped in his grip. Poona was not smiling anymore.","And at the edge of the Plain, Ling had stopped swinging her legs.","Noah stared at the girl in the center of the Plain with the winter in her eyes.","No door shall open? THE First Gu of Time had said the opposite, not long ago. Doors are opening, she had said. The Caretaker had said a door shut long ago was beginning to be unshut. Even the Augury, the one prophecy everyone seemed to be whispering, ended by promising that the True would walk out the far side of the Night.","And this voice said no. No door. No new Immensity. Not ever.","So who was speaking?","He did not know!","The pale light drained out of Minerva’s eyes.","She collapsed into the snow.","Above, THE Verdant Regard rose from her throne.","For the first time, an Immense One left its seat. A vast green presence sank down out of the sky, soft as spring, shrinking as it came, until it was only a figure made of gentle green light kneeling in the snow at the center of the Plain. She gathered her daughter’s limp body against her and held her.","She looked down at Minerva with grief. Pure and plain! And under the grief, something unfathomable rose!","Then she lifted her head, and looked at Noah.","Her gaze was cold.","She said nothing. Not one word. And then she was gone, and her daughter with her.","The center of the Plain of Accord lay empty.","In the snow where Minerva had fallen, an illusory Root lay smoking, green and severed, broken clean in two. As Noah watched, frost began to creep across it from the broken end.","Slowly, it was freezing."]}]);
